{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'review|delegate|reap|abandon|abandoned|review-run-reaps' .pose/knowledge .pose/adr .pose/specs --glob '*.md'\"","aggregated_output":".pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-range-names-its-other-work.md:25:Origin: the open follow-up of `pose-abm-subject-evidence` (crit medium), prioritized by the maintainer on 2026-10-09. The observation counted unattributed commits, so a reviewer knew the range was contaminated but not by what; the ABM field pilot's false positives came from exactly that mixing.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-range-names-its-other-work.md:40:- R2: The review bundle warning shall name them.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-range-names-its-other-work.md:51:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-range-names-its-other-work.md:53:- modified: pose-mcp/schemas/v1/review-bundle.schema.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-range-names-its-other-work.md:91:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable.md:22:`pose-contract-adoption-registry` introduced `contract_adoptions` in the review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable.md:23:policy, and `pose update` writes it. The review policy decoder calls\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable.md:28:pose: invalid schema-v2 review policy: json: unknown field \"contract_adoptions\"\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable.md:33:started failing every review closeout in that repository. Any environment not\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable.md:63:- R4: The review policy decoder shall ignore fields it does not know.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable.md:74:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go` — the policy decoder\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable.md:178:  1.8.1 declares `component_aware_adopted_at` and `review_bundles_adopted_at`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable.md:200:- R4 [satisfied] <the review policy decoder no longer disallows unknown fields, so a field added after 2.0.2 is ignored rather than fatal by any engine from 2.0.2 on. This is forward-looking by construction and cannot be demonstrated against 1.8.1, which is the strict reader it does not change>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable.md:218:- [done] Report unrecognised review policy keys as a doctor finding, recovering what dropping DisallowUnknownFields gave up. Delivered by `pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys`: `review.policy-keys` warns on any top-level key the engine does not model, derived from the struct's own json tags. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-11-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable.md:219:- [done] Say in the release notes that adopting a contract makes the instance unreadable to engines predating it, since no encoding avoids that. Done in `pose-release-notes-name-contract-adoption`: the notes carry a Compatibility section built from the contract registry, so the release that introduces a contract names it without anyone remembering to, stating the boundary each contract actually has — a top-level key refuses engines before 2.0.2, an id in `contract_adoptions` does not — and a contract added without its introducing release fails a test. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-10-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable.md:220:- [done] Run the previous release's binary against a policy this one writes, as a test rather than by hand. Done in `pose-release-boundary-rehearsal`: the previous release is built from its own tag and probed with `review-plan`, which reaches the loader the by-hand `check --strict` never did — that wrong probe is what produced the retracted claim. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-12-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-06-pose-install-and-upgrade-journeys.md:22:Walk, in CI, the two ways a project meets this engine — a fresh install, and an instance installed by the latest published release and then updated — asserting what onboarding promises: a strict check that passes, a doctor with no warning, one next step, a configuration review that asks once per new capability, and a signed answer applied with `pose adopt --request`. Fix what walking them exposed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-06-pose-install-and-upgrade-journeys.md:26:Every onboarding change so far was tested on fixtures built by the current engine. The release that matters is the one users already have: an upgrade from it must read clean and must not leave a review addressed to a role nobody holds. Part of roadmap pose-v7-onboarding-and-consolidation (milestone guided-onboarding).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-06-pose-install-and-upgrade-journeys.md:40:- R1: `tests/journeys/install-and-upgrade.sh` shall walk a fresh install (strict check, clean doctor, the onboarding spec as the next step, nothing to review) and an upgrade from the latest published release (strict check, clean doctor naming the pending decisions, one review request per new capability, a second update asking nothing, a signed answer applied with `pose adopt --request`); CI and `scripts/verify.sh` shall run it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-red-signal-clears-only-at-the-head.md:82:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-slsa-provenance.md:117:- [done] After the first tagged release, confirm `gh attestation verify` passes for all six archives and checksums.txt, and record the evidence. Confirmed on v0.18.2: all six archives and checksums.txt verify against signer workflow `release.yml@refs/tags/v0.18.2` (SLSA v1 predicate, source digest f62c014). Evidence in `pose-first-release-evidence-confirmation`. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:high review:2026-09-18)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-report-help-names-every-flag.md:166:- [open] Hold every command's help to the flags its parser accepts, not only `pose report`'s — measure how many commands accept flags their help does not name before deciding whether it is worth one check (owner:unowned crit:low review:2027-03-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-quickstart-real-lifecycle.md:22:Rewrite the quickstart as chapters that follow the lifecycle a project actually runs — setup, the entry gate, `pose start`, a decision the agent cannot take alone (answered with a signature), review and `pose close` — each executed in CI exactly as documented, and fix what walking it exposed: `pose close` marked a spec done with an untraced requirement, the spec template's example delivery target blocked closeout, and the reviewer had to discover evidence refs and required tools by trial and error.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-quickstart-real-lifecycle.md:41:- R2: When `pose close --apply` stops for a reviewer, it shall print the sealed evidence refs and an attest command filled with them, one `--tool` per required tool and one `--criterion` per pending judgment; a tool or mechanical criterion with no sealed evidence of its class shall be proposed as deferred (no delivery target in scope), not-used (no producer) or not-applicable with a reason to write — never with evidence of another class — and each material structural fact shall get a `--mapping` placeholder for the criterion that answers for it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-quickstart-real-lifecycle.md:43:- R4: The quickstart shall follow, in chapters, install and `pose setup`, the entry gate, `pose start`, implementation and evidence, an action request answered with a registered key's signature and visible in Attention, review with the filled attest command, the trace gate refusing and then accepting `pose close`; `tests/quickstart/first-governed-loop.sh` shall execute every chapter and assert the documented states in CI.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-quickstart-real-lifecycle.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-quickstart-real-lifecycle.md:70:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-validation-runtime-guardrails.md:16:bound local checks and delegate untrusted execution through an isolated Harness contract.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-validation-runtime-guardrails.md:117:- [open] Wire the approval-identity stamping (ADR-007 execution identity) once Conductor exposes the endpoint, so emitted plans become executable by the Harness. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-16)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-delivery-authority-diagnostics.md:32:  unrelated review profile schema constant.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-delivery-authority-diagnostics.md:36:- R4: Excluded lifecycle inputs shall use repository-relative paths so review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-delivery-authority-diagnostics.md:46:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-delivery-authority-diagnostics.md:47:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-delivery-authority-diagnostics.md:48:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-delivery-authority-diagnostics.md:49:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_authority_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-delivery-authority-diagnostics.md:90:  is regenerated before sealing the governed review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-delivery-authority-diagnostics.md:114:Implementation validated and closed through the governed review gate on 2026-10-01. Canonical strict validation passed 48/48 checks at f41b5aa; review bundle `rvb-dc6e8974393c12d4` was fresh and approved before `pose close`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:21:Make `pose assess` commands leave a sealed review checkout unchanged, so a reviewer running a planned assessment tool does not fail its own run.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:27:Assessments outside sealed checkouts keep persisting as today. The output a reviewer sees is the same JSON the persisted run would write.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:36:- R2: When the working root is a sealed review checkout (`POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT` or the review runtime marker), `pose assess` shall not persist, whether or not `--no-persist` is given, and shall say so.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:37:- R3: The review brief shall plan assessment tools with the non-persisting form.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:39:- R5: The review brief shall tell the reviewer to run the planned `pose` commands with the engine that dispatched the run (`\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\"`), since the `pose` its shell resolves may be an older engine that ignores `--no-persist`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:62:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:63:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:64:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:65:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:66:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:82:`pose assess discover|integrate|tech-debt` accept `--no-persist`. In a sealed review checkout they do not persist, and `init`, `snapshot` and `request` refuse. The review plan's assessment tools carry `--no-persist`, so bundles sealed from now on plan that form.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:112:The review plan carries `--no-persist` explicitly rather than relying on the environment, so the planned command is correct in any checkout a reviewer copies it into.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:126:- 2026-11-24: review round 1 (rrn-cd0ac9394ca5892b, gpt-6-luna at max effort) failed: the reviewer ran the planned `pose assess ... --no-persist` with the installed `pose` its login shell resolved, an older engine that ignores the flag, and it wrote into the sealed checkout. Its draft also found N1: `GenerateComponentAssessmentMarkdown` wrote without the guard. Fixes: every writer in the assessment files calls the guard, and `TestEveryAssessmentWriterRefusesASealedCheckout` scans them so a new unguarded writer fails; R5 adds `review-brief/9`, which has the planned `pose` commands run as `\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\"`. Both fixes have tests that fail with them mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:148:`pose assess discover|integrate|tech-debt --no-persist`; no persistence and refusal of the writing subcommands in a sealed review checkout; the Store's assessment writers refuse there; the review plan runs assessments without persisting, and `review-brief/9` has the planned `pose` commands run by the dispatching engine.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md:160:L1: the guarantee rests on `POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT`, which the dispatch sets; a reviewer process that clears it can still write, and the dispatch's comparison of the checkout after the run still fails that run.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:12:delivers: capability:delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:15:# Spec: The approval of a delegated review survives routine drift of a done scope\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:21:A scope that is done keeps the approval a delegated review gave it when the repository moves on, as it keeps the approval a person attested.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:25:Every spec closed with a delegated review turned non-terminal as soon as another spec changed a file the closed one had sealed. `validation-matrix.json` is sealed by nearly every spec and `POSE.md` by many, so five specs closed in one day (B31, B33, B36, the material-binding spec and the sealed-plan spec) read \"no review attempt exists\" a day later, and `pose closeout-check` named each as unreviewed. The retention rule for a done scope exists (`retainedCompletedReview`): a person's attestation is kept over drift. It never applied to a run-backed one, because verifying a run proof asks whether the run still governs the repository as it is now, which no completed scope can answer after anything moved. Measured on a real tree: the proof of B31 failed with \"the bundle was superseded or its inputs changed while the run was going\" and that of B36 with \"sealed bytes changed for .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\".\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:36:- Changing what a reviewer must judge or how a run is dispatched.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:43:- R1: When a scope is done, the approval of a delegated run attested over its sealed bundle shall remain retained after a later change to a file of that bundle's subject, with the same disclosure as any retained approval.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:46:- R4: An open scope shall be verified as before: a delegated approval of an open scope is not retained over a change to what it sealed.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:49:- R7: The assurance read for a retained delegated approval shall be the one of the sealed run, verified, so that `review verify`, closeout and the assurance disclosure agree.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:61:- Scopes closed with a delegated review that read non-terminal read terminal again, with no re-review. A scope whose record was altered still does not.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:67:`internal/pose/review_dispatch.go` (the run's record checks split from its present-state checks), `internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go` (the proof verified as sealed), the retained path of `computeReviewVerification`, the ADR on native signed run proofs and the manual.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:71:- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:72:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:73:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:74:- modified: .pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:76:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:86:- capability:delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:99:- [ ] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:108:- Consequences: the retention of a delegated approval ends only by revoking the issuer's pin, altering the record, or reopening the scope\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:116:- Consequences: the brief a delegated approval was given on is trusted as the signed record says\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:130:- R1 [satisfied] test:TestADelegatedApprovalSurvivesRoutineDriftOfADoneScope check:delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:139:- A run's brief is not re-rendered for a done scope. The text of `review-brief/4` changed three times under one version in this repository, so the runs briefed with its earlier texts could not re-render; the template version is not guarded against that. It is a follow-up.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:148:A done scope keeps the approval a delegated run backed over later drift of the files it sealed (R1); the verification of that approval is the sealed record's own (R2, R3); an open scope, an altered transcript and a revoked issuer keep their refusal (R4, R5); live verification and issuing are unchanged (R6); the assurance of a retained delegated approval is the sealed run's (R7). Left out: guarding the immutability of a template version, and a superseding-run test of its own.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:151:- pose-mcp/internal/pose (review_dispatch.go, review_run_provenance.go, retained_run_approval_test.go)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:152:- ADR native signed run proofs (amendment); POSE.md and its pt-BR and scaffold copies; the validation matrix gains `delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift-integration`\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:155:- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head, and the suites of `internal/pose`, `internal/cli` and `internal/mcpserver`\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:156:- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review (Claude Opus 5.5, independent by model) concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:159:- The brief of a retained delegated approval is trusted as signed, not re-derived.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift.md:164:- [open] Guard the immutability of every review brief template version by a golden digest of its rendering, so a text change must take a new version, and name the versions in use. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2027-01-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:7:depends_on: pose-hierarchical-review-closeout, pose-version-contract, pose-release-compatibility-matrix\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:48:- Keep Git mutation explicit and reviewable; never stage unrelated files,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:92:  for that version; unreleased preview shall require an explicit preview mode and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:139:  explicit reviewed work.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:181:- Warn rather than fail for pre-adoption tags until backfill is reviewed.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:323:5. Backfill legacy tags with reviewed confidence, then enable strict no-tag-\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:349:  closeout/review evidence.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:393:- Rationale: Notes, fragments and version identity become one reviewable\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:446:- 2026-08-03, review remediation: rejected symlink escapes, unknown evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:457:- Failures: the first full run exposed only expected scaffold drift; review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:482:- R20 [satisfied] report:.pose/reports/2026-08-03-pose-release-lifecycle-closure-review.md.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:483:- R21 [satisfied] check:workflow-security; report:.pose/reports/2026-08-03-pose-release-lifecycle-closure-review.md.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-release-lifecycle-closure.md:515:  secure, reviewable evidence reconciliation path rather than local inference.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-machinery-distribution-contract.md:25:merge still cannot keep. Everything else under `.pose/` — the rules a review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-machinery-distribution-contract.md:189:- R4 is deferred, not abandoned: it needs a real artifact to publish.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-machinery-distribution-contract.md:228:- [spawned: pose-extension-reference-publication] R4: publish a first real signed reference extension end to end through the release-signing pipeline. Deferred from this spec because no artifact worth publishing exists yet, and inventing one to satisfy a checkbox would prove nothing. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-19)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-machinery-distribution-contract.md:229:- [open] Once machinery delivery lands, revisit whether `pose upgrade --force` still has a legitimate use, or whether it only exists because plain upgrade used to be incapable. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-18)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-machinery-distribution-contract.md:230:- [open] The machinery manifest cannot tell a deliberate deletion from unseen content on its first run, so one deleted file returns once per pre-existing instance. If that proves to matter, seed the manifest during the schema migration instead. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-cli-live-helper-coverage.md:68:  is regenerated before sealing the governed review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-cli-live-helper-coverage.md:83:Implementation validated and closed through the governed review gate on 2026-10-01. Canonical strict validation passed 48/48 checks at f41b5aa; review bundle `rvb-725c997a4ffe827c` was fresh and approved before `pose close`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-docs-canonical-route.md:133:  *abandon*. Option 3 actively harms the independence argument it is meant to\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-docs-canonical-route.md:173:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-docs-canonical-route.md:177:- [open] Configure a path-preserving redirect from oseiaspereira88.github.io/pose to docs.harne8.com/POSE; the old host still answers 200 (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-docs-canonical-route.md:178:- [open] Make the Harne8 docs portal emit `<link rel=\"canonical\">` on the POSE pages it serves at docs.harne8.com/POSE (owner:@harne8-platform crit:low review:2026-11-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-integrated-agency-and-runtime-pilot.md:6:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-capability, pose-residual-triage-and-risk-acceptance, pose-condition-response-and-work-metrics, pose-proportional-next-action, pose-release-shared-sufficiency-contract, pose-release-scope-selection-and-exclusivity, pose-agency-readiness-pilot, pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-integrated-agency-and-runtime-pilot.md:45:- R2: Executar cada percurso em trilhas distintas de pessoa e agente, identificando quem operou, quem preparou/confirmou conclusões, execution/run e assurance realmente verificada. Medir a pessoa sem script responder em seu nome; registrar assistência/conhecimento interno, tentativas/loops do agente e limitações de amostra. Sem participante humano real, declarar essa trilha pendente; principal human:* em fixture e rehearsal não contam como experiência humana ou review independente.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-integrated-agency-and-runtime-pilot.md:97:   gates de fase que ainda não existe. R9/trace/review devem verificar essas provas\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-integrated-agency-and-runtime-pilot.md:156:Conferir lint/check, artifact/surface e review independente atual; roadmap-check\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-integrated-agency-and-runtime-pilot.md:186:participantes reais ainda precisam ser fixados. Provas de runtime e reviewer independente\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:2:slug: pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:10:delivers: surface:shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:14:# Spec: The shipped review profiles are at the schema the migration targets\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:23:Two of the five shipped review profiles carried `schema_version: 1`. The v1-to-v2\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:25:over the instance's and logs `review-profile (migrated): <name> (v1 -> v2)`. With\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:56:- R1: Every review profile the distribution ships shall be at\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:69:- `.pose/review-profiles/milestone-integration.json`,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:70:  `.pose/review-profiles/roadmap-outcome.json` — the shipped profiles\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:74:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:75:- renamed: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md -> .pose/changelogs/v4.0.1/pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:77:- modified: .pose/review-profiles/milestone-integration.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:78:- modified: .pose/review-profiles/roadmap-outcome.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.pose/review-profiles/milestone-integration.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.pose/review-profiles/roadmap-outcome.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:88:- surface:shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2 module:pose-mcp profile:cli-surface entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:155:- R1 [satisfied] <TestEveryShippedReviewProfileIsAtTheCurrentSchema reads every profile from the embedded scaffold and requires ReviewPolicySchemaVersion, failing when one is reverted> surface:shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2 evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:156:- R2 [satisfied] <shippedProfileIsCurrentSchema gates the copy-and-log branch; TestTheMigrationOnlyClaimsACopyThatMigrates covers current, stale and unreadable content> surface:shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2 evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-shipped-review-profiles-are-schema-v2.md:172:- [done] Report an instance profile still at schema v1 as a `pose doctor` finding, so an instance that has not run an update since the fix is visible rather than waiting to be noticed (owner:unowned crit:low review:2027-01-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-spec-transfer-reconcile-terminal.md:25:and reviewed. `spec-transfer preview` refuses them with\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-spec-transfer-reconcile-terminal.md:39:Do not reopen, restage or re-review a done executor; do not add a policy\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-spec-transfer-reconcile-terminal.md:48:  and refuse, retiring nothing, when it changed after preview.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-spec-transfer-reconcile-terminal.md:93:Preview selects schema 2 for the mode, checks the executor's status and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-spec-transfer-reconcile-terminal.md:107:- [x] Run the matrix, review and close.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-spec-transfer-reconcile-terminal.md:121:| Negative gates, R1-R3/R5 | matrix check `spec-authority-transfer-negative-gates` | Open executor, unreviewed executor, uncovered or unresolvable targets, owed requirement in a closed spec, changed executor and schema downgrade refused. |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-spec-transfer-reconcile-terminal.md:126:2026-09-26: `spec-transfer preview` of `pose-abm-subject-evidence` from Harne8\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-spec-transfer-reconcile-terminal.md:137:reviews were resealed and reattested.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-spec-transfer-reconcile-terminal.md:160:- [open] Apply the reconciliation to Harne8's seven ABM coordinators after a rehearsal on populated copies. (owner:@harne8-platform crit:high review:2026-10-03)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-subject-includes-its-index.md:2:slug: pose-review-subject-includes-its-index\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-subject-includes-its-index.md:16:# Spec: pose-review-subject-includes-its-index\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-subject-includes-its-index.md:21:Let a review bundle's subject include the index commit that follows the last attributed commit, so the sealed checkout indexes the validation record it is reviewed against.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-subject-includes-its-index.md:24:Committing a validation record with a spec trailer and then the index leaves the subject at the record commit, whose tree still indexes the previous record. The sealed checkout then reports `no passed structured validation evidence is attributed to the review scope`. Every round of the last batch needed an extra binding commit after the index to work around it.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-10-pose-dora-five-metrics-v2.md:183:- [covered: pose-usage-metrics] Add explicit human confirmation of usage findings as `valid`, `wont-fix` or `false-positive`; keep automatic observation counts separate from adjudicated outcomes. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-09-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-09-pose-composition-contract.md:267:- [open] Publishing the contract does not make the composition consume it. Until `docker-compose.prod.yaml` derives its build contexts, ports and environment names from the published artifact, both sides still restate the same facts and the contract is documentation. Coordinate the monorepo-side change, and decide whether a check there should fail when its compose disagrees with the contract this repository ships. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-09-pose-composition-contract.md:268:- [done] `EXPOSE` is the source: the contract already derives from it, and `TestDockerfilePortIsSingleSourced` now fails when the same Dockerfile's `ENV *_ADDR` default disagrees — proven by setting one to :9000 against an EXPOSE of 8799. The compose mapping remains the consumer's copy, which is what the contract exists to let it stop maintaining. Original item: the internal port is declared in the Dockerfile's `ENV` and `EXPOSE`, in the compose mapping, and would be declared a fourth time by the contract. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-13)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-stack-detection-consolidation.md:211:  `discoverValidationModules` delegate to it or get retired, and reusing\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-consolidation-batch-7-authoring.md:95:Gates locais e critérios de saída julgados no [bundle rvb-d90fcc8b6b44054b](../review-bundles/rvb-d90fcc8b6b44054b.json), com [atestação rva-067fe928ac580fe3](../review-attestations/rva-067fe928ac580fe3.json) de uma execução separada do Codex, mesmo fornecedor/modelo herdado. Sem alegação de identidade autenticada ou revisão entre fornecedores.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-20-pose-retire-unused-first-party-action-exception.md:54:- 2026-10-21: Workflow contract, full race suite, native strict matrix (141/141), separate declared review, native verify and guarded close passed.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-19-pose-agy-smoke-test.md:132:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-19-pose-agy-smoke-test.md:145:- [open] Avaliar automação periódica de smoke tests em CI. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:45:- R8: Consumidores de review/closeout, follow-ups, obligations e Attention devem preservar os diagnósticos de domínio em JSON e humano; fontes válidas e legado compatível devem continuar úteis sem blocker global por dados de escopo alheio.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:56:scan de marcadores de dívida técnica e a leitura do histórico de reviews\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:65:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/source_coverage_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:78:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:82:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:126:- [x] Context, readiness e assessment freshness; inventário dos leitores que descartam em silêncio (follow-ups, obrigações, scan de marcadores, histórico de reviews) contra a main 0b2a726f.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:130:- [x] Produtores de obrigação: estado `incomplete`; obrigação descartada por validação, spec ilegível e registro de review ilegível tornam o produtor incompleto, com recorte por escopo.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:132:- [x] Histórico de reviews: tentativas, bundles e atestações ilegíveis atribuídos por nome/cabeçalho; bloqueio quando podem ser posteriores, aviso quando comprovadamente anteriores; `review record` recusa histórico com buraco.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:135:- [x] Revisão por ator diferente e closeout nativo: agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review; rvb-d4e49da25f48b9ae; rva-eb2a3da043e02b89.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:196:`incomplete` de produtor cobre obrigação descartada por validação, spec e registro de review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:198:declara arquivos varridos, perdidos e excluídos. Histórico de reviews: tentativa ou\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:200:comprovadamente anterior apenas avisa; `review record` recusa um histórico com buraco. Sem\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:221:ledger ilegível é perda; o leitor global de reviews valida decisão, `reviewed_at` e fechamento\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:227:de perdas por instante (offsets e frações), não por texto; linha estruturada de review cortada\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:228:é perda; link de pasta de spec e raiz de reviews ou roadmaps que não resolvem são perdas;\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:232:A quarta revisão (6 achados) levou a: item estruturado de review cortado em qualquer ponto\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:244:A sexta revisão (3 bloqueantes, 1 follow-up) levou a: campo de cabeçalho de review repetido\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:245:(`scope`, `review_id`, `decision`, `reviewed_at`) é perda, não registro de outro escopo; o\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:250:tentativa é lida (`schema_version`, `review_id`, `scope`, `scope_digest`, `plan_digest`,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:251:`profile`, `reviewer`, `decision`, `reviewed_at`, `supersedes`, `evidence_refs`) vale uma vez, e um\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:259:`b06-implementation-validation.json`. A oitava revisão independente por `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review`, Codex/OpenAI,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:263:motor até `pose-delegated-review-run-provenance`. Bundle `rvb-d4e49da25f48b9ae`,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:264:atestação `rva-eb2a3da043e02b89`; review verify fresh/approved e close nativo aprovados.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:268:[review B06](../reports/2026-10-17-pose-b06-source-coverage-review.md) e\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:269:[evidência compacta](../results/b06-independent-review.json).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:277:A verificação permanece vinculada ao bundle que casa com as entradas atuais. Um repositório com um registro de review ilegível mais novo que a aprovação\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:279:Journals de action requests são da B13; o ledger legado de reviews mantém a leitura própria\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:280:dele. Registros de outras fontes (por exemplo o histórico de docs-review) continuam fora desta\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:288:- [open] Raiz de estados de componentes que é link quebrado perde o diagnóstico em `updateProjectStateArchitecture` (o estado fica `unavailable` e o `discover` falha antes de publicar; sem aprovação indevida demonstrada, achado R6-F04 da revisão independente) (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-source-coverage-integrity.md:290:- [open] O diagnóstico de um estado de componente ilegível no `updateProjectStateArchitecture` perde o arquivo e o tipo da perda, embora o estado derivado continue conservador (achado R7-F04) (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-spec-transfer-completion-and-references.md:70:- [x] Run the matrix, review and close.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-spec-transfer-completion-and-references.md:93:executor reviews were resealed and reattested.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-public-claims-publication-provenance.md:152:Delivers candidate, prepared and published versions with provenance. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-04-mcp-governance-write-risk-class.md:19:1. **Classify it as `gate`.** Rejected: `gate` promises no writes, and reviewers and\n.pose/adr/2026-10-04-mcp-governance-write-risk-class.md:28:  governance journal, previews unless `apply` is true, and never touches the network.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-04-mcp-governance-write-risk-class.md:30:  as the CLI (`PrepareActionRequest` for the preview, `OpenActionRequest` with\n.pose/adr/2026-10-04-mcp-governance-write-risk-class.md:41:- A later write tool must fit the same definition (local journal, preview by default,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-requests.md:20:Let an agent open, preview and read a material request to an actor — question, options,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-requests.md:52:- R1: `pose action open` (preview by default, `--apply` to write) and the MCP equivalent shall create a request with stable ID, request digest, origin, requested_by (principal, execution), recipient role, kind (decision, approval, input, external-operation, acceptance), question, options with consequences, recommendation when present, qualified targets and per-phase effects.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-requests.md:53:- R2: The request shall be stored in an append-only journal under `.pose/actions/` and reappear after the session ends with ID and digest preserved.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-requests.md:110:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-requests.md:111:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_subject_capabilities_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-requests.md:180:- R1 [satisfied] surface:action-requests evidence:integration <CLI open previews until --apply; MCP pose_action_open is the same domain call> test:TestActionOpenPreviewsThenRecordsAndShowsTheBoundContent check:action-identity-integration test:TestActionRequestSurvivesTheSessionWithIDAndDigest check:action-requests-integration test:TestToolsCall_ActionOpen_PreviewsThenRecords\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-requests.md:182:- R3 [satisfied] <show/list and pose_action_requests return the derived state> test:TestActionOpenPreviewsThenRecordsAndShowsTheBoundContent check:action-identity-integration test:TestSupersededRequestLeavesTheProjection check:action-requests-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-requests.md:183:- R4 [satisfied] <an unassigned recipient is accepted and rendered> test:TestActionRequestOpeningRefusesIncompleteRequests check:action-requests-integration test:TestToolsCall_ActionOpen_PreviewsThenRecords\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-requests.md:189:R1 also asks for the MCP equivalent of `pose action open`, which the first implementation left out: MCP could only read requests. `pose_action_open` now previews unless `apply` is true and calls the same domain function as the CLI. It needed a fourth catalog risk class, `governance-write`, recorded in ADR `2026-10-04-mcp-governance-write-risk-class`, because `gate` promises no writes. Resolution stays CLI-only.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-requests.md:195:Delivers the request domain, append-only journal, CLI open/list/show, MCP pose_action_open and pose_action_requests and the projection adapter named in the spec; resolution is the separate resolution spec. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bound-trusted-reviewer-execution-and-disclose-unavailable-isolation.md:1:# ADR: Bound trusted reviewer execution and disclose unavailable isolation\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bound-trusted-reviewer-execution-and-disclose-unavailable-isolation.md:4:Accepted (2026-10-25), spec `pose-delegated-adapter-containment`.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bound-trusted-reviewer-execution-and-disclose-unavailable-isolation.md:14:Record actual profile, limits and an OperationResult for cleanup in the immutable run before publication. Cleanup removes operation-owned resources through root descriptors opened before spawn, including the exact Git worktree registration; never call recursive git worktree remove on an adapter-controlled path or prune unrelated registrations. Verify identities/backlinks/locks and bound inventories, refusing oversized resources/replacements. Bound setup subprocess wait/capture and disable unsealed checkout hooks. Filesystem calls are subject to OS I/O latency; no hard syscall deadline is claimed. Failed cleanup remains operational failure separately from the domain draft and cannot govern review authority. Keep legacy records readable without fabricating observed capabilities. Raw-output hashes precede redaction; redacted-byte hashes, canonical record and signatures follow. Permissions restrict newly retained artifacts to the executing user.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-attest-refuses-what-verify-rejects.md:22:Run the verifier's attestation rules when an approving attestation is previewed or applied, so `pose review attest` and `pose review auto-attest` refuse, with the verifier's own reasons, what `pose review verify` would reject.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-attest-refuses-what-verify-rejects.md:26:In the measurement for act-08a9fd2d9a0e50bb every malformed attestation — a structural fact left unmapped, a basis the scope does not declare, a mapping without a reason, an integrity fact accepted as a risk, evidence absent from the bundle — was previewed as `plan=record` and written with `--apply`; the refusal only appeared at `verify`. Each mistake left an immutable attestation behind and cost a second one. The maintainer asked for the refusal to come first.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-attest-refuses-what-verify-rejects.md:40:- R1: When an approving attestation would fail verification against its sealed bundle, `pose review attest` shall refuse it with each reason the verifier gives and exit non-zero, both in preview and with `--apply`, and shall write nothing.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-attest-refuses-what-verify-rejects.md:41:- R2: `pose review auto-attest --apply` shall refuse the same way an assembled attestation the verifier would reject.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-attest-refuses-what-verify-rejects.md:43:- R4: An approving attestation the verifier accepts shall be previewed and recorded as before.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-attest-refuses-what-verify-rejects.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-attest-refuses-what-verify-rejects.md:69:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-attest-refuses-what-verify-rejects.md:70:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_attest_preflight_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-attest-refuses-what-verify-rejects.md:71:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-attest-refuses-what-verify-rejects.md:91:CLI fixtures with a sealed bundle: an approving attestation citing evidence the bundle does not seal, a negative decision, and a valid approval, previewed and applied.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-23-shared-supported-scope-taxonomy-for-review-policy.md:1:# ADR: Shared supported scope taxonomy for review policy\n.pose/adr/2026-10-23-shared-supported-scope-taxonomy-for-review-policy.md:9:B05 reproduces an arbitrary identity_assurance key (spce) accepted by the loader and counted as verified protection, whereas real bundle selection consumes spec, milestone and roadmap. Independence keys have the same missing validation. Existing policy parsing deliberately accepts unknown top-level fields for forward compatibility; that does not authorize unknown members of a security selector map. The component-aware effective review plan ADR governs selection, not arbitrary new scope kinds.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-23-shared-supported-scope-taxonomy-for-review-policy.md:13:Use one closed scope-kind taxonomy for canonical scope parsing, current policy maps identity_assurance and reviewer_independence, and the identity assurance getter. Validate exact keys without trimming or case folding in every supported policy schema, including inactive maps. Known kinds retain their current defaults; an unsupported direct getter input returns no assurance rather than declared/verified. Diagnose field, quoted key and supported kinds deterministically. A current invalid policy fails as a whole through domain, CLI and MCP; no partial projection advertises effective protection. Preserve operator bytes and permissive unknown top-level fields. Future scope kinds require an explicit engine contract/version extension; older engines refuse them.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-23-shared-supported-scope-taxonomy-for-review-policy.md:23:Rejected: silently normalize typos — guesses alter security selection. Ignore unsupported keys with an effective partial policy — hides broken intended protection. Reject unknown top-level fields — violates established forward compatibility. Rewrite sealed history — changes the reviewed contract. Expand into unrelated profile/configuration validation — not needed to close B05's assurance/independence defect.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-cross-version-guard-is-this-repositorys.md:168:- [done] Assert in the workflow contract that this repository's CI sets the environment the guard keys on, so a provider or workflow change cannot turn the failure back into a silent skip. Done in `pose-the-guard-signal-is-declared-not-inherited`, and better than asked: rather than asserting the provider sets something, the workflow declares `POSE_RELEASE_HISTORY_AVAILABLE` and the contract test requires every job running the suite to declare it — which found a third such job, the release workflow's own. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-12-10)\n.pose/adr/2026-10-16-operation-results-separate-execution-from-verdict.md:106:  fresh preview has another digest; a spec that has not moved published\n.pose/adr/2026-10-16-operation-results-separate-execution-from-verdict.md:116:  new preview. Every state the failure confirms is an effect: the recorded\n.pose/adr/2026-10-16-operation-results-separate-execution-from-verdict.md:128:  record and remove it once no start is running, then preview again. The\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-27\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:11:  workflow: .pose/workflows/review.md\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:13:    - pose review verify spec:pose-delegation-mcp\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:14:    - pose delegate ls --json\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:19:# Handoff: delegation MCP review residual risks\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:23:Independent round 5 reviewed implementation f0514d01404e7bed0cfc602f2db065f3e0c6289e of spec pose-delegation-mcp. The maintainer-authorized reviewer agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review declares Codex/OpenAI, another vendor than implementer Claude/Anthropic. Identity is declared; this instance uses unsigned attestations. Last reviewed: 2026-10-27. Native global strict validation passed 158/158 checks at that implementation head.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:33:For F02, start or continue a synthetic run through MCP: observe attempt in the immediate response and run in wait. Align the public identity contract or allocate run identity at handback, with regressions for retries. For F03, cancel the invoking process after the active marker is visible and before handback; inspect ls/status, then wait for the same attempt to finish. Document recovery, correlation and checking the ledger before retrying. A transport cancellation is not delegate cancel. Re-review by 2026-11-26 or before changing handback identity/retry behavior.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:37:F02 is an initial presentation limitation, not loss of the run. F03 is an operational recovery window in intentional detached execution; the run is discoverable and explicit cancellation remains available. Fake-agent tests establish the engine contract, not reviewer cognition or a provider receipt. Neither finding authorizes repeated execution without the ledger's required reason or turns task/partial output into governance evidence.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:41:@oseiaspereira88 owns F02 and F03, both low; review 2026-11-26. The institutional handoff owner is @pose-maintainers. No upstream contribution draft, issue or PR was created.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:45:Spec: .pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md. Consumed knowledge: knowledge:delegation-observation-round4, knowledge:delegation-routing-round3 and knowledge:delegated-rounds-legacy-status. Canonical validation: .pose/results/delivery-validation.json. Local probes, seven mutations and reports: .review-work/round5/ (deliberately untracked). Native bundle and attestation IDs are recorded in the spec Final Report after closeout.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-subject-evidence.md:28:- Invalidation stays narrow: what a review did not consume must not stale it.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-subject-evidence.md:51:  update, and Tasks or Final Report edits do not require a new review.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-subject-evidence.md:53:  surfaced to the reviewer, and it never enters the sealed identity.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-subject-evidence.md:72:review-bundle schema, the manual and its pt-BR translation, the embedded scaffold.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-subject-evidence.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-subject-evidence.md:78:- modified: pose-mcp/schemas/v1/review-bundle.schema.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-subject-evidence.md:145:  observed to carried-forward and stale a review of content that did not move — exactly\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-subject-evidence.md:235:  deliberately louder than a silent pass, and reviewers will see it often at first.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-subject-evidence.md:241:  (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-17)\n.pose/adr/2026-10-23-explicit-channel-scope-for-action-presence.md:47:pinned review policy. Both proofs bind the same actor, request ID/digest,\n.pose/adr/2026-10-23-explicit-channel-scope-for-action-presence.md:61:Expose effective policy in previews as not-evaluated, and distinguish identity\n.pose/adr/2026-10-23-explicit-channel-scope-for-action-presence.md:77:authenticated protocol. Existing review-policy semantics and completed foundation\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:2:slug: pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:7:depends_on: pose-review-attribution-roles, pose-mcp-action-resolve-signed-only\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:13:delivers: capability:mcp-signed-review-attestation\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:16:# Spec: An agent records a review confirmation over MCP only inside a trusted issuer's envelope\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:22:Add `pose_review_attest`, the MCP way to record a review attestation, accepting only an attestation signed by a trusted issuer (`ReviewAttestationEnvelope`), the same proof `pose review attest --envelope` already verifies. Its preview completes a draft attestation for a sealed bundle (schema, bundle digest, attested time, attestation id, confirmation digest) and returns the exact bytes the issuer signs, recording nothing.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:26:A person confirming an agent's review conclusions (`confirmation_mode: adopted-conclusions` or `authorized-operation`) is only provable today from the CLI, by importing an envelope file. A trusted interaction channel, such as the Harne8 issuer of `xref:proj.harne8/spec:harne8-action-request-confirmation-channel` (its R4), has no way to deliver that proof over MCP. The envelope already binds the whole attestation, including `confirmed_by`, `confirmation_mode` and `confirmation_digest`, and the authority claim inside it names the human; this spec only opens the write path, the way `pose_action_resolve` did for action requests.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:30:The same verification and recording as `pose review attest --envelope`: no new claim or envelope format, no second assurance mode. No declared attestation over MCP under any policy. The server never holds a key.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:34:Signing inside the MCP server; changing what makes a confirmation verified (spec pose-review-attribution-roles); attribution supplements over MCP.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:40:- R1: When called without `apply`, `pose_review_attest` shall complete the given draft attestation for its sealed bundle with the values recording would set (schema version, bundle digest, attested time, attestation id) and, when it names a confirming principal, its confirmation digest, and return the completed attestation, its canonical signing bytes and the blockers `pose review verify` would report, recording nothing.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:43:- R4: A recorded attestation whose authority claim names a `human:` principal equal to `confirmed_by`, signed by an issuer the review policy trusts, shall be disclosed with confirmation assurance `verified`; the same attestation with an agent principal or without the claim shall be disclosed as `declared`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:44:- R5: The tool catalog, `pose_review_bundle` and the manuals shall name the tool and its proof requirement.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:45:- R6: A read-only `pose_review_prepare` shall return, for a sealed bundle and a reviewer principal, the auto-attest draft and its pending judgment criteria, writing nothing, so a channel can present a draft for a person to complete and confirm.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:63:Review attestation preparation (shared by recording and preview), MCP tool dispatch, definitions and catalog, manuals.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:67:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:73:- created: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/review_attest_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:74:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attest_signed_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:81:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:85:- capability:mcp-signed-review-attestation module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:89:- New governance-write MCP tool `pose_review_attest` and read-only `pose_review_prepare`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:97:- The preview and recording must normalize the attestation identically, or a signed preview would not verify; one shared preparation function removes the drift.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:103:- Context: Harne8's trusted confirmation channel needs to record a person's confirmation of review conclusions with proof. The engine already verifies an issuer-signed `ReviewAttestationEnvelope` over the whole attestation, and discloses a confirmation as verified when the authority claim names the confirming human; only the MCP write path is missing.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:104:- Options considered: (a) expose the existing envelope import over MCP; (b) add a dedicated confirmation claim bound to the confirmation digest; (c) let the channel run `pose review attest --envelope` through the CLI.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:106:- Rationale: one proof form, already bound to the conclusions through `confirmation_digest`; (b) would be a second claim format for what the envelope already proves, and (c) makes a remote service write into a checkout through a path no decision approved. On 2026-10-08 the maintainer chose an engine tool over (c); (a) over (b) is this spec's proposal, open to review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:113:The tool driven over HTTP JSON-RPC on a fixture with a sealed bundle and a trusted test issuer: the preview's signing bytes, a call without an envelope refused, an untrusted issuer and a tampered confirmation refused, a valid envelope recorded and disclosed as a verified confirmation, and an agent principal disclosed as declared.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:124:- R1 [satisfied] capability:mcp-signed-review-attestation check:mcp-review-attest-integration evidence:integration test:TestSignedPreviewIsWhatTheEnvelopeRecordsAndTheConfirmationIsVerified test:TestThePreviewBindsOnlyWhatItIsGiven test:TestToolsCall_ReviewAttest_PreviewNeedsADraftForASealedBundle\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:125:- R2 [satisfied] capability:mcp-signed-review-attestation check:mcp-review-attest-integration evidence:integration test:TestToolsCall_ReviewAttest_RefusesAnAttestationWithoutAnEnvelope test:TestSignedPreviewIsWhatTheEnvelopeRecordsAndTheConfirmationIsVerified\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:126:- R3 [satisfied] check:mcp-review-attest-integration evidence:integration test:TestAnEnvelopeOverOtherContentIsRefused test:TestToolsCall_ReviewAttest_RefusesAnUntrustedEnvelope\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:127:- R4 [satisfied] check:mcp-review-attest-integration evidence:integration test:TestSignedPreviewIsWhatTheEnvelopeRecordsAndTheConfirmationIsVerified test:TestAnAgentConfirmationStaysDeclared\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:129:- R6 [satisfied] check:mcp-review-attest-integration evidence:integration test:TestToolsCall_ReviewPrepare_IsReadOnlyAndNeedsABundleAndAReviewer test:TestCatalogMatchesGolden\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:133:- The signed positive path runs in package `pose`, where the sealed-bundle fixture lives; over JSON-RPC the tool is driven through its refusals and preview errors.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:139:`pose_review_attest` (governance-write): a preview that completes a draft attestation as recording would, binding the confirmation digest when it names `confirmed_by`, and returns the exact signing bytes with the blockers verify would report; with `apply`, recording only from a trusted issuer's envelope, the same verification and record path as `pose review attest --envelope` (now shared through `RecordReviewAttestationEnvelope`). Recording and preview share `completeReviewAttestation`, so a signed preview records under the id it was signed with.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-mcp-review-attest-signed-only.md:143:Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent. The install-and-upgrade journey fails at origin/main as well (the update from the published 7.0.0 opens no configuration review), outside this scope.\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:3:slug: multirepo-review-continuation\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-09-24\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:11:  workflow: \"review\"\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:12:  commands: [\"pose review verify spec:pose-agent-project-context\", \"pose closeout-check roadmap:pose-multirepo-foundation\", \"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --json .pose/results/delivery-validation.json --report\"]\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:16:# handoff: multirepo-review-continuation\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:20:The multi-repository source roadmap was reviewed autonomously on 2026-09-24.\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:21:The technical record is `.pose/reports/2026-09-24-multirepo-autonomous-review.md`.\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:28:approved spec reviews. The latter two were closed with `pose close`, and all\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:30:has a sealed `changes-requested` review (`rva-b178e83cb461ba31`) because R8\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:44:   and complete its explicit review only after R8 is proven.\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:46:   the approved source and run Harne8's populated preview/rollback before\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:61:`last_reviewed_at: 2026-09-24` reflects the autonomous review above.\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:67:- `.pose/reports/2026-09-24-multirepo-autonomous-review.md`\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:4:Accepted (2026-10-26) by the maintainer. Amends [A delegated reviewer is an adapter that turns a sealed bundle into a draft](2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md)\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:11:The 2026-10-09 ADR made the engine the owner of delegated review. Since then\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:13:containment were delivered. In practice no review has run through them: every\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:14:delegated review, adjudication and closeout attestation still goes through two\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:19:- **They do more than review.** The launcher also hands general tasks to the\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:21:  that, and `pose review` is the wrong home for it.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:24:  concerns. The engine spreads its share of them across `pose review dispatch`,\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:25:  `pose review resume` and `pose review status`, beside commands that govern\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:26:  the review subject (`bundle`, `attest`, `verify`).\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:34:- `reviewers.json` declares the implementation identity statically\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:37:  identity makes \"the other vendor\" unanswerable and compares the reviewer with\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:39:- `pose review resume` continues only the same adapter; switching vendor after\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:41:- `pose review status` lists interrupted runs only; there is no live watch.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:43:- The capability is opt-in (`pose adopt delegated-review`), and turning it off\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:45:  delivery without declaring a reviewer it does not have.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:49:1. **Keep `pose review dispatch` and add flags.** Leaves general tasks outside\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:55:   `pose agent review` reads as an agent reviewing itself.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:56:4. **A `pose delegate` verb owning every delegated execution**, with the\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:65:- `pose review` governs the subject: bundle, brief, attestation, verify,\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:67:- `pose delegate` governs executions: who runs, how, with which access, and\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:73:pose delegate review     <scope|bundle> [--agent auto|<name>] [--detach]\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:74:pose delegate adjudicate <scope|bundle> [--agent auto|<name>] [--detach]\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:75:pose delegate smoke      <target>       [--agent auto|<name>] [--detach]\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:76:pose delegate task       <prompt-file|-> [--agent auto|<name>] [--access read|sandboxed|write|full]\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:79:pose delegate ls      [<run>|<bundle>] [--active] [--json]\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:80:pose delegate watch   [<run>|<label>] [-v] [--lines <n>] [--no-follow] [--json]\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:81:pose delegate wait    <run> [--timeout <d>] [--json]\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:82:pose delegate resume  <run> [--wait-until-reset[=<max>]]\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:83:pose delegate handoff <run> --to <agent>\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:84:pose delegate cancel  <run>\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:85:pose delegate agents  [--json]\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:95:  guarantees. `review`, `adjudicate` and `smoke` force `read` access, the\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:99:- Keep `pose review dispatch`, `pose review resume` and `pose review status`\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:114:- Replace `reviewers.json` (schema 1) with `delegation.json` (schema 2):\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:129:  reviewer with the implementation recorded in the bundle, not with whoever\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:137:- Read availability from `pose delegate agents`: the CLI on the path and the\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:147:  the partial into a review.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:158:  or a non-interactive run records `delegated_review: false`. `pose update`\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:160:- When `delegated_review` is false, a plan that requires `different-actor`\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:162:  limitation `delegated-review-disabled`. One agent of one vendor can take a\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:164:- `pose delegate task` does not depend on the capability: it is a tool, not a\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:165:  review rule.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:170:  delegated run, read its status and wait with a bounded timeout. The attempt\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:191:by label, run name or session prefix; picker with live preview and refresh;\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:198:1. **Name:** `pose delegate`.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:216:[`pose-delegated-review-conclusions`](../specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md),\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:228:- `pose review dispatch`, `resume` and `status` become aliases and then\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:229:  disappear; documentation, skills and help move to `pose delegate`.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:230:- `reviewers.json` becomes `delegation.json`; instances migrate through\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:234:- 