iew_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-fixtures-exercise-production-path.md:83:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-fixtures-exercise-production-path.md:162:  tool half of `review.evidence-vocabulary` — are executed. The remaining twelve\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-fixtures-exercise-production-path.md:185:- [done] Run the same coverage audit over the other command surfaces, since this one found three unreached behavioural branches in a single command. Run in `pose-policy-keys-and-release-surface-coverage`: it found 36 functions at zero, the largest being the whole release surface, which now runs under test from 0 of 20 functions to 20 of 20; the rest are carried as a follow-up there. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-12-09)\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-08-15\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:27:finished spec's `review bundle --seal` failed with \"no immutable attributed\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:80:  existing local alternative (`pose review attest`/`auto-attest`). Both now\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-verified-public-install-contract.md:47:  owner/repo placeholders reappear in `docs-site/docs/ci.md` or\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:3:slug: pr15-component-aware-review-provenance\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-08-13\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:10:  spec: \"pose-component-aware-review-plans\"\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:11:  workflow: \"review\"\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:12:  commands: [\"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp\", \"pose review-check spec:pose-component-aware-review-plans\", \"pose artifact-check --spec pose-component-aware-review-plans --strict\", \"pose surface-check --spec pose-component-aware-review-plans --strict\"]\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:16:# handoff: pr15-component-aware-review-provenance\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:20:Formal review of spec `pose-component-aware-review-plans` (PR #15) ran in a\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:28:  closes all four blocking review findings and the low-severity ordering-text\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:50:  inline review threads with links to the regressions.\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:51:- In a separate review execution, inspect the remediation and record a new\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:54:  `pose review-check spec:pose-component-aware-review-plans`, then run\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:59:- Do not treat this remediation execution as an approval: the next review\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:61:- Keep prior review attempts and committed provenance immutable; corrections\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:69:`@pose-maintainers` (independent reviewer for the superseding review attempt).\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:73:- `spec:pose-component-aware-review-plans`\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:74:- `adr:2026-08-12-component-aware-effective-review-plans`\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:75:- Review attempt `.pose/reviews/rvw-20260813T032130Z-c42b8c1e.md`\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:76:- Review attempt `.pose/reviews/rvw-20260813T063956Z-b11e7bcc.md`\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-24-decision-log-action-recovery-intent-and-refusal.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-24\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-24-decision-log-action-recovery-intent-and-refusal.md:22:Use one immutable intent per predecessor and the existing nonblocking journal lock. A command refuses without recording an action event; previews never sign. Keep incomplete operations visible and restrictive. Reference the prospective ADR for protocol and compatibility.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-24-decision-log-action-recovery-intent-and-refusal.md:34:@pose-maintainers reviews changes to persistence or audit contracts.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-04-obligations-are-projected-action-requests-are-persisted.md:21:own shape: `WaitingOn` in readiness, `ReviewAttestationPendency` in review,\n.pose/adr/2026-10-04-obligations-are-projected-action-requests-are-persisted.md:24:docs review and `OpenObligations` in spec transfer (findings F05, F08). An agent\n.pose/adr/2026-10-04-obligations-are-projected-action-requests-are-persisted.md:36:schema-valid; the reading \"a person reviewed this\" is not supported by them.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-04-obligations-are-projected-action-requests-are-persisted.md:78:copied from `reviewer`. A declared `confirmed_by: human:x` written by an agent\n.pose/adr/2026-10-04-obligations-are-projected-action-requests-are-persisted.md:114:  creates a second ledger to reconcile with specs, reviews and follow-ups.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-04-obligations-are-projected-action-requests-are-persisted.md:135:consult. The first vertical slice covers spec dependencies, review judgment,\n.pose/adr/2026-10-04-obligations-are-projected-action-requests-are-persisted.md:136:closeout and ActionRequest; release queues, docs reviews, capability triggers\n.pose/adr/2026-10-04-obligations-are-projected-action-requests-are-persisted.md:143:Every new gate in this program is reviewed against its cheapest formal\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:2:slug: pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:12:delivers: capability:delegate-picker-and-claude-runs\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:15:# Spec: The delegate picker runs in any login shell and reads at a glance\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:21:`pose delegate watch` opens a picker whose preview works whichever login shell the user has, and whose list shows state, agent and age in columns.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:25:The picker handed fzf a preview written as a POSIX `while` loop; fzf runs a preview with the user's login shell (`$SHELL -c`), and fish refused it (\"Missing end to balance this while loop\"), leaving the preview pane empty. The list also put the id first and cut the agent column, so a run could not be told from another. The same session found that a delegated Claude task failed on this repository: its instance policy still carried an older Claude profile whose runs end with \"the agent's output could not be redacted\", so the Claude runs showed as failed and never as work done; the profile of the engine repository ran them.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:29:- The mechanisms are the existing ones: the fzf picker of `delegate watch`, `--refresh`, and the delegation policy of the instance.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:33:- Changing what `delegate watch` follows or prints.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:39:- R1: The preview command handed to fzf shall be one POSIX `sh -c '<script>' <pose> {1}` word, with the refresh loop inside the quoted script and the pose path and the run id passed as arguments, so that fish, zsh and bash all parse it.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:40:- R2: The list shall show the state with a one-cell glyph, the agent and the age in aligned columns and the label last, under a header, with the id hidden and still handed to the preview.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:41:- R3: The layout shall put the list at the top with a border, so that the preview and the list stay readable on a narrow terminal.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:53:- `delegate watch` with `--refresh 0` and the numbered menu behave as before.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:59:`internal/cli/delegate_watch.go` and its tests.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:63:- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:64:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:65:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:67:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:69:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_picker_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:73:- capability:delegate-picker-and-claude-runs module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:82:- [x] Make the preview command shell-independent and test it under fish\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:85:- [ ] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:94:- Consequences: the preview needs `sh`, which every system fzf runs on has\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:101:The preview command is run by `sh` with a fake pose and checked by `fish -n` when fish is installed; the existing picker tests keep their fake fzf.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:108:- R1 [satisfied] test:TestThePickerPreviewIsOnePOSIXWordTheLoginShellCanParse check:delegate-picker-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:113:- A delegated Claude task on an instance whose policy carries the older Claude profile ends with \"the agent's output could not be redacted; it was not kept\", a message that does not name the profile. The cause inside the redaction path was not isolated; this repository's policy now carries the engine repository's profile, under which Claude tasks complete. It is a follow-up.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:114:- The list is not sorted or filtered by agent in the picker; `delegate ls --agent` does that.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:121:The picker's preview is one `sh -c` word that fish parses (R1); the list shows glyph, state, agent and age in columns under a header with the label last and the id hidden (R2); the list sits on top with a border (R3). Left out: the diagnosis of the legacy Claude profile in the engine.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:124:- pose-mcp/internal/cli (delegate_watch.go, delegate_watch_test.go, delegate_watch_picker_test.go)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:125:- the validation matrix gains `delegate-picker-integration`\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:128:- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:129:- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:136:- [open] Quote the preview command for a pose path with a backslash under a fish login shell, where single quotes still process `\\\\`; and run the fish parse check where fish is absent by failing instead of skipping in CI. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md:137:- [done] Name the profile in the failure of a delegated task whose agent output could not be redacted, and find why the older Claude profile produces it. Delivered by spec:pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause on 2026-11-12; approved review rva-e5f68c7fb514f381.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-26\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:11:  workflow: .pose/workflows/review.md\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:13:    - pose review verify spec:pose-delegation-routing\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:17:# Handoff: routing review residual follow-ups\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:21:Independent round 3 of commit 040cae6f41090c07e72dd27626cbaace4ddb5f7b reconciled B09, F06 and F07 as fixed. The reviewer is the maintainer-authorized declared identity agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review (Codex/OpenAI); implementation was Claude/Anthropic. The review records two low-severity residual issues. Reproductions and original assertions are retained locally in .review-work/round3/new-probes.log and its overlays; that directory is deliberately untracked. Reproduction recipes below do not depend on those files.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:25:F08: internal/cli/delegate.go computes independent_of_lead using vendor inequality alone. Configure a schema-2 agent with vendor unknown, model unknown, cli sh and read command [sh]. Both `pose delegate agents --lead anthropic/opus --json` and its text form disclose independent_of_lead=true. The correct conservative result is false or explicitly unknown. The auto router, achieved independence and run-backed authority do not consume this boolean. Acceptance is limited to this disclosure defect, not permission to credit unknown identities with independence.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:39:@oseiaspereira88 owns F08 and F09, both low, review 2026-11-25. Keep them as open follow-ups in the spec and link their dispositions to the native review judgments. No upstream contribution draft or issue was created.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:43:Spec: `.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md`. ADR: `.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md`. Review report: `.review-work/round3/REPORT.md` (local evidence only).\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-append-only-spec-amendment-history.md:11:the edit but not the rationale, reviewer or materiality. Comparable systems\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-append-only-spec-amendment-history.md:14:lifecycle) treat intent changes as first-class reviewable events.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-append-only-spec-amendment-history.md:22:   review; unusable as a deterministic gate.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-append-only-spec-amendment-history.md:37:  rationale (required except baseline), pseudonymous `author`/`reviewer`\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-append-only-spec-amendment-history.md:55:  unacknowledged findings (additive catalog change, golden reviewed).\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-append-only-spec-amendment-history.md:65:- Residual: an author can falsify rationale; review owns truthfulness, the\n.pose/adr/2026-10-24-recover-supersession-from-one-immutable-predecessor-intent.md:9:B09 authorizes retirement but cannot converge two journals after an interrupted opening. Returning an existing successor skips retirement. Concurrent successor intents can otherwise race. Preview omits the domain checks and presentation repeats invalidated answers or hides declined/missing-subject conditions.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-24-recover-supersession-from-one-immutable-predecessor-intent.md:15:Share resolution preparation between preview and apply. Missing required proof is pending in a read-only preview, with acceptance explicitly not certified; supplied bad proof is refused. Recheck structural preconditions, policy, proofs and state under the protected append, including answers. Exact semantic idempotency excludes emitter bytes so a renewed proof can acknowledge the same operation, but conflicting payloads cannot. Allow recipient-authorized waiver of a declined, materially current condition; invalidated/missing content requires replacement/repair.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-24-recover-supersession-from-one-immutable-predecessor-intent.md:24:- Skip proof on partial retry: rejected because a prior preview/opening is not current retirement authority.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-24-recover-supersession-from-one-immutable-predecessor-intent.md:28:The public preview/refusal and competing-intent semantics are breaking and need release compatibility review before publication. No policy or issuer is adopted. Upgrade all writers sharing these journals before adoption; older writers do not enforce the new intent reservation. Filesystem replacement by arbitrary external writers remains outside authenticated historical authorization. A corrupt intent or partial journal yields repair-required, not automatic repair. Revisit this decision if transaction storage or the action audit policy changes.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:3:slug: adr-sealed-review-bundles-review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-08-13\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:10:  spec: \"pose-review-bundle-convergence\"\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:12:  commands: [\"pose lint-spec pose-review-bundle-convergence --ready-check\", \"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --report --report-task review-bundle-convergence\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:16:# decision-log: adr-sealed-review-bundles-review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:20:The current full-body review scope digest lets closeout bookkeeping alter the\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:21:subject that was just approved. Component-aware review also exposed transient\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:22:provider merge provenance and excessive full-plan rereview. The proposed ADR\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:28:ADR `2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations` is accepted. The core,\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:31:implemented under `pose-review-bundle-convergence`.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:35:- Prove `prepare -> validate -> seal -> review -> attest -> close` converges\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:36:  without a second bundle or review.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:48:  promoting the feature from preview.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:54:require include/exclude golden fixtures and review production deltas after the\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:64:- `spec:pose-review-bundle-convergence`\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:65:- `adr:2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations`\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:66:- `adr:2026-08-12-component-aware-effective-review-plans`\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:67:- `knowledge:pr15-component-aware-review-provenance`\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-qualified-artifact-authority-and-explicit-spec-transfer.md:31:  lifecycle, requirements, review or delivery claim. Separate transfer from\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-qualified-artifact-authority-and-explicit-spec-transfer.md:62:Negotiate required reference metadata with review policy schema 3 and\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-qualified-artifact-authority-and-explicit-spec-transfer.md:84:reviewed scope, which this ADR forbids. The terminal mode requires the\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-11-06\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:35:Consultar `report:2026-11-06-pose-b34-global-review-view-budget.md`. Ainda não há\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:112:@pose-maintainers. A coordenação mantém integração e gates. Use `pose delegate`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-validate-report-carries-its-run.md:23:A review of pose#93 pointed at the validation report its evidence commit\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-validate-report-carries-its-run.md:35:Regenerating the report, which is what the review asked for, would have\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-validate-report-carries-its-run.md:104:- [x] The test fails against the previous code with the symptoms the review saw\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-validate-report-carries-its-run.md:144:  manually_` and `_No validation output detected_` — the review's symptoms. With\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-14-decision-log-escalation-validate-native.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-08-14\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-14-decision-log-escalation-validate-native.md:10:  spec: \"pose-component-aware-review-plans\"\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-14-decision-log-escalation-validate-native.md:22:`.qwen/worktrees/pr15-review`; module discovery recursively treated that\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-14-decision-log-escalation-validate-native.md:45:  review closeout. Success means zero new uncovered failures, not deletion of\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-14-decision-log-escalation-validate-native.md:61:- `spec:pose-component-aware-review-plans`\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-14-decision-log-escalation-validate-native.md:62:- `knowledge:pr15-component-aware-review-provenance`\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-26\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:10:  spec: pose-delegated-review-completion-signal\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:11:  workflow: .pose/workflows/review.md\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:13:    - pose review verify spec:pose-delegated-review-completion-signal\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:17:# Handoff: observation review residual follow-ups\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:21:Independent round 4 of commit a8ce8cf97acb89815cc8440f028ec319c63ec1c3 closes the milestone `observation` of the roadmap `delegation`. The reviewer is the maintainer-authorized declared identity `agent:independent-claude-sonnet-5-5-review` (Claude Sonnet 5.5, Anthropic), the same vendor and another model than the implementer (Claude Opus 5.5, session `f2a4d9f2-d557-4064-ae96-6ed52bb47cd2`); by the rule of 2026-10-09 another model satisfies `different-actor`, another vendor would be preferred. Rounds 1 and 2 were Codex (OpenAI), round 3 and this one Claude Sonnet 5.5. N02 (a detached run read a relative `--note-file` from the project root instead of the caller's directory) and the follow-ups F-R3-01, F-R3-03, F-R3-04, F-R3-06, F-R3-08 and F-R3-10 were reconciled as fixed; no blocker remains.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:25:Open, all owned by @oseiaspereira88 with review on 2026-11-25:\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:28:- F-R3-02 (low, graded medium in round 3 and lowered because the hand-back now precedes the agent, which leaves a window of about 100ms or a supervisor hung over 30s; the engine accepts only low as accepted risk): the SIGTERM, 30s grace and SIGKILL path of a stopped supervisor has no test (swapping SIGTERM for SIGKILL keeps the delegate suites green), and the SIGKILL fallback on the supervisor group does not reach the agent's own group.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:30:- F-R3-07 (low): `on_terminal` fires for `pose delegate review|resume`, not for the deprecated alias `pose review dispatch --via … --apply` nor for a run recorded `stalled`.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:36:- F-R4-05 (low): the regression tests of the review rounds are named outside the `TestDelegat*`/`TestDelegate*` family (`TestADetachedRunReadsTheCallersFiles`, `TestHookBoundAndRelativeCommand`, `TestAnUnrecordedHookOutcomeIsReported`, `TestADetachedRunThatCannotHandBackDoesNotRun`), so the `delegation-surface-integration` check and the documented race selection do not run them; only the unit lane does.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:40:`go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'TestADetachedRun|TestHookBound|TestAnUnrecordedHook' -count=1` and the race selection extended with those names. For F-R3-02 a test that holds a supervisor past the grace. For F-R4-01 a stalled-watch test and a test whose live file cannot be read. Run `pose delegate --help` and the four manuals after any change.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:44:None of these changes dispatch, ledger, continuity, provenance or containment; each is either a disclosure gap, a test gap or a window of at most six minutes. F-R3-05 and F-R3-02 can leave an agent running after its supervisor died; the stalled state and `ls` name the run, and `pose delegate cancel` stops one that is still recorded.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:48:@oseiaspereira88, review 2026-11-25. No upstream contribution draft or issue was created.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:52:Spec: `.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md`. ADR: `.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md`. Roadmap: `.pose/roadmaps/delegation.md`. Review report: `.review-work/round4/REPORT.md` (local evidence only).\n.pose/adr/2026-10-01-reviewable-usage-verdict-journal.md:19:verdict, reason, reviewer alias and timestamp. The CLI accepts bounded relative\n.pose/adr/2026-10-01-reviewable-usage-verdict-journal.md:23:the effective verdict; earlier lines remain reviewable. Reports hash each\n.pose/adr/2026-10-01-reviewable-usage-verdict-journal.md:37:reviewer and no network transmission is added.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-01-reviewable-usage-verdict-journal.md:41:- A verdict can be shared and reviewed in Git while local events remain\n.pose/adr/2026-10-01-reviewable-usage-verdict-journal.md:43:- A tracked review decision names its subject, so contributors must review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-recurrence-flapping-signal.md:98:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-recurrence-flapping-signal.md:102:- [open] Investigate why validate-native alternates in both repositories (11 transitions in 50 runs on pose-dist, 10 in 40 on Harne8); environment-dependent checks such as the release-listing journey and disk-bound builds are the first suspects (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-30)\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-action-answer-proof-and-historical-time.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-13\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-action-answer-proof-and-historical-time.md:30:Invalid proof remains on disk but its consumer receives an explicit error/incomplete coverage. Declared legacy answers remain declared. This scoped fix does not introduce an immutable historical authorization receipt, reauthorize old role membership, or complete the broader review-source reuse contract. Regression tests cover both emitter paths and consumer degradation.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-19-structural-delta-is-a-bounded-observation.md:30:`DesignDeltaReport` compara o subject canônico do review e só afirma fatos\n.pose/adr/2026-09-19-structural-delta-is-a-bounded-observation.md:35:essa conclusão pertence ao profile/julgamento de review.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-19-structural-delta-is-a-bounded-observation.md:59:- A classe `structure` só pode ser usada depois que CLI, MCP, review bundle,\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-11-02\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102.md:11:  workflow: \".pose/workflows/review.md\"\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102.md:15:# Handoff: independent roadmap outcome review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102.md:19:Independent review of bundle rvb-c8e5358c3fcf5b42 at cd22fe8d on 2026-11-02.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102.md:20:last_reviewed_at: 2026-11-02. No commit, push, roadmap close or release authorized.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102.md:24:Fresh CLI build, focused CLI/signature/MCP/presence tests, all quickstart chapters and install/6.2.0-upgrade journeys pass. Supplied strict validation has 184 passing checks at HEAD; full matrix was inspected, not rerun. All three prose milestone gates and their current dependency order were independently reviewed.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102.md:29:- f2 (low follow-up): encode prose release-cut conditions as structured roadmap criteria and bind evidence. Strict roadmap-check reports criteria=0 and only member acceptance; independent outcome review currently covers this gap. Review by 2026-12-02.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102.md:38:@pose-maintainers. Retain f1/f2 until the next review; do not stage upstream contribution feedback without user consent.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102.md:43:Command logs and exact argv: /var/tmp/pose-work-go/review-reached/rm-pose-v7-onboarding-and-consolidation/attest/.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-15-decision-log-github-issue-closing-keyword-format.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-08-15\n.pose/adr/2026-10-17-index-sets-are-published-as-verified-generations.md:23:  `pose artifact-check`, and the bootstrap of `pose review bundle`) changed that\n.pose/adr/2026-10-17-index-sets-are-published-as-verified-generations.md:111:store whose index reads all come from it. The review plan, the review bundle (its plan and\n.pose/adr/2026-10-17-index-sets-are-published-as-verified-generations.md:129:review plan's component map and observed paths, the obligation snapshot's index\n.pose/adr/2026-10-17-index-sets-are-published-as-verified-generations.md:131:reader that needs it (`GetDeliveryIntegrity`, the review plan's component map) and\n.pose/adr/2026-10-17-index-sets-are-published-as-verified-generations.md:133:(observed paths in a review plan, the snapshot's index digest becomes\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:21:A vinculação das entradas do índice, que `review-check`, `closeout-check` e `artifact-check` recalculam a cada chamada, lê os planos de transferência de cada projeto uma vez por operação em vez de uma vez por artefato resolvido, e dá às lojas de origem do acceptance federado o mesmo snapshot de specs que o resolver já usa.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:25:Medido em 2026-11-10 neste repositório (2833 commits, 11 MB de índice): `review-check spec:<slug>` leva cerca de 56 s, `closeout-check` cerca de 51 s e `artifact-check --spec` cerca de 137 s por chamada. O perfil de CPU mostrou o cache de grafos da B33 sem efeito (a segunda chamada no mesmo processo levou os mesmos 51 s) e o custo dominante em `incompleteTransferFor`, que lê e valida cada plano de `.pose/transfers` a cada `Resolve`, ou seja, uma vez por dependência de cada roadmap. Este é o achado que redireciona a fatia 2 da B35: o runtime residente não acelera o que a operação recalcula; a operação precisa deixar de recalcular. O ganho vale para toda chamada, com ou sem runtime.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:29:- Nenhuma resposta muda: a saída de `review-check` e de `closeout-check` é a mesma, byte a byte.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:35:- As cerca de 3100 chamadas ao `git` por `review-check` (348 `git log -1 -- <path>` somam 20 s): é o próximo gargalo e fica como follow-up, porque agrupá-las muda a semântica da simplificação de histórico.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:42:- R3: A saída de `review-check` e de `closeout-check` num repositório real é idêntica antes e depois, e o tempo de `review-check` diminui de modo medido.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:72:- [x] Medir o custo: perfil de CPU e contagem das execuções do `git` de um `review-check`\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:86:- Falsifier: uma resolução que responde de forma diferente com e sem o listing compartilhado, ou uma saída de `review-check` que difere\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:104:- R2 e R3 não têm teste próprio: a comparação byte a byte e o tempo (56 s para 38 s no `review-check`, medidos com o binário anterior e o novo no mesmo repositório) são medições feitas à mão e registradas aqui, não um teste de regressão; a variação de carga da máquina entra nesses números.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:111:O listing dos planos de transferência de um projeto é lido uma vez por operação e repassado às resoluções (R1); as lojas de origem do acceptance federado usam o snapshot de specs da operação (R2); a saída de `review-check` e `closeout-check` ficou idêntica e o `review-check` passou de cerca de 56 s para cerca de 38 s (R3).\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:118:- Result: registrado pela evidência de validação selada; revisão delegada independente concluída com `pose review conclude`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:122:- O gargalo restante é o `git`: cerca de 3100 execuções por `review-check`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:126:- [open] Reduzir as cerca de 3100 execuções do `git` por `review-check` (348 `git log -1 -- <path>` somam cerca de 20 s), sem mudar a simplificação de histórico que cada uma aplica. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once.md:127:- [open] Dar teste de regressão à saída idêntica e ao tempo da vinculação das entradas do índice. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-release-temporal-evidence-review.md:3:slug: adr-release-temporal-evidence-review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-release-temporal-evidence-review.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-14\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-release-temporal-evidence-review.md:16:# decision-log: adr-release-temporal-evidence-review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-release-temporal-evidence-review.md:26:Last reviewed: 2026-10-14. TTL of 90 days covers the staged documentary authoring\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-release-temporal-evidence-review.md:27:and the contract review before functional start; this operational review note\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-release-temporal-evidence-review.md:38:legacy/cutoff, preview, lineage/correction identity, support/coverage and measured\n.pose/adr/2026-09-19-material-design-basis-remains-an-advisory-projection.md:9:ABM slice needs stable, reviewable relationships without inventing a second\n.pose/adr/2026-09-19-material-design-basis-remains-an-advisory-projection.md:20:proportionality and technical truth to the review judgment.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:3:slug: agency-readiness-outcome-review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-11-02\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:11:  workflow: \".pose/workflows/review.md\"\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:12:  commands: [\"pose review verify roadmap:agency-readiness\", \"pose knowledge-check --strict\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:16:# Handoff: agency-readiness outcome review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:20:Independent outcome review of roadmap:agency-readiness at d72b6abb, bundle\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:39:  Harne8 (existing review 2026-11-05), and its adopted authority-transfer exercise\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:40:  (existing review 2026-11-15). These remain open in the pilot spec.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:45:  review of its prose outcome remains necessary.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:72:- Fresh argv/results: `/var/tmp/pose-work-go/review-reached/rm-agency-readiness/attest/round3/`.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-24-seed-first-amendment-from-recorded-start.md:14:Expose a readonly shared history assessment: missing/empty history remains opt-out, malformed history refuses, existing history uses the adopted schema gate. Lint reports pending findings as warnings on in-progress specs and errors on done specs; close checks before transition and again under the lifecycle lock. No automatic baseline, waiver, review or policy adoption at close.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-verifier-assets-variable-fix.md:166:- [spawned: pose-shellcheck-ci-gate] Add shellcheck to CI over tests/release/*.sh and tests/install/*.sh: it catches unbound variables that `bash -n` cannot, which is precisely how this reached a release. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-09-18)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-verifier-assets-variable-fix.md:167:- [open] Decide whether verify-release.yml should verify published artifacts with the verifier from the tag or from the default branch. The tag-based checkout made a fixable verifier defect permanent for v0.20.1. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-02)\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-18-handoff-pose-b06-source-coverage-closeout.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-18\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-18-handoff-pose-b06-source-coverage-closeout.md:11:  workflow: \".pose/workflows/review.md\"\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-18-handoff-pose-b06-source-coverage-closeout.md:12:  commands: [\"pose review verify spec:pose-source-coverage-integrity\", \"pose close spec:pose-source-coverage-integrity\", \"pose check --strict\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-18-handoff-pose-b06-source-coverage-closeout.md:21:Identidade agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review, Codex/OpenAI, declarada;\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-18-handoff-pose-b06-source-coverage-closeout.md:27:rva-eb2a3da043e02b89; review verify fresh/approved. Validação global 139/139,\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-18-handoff-pose-b06-source-coverage-closeout.md:29:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-18.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-18-handoff-pose-b06-source-coverage-closeout.md:52:[parecer](../reports/2026-10-17-pose-b06-source-coverage-review.md) e\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-18-handoff-pose-b06-source-coverage-closeout.md:53:[evidência compacta](../results/b06-independent-review.json).\n.pose/adr/2026-11-22-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:9:The canonical structured result at `results_path` is the only validation evidence that review bundles and closeout load. Producing it means running the whole matrix. `--changed-from` already selects the modules a change can affect: it uses changed paths, declared `dependsOn` edges and the high-criticality policy, and falls back to every module for a change outside all modules. Its record, though, marks the other checks as skipped, so it cannot stand in for the canonical result. In an instance with a slow and partly intermittent matrix, every review round pays for the full run.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:3:slug: module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-08-16\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:12:  commands: [\"pose update --force\", \"pose install\", \"pose index\", \"pose review bundle --seal\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:16:# decision-log: module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:29:generalizes) and superseded the review attestation of every already-closed\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:42:reclassified — still invalidates every closed spec's review attestation\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:45:provenance digest so it only invalidates reviews whose scope actually\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:48:provide) that deserves its own spec and explicit review, not a side effect\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:55:  (`ProvenanceDigest`) and `pose review bundle --seal`'s scope-provenance\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:65:  in `pose-review-bundle-roadmap-path-portability`/session knowledge about\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:69:  to reseal/reattest every closed spec whose review scope includes\n.pose/adr/2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type.md:15:re-review on any predictable timeline, but that also does not represent a\n.pose/adr/2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type.md:20:Nothing was decided here and nothing will change on a review cadence; it was\n.pose/adr/2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type.md:28:   `expires_at` or governed by a materially longer review-not-expire\n.pose/adr/2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type.md:77:  not become false or need review on a predictable timeline, (b) does not\n.pose/adr/2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type.md:92:  `decision-log`\" (a decision was made, a review trigger exists) from\n.pose/adr/2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type.md:122:  `.pose/rules/` rely on ordinary code review for quality control, not\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflig