t.md:189:changes on F1 (medium): `pose review attest` still refused criterion and tool\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:192:from a negative decision. Remediation: `reviewCriterionDispositions` and the new\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:196:a post-review gate deferred, a recommended tool not used), and an unanswered\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:198:approval and a negative does not owe it. The legacy `pose review record` path,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:200:`reviewToolDispositions`. New regressions drive orphan and nameless findings,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:209:Second independent review (2026-10-16, same reviewer, same report) accepted F1\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:218:compares the command's preview and write with the Store's typed refusal (both\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:220:command and the Store; it fails against the previous `review_closeout.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:222:`review_closeout.go` drops from 124 to 122. `go vet ./...` and\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:225:Third independent review (2026-10-16, same reviewer and report, after an\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:233:supersession guard and its preview of a complete draft did not consult the\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:234:admission, so preview succeeded where apply was refused on unchanged inputs; it\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:235:now prepares the bundle as named and the preview of a complete draft reports the\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:241:superseded bundle, preview and apply equal to the domain) fail against\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:242:`c87a7ffc` and pass now. The direct-print ratchet for `review_closeout.go` drops\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:256:Revisor `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review`, execução Codex/OpenAI distinta\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:258:`rva-98ebc45a80704275`; review verify fresh/approved/closed, close nativo, lint-spec\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:261:exigência declarativa atual até pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:262:Consultar a [Fourth round do parecer](../reports/2026-10-16-pose-b02-domain-preflight-review.md)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md:275:proporcional a review bundle. O caminho legado review record sem bundles,\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-20-handoff-pose-b07-implementation.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-20\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-20-handoff-pose-b07-implementation.md:21:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-20.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-20-handoff-pose-b07-implementation.md:34:2. The unused expired Actions waiver was removed separately in d957b4f. No pin or enforcement change. Reconciled full suite, 11/11 mutations and native 141/141 validation passed before the latest three review fixes; regenerate final evidence at the configured .pose/results/delivery-validation.json.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-20-handoff-pose-b07-implementation.md:36:4. Finish artifact/surface checks, native sealed review and closeout before done or adoption. Default artifact attribution reconciled 82 claims with no errors. The Harne8 binding still points at 8aa729a7; do not update it merely because local tests pass.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-agent-skills-compatibility-metadata-and-conformance-gate.md:14:link no prior review had caught. The spec's own stated technical risk —\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:3:slug: delegated-rounds-legacy-status\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-27\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:10:  spec: pose-delegated-review-round-protocol\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:11:  workflow: review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:13:    - pose review status --json\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:14:    - pose delegate ls --json\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:23:Independent round 4 of spec pose-delegated-review-round-protocol reviewed fa0c589aac678fe548e3725f745ba6628cef3e8f. All earlier blockers are corrected. Reviewer agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review is the maintainer-authorized declared Codex/OpenAI identity, another vendor than Claude/Anthropic implementation. This instance uses unsigned attestations. Last reviewed on 2026-10-27.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:27:f-r4-01 is low severity: the deprecated pose review status path omits round/thread fields when constructing interrupted summaries in pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go:611; its text renderer in internal/cli/review_run_continuity.go:116 also omits the round. The current pose delegate ls path and persisted run contain the correct round, and verify/approval do not consume this legacy presentation.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:29:The independent composed-handoff fixture produced a native interrupted run with Round=1. Before handing it off, pose review status --json returned an interrupted_runs row with no round field, while the recorded run had Round=1. The same fixture then handed off and continued the handoff-owned session successfully in round 2. Local reproduction and output: .review-work/round4/handoff-probe.txt and handoff-probe.log (deliberately untracked).\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:33:Reproduce with the existing run-continuity fixture or a fake agent that captures a synthetic session and exits with declared limit code 75. Compare the persisted run, pose delegate ls --json, and pose review status --json before resume. Add regression coverage that the legacy summary/text reports the round and relevant lineage, or explicitly document its narrower legacy projection before retirement. Run the continuity, delegation and round suites. Review by 2026-11-26 or before removing the deprecated alias.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:37:Users of the deprecated status command miss round context; the deprecation hint already points to pose delegate ls. This does not turn partial output into a decision, alter the ledger, or bypass approval. Acceptance is limited to this low-severity presentation gap and its existing replacement.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:41:@oseiaspereira88; low criticality; review by 2026-11-26.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:45:Spec: .pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md. Review: .review-work/round4/REPORT.md (local). Native attestation rva-78b867ebfada5dcb on bundle rvb-aaec9b9e16165671 and the spec follow-up record f-r4-01.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-27-versioned-governance-outcomes-cohorts-and-lineage.md:9:review bundles and attestations, but does not return the identity used to tell\n.pose/adr/2026-09-27-versioned-governance-outcomes-cohorts-and-lineage.md:10:a replayed history row from a distinct attempt, expose the review band's\n.pose/adr/2026-09-27-versioned-governance-outcomes-cohorts-and-lineage.md:12:offer those views without either inferring relationships or reading raw review\n.pose/adr/2026-09-27-versioned-governance-outcomes-cohorts-and-lineage.md:14:`report_type`, `task_slug` and `sequence`; review plans seal a band; remediation\n.pose/adr/2026-09-27-versioned-governance-outcomes-cohorts-and-lineage.md:15:links are explicit in spec frontmatter and validated against immutable review\n.pose/adr/2026-09-27-versioned-governance-outcomes-cohorts-and-lineage.md:26:Accept only the closed report type and review band vocabularies. Apply report\n.pose/adr/2026-09-27-versioned-governance-outcomes-cohorts-and-lineage.md:27:type only to report-history attempt dimensions and band only to review and\n.pose/adr/2026-09-27-versioned-governance-outcomes-cohorts-and-lineage.md:34:spec slugs, category and source band. Do not return reviewer, owner, rationale,\n.pose/adr/2026-09-27-versioned-governance-outcomes-cohorts-and-lineage.md:46:  leaves review metrics unchanged; the report states this facet scope.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-27-versioned-governance-outcomes-cohorts-and-lineage.md:49:  to open only the same project's existing spec/review surfaces.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-27-versioned-governance-outcomes-cohorts-and-lineage.md:54:authority; passing through whole attestations exposes more review data than the\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-v7-2-0-version-alignment.md:23:The native attestation issuer (`pose-native-attestation-issuer`, closed after five independent reviews) lets a project with POSE alone adopt signed attestations and verified identity. Harne8 deferred both until such a release exists; this release delivers it. One unreleased fragment, `added` and not breaking, makes it a minor release.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:3:slug: delegated-conclusions-round4\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-28\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:10:  spec: pose-delegated-review-conclusions\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:11:  workflow: review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:14:    - pose review verify spec:pose-delegated-review-conclusions\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:18:# Handoff: delegated conclusion lock diagnostics\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:22:Independent round 4 reviews implementation 153d54bb2690bbe6b96d8da9760b1f97b6502728. Reviewer agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review declares Codex/OpenAI, another vendor than Claude/Anthropic implementation. Identity is declared; the local review attestation is unsigned. Last reviewed: 2026-10-28 UTC.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:26:R3-B1, R3-F1 and the unsupported-platform case of R3-F2 are corrected. Reused probes cover complete-history recovery, symlink refusal, separate processes and owner death. f-r4-01 remains low severity in pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go:345: only errFileLockUnsupported stops retries immediately. Other permanent backend errors eventually report another owner and omit the cause.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:28:The Unix backend propagates flock errors unchanged. A synthetic overlay returning syscall.EOPNOTSUPP, with only the wait bound reduced from two minutes to 200 ms, reached the deadline in 201 ms and reported another conclusion holding the lock. It published zero proofs and attestations. This is injected error-path evidence, not a claim that the local filesystem lacks flock. Evidence: .review-work/round4/permanent.log, permanent-overlay.json, permanent_lock.go and permanent_wait.go (local, untracked).\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:36:Accept f-r4-01 as a low operability risk: unusual filesystem/backend errors delay failure and misdirect diagnosis. Failure stays closed and does not weaken locking, record an attestation or approve a scope. Linux process coordination was exercised; Windows/Darwin were cross-built, not run. Synthetic signers prove engine handling, not provider identity or reviewer cognition. R2 destinations and capability adoption remain separate work under D2.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:40:@oseiaspereira88 owns f-r4-01, low criticality, review 2026-11-27. Institutional owner: @pose-maintainers.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:44:Spec: .pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md. Review report and independent probes: .review-work/round4/report.md. The spec Final Report records the sealed bundle and attestation after closeout. No upstream contribution draft, issue or PR was created.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-authoritative-release-version-source.md:21:   drift by construction, but the repository stops carrying reviewable release\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-authoritative-release-version-source.md:46:  therefore a single reviewable commit touching `internal/version` and\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review.md:3:slug: adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-14\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review.md:16:# decision-log: adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review.md:26:Last reviewed: 2026-10-14. Proposal is Proposed; specs draft, no IPC/cache/runtime\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review.md:28:the contract review before functional execution; reassess when design/scope changes.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-mcp-tool-catalog-is-a-release-gated-contract.md:22:   removes drift but hides the contract from review; a code change would\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-mcp-tool-catalog-is-a-release-gated-contract.md:25:   into a reviewed fixture; any divergence between runtime, fixture, docs and\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-mcp-tool-catalog-is-a-release-gated-contract.md:35:  `go test ./internal/mcpserver -run Golden -update` followed by human review\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-mcp-tool-catalog-is-a-release-gated-contract.md:36:  of the diff — golden updates are review-gated, never automatic.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-mcp-tool-catalog-is-a-release-gated-contract.md:56:  require only the reviewed golden diff plus docs.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-mcp-tool-catalog-is-a-release-gated-contract.md:63:- Positive: risk classes give reviewers and policy authors (OPA) a stable\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-mcp-tool-catalog-is-a-release-gated-contract.md:66:  review; that friction is the point — the golden diff is the reviewable\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-mcp-tool-catalog-is-a-release-gated-contract.md:68:- Residual: golden updates could still normalize drift if reviews rubber-stamp\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-mcp-tool-catalog-is-a-release-gated-contract.md:69:  them; CONTRIBUTING requires the reviewer to treat golden diffs as public\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-follow-up-ownership-and-triage-sla.md:8:Open follow-ups had a disposition but no owner, urgency or review date — a\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-follow-up-ownership-and-triage-sla.md:21:   `(owner:@alias crit:low|medium|high review:YYYY-MM-DD [by:@actor])`\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-follow-up-ownership-and-triage-sla.md:29:  (required), `crit:` and `review:` (required together with owner) and\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-follow-up-ownership-and-triage-sla.md:40:  reviews `OVERDUE`, and exposes the fields in `--json`.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-follow-up-ownership-and-triage-sla.md:42:  exits non-zero when any open follow-up has an expired review date. CI and\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-follow-up-ownership-and-triage-sla.md:53:- Positive: the live backlog answers \"whose, how urgent, when reviewed\" —\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-follow-up-ownership-and-triage-sla.md:61:- Residual: an SLA can be renewed forever by editing `review:`; the\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-follow-up-ownership-and-triage-sla.md:62:  amendment-history spec will make such renewals visible and reviewable.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-consolidation-batch-9-authoring.md:84:Gates locais e critérios de saída julgados no [bundle rvb-438c67b6d3ae08db](../review-bundles/rvb-438c67b6d3ae08db.json), com [atestação rva-0f6fbc2944934ece](../review-attestations/rva-0f6fbc2944934ece.json) de uma execução separada do Codex, mesmo fornecedor/modelo herdado. Sem alegação de identidade autenticada ou revisão entre fornecedores.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-09-12\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:12:  commands: [\"pose check --strict\", \"pose knowledge-check --strict\", \"pose specs --json\", \"pose followups --json\", \"pose usage --json\", \"pose doctor --json\", \"pose review-plan spec:<slug> --json\", \"pose artifact-check --spec <slug> --json\", \"pose check --json\", \"pose lint-spec <slug> --json\", \"pose history-check --json\", \"pose knowledge-check --json\", \"pose skills-check --json\", \"pose recurrence-check --json\", \"pose index --json\", \"pose state --json\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:31:30-day expiry would retire it in the middle of that work. It should be reviewed\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:103:`artifact-check`, `review-plan`). In `pose validate` it takes a **path** and\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof.md:3:slug: review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-10-13\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof.md:10:  spec: \"pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof\"\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof.md:14:# Decision log: Authenticate review proof before disclosing assurance\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof.md:26:Direct disclosure, verify, review-check, closeout and attribution consume the same authority proof check. Invalid proof never yields a verified claim that could authenticate human confirmation. No records, policy, schema or capability adoption are rewritten. Current issuer pins/grants and current expiry semantics remain; historical trust and reuse provenance require the separate B04 delta.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof.md:30:- spec:pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof\n.pose/adr/2026-10-16-writers-publish-through-one-exclusive-cas-publisher.md:110:inside the protected region — a review that stopped being approved, or an\n.pose/adr/2026-09-25-review-evidence-versus-delivery-target.md:7:`reviewScopeRequiresValidationEvidence` correctly requires evidence for a spec with implementation components, even when it declares no delivery target. Attestation coverage reused that answer as `hasDeliveryTarget`. Consequently, a `validate` tool gated by `delivery-target-declared` cannot be deferred for a componentful spec without a target. The adopter reproduced this failure after its harness checks passed.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-25-review-evidence-versus-delivery-target.md:13:Componentful specs still require current test evidence. Tools conditioned on a declared delivery target follow the target inventory instead of inferred component presence. Invalid paths and unclassified subjects retain their blockers. The change is covered by positive and negative tests under `pose-review-root-binding-parity`.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:3:slug: adr-component-aware-review-plans-review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:7:last_reviewed_at: 2026-08-13\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:10:  spec: \"pose-component-aware-review-plans\"\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:12:  commands: [\"pose assess discover --component pose-mcp/internal/pose\", \"pose lint-spec pose-component-aware-review-plans --ready-check\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:16:# decision-log: adr-component-aware-review-plans-review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:20:POSE 1.0 binds immutable review attempts to a scope-kind profile but does not\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:23:new plan digest, so the design needs an explicit future-review trigger.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:27:ADR `2026-08-12-component-aware-effective-review-plans` is accepted. It chooses\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:30:tracked by `pose-component-aware-review-plans`.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:51:- `spec:pose-component-aware-review-plans`\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:52:- `adr:2026-08-12-component-aware-effective-review-plans`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-engine-package-stays-mirrorable.md:61:- [x] Prove a Harne8 mirror sync builds and passes; strict validation, review and closeout.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-engine-package-stays-mirrorable.md:95:Independent reviewer `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review` approved bundle `rvb-e9c5e6e54616df45` in attestation `rva-bdd5a9d2b672d719`. This was a maintainer-authorized Codex/OpenAI execution distinct from Claude/Anthropic implementation session `296d1fcb-e989-40ae-9362-cf3514db8b26` (`agent:claude-opus-5-5`). The `agent:independent-` prefix is an engine-required declaration until `pose-delegated-review-run-provenance` replaces it; identity is declared and these attestations are unsigned.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-engine-package-stays-mirrorable.md:97:On 2026-10-16, the reviewer independently demonstrated the guard failing with only `assessment_freshness.go` reverted to `origin/main`, restored the exact implementation bytes, and observed the guard passing. `go vet ./...` and `go test ./... -count=1` passed in `pose-mcp`. Auditing `cmd/pose`, CLI hooks, bootstrap and MCP startup found no binary binding path outside version initialization.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-engine-package-stays-mirrorable.md:99:The prepared Harne8 `cirepro` mirror at engine commit `4dcf70b6` passed Harness build, vet and tests. Its parity self-test passed all six drift cases, overlaid 98 upstream test files successfully and confirmed mirror parity. That clone was not edited, committed or pushed by this review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-engine-package-stays-mirrorable.md:101:Native full validation passed 133/133 checks, and explicit module validation passed 130/130, without failures, errors or skips. Strict `surface-check` reported one composed capability and zero findings. `review verify` reported fresh and approved; guarded `close`, strict spec lint and strict structure check passed. Evidence is recorded in `.pose/results/delivery-validation.json`, `.pose/results/pose-engine-package-stays-mirrorable-module-validation.json` and `.pose/results/pose-engine-package-stays-mirrorable-independent-review.json`, plus the sealed bundle and attestation. Discovery with `--update-state` was executed; its generated output was excluded as directed by the maintainer.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-engine-package-stays-mirrorable.md:107:The review identity and vendor separation are declared, without signed provenance. The repository-wide strict check retains 29 warnings, including legacy changelog and capability-assessment age diagnostics. No policy, capability assessment, adoption setting, production code or test was changed by the reviewer. Dedicated vulnerability and secret-scanner binaries were unavailable; the changed diff was inspected and a bounded secret-pattern scan found no matches.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-package-manager-channels-generated-not-hosted.md:23:   upstream review dependency for a project that doesn't yet meet its\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-package-manager-channels-generated-not-hosted.md:56:  and zero upstream review dependency, at the cost of a longer install\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated.md:143:Rodada 1 (run rrn-c5171f8ff89f3ebb, attestation rva-f215ab03914d85c5, changes-requested): 1 bloqueador, tratado. F1 o executor que transmite a saída do Git (`runGovernanceGitStreamContext`) não recebia o ambiente sem tradução: os dois executores passaram a usar o mesmo `governanceGitEnv`, e um teste com um `git` falso no PATH registra o locale de cada um sob uma sessão pt_BR; reprova com o executor de streaming antigo. Os outros executores de Git do motor (`snapshotGit`, `previewGit`, `gitCheckIgnore`) não classificam texto do stderr e ficam como estão. As ferramentas `artifact-check` e `surface-check` da rodada 1 saíram sem resultado porque o revisor usou um `pose` instalado no PATH, de outra revisão, que leu outro change set.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-validate-refuses-empty-go-checks.md:95:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-validate-refuses-empty-go-checks.md:115:`pose validate` fails a `go test` check of the plain form that selects by name when Go reports that no package ran a test, instead of passing on Go's exit 0. pose-dist's matrix passes with the rule on. Independently reviewed by Codex over four rounds; it replaces the abandoned shared test run.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-check-shares-the-federated-material.md:38:- R1: A scope operation created by a review coordinator shall check the consumed index generation's inputs through the coordinator's operation, computing each input's binding once per (root, generation, producer) for all its scopes.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-check-shares-the-federated-material.md:55:- `pose/review_operation_view.go`: a operação de escopo recebe a operação do coordenador.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-check-shares-the-federated-material.md:59:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-check-shares-the-federated-material.md:61:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_scope_index_inputs_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-check-shares-the-federated-material.md:101:- Rationale: (a) precisaria de uma chave que capturasse todas as leituras do material, que não existe hoje; (b) reaproveita a auditoria do coordenador e a interface ciente do vínculo que o D7 exige.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-doctor-guided-remediation-confined-fix-registry.md:62:- **`--fix` defaults to preview; `--yes` is required to mutate; `--only\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-reproducible-release-verification.md:122:- [done] Review the first Verify release run on the next published release: confirm all layers pass and record the reproducibility result (MATCH or explained delta). Reviewed run 31148431844 on v0.18.2: six layers PASS and a bit-identical rebuild (sha256 7b5e82da…). Recorded as MATCH. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:high review:2026-09-18)\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:12:implementation review; accepting remote done alone bypasses composition.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:34:  changes stale the coordinator review. Scope caches by digests and authorization.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:36:  `observed`, or `carried-forward` with a recorded Git head after the reviewed\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:58:  Keep composition criteria and explicit outcome review at the coordinator.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:65:  identity rules. Never fetch, write another project or trigger its review as a\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:72:commits would stale its review without changing the governed contract.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:74:would reject validation recorded after a reviewed implementation without\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:78:Extend existing roadmap/index/review contracts; do not build another gate engine.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:80:contract. Preview migration without rewriting evidence. A program may remain\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:89:closeout agree with `review verify`: any difference between a closed scope's\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:94:recorded and been reviewed again.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:97:the commitment the reviewer accepted:\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:102:- its spec, read in its own project at the sealed and the current revision, is the same before its Final Report (intent, requirements, plan, decisions, validation), found in its CommonMark structure, or, for a section-split spec, in every section but `final-report.md`: a plan digest covers the review procedure, not the requirements;\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:103:- a current review bundle;\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:107:review of the dependency. Its revision, content, evidence, implementation\n.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:108:digest and review may move with the pin. The trust policy digest, which holds\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-v7-1-0-version-alignment.md:77:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-v7-1-0-version-alignment.md:81:- [open] Clean up the temporary directories journey and compatibility tests leave in /tmp when a run is interrupted: 200 were found on 2026-10-09, about 5 GB, and they filled the user quota twice (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-23)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:28:- Evidência de origem: [review ABM](../reports/2026-09-18-pose-abm-review.md), achados Cronologia de base e integridade de transição.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:39:- R1: Oferecer pose start spec:slug com preview/dry-run e apply explícito, resolvendo readiness, dependências e obligations pré-implementação.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:63:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:89:- `pose start spec:<slug>` é preview por padrão, somente leitura e sempre\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:91:  pré-implementação a partir do plano de review declarado (sem structural\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:94:- `--apply --digest` exige `atomic_start_version: 1` na policy de review.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:115:Disponibilizar preview antes de adoption; active legacy permanece unbaselined até reconciliação explícita. Nunca backdate.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:123:- [x] Executar matriz aplicável, obter review explícito e anexar evidência por R-ID.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:128:- Date: 2026-09-27. Implementado sem rollout, como o contract-nodes: preview\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:132:- Contexto: a análise inicial propõe novos controles; o review confirmou limites que exigem implementação proporcional.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:155:- `pose review verify spec:pose-abm-atomic-start` antes da transição terminal.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:160:2026-09-27: implementado sem rollout. Testes novos cobrem preview somente\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:178:reviews seladas invalidadas pela matriz foram renovadas.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:181:- R1 [satisfied] test:TestABMAtomicStartPreviewIsReadOnlyAndDigestBound test:TestABMAtomicStartCLIPreviewApplyStatus\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:186:- R6 [satisfied] test:TestABMAtomicStartPreviewIsReadOnlyAndDigestBound\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:195:`pose start` com preview somente leitura, apply atômico, idempotente e\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-atomic-start.md:207:- [done] Adotado no pose-dist em 2026-10-05 por decisão do maintainer (action request act-fa1d72f029d567a0, opção B): primeiro a data de corte (spec pose-atomic-start-adoption-cutoff), depois `atomic_start_version: 1` com `atomic_start_adopted_at: 2026-10-06`; specs mais antigas aparecem como legacy-unbaselined sem bloquear. A adoção no Harne8 segue harne8-adopt-agency-readiness. Item original: adotar `atomic_start_version` depois do stop/go do piloto, junto com `contract_nodes_version`. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-01)\n.pose/adr/2026-10-14-review-time-context-and-reuse-provenance.md:28:is an inconclusive blocker. Reaffirmation requires the current review's judgment.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:40:  `review-check` are POSE commands, and what supports their disposition is that\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:66:- The existing review suite passes, with its fixtures corrected where they were\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:74:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go` — tool coverage evaluation\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:75:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go` — auto-attest's tool half\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:82:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:93:  property of the scope rather than of the reviewer's diligence. Without it,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:119:- Rationale: `artifact-check` and `review-check` do not report a validation\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:131:  precondition the way `review-complete` already is.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:134:  situation — it is not that the reviewer skipped it, it is that there is\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:184:- R1 [satisfied] <reviewToolEvidenceBlocker takes the sealed set and rejects a ref absent from it, for tools declaring classes only; TestToolDispositionMustCiteEvidenceTheBundleSeals asserts a supported attestation is accepted first, then that naming an unsealed id of the right class is blocked>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-tool-dispositions-must-be-supported.md:201:- [done] Match tool evidence to the tool's component, alongside the same work for criteria. Delivered by `pose-evidence-scoped-to-component`: `reviewToolEvidenceBlocker` refuses a component-scoped tool citing evidence from outside that component, the same check the criteria path got. Verified against the code, not the record. (owner:unowned crit:high review:2026-11-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:2:slug: pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:11:delivers: capability:review-assurance-proof-verification\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:14:# Spec: Require verified review proof before disclosing verified assurance\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:20:Make identity, separation and confirmation disclosure depend on the same cryptographic proof and claim bindings as review verification.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:24:Complete the review-disclosure portion of backlog B01/T2-03 after the action-answer correction in PR #157. The pre-fix shared authority checker validated claim fields but not the signed envelope. A coherent claim with a damaged signature therefore produced a rejected verdict and a verified disclosure. Reuse knowledge:action-answer-proof-and-historical-time and knowledge:review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:28:Preserve declared legacy records, existing current issuer pins/grants and review expiry semantics. Keep identity assurance independent of criteria/decision validity. This delta does not change adoption policy, historical authorization, reuse provenance, approval-write preflight (B02) or cognitive-independence claims.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:32:- R1: A malformed, missing, invalid or untrusted signed authority proof shall never disclose verified reviewer identity, verified separation or a verified claim.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:34:- R3: A trusted signature and valid authority claim may disclose verified identity while semantic criteria or the review decision prevent approval; declared legacy identity shall remain declared.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:35:- R4: Review verify, review-check, closeout and attribution shall consume the shared proof result; invalid proof shall never produce verified human confirmation, including in JSON and human rendering.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:41:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:42:- created: .pose/starts/pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:43:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:44:- created: .pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:45:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-13-review-proof-validate-native.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:47:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:48:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_assurance_proof_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:50:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_assurance_proof_cli_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:52:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-15-pose-b01-disclosure-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:64:- capability:review-assurance-proof-verification module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:71:- [x] Obtain the required different-actor review and verify the sealed subject.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:85:Test damaged signatures, unsigned content tampering, missing proof, revoked pins, coherent claims with other bundle bindings, invalid human confirmation and valid identities with invalid criteria. Compare direct disclosure, verdict, review-check and closeout, plus JSON and human rendering. Run the complete Go suite and CI/Security on the published head.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:96:Domain and CLI/MCP qualification passed. Current global native strict validation passed 132/132 (241.1s) on published subject ea53653b, including 129 checks of the affected component. Targeted race and independent different-actor review passed; native close applied the terminal transition on 2026-10-15. See [the qualification report](../reports/2026-10-15-pose-b01-disclosure-qualification.md), the independent review and native b01-disclosure-* snapshots for current published verification. Both B01 specs now have native closeout; B02 waits for merge. The renamed human-confirmation test now matches the existing ReviewAssurance integration selector; no matrix check is weakened.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:100:Regression mapping: R1 uses TestReviewAssuranceRejectsInvalidCryptographicProof; R2 adds TestReviewAssuranceBindsTheSuppliedBundle; R3 uses TestReviewAssuranceKeepsIdentitySeparateFromApproval; R4 uses TestReviewConsumersAgreeOnTamperedProof and TestReviewInvalidProofCannotVerifyHumanConfirmation (renamed to TestReviewAssuranceInvalidProofCannotVerifyHumanConfirmation in the current qualification). Execution evidence and exact tested commits are recorded in [PR #158](https://github.com/oseiaspereira88/pose/pull/158). Keep the spec in-progress until independent review and closeout.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:104:Current R1–R4 qualification has no unresolved blocker. The current native run and independent review supersede the old environment limitation below; current pins/grants remain the explicit trust boundary. Final-head CI/Security must pass before review readiness.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof.md:112:Native closeout applied on 2026-10-15 after strict 132/132 on ea53653b and independent different-actor review by agent:independent-codex-pr182. Admission closeout-check reports terminal=true, lifecycle_done=true and no blockers; review verification is fresh/approved/closed. Identity and separation remain declared, with no human confirmation. The [qualification report](../reports/2026-10-15-pose-b01-disclosure-qualification.md), [independent review](../reports/2026-10-15-pose-b01-disclosure-review.md) and native b01-disclosure-* snapshots retain admission and current publication evidence. B01 is complete at the spec level; B02 waits for this PR merge. The overall consolidation program remains active.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-cross-repo-portfolio-reuses-mcp-project-authorization.md:80:  reappears — a disappearance is explicit, never a silent gap in the next\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-stack-catalog-expansion.md:122:- [open] Add fixture repositories (poetry, pipenv, dotnet solution) under tests/ to exercise pose stacks end-to-end once the monorepo recipes milestone lands. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-validation-check-additions-are-not-material.md:26:The second measurement for action request act-08a9fd2d9a0e50bb (causality closeout) found that 30 of 34 recent specs would select `structural-materiality@1`, and in 21 of them the only material fact was the validation matrix, because registering a spec's own check rewrites the file. A mapping owed for every registered check is a ceremony every instance pays, and it trains reviewers to paste \"the matrix registers the check that proves Rn\". The maintainer chose to fix this in the engine before adopting the contract.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-validation-check-additions-are-not-material.md:34:Judging whether an added check is adequate to its requirement; that remains the requirement trace and the review criteria.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-validation-check-additions-are-not-material.md:51:- An addition that reuses an existing check name stays material, so it cannot shadow existing evidence unreviewed.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-20-explicit-remediation-links-in-spec-frontmatter.md:8:similar titles, `depends_on`, or a reviewer's identity. A finding ID is local to\n.pose/adr/2026-09-20-explicit-remediation-links-in-spec-frontmatter.md:22:Include nonempty links, sorted, in the semantic review subject and legacy scope\n.pose/adr/2026-08-03-immutable-release-ledger.md:26:and asset digests. Provider workflows retain minimized evidence for reviewed\n.pose/specs/2026-09-30-pose-dist-adopt-published-v6-1-0.md:45:- [x] Run strict checks, obtain review and close adoption.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-consolidation-batch-1-authoring.md:49:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-historical-trust-and-review-reuse.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-consolidation-batch-1-authoring.md:50:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-review-approval-domain-preflight.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-consolidation-batch-1-authoring.md:94:Gates locais e critérios de saída julgados no [bundle rvb-55278fd26bc525db](../review-bundles/rvb-55278fd26bc525db.json), com [atestação rva-408e3a90e46080a0](../review-attestations/rva-408e3a90e46080a0.json) de uma execução separada do Codex, mesmo fornecedor/modelo herdado. Sem alegação de identidade autenticada ou revisão entre fornecedores.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:25:`go test ./internal/cli` takes 192 s of the uncached 280 s suite. Its 131 delegation tests alone take 100 s, strictly one after another (sum of test times 109 s ≈ package time); the fifteen slowest take 63 s: MCP-over-stdio journeys (`TestDelegateToolsOverMCP*`, 4.7–10.9 s), detach and wait loops (`TestDelegateDetachAndWait` 5.2 s, `TestDelegateWaitsForTheFirstReset` 4.1 s, `TestDelegateWatchFollowsLive` 3.5 s), and review-dispatch runs (`TestReviewDispatch*` 2.6–5.4 s). Measured 2026-10-30 with `go test -json`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:59:`internal/cli` delegation, MCP and review-dispatch tests and the helpers they share.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:66:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_wait.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:67:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_mcp_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:69:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_observation_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:70:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_wait_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:71:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:72:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:81:No public surface. Internal: `delegate wait` polls the run's marker every 100 ms instead of 500 ms; `posemodel.AdapterPipeGrace` (default 5 s, unchanged) holds the adapter pipe grace so a test can shorten it; and `POSE_TEST_DELEGATE_WAIT_SIGNAL`, an unsupported test seam, makes a waiter create — exclusively, once, empty — an entry named after its pid in the named directory when it starts waiting on a running run. It controls nothing about the run, and an existing entry is never truncated, followed or opened.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:89:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:101:- R1 [satisfied] check:cli-test-wall-time-integration test:TestDelegateToolsOverMCPHoldAgainstTheFirstReview test:TestDelegateDetachAndWait test:TestADetachedRunThatDoesNotHandBackIsStopped test:TestDelegateWatchFollowsLive test:TestTheWaitAcknowledgementNeverTouchesAnExistingEntry report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:1dc147707c59f910c2cc8bbae2e745cd041e714c — The slowest delegation tests hold their runs on gates and release them on observed events (live events, waiter acknowledgements, process exit, watch output) instead of sleeping; the reviewer's privacy and waiter mutants fail them.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:108:Real-time waits removed from the slowest `internal/cli` delegation tests: package time 191 s → 156 s on 1085 tests, serial, same machine (per-test timings kept outside the checkout). `delegate wait` polls every 100 ms. Independently reviewed by Codex over three rounds.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:112:The package remains serial, so most of its time is the sum of many short tests. A pre-existing race in review dispatch (the active marker is removed before the continuation receipt is written) can make a wait refuse; it was observed once in about twenty race runs (F1).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:116:- [covered: pose-delegation-result-before-marker] F1: write the continuation result receipt before removing a run's active marker, keeping the marker when the receipt fails, so a waiter never reads a terminal run without its receipt (review round 1, F01; reproduced on code before this spec). Next engine bugfix spec.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-cli-test-wall-time.md:117:- [open] F2: make `Main` take its working directory instead of tests changing the process's, so `internal/cli` tests can run in parallel. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-security-baseline-gates-and-pinning-policy.md:10:The repository had CI tests but no static analysis, no dependency review, no\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-security-baseline-gates-and-pinning-policy.md:21:(GitHub dependency review) without redundancy.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-security-baseline-gates-and-pinning-policy.md:32:  `actions/dependency-review-action` failing on high severity. Go-module\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-security-baseline-gates-and-pinning-policy.md:49:  their review.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-release-cycle-debt-closure/spec.md:27:structural gate broke after every cut and cost several reindex-and-review cycles\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-release-cycle-debt-closure/spec.md:31:line, so five wrapped items silently lost their owner and review date with no\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-release-cycle-debt-closure/spec.md:56:  without a manual reindex-and-review pass.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-release-cycle-debt-closure/spec.md:62:  spec and the text. Today `(owner:… crit:… review:…)` is only parsed on the\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-release-cycle-debt-closure/spec.md:63:  first line: a wrapped item silently loses its owner and review date, and no\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-release-cycle-debt-closure/spec.md:164:  idempotent reapply → preservation verified)`. The machinery works. The entry\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-release-cycle-debt-closure/spec.md:178:- R4 [satisfied] test:TestFollowupMetadataSurvivesLineWrapping — a wrapped follow-up keeps its owner, criticality and review date, and its continuation lines join the text; verified against the real repository by wrapping an existing item and watching `unowned` stay at 0\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-release-cycle-debt-closure/spec.md:230:- [done] R1: the v0.19.0 cut added the 0.18.2 pair with its verified pin, and the gate reported `PASS: 0.18.2 → 0.19.0` — the first real upgrade pair it has ever exercised. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:high review:2026-09-04)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-release-cycle-debt-closure/spec.md:231:- [done] Reassess whether these items belonged together: R2 was the largest but not disproportionately so, and all four shared the release cycle as their cause, so keeping them in one spec held up. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-10-02)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-release-cycle-debt-closure/spec.md:232:- [open] R3's stub proves the script's logic, not the network: a provider redirect, rate limit or partial body is still unexercised. Decide whether that is worth a real local HTTP origin. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-assessment-engine-precision.md:83:  relied on component-name matching will see previously covered debt reappear.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-assessment-engine-precision.md:162:- [spawned: pose-governance-gate-activation] Debt marker ids are positional (`DEBT-001`), the same defect this spec fixed for integration gaps, so citing one in a spec is evidence that silently retargets when a marker is added earlier in the scan. Derive debt ids from file and marker identity too. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-07)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-sbom-license-coverage-gate.md:180:- [covered: pose-sbom-negative-coverage] The coverage gate's rejection path is not exercised by any standing check, because verify-negative.sh's fixtures fail signature verification before reaching it. Splitting verify.sh's SBOM assertions into a separately callable path would let the negative harness cover them, and would close the same gap for any future SBOM assertion. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-02)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-dispatch, pose-delegated-review-conclusions, pose-delegated-review-run-provenance, pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger, pose-delegated-adapter-containment, pose-action-target-and-node-scoping, pose-action-waiver-and-supersession-authority, pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight, pose-review-approval-domain-preflight\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:12:delivers: capability:delegated-review-action-fulfillment\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:15:# Spec: A delegated review requested as an action and fulfilled by any runner\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:21:Let a project request a delegated review as an action request that a local agent, CI or Harne8's Conductor fulfils through the same contract.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:25:The maintainer requires that a developer can work with the repository and POSE alone or with Harne8, neither excluding the other. A review request that any runner can fulfil keeps both paths equal.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:27:Origin: the 2026-10-09 review of `pose-native-attestation-issuer` by Codex through a personal launcher; it found three real defects in three rounds and exposed what the engine lacks (ADR `2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter`, roadmap `delegated-review`). Command names follow the [delegation ADR](../adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md) of 2026-10-26.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:31:The runner produces the same run record and draft as `pose delegate review`; the request is satisfied only by a valid run. Requirements assume the ADR's provisional answers until `pose-delegated-review-contract` closes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:37:- R1: `pose review request <bundle> --kind delegated-review` shall open an action request carrying the brief digest and the accepted agents.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:39:- R3: The same request shall be fulfillable by a local `pose delegate review` and by a non-local runner, demonstrated with a CI job and documented for the Harne8 Conductor.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:41:R4–R11 reconcile the extensions F1–F8 of the [batch 11 report](../reports/2026-10-13-pose-batch-11-authoring.md) (amendment of 2026-10-27); R1–R3 are unchanged. The phase B19 acceptance that this milestone requires is [`pose-delegated-review-conclusions`](2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md) being done, by the amendment of 2026-10-27 to the delegation ADR; this spec does not require the capability to be done.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:45:- R6: (F3) Fulfilling the requested review shall be distinct from satisfying an approval: a valid rejecting run fulfils the service while approvals and gates stay unsatisfied and the rejection stays visible; a negative outcome never becomes an approval.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:46:- R7: (F4) A criterion that policy reserves for a person shall not be satisfied by an agent's run; exhausted budget, reviewers in conflict and a business decision shall produce the question, its options, context and authority, as R6 of `pose-delegated-review-capability` defines.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:60:- modified: .pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:61:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:62:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:63:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:66:- modified: docs-site/docs/review-and-trust.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:69:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:70:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:71:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegated_review_request_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:74:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_request.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:75:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:78:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:84:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_review_escalation.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:85:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_review_request.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:86:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_review_request_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:89:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:90:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:91:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:97:- capability:delegated-review-action-fulfillment module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_request.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:106:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:110:The contract is ADR `2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter`, accepted on 2026-10-09, amended by the [delegation ADR](../adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md) of 2026-10-26 (command names) and its amendment of 2026-10-27 (phase B19 as a spec). R4–R11 reconcile F1–F8 of batch 11 before the start, as the roadmap gate requires.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:114:- Minimal option: reuse the external-operation kind with review metadata\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:115:- Selected option: a new action kind `delegated-review`, opened by `pose review request <scope|bundle> --kind delegated-review`, carrying its material — purpose, scope, bundle and digest, brief digest and template, notes digest, policy digest, worktree, accepted agents and the destination of the conclusion — in the request digest; its subject is the scope's current bundle and the policies, read by the engine, so a superseded bundle or a policy change invalidates it. It admits no answer. The maintainer chose this on 2026-10-28\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:118:- Falsifier: a delegated-review request satisfied by an actor's answer\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:122:- Minimal option: only `pose delegate review --request` in the repository fulfils it\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:123:- Selected option: a verified envelope — request, request digest, expected revision, idempotency key, run, an `agent:` runner and a channel (cli, mcp, ci, conductor) — submitted by `pose action fulfil` (flags or `--envelope`) or the MCP tool `pose_action_fulfil`, and by `pose delegate review --request` locally. The engine reads everything else from the run — its kind, bundle, brief, agent, completion and containment, its signed proof, the attempt ledger, and the conclusion it recorded at the request's destination — and records a `fulfilled` event; it verifies it again inside the request's lock, and again on read while the request's subject is current. A rejecting run fulfils without approving. The maintainer chose this on 2026-10-28\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:125:- Consequences: a fulfilment that no longer verifies satisfies nothing but never makes a journal unreadable; the event's header must say what its payload says; once the subject moves on a fulfilled request, like an open one, satisfies nothing — it stays visible as history and the new bundle is asked with a new request (review rounds 1 and 2). Such a request is retired under the action lifecycle's authority rules: superseded by the new request, or by the person's escalation when the plan now reserves the review for a person; when that escalation is already asked, it is waived, as an answer that no longer satisfies is (review rounds 3 to 6). Its wait ended at the fulfilment the engine counted\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:131:- Selected option: a run proof verifies in any checkout of the project: the origin worktree is recorded in the signed provenance, not required of the reader (the amendment of 2026-10-28 to ADR `2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs`). The maintainer chose this on 2026-10-28\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:138:- Minimal option: move R7 to `pose-delegated-review-capability`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:139:- Selected option: the minimum here — a run never satisfies a review the plan reserves for a person (`mandatory-human`), and each exception opens one decision request to the maintainer role with the question, options and their consequences, context and the request's targets and effects: a plan reserving the review for a person (asked when the request is opened), a spent attempt budget (asked when `pose delegate --request` is refused for it), delegated reviewers in conflict on the bundle and a `business_decision` the reviewer raised in its draft (asked when the request is fulfilled). Opening one again returns the one open. The capability's question format refines this later without breaking it. The maintainer chose this on 2026-10-28\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:142:- Falsifier: an agent's run satisfying a review reserved for a person, or an exception that reaches nobody\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:154:- R3 [satisfied] Local delegate and the documented synthetic CI job transfer verified records between checkouts with a shared project identity; Conductor is a documented MCP boundary: test:TestDelegatedReviewRequestIsFulfilledByACIRunner test:TestDelegatedReviewCIJourneyAsDocumented test:TestToolsCall_ActionFulfil evidence:integration check:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration check:pose-mcp/go/mcp-action-resolve-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:168:Delivered delegated-review action requests, verified fulfillment through one canonical CLI/MCP envelope, portable native run proofs, per-kind conclusion destinations and authority-bound escalation, supersession and stale-service waiver. A verified rejection fulfills the requested service without approving the scope. Historical fulfillments cannot satisfy a changed subject.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:174:Independent round 8 reviewed implementation `b17960c835c9659d4b14f8b04e53c51dcc71d36d` on 2026-10-28, in a new Codex/OpenAI execution (`agent:independent-codex-fulfillment-round8`) distinct from the original Claude/Anthropic implementation. The review confirmed that R7-F01 is resolved: the native requirement parser recognizes eleven requirements and zero orphan trace entries, and all committed text outside the eight declaration prefixes is unchanged. The behavioral review and mutation evidence from round 7 concern identical production code and were read as historical context, not represented as new executions.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:176:Current `pose validate --strict` passed 158/158 checks. The explicit component validation, artifact-check and surface-check passed; the latter observes containing-module integration coverage as inferred coverage, with a separate native synthetic CI journey. Sealed bundle `rvb-f65774ef08fcf69c` and attestation `rva-39b329bab795aac0` record the explicit judgments and tool evidence. Review context: knowledge:action-answer-proof-and-historical-time; knowledge:action-recovery-intent-and-refusal. `pose review verify`, `review-check`, native `close`, strict spec lint and strict structure checks were required for this transition.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:180:Native run proofs are signed executor declarations, not independent vendor receipts. The review identity and original lead are declared; this instance records unsigned attestations. Windows/Darwin runtime and a real Conductor deployment are not claimed by this closeout.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:182:The first fresh validation passed 157/158: a temporary Git status failure (exit 128) in `TestReviewCheckNamesANegativeVerdictOnAClosedScope` interrupted the unrelated retention fixture. The same test passed in the complete suite, the isolated check passed five consecutive repetitions, and the subsequent full native validation passed. Its cause remains undetermined; no code fix is claimed. The failed attempt and successful rerun are preserved in the local round-8 review logs.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md:186:No new actionable product finding was identified in the final review. Existing work on capability composition, parity and adoption remains in its separately governed roadmap members.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-explainable-changed-scope-selection.md:53:  reasons that make gaps reviewable.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-v6-3-0-version-alignment.md:57:- [ ] Record a separate governed review and close this bounded scope.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-v6-3-0-version-alignment.md:65:reviewable frozen candidate and the owner's explicit confirmation.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-09-pose-container-build-gate.md:41:`governance`, `govulncheck`, `secrets`, `dependency-review`,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-09-pose-container-build-gate.md:242:- [spawned: pose-composition-contract] The images are built here and composed in `harne8`, with the build contexts written down independently in both places and nothing keeping them in agreement. A context change in the compose file would not fail anything in this repository, and vice versa. Consider whether the composition should consume a contract this repository publishes — the same problem `pose-machinery-distribution-contract` solved for the scaffold — rather than each side describing the other from memory. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-typed-producer-diagnostics.md:20:Make readiness, review, closeout and start emit typed diagnostics (code, refs,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-typed-producer-diagnostics.md:50:- R1: A pending review judgment shall identify criterion, source bundle/plan and satisfaction condition as structured fields.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-typed-producer-diagnostics.md:72:Readiness, review bundle pendencies, closeout state, start obligations, rendering.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-typed-producer-diagnostics.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-typed-producer-diagnostics.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-typed-producer-diagnostics.md:154:Delivers typed codes on readiness, pendencies and closeout with legacy strings rendered from them. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-07-validation-evidence-binds-to-validated-material.md:12:records (indexes, results, state, assessments, review records, a spec's status)\n.pose/adr/2026-11-07-validation-evidence-binds-to-validated-material.md:29:`.pose/state/`, `.pose/assessments/` and `.pose/review-*` directories. They are\n.pose/adr/2026-11-07-validation-evidence-binds-to-validated-material.md:49:rules. A changed engine makes the evidence stale too. Spec facts, review\n.pose/adr/2026-11-07-validation-evidence-binds-to-validated-material.md:55:that seal, verify, review-check, closeout-check, close, CLI and MCP all consume.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-red-signals-reach-a-person.md:128:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-extension-reference-publication/spec.md:83:- modified: .pose/workflows/review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-extension-reference-publication/spec.md:190:References to the rule in AGENTS.md and the review and recurrence workflows —\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-extension-reference-publication/spec.md:198:- AGENTS.md, .pose/workflows/review.md, .pose/workflows/recurrence-escalation.md, and their pt-BR mirrors\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-extension-reference-publication/spec.md:212:- [open] F1: `frontend-react.md` and `backend-go.md` ship to every instance for the same bad reason `kubernetes.md` did. Decide whether they follow it out of machinery now that the extension path is proven. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-19)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-extension-reference-publication/spec.md:213:- [done] Both ran and passed on v0.20.3: the independent verification (run 31212710370) exercised the extension chain end to end against the published artifact — verified against its real Sigstore signature, installed after verification, and a tampered copy rejected — and `pose release status --version v0.20.3` projects `verified`. Every earlier test of that path had substituted a fake for cosign. Original item: confirm on the next cut that the signing step and the consumer-side extension verification both pass against the published artifact — they have never run. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:high review:2026-09-04)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-extension-reference-publication/spec.md:214:- [open] F2: `pose extension install` gives no signal that the target is the repository the operator is standing in. A confirmation or an explicit target argument would prevent an accidental install into a working tree. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:2:slug: pose-unified-review-convergence\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:11:delivers: capability:unified-review-convergence, contract:review-auto-attest\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:14:# Spec: pose-unified-review-convergence\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:29:Unify the POSE review architecture into a single canonical track based on immutable `ReviewBundles` and `ReviewAttestations`, deprecating legacy Markdown review records, and introduce `pose review auto-attest` for seamless evidence binding in subagents and CI.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:32:Eliminates confusion between dual review paths, removes fragile manual tool disposition flags during attestation, and enables completely automated, deterministic review verification for subagents and CI pipelines.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:35:- Must remain deterministic, offline-capable, and backward-compatible for existing historical reviews.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:46:- R1: When a review bundle is sealed, `pose review auto-attest <bundle-id>` shall automatically inspect the effective plan, extract matching evidence from `.pose/results/delivery-validation.json` and verification reports, and record a valid `ReviewAttestation`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:47:- R2: The review policy and CLI shall establish `ReviewBundle` + `ReviewAttestation` as the single canonical review track, deprecating legacy `pose review record`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:48:- R3: The review verification gate (`pose review verify <scope>`) shall validate bundle attestations as the sole completion criteria for all POSE scopes.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:49:- R4: The review skill (`.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md`) shall guide subagents to execute `pose review bundle <scope> --seal` followed by `pose review auto-attest <bundle-id>`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:59:- Existing historical review attestations and bundles remain valid.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:68:- `.agents/skills/pose-review/`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:69:- `.pose/policy/review.json`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:74:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:75:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:76:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:78:- modified: .agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:79:- modified: .pose/policy/review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:84:- capability:unified-review-convergence module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:85:- contract:review-auto-attest module:pose-mcp profile:api-contract entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:92:- [x] Create ADR and define unified review architecture\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:96:- [x] Implement `pose review auto-attest` in `review_closeout.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:97:- [x] Update review policy to make ReviewBundles the sole canonical track\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:98:- [x] Update skills and documentation for subagent review workflows\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:101:- [x] Unit & integration tests in `review_bundle_test.go` and `review_closeout_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:110:- Context: Deprecating dual review tracks (legacy markdown vs review bundle)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:126:  duplicate of `pose-review-bundle-convergence` and mark it superseded\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:138:- Consequences: Sealing the review bundle for this change set required\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:139:  teaching `reviewBundlePathClass` to recognize `README.md` and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:142:  independently closed spec: `pose-review-bundle-root-file-classification`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:149:Full test suite in `pose-mcp`, CLI E2E tests for `pose review auto-attest`, and `pose validate --strict`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:153:- R2 [satisfied] `TestReviewRecordDelegatesToBundleAttestationWhenAdopted`; `.pose/policy/review.json` `review_bundles: true` since 2026-08-14; commit:422907c.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:154:- R3 [satisfied] `pose review verify` sole-criteria behavior exercised by this very closeout (`review_verify.state=ready-to-close`/`closed`); commit:422907c.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:155:- R4 [satisfied] `.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md` steps 11-12 (bundle --seal, review auto-attest); commit:422907c.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:168:`pose review auto-attest`, the ReviewBundle/ReviewAttestation track as the\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:169:sole canonical review path (legacy `pose review record` delegates to it when\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:172:retroactively records provenance and review evidence for work that had\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:176:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go`, `review_closeout_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:177:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go`, `review_bundle_test.go`,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:178:  `review_closeout.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:179:- `.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md` (and pt-BR locale mirror)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:180:- `.pose/policy/review.json`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:186:- `pose artifact-check --spec pose-unified-review-convergence --from 11e7067..422907c --strict`: zero errors.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:188:- `pose review bundle spec:pose-unified-review-convergence --seal` + `pose review auto-attest --apply`: sealed and approved.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:189:- `pose review verify spec:pose-unified-review-convergence`: `ready-to-close`, `fresh=true`, `approved=true`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-14-pose-unified-review-convergence.md:196:- [open] Monitor adoption of unified review auto-attest across subagents and CI pipelines (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-10-15)\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-cyclonedx-sbom-publication.md:9:enterprise adoption reviews had to reverse-engineer what each binary\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-cyclonedx-sbom-publication.md:38:  are inventory data — incompleteness is reviewed against `NOTICE`, and no\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-cyclonedx-sbom-publication.md:50:- Positive: generation is reproducible from the artifact and diff-reviewable\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-cyclonedx-sbom-publication.md:54:- Residual: generated license fields may be incomplete; the NOTICE review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-release-security-gate-integrity.md:266:  noise. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-release-security-gate-integrity.md:271:  (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:high review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-completion-signal, pose-delegated-review-round-protocol, pose-delegation-handoff\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:14:# Spec: Agents operate delegated runs over MCP\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:20:Expose bounded MCP tools to start, inspect, wait for, resume and hand off delegated runs, with exactly the refusals of the CLI.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:24:Decided by the [delegation ADR](../adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md), which reverses option 4 of the 2026-10-09 ADR. That option was rejected because an implementing agent could rerun a review until it was approved; the attempt ledger now refuses a rerun on an unchanged bundle without a reason, and a rejection stays visible. Agents that reach POSE through MCP should not have to shell out to act on `next_actions`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:38:- R1: `pose_delegate_start` shall start a run of any purpose, always detached, and return the run identifier, attempt, agent and achieved independence.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:39:- R2: `pose_delegate_status` shall return the run's state, heartbeat age, decision when terminal and `next_actions`, without blocking; it replaces the `pose_review_run_status` tool named by the completion-signal spec.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:40:- R3: `pose_delegate_wait` shall wait up to a timeout bounded by the server's maximum and return either the terminal result or `still-running` with the current status.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:41:- R4: `pose_delegate_resume` and `pose_delegate_handoff` shall behave as their CLI commands and return the new run.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:69:- created: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/delegate_tools.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:70:- created: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/delegate_tools_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:72:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_wait.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:78:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:83:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:84:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:85:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_handoff.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:86:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_task.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:87:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_mcp_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:97:- capability:delegation-mcp module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/delegate_tools.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:101:Tools `pose_delegate_start`, `pose_delegate_status`, `pose_delegate_wait`, `pose_delegate_resume`, `pose_delegate_handoff`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:109:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:124:- Selected option: each tool runs `pose delegate … --json` in the project the server resolved, with the binary that serves MCP, under the tool's bound, and reduces the CLI's document to the summary keys; refusals are typed in the engine (`DelegationRefusal`) and carry a `reason_code` in the CLI's error document, which the tool returns as is. A start first previews (`--dry-run`) to report the agent, routing and independence, then starts `--detach`. `pose delegate resume` and `handoff` gain `--detach`, which hands the continuation's attempt back once it starts; a continuation re-planned at execution keeps the hand-back and the routing the caller set\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:135:- Falsifier: a delegate tool that ran in a project the caller could not read, or in an ambiguous selection\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:140:- Selected option: `pose_delegate_start` starts review, adjudicate and smoke runs and refuses a task, which has no detached form yet (follow-up F3 of `pose-delegation-task`) and whose prompt and access are the caller's to choose on the CLI\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:142:- Consequences: R1 holds for the review purposes; a task over MCP waits for `pose delegate task --detach`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:149:Over a fake agent, each tool returns the documented shape; a rerun on an unchanged bundle is refused over MCP with the CLI's code; `pose_delegate_wait` returns `still-running` at its bound; results contain no transcript or session reference.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:153:- R1 [satisfied] Within D4, review/adjudicate/smoke start detached; task start is deferred. D2 returns an attempt handle first and wait resolves the run (F02). test:TestDelegateToolsOverMCPMatchTheCLI capability:delegation-mcp evidence:integration check:delegation-surface-integration commit:f0514d01404e7bed0cfc602f2db065f3e0c6289e\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:156:- R4 [satisfied] Resume/handoff share CLI behavior for review and task runs, including repeated predecessor requests with and without task --record; the attempt identifies the successor through wait (F02). test:TestDelegateToolsOverMCPContinueStoppedRuns test:TestDelegateToolsOverMCPReturnAnExistingContinuation test:TestDelegateToolsOverMCPReturnAnExistingTaskContinuation evidence:integration check:delegation-surface-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:161:Unnumbered non-functional clause (review coverage label R8, not a published requirement ID): Non-functional bound: one shared deadline per call, operation-specific bounds and bounded wait. test:TestDelegateToolsShareOneDeadlinePerCall test:TestDelegateToolsBoundIsTheOperations evidence:integration check:delegation-surface-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:163:Unnumbered security clause (review coverage label R9, not a published requirement ID): Security: existing policy/project authorization and shared CLI ledger/containment refusals remain in force; partial output is not an approval. test:TestDelegateToolsOverMCPHoldAgainstTheFirstReview test:TestDelegateToolsOverMCPMatchTheCLI evidence:integration check:delegation-surface-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:165:Unnumbered compatibility clause (review coverage label R10, not a published requirement ID): Compatibility: catalog/golden and the full module suite preserve existing MCP tools while adding delegation. test:TestDelegateToolsOverMCPMatchTheCLI report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json evidence:integration check:delegation-surface-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:171:Milestone `agent-access` of roadmap `delegation`: five bounded MCP tools start, inspect, wait for, resume and hand off delegated runs through the shared CLI/domain lifecycle, attempt ledger, authorized project root and typed refusal codes. Results project the normalized summary without private transcript, prompt, session, environment values or host diagnostics. Existing review and task continuations return idempotently through MCP and detached CLI, with task history both private and recorded; a consumed handback is not recreated at terminal.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:173:D3 follows the shared explicit/default project selection contract. D4 limits MCP start to review, adjudicate and smoke; starting a task over MCP remains deferred. F02 preserves the attempt-first identity contract: wait returns the run. This delivery does not close the broader roadmap or its remaining members.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:175:### Independent review and evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:177:Approved implementation commit `f0514d01404e7bed0cfc602f2db065f3e0c6289e`, sealed bundle `rvb-557e630823d2fe7a`, attestation `rva-7d020e952840064f`. The maintainer-authorized reviewer `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review` declares Codex/OpenAI, another vendor than implementer Claude/Anthropic, Claude Opus 5.5. The engine-required independent prefix is a declaration, not authenticated separation; this instance uses unsigned attestations and does not observe cognitive independence. The seal explicitly names `anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`; its missing Anthropic execution/session warning is disclosed and no execution digest was invented. The native domain accepted the explicit review; verify returned fresh, approved and ready-to-close before the guarded lifecycle transition.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:179:All blockers B01–B07 are fixed in the reexecuted cases. F01/F04/F05/F06/F07/F08 are reconciled as fixed; F02 and F03 are accepted only at low severity below and in the operability judgment. Their native finding IDs are `f02` and `f03`. Expiring context and reproduction recipes are retained in knowledge:delegation-mcp-round5, consuming knowledge:delegation-observation-round4, knowledge:delegation-routing-round3 and knowledge:delegated-rounds-legacy-status. Local reports, probes and overlays remain in `.review-work/round1/` through `.review-work/round5/`, deliberately untracked.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:189:The spec publishes R1–R7. The three unnumbered non-functional/security/compatibility clauses are covered in Requirement trace using review labels R8–R10, explicitly not invented published requirement IDs; native close refused such orphan IDs before the trace representation was corrected. Requirements, Technical Plan and Decisions were preserved.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:193:F02 limits initial identity presentation; the attempt remains observable and wait resolves the run. F03 is a recovery window of intentional detached execution: cancellation of the transport after reservation can leave the caller without a response while the discoverable run continues. Neither permits duplicate execution beyond the ledger, budget bypass or acceptance of task/partial output as governance evidence. Fake-agent checks establish engine behavior, not a provider receipt or guaranteed reviewer cognition.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:197:- [open] F02: Align the public identity contract with the initial attempt handle or return the new run identity at handback, retaining continuation retry regressions. See knowledge:delegation-mcp-round5. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-26)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md:198:- [open] F03: Document recovery and correlate retries after transport timeout/cancellation; consult ls/status before repeating and keep explicit cancellation separate. See knowledge:delegation-mcp-round5. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-26)\n.pose/adr/2026-09-19-governance-outcomes-remain-append-only-projections.md:8:POSE already owns append-only report history, sealed review bundles and\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-consolidation-batch-14-authoring.md:54:- created: .pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-consolidation-batch-14-authoring.md:87:Gates locais e critérios de saída julgados no [bundle rvb-207e485b164b8e6f](../review-bundles/rvb-207e485b164b8e6f.json), com [atestação rva-ef77ae642c08f009](../review-attestations/rva-ef77ae642c08f009.json) de uma execução separada do Codex, mesmo fornecedor/modelo herdado. Sem alegação de identidade autenticada ou revisão entre fornecedores.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-consolidation-batch-14-authoring.md:97:Manter execução funcional e lotes futuros na matriz. Consultar knowledge:adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review; nenhuma adoção ou runtime iniciado.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-dist-adopt-published-v6.md:42:- [x] Run strict checks, obtain review and close adoption.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:2:slug: pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:6:depends_on: pose-roadmap-reviews-findings\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:11:delivers: governance:review-evidence-fixture-check\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:20:Make the two remaining test follow-ups of `pose-roadmap-reviews-findings` measure the inventory evidence and wait for the detached fixture they start.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:55:- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:56:- created: .pose/starts/pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:59:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:61:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/roadmap_reviews_findings_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_wait_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:72:- governance:review-evidence-fixture-check module:pose-mcp profile:backend-go entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:74:The registered `review-evidence-fixture-integration` check is reached through `pose validate`; this declaration names the strengthened test governance check, not a new runtime capability.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:86:- [x] Validate, independently review and close\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:102:Use the existing migration CLI fixture and its actual before/after tree, replace the historical report's string search with class/count validation, and exercise malformed capture/report inputs. Use guard mutations and repeated wait-acknowledgement runs under load. Run the registered pose-mcp matrix, independent Codex review, strict structure and native closeout gates. No claim is made that the exact historical cleanup race has been reproduced. The prior outcome-review handoff was consulted as knowledge:roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102; it distinguishes supplied full-suite evidence from independent focused execution.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:106:- R1 [satisfied] governance:review-evidence-fixture-check evidence:integration check:review-evidence-fixture-integration test:TestTheCleanupPlanHoldsBothCorpora test:TestCleanupCorporaRejectInvalidEvidence\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:107:- R2 [satisfied] check:review-evidence-fixture-integration test:TestCleanupCaptureProvenanceNamesTheReproduction report:.pose/reports/2026-11-02-pose-v7-legacy-cleanup-both-corpora.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:108:- R3 [satisfied] check:review-evidence-fixture-integration test:TestMigrateDryRunInventoriesLegacyWithoutWriting test:TestMigrationSnapshotDetectsAContentOnlyRewrite\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:109:- R4 [satisfied] check:review-evidence-fixture-integration test:TestTheWaitAcknowledgementNeverTouchesAnExistingEntry\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:115:Implemented the retained-capture comparison and negative evidence cases, preserved the private raw inventory outside Git, strengthened the synthetic read-only snapshot, and joined the detached test agent with a bounded wait before cleanup. Focused tests pass. The earlier phrase-only assertion accepts an intentionally false count; the new comparison refuses it. The old metadata-only snapshot misses a same-size content rewrite with restored mtime; the new test detects it. Nine guard mutations were detected without counting compilation failures. Four concurrent workers each passed 20 repetitions of the wait-acknowledgement test. These samples do not claim reproduction of the exact historical ENOTEMPTY failure. Strict local validation passed all 187 checks at `16ca2589`. The first closeout attempt correctly refused the absent delivery declaration for changed test roots; the spec now names its existing validation entrypoint as a governance check. Fresh local validation at `471abe1d` passed 187/187 checks, and surface-check reported zero findings. The revised bundle `rvb-6078825f64f98044` is approved by `rva-e3255731beef38ef`, from a separate Codex execution with the same vendor and inherited model. Native verify and review-check passed before the governed transition to done. The earlier bundle and attestation are retained as history, not as approval of the revised subject.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes.md:123:- [open] Surface undeclared delivery roots during closeout/review preflight before validation and judgment: this test-only scope reached the transition before the missing declaration was reported. Preserve the delivery gate while avoiding late rework. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:22:Compare each structural subject path over what the scope's own commits changed, instead of the subject's `base..head`, and mark the facts that come from a commit other specs also claim, so the reviewer is asked to confirm them.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:26:Origin: the R8 decision (adjust) of the Harne8 ABM field pilot (`xref:proj.harne8/spec:pose-abm-field-pilot`). An independent reviewer found 7 false positives in 80 sampled structural alerts, all from scope mixing in the attributed subject, and the maintainer chose to resolve the follow-ups before structural judgments leave opt-in. Recomputing the 125 bundles of the pilot showed that the range also made the obligation depend on what other specs committed in between: 14 specs were charged for check-only matrix additions the engine exempts, and one spec's own edit was hidden.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:41:- R2: When a fact comes from a commit whose `POSE-Spec:` trailers also name another spec, the fact and the plan's material fact shall name that spec in `shared_with`, and the plan shall warn the reviewer to map it or answer its mapping `not-applicable` with the reason.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:61:Review bundle subject, design delta, review plan structure, governance replay, schemas and the manual.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:68:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_path_attribution.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:69:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_path_attribution_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:70:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:72:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_structure.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:75:- modified: pose-mcp/schemas/v1/review-bundle.schema.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:76:- modified: pose-mcp/schemas/v1/review-plan.schema.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:126:- R1 [satisfied] capability:structural-attributed-content check:abm-progressive-review-integration evidence:integration test:TestABMStructuralAttributionKeepsOtherSpecsOut\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:127:- R2 [satisfied] capability:structural-attributed-content check:abm-progressive-review-integration evidence:integration test:TestABMStructuralAttributionMarksSharedCommits\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:128:- R3 [satisfied] capability:structural-attributed-content check:abm-progressive-review-integration evidence:integration test:TestABMStructuralAttributionIsContentIdentity\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:133:Mixing inside the scope's own commits and declared ranges that contain a release commit stay with the reviewer.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:139:A sealed subject records, per path, the blobs at the ends of each uninterrupted run of the scope's own commits, and which other specs share a commit of that run. The structural delta compares those runs instead of `base..head`; facts from a shared run carry `shared_with` into the plan, whose warning asks the reviewer to map the fact or answer it `not-applicable` with the reason, and the replay counts them. On the pilot universe, 254 charged facts become 241, 12 are marked shared, 14 check-only matrix additions stop being charged under the existing exemption, and one hidden own edit becomes material.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:143:- Four of the seven adjudicated false positives remain: unrelated content inside the scope's own commit, or a declared range that is a release commit. The reviewer answers them.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:144:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-structural-facts-stay-in-their-commits.md:148:- [open] Evaluate an advisory, never a gate, for a commit carrying several `POSE-Spec:` trailers or a declared range that contains a release commit, once bundles sealed with attribution show how often shared facts occur (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-usage-findings-adjudication.md:32:(2026-08-10) and was reviewed as overdue on 2026-09-11. It was deferred then,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-usage-findings-adjudication.md:67:- The journal is readable and reviewable without POSE.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-usage-findings-adjudication.md:80:- created: .pose/adr/2026-10-01-reviewable-usage-verdict-journal.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-usage-findings-adjudication.md:146:  bounded relative identifiers, and reviewers must inspect each journal line\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-usage-findings-adjudication.md:176:    reviewable in pull requests like a follow-up disposition; each machine joins\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-usage-findings-adjudication.md:184:  team can see and review it; the privacy concern behind hashing was persisting\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-usage-findings-adjudication.md:185:  IDs outside review, which B does not do.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-usage-findings-adjudication.md:187:  `reviewable-usage-verdict-journal`. The journal accepts relative structured\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-usage-findings-adjudication.md:237:  `rva-ee025f7e49b88dd3` passed review verify and review-check. `pose close`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-usage-findings-adjudication.md:264:The reviewable verdict journal, CLI recording command, and shared CLI/MCP\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-parse-the-delivery-index-once-per-content.md:152:| `reviewBundleSubject` | 6.90s | 189 |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-parse-the-delivery-index-once-per-content.md:226:approved; `review-check` fresh and approved; `closeout-check` terminal.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-v7-4-0-version-alignment.md:23:Six closed specs wait for release: the answer's reason covered by its signature, the delegated-review brief and dispatch, the release guard on claimed fragments, an answerable maintainer in setup and resolve, and the lowest independence level admitting a different actor. Harne8 needs the last one to close its open specs with a cross-vendor reviewer. Two fragments are `added` and none is breaking, so this is a minor release. The copy-based dry-run (`pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update`) is left out by the maintainer's decision; its fragment was withdrawn.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-v7-4-0-version-alignment.md:76:Independent review on 2026-10-10 by `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review` (OpenAI, a different vendor from implementer `agent:claude-opus-5-5`): inspected commit 916df895 and withdrawal 4edcb4b4. `POSE_PREVIOUS_RELEASE=7.3.0 bash tests/release/compat.sh v7.4.0` returned COMPATIBLE, 16/16 authenticated populated-instance upgrades, all contract gates and installer E2E passed. `pose public-claims --strict` passed (18 surfaces, zero errors). `pose validate --tolerant --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json` passed all 131 checks at HEAD 916df895. Every prior upgrade pin is unchanged; the 7.3.0 pin matches verified evidence. All six unreleased fragments reference done specs; the dry-run spec remains in-progress without a fragment.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-v7-4-0-version-alignment.md:78:Rules applied: `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md` (diff contains no secrets; checksum authentication retained), `.pose/rules/backend-go.md` (version constant only, no concurrency or handler change), `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md` (both locales and shell variants aligned), `.pose/rules/delivery-evidence.md` (current candidate checks). No knowledge artifact or application API is changed. `pose assess design` observed only the registry version metadata as a public-contract delta; `pose assess tech-debt` found zero uncovered markers. Integration assessment observations are unchanged apart from timestamp and baseline commit. Recurrence check has zero flagged keys; its historical validate-native flapping signal is unrelated to this version-only scope and the current validation is green.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-help-lists-every-command.md:25:The help is the public surface an agent reads to decide which command to run. 17 dispatched commands were missing from it (`setup`, `context`, `identity`, `issuer`, `adopt`, `migrate`, `specs`, `spec-format`, `start`, `action`, `assess`, `docs-check`, `docs-init`, `docs-review`, `docs-sync`, `release-package-manifests`, and `public-claims` in pt-BR) although most were documented in `POSE.md`. The gate that exists (`pose-command-reference-parity`) compares the help against the manual and assumes that a command absent from the help is internal, so a command added to the binary and to the manual but not to the help passed it: the help was checked against the manual and never against the dispatch.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-help-lists-every-command.md:94:- [ ] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-help-lists-every-command.md:132:- Per-command help is a fourth catalog: `pose <command> --help` answers \"No specific help found\" for several dispatched commands (for example `check`, `review-check`, `closeout-check`, `public-claims`). It is a follow-up.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-help-lists-every-command.md:147:- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head, and the suites of `internal/cli`\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-help-lists-every-command.md:148:- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-help-lists-every-command.md:155:- [open] Give every dispatched command a `pose <command> --help` entry, and gate that the per-command help covers the dispatch as the general help now does. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-residual-nature-commitment-and-effect.md:35:- R4: Efeito bloqueante deve derivar de regra/policy/compromisso vigente, autoridade e escopo explícitos, nunca apenas de categoria, high severity, review vencido ou advisory. Item opcional/adiado não cria gate sozinho, enquanto obrigação vigente não vira opcional só por renomeação/classificação. Unknown conserva limitações e efeitos conhecidos, sem inferir ausência de restrição ou blocker global.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-action-runtime-currency-gate.md:58:reasoning that they are SHA-pinned and reviewed on their own schedule. That was\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-action-runtime-currency-gate.md:263:- [open] If the recorded-runtime manifest proves to be pure overhead in practice — R3 never catching a drift R1 would have missed — collapse the two into the online check alone and delete the manifest. Decide on evidence after two or three bump cycles, not on principle. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-05)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-03-pose-release-evidence-trigger-fix.md:118:- R1 [satisfied] report:.pose/reports/2026-08-03-release-evidence-trigger-fix-review.md.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:6:depends_on: pose-review-subject-later-removal\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:21:A review subject reads a later removal only while Git still shows that removal, and a generation says so when the recorded change sets behind it changed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:25:A review subject path that a later spec removed reads as the removal the indexed delivery graph accepted. Generation bindings omit Git and the recorded change sets, so a stale graph keeps giving an accepted witness after a later touch and deletion, which live history would refuse (SR-R1-06, LR-R1-10). The milestone seals are about to hash these witnesses.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:35:- Recomputing the removal rule at review time: the indexed graph stays its only computation.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:43:- R1: A removal witness shall count for a review subject only when its deleting commit is an ancestor of `HEAD` in raw, complete history and no commit after it on `HEAD` touches the path. A shallow clone cannot answer that.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:63:`internal/pose/review_bundle.go`, `internal/pose/index_generation.go`, the manuals.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:71:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:78:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:84:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_subject_later_removal_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:100:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:105:- D2: The binding digests the reader's result, moved to `internal/pose` so both share it, because two rounds of review showed a second decoding keeps diverging. Unrelated report writes then stale nothing, and the same change sets from another file are the same input.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:124:A review subject reads a later removal only while raw, complete history still shows it; otherwise preparation refuses and asks for `pose index`. Generations bind the result of the delivery graph's own reader of the report history, now shared from `internal/pose`. Independently reviewed by Codex over four rounds.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:132:- [open] F1: facts of a spec named by an explicit record stay `unknown` with a reason that says the generation does not bind it, though a generation now does; read a bound, fresh record as fresh, keeping `unknown` for older generations and losses (WF-R1-05). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:133:- [open] F2: a refusal from a shallow clone should say to fetch the full history before `pose index`, which alone does not help (WF-R2-F2). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-removal-witness-freshness.md:134:- [open] F3: bound the allocation of a binding read over a large report history, or memoise it per operation (WF-R3-F1). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-sbom-negative-coverage.md:61:- R5: `verify.sh` shall keep failing the release when the delegated assertions\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-sbom-negative-coverage.md:80:- `tests/release/verify.sh` — delegates to them.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-sbom-negative-coverage.md:118:- [x] R5: `verify.sh` delegates and still fails on their failure\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-sbom-negative-coverage.md:166:- R5 [satisfied] test:tests/release/verify.sh — `verify.sh` delegates to the extracted script and records a failure when it exits non-zero\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-sbom-negative-coverage.md:200:- [open] The positive control parses `pose-mcp/go.mod` for direct dependencies, duplicating what `verify-sbom.sh` does; the two can drift and the failure would look like a real defect rather than a fixture problem. Consider having the harness ask `verify-sbom.sh` for the dependency list it will require, so there is one parser. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-engine-stability-and-diagnostics-convergence.md:22:1. `pose doctor` emitted a false-positive warning under `review.scope-change-set` for valid specs whose changes were attributed via `POSE-Spec:` commit trailers, claiming that sealing a review bundle would fail.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-engine-stability-and-diagnostics-convergence.md:42:- R1: `pose doctor`'s `review.scope-change-set` diagnostic shall query `allCommitsWithSpecTrailers` in addition to `loadRecordedChangeSets`, marking specs with live Git commit trailers as healthy (`ok`).\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-engine-stability-and-diagnostics-convergence.md:62:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_review_scope_trailer_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-engine-stability-and-diagnostics-convergence.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_review_scope_trailer_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-engine-stability-and-diagnostics-convergence.md:105:- [ ] Update `review.scope-change-set` check in `pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-engine-stability-and-diagnostics-convergence.md:164:- Integrated `allCommitsWithSpecTrailers` into `pose doctor`'s `review.scope-change-set` check.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-engine-stability-and-diagnostics-convergence.md:171:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_review_scope_trailer_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md:24:In Harne8 the governance read view of `instance-health-composite` failed intermittently with `review inputs changed during operation: .git` because concurrent reads refreshed the index stat cache. The Harne8 bugfix `harne8-validation-reads-leave-root-index-alone` fixed the instance's own scripts and left this engine part as its follow-up F1.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-closed-scope-stands-over-a-moved-federated-pin.md:38:- R1: A closed scope's sealed manifest shall stand over a dependency of another project whose revision, content, evidence, implementation digest and review moved with the trust pin, when the dependency keeps its reference, identity and relationships, is resolved and done then and now, keeps its plan digest and governing contracts, has a current review bundle, no blocker of the current manifest names it, and, read in its own project at the sealed and the current revision, its spec is the same before its Final Report.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-closed-scope-stands-over-a-moved-federated-pin.md:57:- `pose/review_bundle.go`: `manifestStandsOver`, `externalDependencyStands` e `externalCommitmentUnchanged`, que lê a spec da dependência nas duas revisões, no repositório do projeto dela.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-closed-scope-stands-over-a-moved-federated-pin.md:60:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-closed-scope-stands-over-a-moved-federated-pin.md:69:Composto em produção por `pose review verify` e pelo fechamento, que julgam a aprovação retida de um escopo fechado pela mesma função. Check permanente `closed-scope-stands-over-a-moved-federated-pin-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/pose -run 'TestAClosedScopeStandsOverAMovedFederatedPin|TestAMovedFederatedPinThatChangesTheCommitmentStales|TestATrustPolicyChangeAloneStales|TestAMovedFederatedPinWithChangedRequirementsStales|TestASpecCommitmentEndsAtItsRealFinalReport|TestASplitSpecDependencyIsComparedBySection' -count=1`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-closed-scope-stands-over-a-moved-federated-pin.md:121:- Notes: `closeout-check spec:harne8-abm-governed-execution`: com o motor de edcf5f2, `terminal=false` (\"the federated manifest ... changed in a way that bears on its authority\"); com a mudança, `terminal=true`. As três dependências mudaram `source_revision`, `source_digest`, `source_contract_digest`, `source_policy_digest`, `review_bundle_id`, `review_bundle_digest`, `implementation_digest` e `evidence`; identidade, relação, status, `plan_digest` e `governing_contracts` eram os mesmos. Sem a regra, o caso aceito reprova.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:2:slug: pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:14:# Spec: pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:22:`pose-review-bundle-root-file-classification` and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:23:`pose-review-scope-trailer-check` — for accuracy and completeness before\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:30:was known together. `pose-review-scope-trailer-check` in particular went\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:38:- Read-only review of existing fragments and already-closed specs; do not\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:39:  reopen or re-implement `pose-review-bundle-root-file-classification` or\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:40:  `pose-review-scope-trailer-check` — both are `status: done` and released\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:58:  touch different mechanisms — review-subject classification vs. a new\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:59:  doctor check — but both are review-bundle-adjacent, worth a deliberate\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:66:  holds under review.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:81:      (`pose-review-bundle-root-file-classification`,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:82:      `pose-review-scope-trailer-check`) against their fragments\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:101:  - `pose-review-bundle-root-file-classification.md`: `category: fixed`,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changelog-review.md:103:    `reviewBundlePathClass` classification fix. No drift. `refs:` correctly\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-v1-2-2-changel