ification.md:18:Let a review bundle seal in a repository that vendors a dependency as a Git\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:23:`pose review bundle --seal` refuses any repository with a submodule in the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:26:    [ERROR] unclassified review subject path pose-dist\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:28:`reviewBundlePathClass` decides a path's class from the path alone. A submodule\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:31:blocked. Bumping a vendored dependency is one of the most review-worthy changes\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:32:a repository makes, and it was the one change that could not be reviewed.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:41:- `reviewBundlePathClass` must stay a pure function of the path. It is called\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:48:- Reviewing the submodule's contents. The reviewable unit is the pointer that\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:50:  review.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:58:  be included in the review subject.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:62:  sealed bundle can see which pointer was reviewed without resolving the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:65:  producing `unclassified review subject path` and shall keep blocking the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:76:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go` — subject construction and digest\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:79:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:80:- renamed: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md -> .pose/changelogs/v1.7.11/pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:82:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:86:- capability:review-subject-submodule-classification module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:115:- Options considered: (a) give `reviewBundlePathClass` the repository root and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:132:  of the change under review — a bump changes nothing else — and hashing it\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:165:  original blocker verbatim: `unclassified review subject path vendor/dep`. All\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:173:- R1 [satisfied] <review_bundle.go — reviewBundleGitlinks resolves mode 160000 for every candidate path in one call (it replaced the per-path reviewBundleGitlinkSHA in pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision) and the entry is included; TestReviewBundleClassifiesSubmodulePath asserts class submodule>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:174:- R2 [satisfied] <review_bundle.go — the digest branch hashes the pinned commit instead of calling reviewBundleFileDigest on a directory; the test asserts a non-empty digest>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:180:  working tree is reported by `reviewBundleWorkingTreeChange` as dirty, which is\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:184:  attestation, and `pose review attest` fills any criterion whose evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:186:  `review_bundle.go`. `spec-closeout@1` asks for `validation` and `test`, and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-subject-submodule-classification.md:201:- [open] Report the submodule's own dirty detail rather than just the directory (owner:unowned crit:low review:2026-12-07)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:19:Accept current, post-subject validation evidence from an approved source review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:23:Harne8 pins a reviewed POSE outcome, but federated acceptance rejects all four\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:28:review and delivery profile requirements. The source review classifies these\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:30:remains a separate authority. knowledge:multirepo-review-continuation records\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:35:subject, stale reviews, changed trust pins or status-only delivery claims.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:40:- R1: A source spec with a fresh approved review may satisfy a delivery class\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:42:  of the reviewed subject head and an ancestor of the pinned source revision.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:44:  ancestry, failed, or from an unapproved/stale source review must not satisfy\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:88:source reviewer approved its current provenance; temporal ordering is an\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:100:| Post-subject carried evidence, R1/R3 | `go test ./internal/pose -run TestFederatedAcceptanceCarriedForwardProof -count=1` | A reviewed pinned source composes and the manifest names the accepted check. |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:108:2026-09-26: Harne8's trusted federated policy resolved source reviews at\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:112:`review verify` is fresh and approved. The new regression failed before the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:132:validation from an approved review within the pinned Git ancestry. Manifest\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:136:Do not activate consumer trust if the source review, pin or validation\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:140:- [open] Recheck Harne8's federation pin after the source fix is reviewed and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-carried-forward-proof.md:141:  adopted. (owner:@harne8-platform crit:high review:2026-09-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-consolidation-batch-6-authoring.md:94:Gates locais e critérios de saída julgados no [bundle rvb-ea970b28efa27b37](../review-bundles/rvb-ea970b28efa27b37.json), com [atestação rva-c583a5089e4cb77d](../review-attestations/rva-c583a5089e4cb77d.json) de uma execução separada do Codex, mesmo fornecedor/modelo herdado. Sem alegação de identidade autenticada ou revisão entre fornecedores.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:7:depends_on: pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:32:- R1: When doctor asks for closeout reviews owed on a versioned-index instance, the engine shall evaluate that query under one bounded review operation and publish no successful list when its final audit fails.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:33:- R2: When a keyable review operation resolves repeated spec references in authorized projects, it shall parse each project's resolver catalogue at most once in that operation, using fresh spec snapshots over the operation's captured Files.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:34:- R3: When operation inputs are stable, the shared resolver shall preserve resolution identity/status/errors and closeout-review findings, including missing, unauthorized and conflicting identities.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:43:Concluir o experimento CloseoutReviewsOwed já existente com snapshots do resolver alocados depois de withGovernanceReadView e antes de fixar o ponteiro de binding de reviewOperationView. Aplicar também à entrada de scope operation, mantendo capturas independentes por escopo. Reusar ArtifactResolver.WithSpecSnapshots; não preservar o map antigo zerado intencionalmente pelo read view. Instrumentar somente o número de listSpecs por hook interno de teste, pois contar ReadFile no filesystem base não mede parse sobre bytes já capturados.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:48:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:49:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:64:O DAG ainda pode repetir verificações de fechamento por caminhos diferentes. Não memoizar isso só por ref: closeoutChain e ciclos fazem parte do contexto. A medição real deve distinguir melhoria de parse e conclusão dos checks F5. knowledge:adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review foi consultado como histórico; esta correção usa apenas reuso por operação já auditada e não ativa runtime/persistência.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:79:- Decision: criar snapshots federados novos no início da operação, antes do binding, sem reaproveitar capturas de outra operação.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:100:| Controle negativo obrigatório | overlay somente de review_operation_view.go sem inicialização de snapshots | Teste de custo reprova por listagem repetida; checkout não é revertido |\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:128:- [open] F1: reforçar a prova de que uma consulta com relógio diferente ignora o memo, distinguindo um hit de uma avaliação direta. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-18)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:129:- [open] F2: cobrir diretamente o erro da auditoria final em CloseoutReviewsOwed com índice versionado e a listagem legada no mesmo teste de integração. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-18)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation.md:132:A terceira rodada independente, com Claude Opus 5.5 via `pose delegate`, aprovou o bundle `rvb-802a1ee45eef5bf9` no commit `d0102317`. O POSE registrou o run `rrn-f77daa74c95f8273` com a atestação `rva-19397cf4e66e3506`. No commit aberto pelo revisor, o surface-check passou sem achados, o artifact-check passou e os testes focados com race detector passaram. A validação isolada registrou 233 checks aprovados. O parecer discrimina os checks que falharam nas condições do sandbox do revisor. F1 e F2 permanecem abertos.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:6:depends_on: pose-review-approval-domain-preflight\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:42:- [x] Run strict checks, obtain review and close the adoption.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:82:### Independent review and closeout evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:84:On 2026-10-16, `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review` (Codex/OpenAI) reviewed the\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:87:findings. The maintainer authorized this reviewer id. The `agent:independent-`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:89:`pose-delegated-review-run-provenance` replaces it; identity is declared, without\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:97:five review judgments and all six tool dispositions. Strict artifact\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:101:were deferred until attestation: review-check then approved, and closeout-check\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:106:### Rules applied during review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:108:Change type: documentation update and operational refactor. The review workflow,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:117:between two batches sharing the same release base. This review independently\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:119:review of any managed-file changes. The 29 existing warnings and unmapped docs\n.pose/specs/2026-10-16-pose-dist-instance-follows-engine.md:124:No follow-ups were created by this review. Future batch and published-release\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication.md:74:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication.md:175:rodadas em [review](../results/b14-independent-review.json).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication.md:200:`agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review`, autorizado pelo maintainer, numa\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication.md:208:O [parecer, com First e Second round](../reports/2026-10-16-pose-b14-writer-coordination-review.md)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication.md:209:e a [evidência compacta das duas rodadas](../results/b14-independent-review.json)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-monorepo-validation-recipes.md:65:- [x] Implement recipes that delegate to native task graphs: every recipe uses only `module-metadata.json` (`dependsOn`, `criticality`) and `validation-matrix.json` — no new orchestrator, no BUILD-file parsing; the doc explicitly shows how a real Bazel/Nx repo fronts its own graph as a structured check instead. ([reference](https://nx.dev/ci/features/affected))\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-monorepo-validation-recipes.md:120:- [done] Verify mkdocs build --strict picks up the new nav entry and internal links cleanly on the next docs.yml CI run. Confirmed on run 31148183904: nav entry at mkdocs.yml:36 resolves, strict build clean. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-08-14)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-shared-sufficiency-contract.md:6:depends_on: pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read, pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof, pose-review-approval-domain-preflight, pose-action-target-and-node-scoping, pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding, pose-release-lifecycle-closure\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-shared-sufficiency-contract.md:32:- R1: Investigar compromisso de escopo e blockers derivados nos producers existentes e formalizar contrato compartilhado de suficiência. Plan e apply devem avaliar a mesma seleção, milestones/fragments/targets, profiles/criteria, policy/autoridade e source bindings; apply revalida inputs correntes antes de freeze, sem confiar em preview stale.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-shared-sufficiency-contract.md:37:- R6: P03 deve distinguir resolução de manual-review:path de approval/judgment observado. Arquivo existente ou vazio prova no máximo path resolvido; condição de aprovação exige decisão, authority/assurance e binding adequados de B01/B02. Não converter texto/identidade declarada em confirmação humana observada.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-shared-sufficiency-contract.md:55:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-shared-sufficiency-contract.md:90:| V2 — Preview adequado e inputs/profile/policy mudados antes de apply | Revalidação detecta stale e divulga diagnóstico/coverage. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-result-before-marker.md:21:A waiter never sees a delegated run end without the receipt of its result.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-result-before-marker.md:25:`RunReviewDispatchContext` registers the deferred publication of the attempt result (the attempt receipt, or the continuation result receipt) before it marks the run active, and the deferred removal of the active marker after. Deferred calls run in reverse, so the marker was removed first. A `pose delegate wait` that read the run in that window found a terminal record without its receipt and refused: \"the run history could not be read whole, so the run's end cannot be told (unread: missing continuation result receipt …)\". Found by the independent review of `pose-cli-test-wall-time` (F01); reproduced on code before that spec by delaying the receipt by one second, and seen once in about twenty race runs of `TestDelegateToolsOverMCPContinueStoppedRuns`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-result-before-marker.md:59:`internal/pose/review_dispatch.go`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-result-before-marker.md:65:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-result-before-marker.md:66:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_result_before_marker_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-result-before-marker.md:67:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_result_return_paths_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-result-before-marker.md:82:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-result-before-marker.md:94:- R1 [satisfied] check:delegation-result-before-marker-integration test:TestARunsResultIsPublishedBeforeItsMarkerGoes test:TestARunsReturnPathsPublishOnceAndKeepTheirMarker test:TestAContinuationsReturnPathsPublishOnceAndKeepTheirMarker report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:8cb9d00db53ef6d1678a1274f193395fefc6997b — The result is published inside the marker's deferred removal, before it; a failed publication keeps the marker. The regression failed for a first attempt and a handoff on the old order; the reviewer's one-second receipt-delay probe no longer makes a wait refuse.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-result-before-marker.md:101:A delegated run's attempt result — attempt receipt or continuation receipt — is published before its active marker is removed, once, on every return path. Independently reviewed by Codex (approved in round 1), who found the defect.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-result-before-marker.md:110:- [covered: pose-delegation-marker-stop-joins-heartbeat] F1: join a run's heartbeat watcher, or share its lock, before the active marker is removed, so an in-flight heartbeat cannot recreate a removed marker (review round 1, F04; reproduced with a scheduling probe on code before this spec). Next engine spec.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-result-before-marker.md:111:- [open] F2: decide whether a run's private live events are kept, bounded, when its record cannot be published, or document them as ephemeral even then (review round 1, F03). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:2:slug: review-check-names-a-negative-verdict\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:7:depends_on: retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:11:delivers: capability:completed-review-verdict-reporting\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:14:# Spec: `review-check` names a negative verdict on a closed scope\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:20:For a closed scope whose newest review rejected it or requested changes,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:21:`pose review-check` and `pose check --strict` report that review, its decision and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:26:After a changes-requested review of two closed specs in audio-relay, `review-check`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:27:and `check --strict` said `no review attempt exists` for both, while `review verify`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:29:looking for a missing review record instead of the findings that block the scope.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:34:report changes. Scopes that predate review bundles keep the legacy path.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:43:  `changes-requested` attestation, `review-check` reports that attestation as the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:44:  current review, a blocker naming its decision, and one blocker per open or\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:52:of falling through to the legacy lookup, which only knows review attempts.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:56:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:57:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:58:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:59:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/completed_review_retention_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:67:- capability:completed-review-verdict-reporting module:pose-mcp/internal/pose profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:75:- [x] Reproduce the message on audio-relay's two reviewed specs and compare with `review verify`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:98:`stream-session-reconnect-recovery`, `review-check` and `check --strict` reported\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:99:`no review attempt exists`, while `review verify` reported `changes-requested` with\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:101:fails with `[no review attempt exists for spec:backend]`. The full suite passes.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:112:- R1 [satisfied] capability:completed-review-verdict-reporting evidence:integration check:completed-review-retention-integration test:TestReviewCheckNamesANegativeVerdictOnAClosedScope — the changes-requested attestation is reported as current,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:114:- R2 [satisfied] capability:completed-review-verdict-reporting evidence:integration check:completed-review-retention-integration test:TestReviewCheckNamesANegativeVerdictOnAClosedScope — the scope stays unapproved\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:120:`review-check` and `check --strict` name the negative verdict and its open findings\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-review-check-names-a-negative-verdict.md:121:for a closed scope instead of reporting that no review exists.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:20:Oferecer próximos passos suportados para condições pendentes e convergir supersession parcial no retry da mesma intenção, com preview útil e read-only.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:41:- R4: Preview deve compartilhar validação de admissibilidade do domínio para ator/role, opção, digest, revisão, projeto, estado e authority aplicáveis, com causas tipadas e zero writes/assinatura/toque; checks dependentes de prova ainda não produzida devem aparecer como pendentes, sem exit 0 certificar aceite futuro.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:42:- R5: Apply deve revalidar precondições, autoridade/prova exigidas por B09 e revisão/digest no ponto protegido de escrita; preview admissível não autoriza apply stale. Retry com mesma idempotency key e payload deve manter identidade e não duplicar decisão; chave conflitante não deve ser aceita como retry equivalente.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:63:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-24-b10-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:92:- renamed: .pose/knowledge/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md -> .pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:111:- [x] Reproduzir preview permissivo e retomada interrompida.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:121:- Rationale: Um preview útil deve explicar o que ainda falta sem assinar ou prometer efeito futuro.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:141:| V3 — Preview ator/answer/digest/revision/projeto/estado inválidos | Causas tipadas, nenhum write/toque; prova não produzida divulgada como pendente. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:142:| V4 — Preview válido seguido de stale/authority change e retry de resolução | Apply revalida; mesma intenção não duplica; payload conflitante recusado. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:153:| Transport and session smoke V8 | `cd pose-mcp && go test ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run ActionRecovery -count=1` | readonly previews reject structural errors and disclose pending proof; real apply/next steps match domain |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:179:- R8 [satisfied] test:TestActionRecoveryCLIPreviewRefusesWithoutSigningOrAuditing\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:199:Prova ausente permanece pendente no preview; apply sempre revalida. Estado corrupto\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-request-recovery-and-preflight.md:207:- [open] Expandir corpus adversarial genérico de recovery para além das regressões B10 permanentes; não bloqueia os cenários R1–R9 já cobertos. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:2:slug: pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:10:delivers: contract:review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:19:Let a review bundle seal a change that records a spec transfer or\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:23:After Harne8 retired its ABM coordinators, the review bundle of\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:25:review subject path .pose/transfers/...` blockers: the classifier refuses\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:30:Transfer records are authority records and must be reviewed as governance.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:38:- R1: Plans, receipts, archived sources and redirects under `.pose/transfers/` classify as governance and are included in the review subject.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:44:`pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go` (`reviewBundlePathClass`).\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:47:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:48:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:52:- contract:review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records module:pose-mcp profile:api-contract entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:63:- [x] Run the matrix, review and close.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:67:Transfer records decide who owns a spec, so they are reviewed like roadmaps\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:75:| Harne8 consumer | `review bundle spec:harne8-abm-spec-authority-reconciliation` | No unclassified path blockers. |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-review-bundle-classifies-transfer-records.md:85:explicit authorization from the user to self-attest; superseded reviews were\n.pose/adr/2026-10-24-verify-terminal-state-with-the-applicable-closeout-contract.md:7:PlanCloseout currently certifies every step and terminal=true from lifecycle done, while closeout-check can refuse the same scope. B12 already distinguishes operation result from effect. Existing review verification preserves sealed historical contracts and adoption cutoffs; reconstructing a current bundle for done scopes would impose retrospective requirements. The amendment prerequisite is now done and owns its one journal/schema/gate.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-24-verify-terminal-state-with-the-applicable-closeout-contract.md:10:Use GetCloseoutState as the shared applicable terminal verifier for done plans, checks and apply/resume. It retains ReviewCheck's historical/cutoff policy and action restrictions and consumes the existing InspectAmendmentHistory gate. Report verification basis and historical limitations explicitly, without inventing a receipt. Missing required review or unreadable context cannot certify terminal.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-24-verify-terminal-state-with-the-applicable-closeout-contract.md:12:A done plan records lifecycle_done separately, runs context/verify checks, and marks historical execution steps `not-run`, never done by status alone. Transition is already recorded by lifecycle, not executed again. `not-run` is a new non-executable step state; NextCloseoutStep skips it. A blocked done plan offers explicit repair/review next actions and cannot auto-regenerate evidence, seal, attest, reopen or mutate checkpoints. Apply/resume returns B12 already-satisfied only after successful verification and reports the current readonly verification in data, with empty steps_run/effects (preserving B12: no operation step ran); failed verification returns blocked with zero effects. Plain close also verifies an already-done spec and performs no transition. No new top-level command or automatic policy adoption.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-release-signing-rejection.md:181:- [open] Consider exercising the tamper case during a release run, where a signing identity exists: sign a fixture, alter it, and require the gate to reject it. That is the one rejection reason still asserted rather than demonstrated. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-02)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:2:slug: pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:9:delivers: contract:review-bundle-root-manifests\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:18:Ensure `pose review bundle` properly classifies root-level project manifests, lockfiles, toolchain configs, documentation files, and single-module root components without raising unclassified path blockers:\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:25:Unblocks single-module repositories across Go, Rust, Node, Python, and other ecosystems from sealing review bundles and closing specs when modifying root-level manifests.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:36:- R1: `reviewBundlePathClass` shall classify standard project manifests and toolchain configs as `governance`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:37:- R2: `reviewBundlePathClass` shall classify root `.md` and `.txt` documents and license files as `documentation`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:38:- R3: `reviewBundlePathClass` shall support root components (`Path == \".\"` or `Path == \"\"`) matching direct implementation files.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:39:- R4: `reviewBundlePathClass` shall recognize common implementation source directories (`cmd/`, `internal/`, `pkg/`, `src/`, `lib/`, `app/`, `api/`).\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:50:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:51:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:52:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:55:- contract:review-bundle-root-manifests module:pose-mcp profile:api-contract entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:62:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:63:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:64:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:67:- [x] Increment 1: Add manifest and root documentation patterns to `reviewBundlePathClass` (R1, R2).\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:69:- [x] Increment 3: Add unit tests in `review_bundle_test.go` and E2E test in `review_closeout_test.go`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:83:- R1 [satisfied] contract:review-bundle-root-manifests check:root-classification test:TestReviewBundleClassifiesRootManifestsAndProjectFiles evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:84:- R2 [satisfied] contract:review-bundle-root-manifests check:root-classification test:TestReviewBundleClassifiesRootManifestsAndProjectFiles evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:85:- R3 [satisfied] contract:review-bundle-root-manifests check:root-classification test:TestReviewBundleSealSingleModuleRootFilesAndManifests evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:86:- R4 [satisfied] contract:review-bundle-root-manifests check:root-classification test:TestReviewBundleClassifiesRootManifestsAndProjectFiles evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:93:- contract:review-bundle-root-manifests -> pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-root-manifests-classification.md:103:- Classified root-level manifests, project docs, and root components in review bundles.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-lint-spec-all-is-a-gate.md:122:- [x] Run the checks, obtain review and close\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-lint-spec-all-is-a-gate.md:181:  their approved reviews (retained completed scope).\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-lint-spec-all-is-a-gate.md:210:- [open] Decide in the next major, with an ADR, whether `pose check --strict` lints every spec against the template for all instances (Decision 1, option B) (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-12-29)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-operation-performance.md:65:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-operation-performance.md:66:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-operation-performance.md:67:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-operation-performance.md:259:- [open] Medir o restante de `check --strict` após esta redução, em especial descoberta de fragments arquivados e subject hashing, antes de ampliar reuso no B33 (`pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches`). Não introduzir cache de autorização nem prometer SLO a partir desta máquina compartilhada. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/adr/2026-10-31-review-reads-raw-history-and-roots-diff-from-the-empty-tree.md:8:The delivery graph read raw object history while structural review honoured replace refs and grafts, so a commit could mean two things to two gates. A trailer change set was resolved from `<first>^`, which a repository's first commit does not have, so a new project's first spec had none. `resolved_base` is a contract: facts, reports, the review subject and the policy baseline read it, and it must be filled.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-31-review-reads-raw-history-and-roots-diff-from-the-empty-tree.md:18:- A repository with replace refs or grafts gets other review inputs: `pose index` and a reseal settle it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-extension-target-preview.md:2:slug: pose-extension-target-preview\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-extension-target-preview.md:9:delivers: surface:extension-target-preview\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-extension-target-preview.md:37:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-extension-target-preview.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-extension-target-preview.md:39:- surface:extension-target-preview module:pose-mcp profile:cli-surface entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-extension-target-preview.md:55:- Rationale: automation keeps using --yes, while preview and withheld consent both identify the affected repository.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-extension-target-preview.md:67:- R1 [satisfied] surface:extension-target-preview evidence:integration check:extension-target-integration — explicit and default target tests assert the absolute extension.target field before writes or withheld consent.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-extension-target-preview.md:68:- R2 [satisfied] surface:extension-target-preview evidence:integration check:extension-target-integration — TestExtensionInstallRejectsInvalidTargetBeforeLookup rejects missing values, following flags and absent directories without lookup or creation.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-extension-target-preview.md:69:- R3 [satisfied] surface:extension-target-preview evidence:integration check:extension-target-integration — TestExtensionInstallTargetFlag and TestExtensionInstallDryRunShowsDefaultTargetWithoutWriting prove destination isolation; existing doctor regressions remain passing.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-extension-target-preview.md:75:Install previews identify their absolute destination. Malformed target arguments fail before package lookup and absent directories are never created implicitly.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-first-governed-loop-quickstart.md:164:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-first-governed-loop-quickstart.md:168:- [open] Observe a first use by a person following only the published quickstart, timed, to measure what the automated budget excludes (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:12:delivers: governance:delegated-output-redaction-diagnostics\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:47:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:51:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_redaction_failure_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:52:- created: .pose/investigations/pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause/2026-11-12-findings.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:53:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:54:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:59:- governance:delegated-output-redaction-diagnostics module:pose-mcp profile:backend-go entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:102:- `pose lint-spec pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause --strict`: passou.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:103:- `pose review conclude rrn-e0ff67e5650fa813 --apply`: state recorded, decision approved; `pose review-check spec:pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause`: fresh=true, approved=true, different-vendor.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:104:- `pose close spec:pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause`: exit 0, Closed. O material de código validado está no commit `1af0142e`; este relatório final registra o resultado posterior da revisão e da transição.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:105:- `pose artifact-check --spec pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause --strict`: passou após corrigir os caminhos literais; 9 claims, 17 caminhos observados (incluindo saídas derivadas), sem erros.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:115:- [open] Fazer TestCheckRefusesAnIndexSetThatItsDescriptorDoesNotDescribe reconhecer o símbolo de warning tanto no perfil UTF-8 quanto no ASCII; hoje a matriz precisa de LC_ALL=C para esse teste existente. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-12)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:116:- [open] Distinguir ambiguidade de session/reset e padrões com múltiplos grupos antes de sugerir system/init, com testes dos casos; finding:rva-e5f68c7fb514f381/F1. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-12)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-delegated-output-redaction-root-cause.md:117:- [open] Usar sentinels compartilhados ou testar todos os motivos a partir dos produtores reais, para que mudanças no texto não degradem o diagnóstico silenciosamente; finding:rva-e5f68c7fb514f381/F2. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-12)\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md:1:# ADR: Bind delegated review authority to native signed run proofs\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md:4:Accepted (2026-10-25), spec `pose-delegated-review-run-provenance`.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md:7:B01/B04 already verify native issuer authority and current trust. B16 preserves runs and attempts, but configured vendor/model and a reviewer prefix are declarations. B17 must bind executor assertions to actual sealed execution inputs without inventing vendor receipts or automatically applying a draft (B19).\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md:10:Capture optional provenance before dispatch from explicit reviewers policy: implementation principal/execution/vendor/model and adapter executor principal, with an explicit executor-attested trust declaration. Normalize identity components and reject unknown baselines for authority. Bind the project/audience protected by review policy, origin worktree identity, sealed scope/kind/bundle/commit, complete adapter/config/argv, brief body and wire digests, template and notes, raw/redacted output/transcript digests, completeness and run lineage.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md:14:Recognize an opt-in `delegated_review` review-policy gate for agent different-actor proof; do not add or enable the catalog capability here. The live opt-in bar rejects prefix-only agent reviews when enabled, analogous to the existing live signing bar; non-adopting instances retain declared behavior. This prospectively extends the single-live-signing-bar invariant of `pose-only-the-signing-gate-is-read-live`: exactly RequireSignedAttestations and DelegatedReview remain live, with every other verdict gate sealed. An old declared bundle cannot grandfather a prefix into current machine assurance; no historical proof is reconstructed and no older record is rewritten. The source guard retains its historical test name for requirement traces and now asserts exactly those two trust bars. B19 owns adoption UX, cutoffs/rollback and semantic conclusion application.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md:17:Machine-attested identifies an authorized executor's signed declaration, not an independent vendor receipt, a human confirmation or cognitive independence. Private sessions and issuer keys never enter the proof; commands bind their policy template rather than interpolated session/output paths. Raw hashes record what the executor observed while retained redacted artifacts remain directly verifiable; truncated output cannot establish a completed review. Signature validity cannot erase rejection history, quota or supersession. Rejected alternatives: trusting configured strings without proof, signing today's configuration for old runs, a parallel issuer chain and automatic draft-to-attestation conversion.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md:27:[`pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment`](../specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment.md)\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md:34:the project and audience review policy protects, the sealed scope, kind,\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md:41:Spec `pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift`. Verifying a run proof asks whether\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md:44:sealed changed: five specs closed with a delegated review read unreviewed a day later,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-derived-index-self-referential-leak.md:289:  policy/review-profiles/some indexes removed to simulate an old instance,\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:2:slug: pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:12:delivers: capability:closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:42:- R2: Chaves `milestone_review_required` e `roadmap_review_required`, com os valores `never`, `when-justified` e `always`, lidas pelo motor; valor desconhecido é recusado.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:44:- R4: Quando a revisão não é exigida (`never`, ou `when-justified` sem os critérios), `pose close` do milestone e do roadmap continua exigido e passa sem a revisão do escopo, e o resultado registra `review: not-required`, a chave, o valor e o motivo (por exemplo `members=1, threshold>2`).\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:53:Planejamento local somente, em 2026-11-12. `pose context --task spec:pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --json` resolveu a autoridade existente `xref:proj.pose-dist/spec:pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit`, status `draft`, revisão `f6fa91fee8aa7f2abbc314bb077bb0aa1d824a1b`; nenhuma autoridade nova ou escrita qualificada. Não iniciar nem adotar a política nesta execução. O estado agregado consultado está stale (`commits_exceeded`); usar fontes atuais, sem refresh.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:55:Base arquitetural aceita: [ADR de custo e ganho](../adr/2026-11-12-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-and-benefit.md), aprovação explícita do mantenedor em 2026-11-12. Sua aceitação não satisfaz implementação de R1-R7. Consultados `knowledge:adr-component-aware-review-plans-review` e `knowledge:adr-sealed-review-bundles-review`; TTL terminou em 2026-11-11, portanto são contexto histórico, conferido no código atual, não evidência vigente.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:59:Hoje `ReviewPolicy`/loader e `reviewRequiredForScope` estão em `review_closeout.go`; `roadmaps.go` e `review_bundle.go` implementam herança e reached; `review_plan.go` transporta exit gates; `review_policy_baseline.go` restaura proteção. `cmdCloseLocalWithGuardedStore` apenas verifica milestone, sem persistir uma transição; roadmap escreve status. `artifact_ref.go` aceita spec/roadmap/milestone, não ADR. `pointers.go` já aceita `adr:<filename.md>` local. Não tratar nenhum desses pontos como suporte já existente à decisão nova.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:63:- Planejar schema de review policy **5** (o maior atual é 4); reservar esse número novamente antes de implementar. O loader antigo recusa 5. Schema 5 exige ambas as novas chaves e preserva os contratos previamente adotados: qualified refs e transfer continuam opcionais, com versões 0/ausente ou 1 e transfer 1 exigindo qualified refs 1. Não habilitar refs/transfer ou overlays por adotar o par; schema 5 desacopla reconhecimento da versão da policy da adoção dessas capacidades. Manter os pré-requisitos existentes de component-aware/bundles e validar sua combinação sem os ativar silenciosamente. Atualizar também os probes manuais de schema do resolver; não mudar schema de profiles, planos ou bundles históricos por consequência automática.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:64:- Schemas 1-4 sem ambas as chaves, e instâncias sem policy, conservam exatamente a regra legada, inclusive enabled/cutoffs, singleton e `unreviewed_milestones`. Chave nova em schema antigo, uma chave só, null, vazio, tipo errado, duplicação JSON e enum desconhecido são inválidos antes de planejar ou escrever. Schema 5 sem ambas as chaves é inválido.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:66:- Reutilizar catálogo de capacidades e `pose adopt` como comando de configuração, sem criar outro comando genérico de settings. Planejar capability `closeout-review-policy`, com tratamento próprio do par (o registro simples VersionKey não representa dois enums). `pose adopt closeout-review-policy --apply` adota com `never/never`; preview sem apply mostra legado efetivo, novos valores e impactos. Planejar flags `--milestone-review-required` e `--roadmap-review-required` nesse caminho: exigir as duas quando qualquer uma for informada, tanto na adoção quanto em mudanças posteriores. Recusar essas flags com outra capability, --off, --decline ou --defer. Não oferecer rollback por remoção de chaves/schema.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:74:2. Adicionar frontmatter flat opcional `adrs: [adr:2026-11-12-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-and-benefit.md]` no roadmap. O valor de cada pointer é exatamente um basename `.md` dentro de `.pose/adr/` do projeto proprietário. Reusar contenção do resolver de pointers, acrescentando leitura real e validação de arquivo regular; rejeitar subdiretórios, traversal, symlinks externos, URI e qualificação `xref:.../adr:...` (não suportada). A identidade normalizada da associação é a tupla `(project_id, adr basename)`; ordenar/deduplicar pela tupla, sem inventar ArtifactRef ADR.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:83:Criar avaliador de domínio versionado `closeout-review@1`, compartilhado por review-plan, ReviewCheck/VerifyReviewBundle, closeout state/plan, reached/next action, doctor e federation. Produzir `required`, `policy_key`, `policy_value`, `evaluator_version`, razão estável, contagem e refs canônicas, associações resolvidas, overrides de proteção e diagnósticos. Projeções só renderizam a resposta; não reimplementam limiares.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:91:Ordem: verificar história terminal selada primeiro; para escopo aberto validar schema/resolução, calcular a regra, unir obrigações do baseline protegido e mandatory-human, verificar qualquer revisão voluntária e seu veto, validar membros/arestas/exit gates, então permitir close explícito. `enabled:false`, cutoff antigo, singleton ou `unreviewed_milestones` não podem anular `always` adotado ou proteção mais forte. Nunca usar um early return de dispensa para ocultar rejeição autêntica, história ilegível ou revisão voluntária inválida. Revisão voluntária deve passar o mesmo verificador, freshness, assinatura e independência da obrigatória; requests-changes/rejected só saem pela remediação/supersessão existente. Não criar uma aprovação de revisor para representar dispensa.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:96:- Criar receipt schema 1 em `.pose/review-closeouts/milestone/<roadmap>/<milestone>.json` e `.pose/review-closeouts/roadmap/<roadmap>.json`, com escopo canônico, instante, subject/input digests, snapshot da policy e decisão do avaliador, membros/associações resolvidos e refs de revisão opcional/obrigatória. Reutilizar a classe administrativa existente `.pose/review-*` para JSON de evidência derivada, sem ampliar a lista de exclusões materiais. Para dispensa persistir literalmente `review: not-required`, chave, valor, versão e razão com counts (`members=1, threshold>2`, por exemplo); uma revisão voluntária aprovada fica referenciada à parte. Para revisão exigida registrar `review: required` e evidência verificada, nunca um revisor inventado.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:104:Encadear `cmd/pose/main.go -> internal/cli/review_closeout.go -> Store/evaluator/receipt verifier`; `internal/mcpserver/server.go -> Store` para `pose_review_plan`, `pose_closeout_state`, review verification e aceitação federada. Mesmos modos, counts, veto, resolução e diagnóstico em JSON/texto/MCP. MCP permanece nas permissões atuais; não adicionar ferramenta de configuração ou close write. CLI faz a configuração e o close; MCP observa resultado e próxima ação.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:106:Na federação, avaliar o escopo na sua autoridade, com bindings/autorização/pins/revisão selecionada existentes. Não usar default never do consumidor para dispensar review do produtor. Manifesto novo vincula receipt e decisão; produtores legados continuam no verificador legado. Unknown/unauthorized/transfer-in-progress/stale source e rejeição remota bloqueiam; aliases de redirects verificados deduplicam. Usar somente projetos sintéticos temporários nos testes, nunca outros checkouts reais.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:110:Lista do change set completo da spec, incluindo a ADR criada e aprovada nos commits de planejamento. Os demais caminhos são previstos para implementação futura; não recriar a ADR nem adotar `.pose/policy/review.json` local. Artefatos de runtime dos testes ficam em `t.TempDir`, não no repositório.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:112:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:113:- created: .pose/adr/2026-11-12-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-and-benefit.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:115:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:116:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:117:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:133:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:136:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:142:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/progressive_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:144:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:149:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/closeout_review_policy_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:150:- created: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/closeout_review_policy_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:151:- modified: pose-mcp/schemas/v1/review-plan.schema.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:159:- created: .pose/starts/pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:160:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:162:Reconciliação na implementação (2026-11-13): a lista acima é o change set real. Saíram do plano `review_policy_baseline.go` (a proteção reusa `resolveReviewGovernanceGuard` e `parseReviewPolicyAt` a partir do avaliador, sem mudar o arquivo), `state.go` e `mcpserver/server.go` (a projeção MCP é a do `CloseoutState`, que já carrega a decisão e o recibo), `cli/index.go` e `cli/help.go` (nenhuma projeção de índice nova; o uso do `pose adopt` vive em `adopt.go`), `distpolicy.go` (instalação nova adota pelo catálogo, `DefaultForNew`, com o mesmo produtor de `pose adopt`) e os arquivos de teste separados de recibo e associações, unidos em `closeout_review_policy_test.go`. Entraram `federated_acceptance.go` (prova de origem atrelada ao recibo de um fechamento sem revisão exigida, achado F7 da revisão), `cli/surface_check.go` (o gate do milestone normaliza `spec:<slug>`, F13) e `spec_transfer.go`, cujo gate de capacidade recusava schema 5 com transferência adotada. Entraram `go.mod`/`go.sum` e a ADR governance-association-links-are-read-with-a-commonmark-parser (decisão D3): o leitor de associações passou a usar o parser CommonMark goldmark. Entraram `governance_read_view.go` e a ADR de leituras de governança (emenda D10): no fechamento, o histórico atribuído do repositório passou do orçamento de 512 MiB de entrada do read view, e todo `pose index` do pose-dist passou a ser recusado; o orçamento foi recalibrado para 1 GiB com a medição, e os dois testes que fixavam o valor antigo passam a ler a constante exportada (`GovernanceReadViewMaxInputBytes`). Entraram `readiness.go` e `cli/portfolio_projection.go` (a dependência de uma spec em milestone ou roadmap só se satisfaz com o escopo fechado, achado N27 da revisão). Entraram também `diagnostic_codes.go` (três códigos novos catalogados) e os testes existentes que fixavam o catálogo, o schema após `adopt` e a compatibilidade com a release anterior: uma instalação nova agora adota o par, logo schema 5, que a v7.4.0 recusa por decisão da ADR; o teste passa a exigir que essa recusa seja a do schema e que uma instância legada continue legível pela release anterior depois do `pose update`, que não adota o par.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:166:- capability:closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:168:Produção composta exige integração atravessando CLI e MCP até o avaliador e receipt verificado, mais teste de federação e instalação sintética. Registrar check permanente `closeout-review-policy-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required, em moduleOverrides.pose-mcp; comando no módulo: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run '^TestCloseoutReviewPolicy' -count=1`. Os novos testes usam esse prefixo e subtestes da tabela abaixo. Build/unit isolados não provam esse alvo.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:185:- Selected option: ADR [Closeout review policy by cost and benefit](../adr/2026-11-12-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-and-benefit.md), Accepted, aprovação explícita em 2026-11-12.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:220:| Required integration R6/R7 — install, update, preview/adopt/config/setup, par inválido e sem confirmação | `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '^TestCloseoutReviewPolicyAdoption$' -count=1 -v` | New/adopting never/never; update legado sem mudança; preview/read-only não escreve; par/schema publicados juntos sob guard. |\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:222:| Required contract R2-R7 — CLI text/JSON e MCP review-plan/state/verifier sobre fixtures iguais | `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run '^TestCloseoutReviewPolicyParity$' -count=1 -v` | required/counts/reasons/diagnostics e next close iguais; nenhum write por leitura MCP; schema JSON confere. |\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:226:| Required permanent integration — todo prefixo novo | `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run '^TestCloseoutReviewPolicy' -count=1` | Check closeout-review-policy-integration verde e todas as famílias acima presentes; não aceitar filtro vazio. |\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:228:| Required module baseline / build/security/contract | `LC_ALL=C LANGUAGE=C pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --report --report-task test-plan-baseline-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit` | Todas as checks required da matriz passam, inclusive integração permanente; relatório contém comandos/outcomes/classes vigentes. |\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:233:| Required artifact gate futuro (raiz) | `pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict` | Claims reconciliadas com observações dos commits atribuídos; emendar lista se houver divergência real. |\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:234:| Required composition futuro (raiz) | `pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict` | Alvo capability ligado ao entrypoint e integração atual; sem alegar entrega com unit/build apenas. |\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:236:Não criar check permanente para cada subteste: uma integração registrada com o prefixo novo é suficiente; preservar checks existentes de milestone-review-proportional, milestone-closes-when-reached, review-policy-adoption, policy-scope-validation, federated-roadmap-acceptance e done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan. Nenhuma atualização da matriz nesta tarefa de planejamento.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:240:- R1 [satisfied] test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicySchema test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyThresholds check:closeout-review-policy-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:241:- R2 [satisfied] test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicySchema test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyAdoption test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyUnavailable check:closeout-review-policy-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:242:- R3 [satisfied] test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyThresholds test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyMembers test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyAssociations test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyFederation check:closeout-review-policy-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:243:- R4 [satisfied] test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyReceipt test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyPublication test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicySmoke test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyParity check:closeout-review-policy-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:244:- R5 [satisfied] test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyVeto test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyProtection test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyAlwaysRefusesWithoutReview check:closeout-review-policy-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:245:- R6 [satisfied] test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyAdoption test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicySetupShowsTheLegacyRule test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyDoctor check:closeout-review-policy-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:246:- R7 [satisfied] test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyHistory test:TestPreviousReleaseReadsThisEnginesReviewPolicy check:closeout-review-policy-integration check:milestone-review-proportional-integration check:milestone-closes-when-reached-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:252:2026-11-13, sobre o código de `36fdc959` e índices de `8fc1e9a6`: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run '^TestCloseoutReviewPolicy' -count=1` passa com 17 testes de topo e todos os subtestes (61 em `internal/pose`), nenhum skip. A regressão completa dos três pacotes reprovou primeiro 11 testes existentes, todos corrigidos e reexecutados: inventários (catálogo de capacidades, códigos de diagnóstico, classe de `.pose/review-closeouts/`, limite de prints diretos), `POSE.md` citando um diretório ausente (o gate pós-instalação reprovava, arrastando quickstart e preview do update), fixtures que forçavam schema 2 numa policy com o par, e a compatibilidade com a release anterior, que agora exige recusa pelo schema e leitura da instância legada após `pose update`. `pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`: 210/210 pass em 404,5s (a execução anterior, concorrente com `pose check`, perdeu só o `test` por timeout de 600s). `go vet ./...` exit 0. `govulncheck ./...`: nenhuma vulnerabilidade alcançável; dois avisos em módulos requeridos não chamados. `pose artifact-check --spec … --strict` e `pose surface-check --spec … --strict` exit 0 (surface: 1 alvo, 210 resultados, 0 findings). `pose lint-spec … --strict` SUCESSO. `pose check --strict` lista 19 erros de contrato de entrega, nenhum desta spec: são de `pose-optional-worktree-runtime`, `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement`, `pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache`, `pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff`, `pose-governance-operation-performance` e `pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches`. O mesmo `pose check --strict` no commit base `956153f1`, com o binário daquele commit, lista os mesmos 19 erros, linha a linha: nenhum é introduzido por esta entrega (R7).\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:256:Executado em 2026-11-12: `/tmp/pose-redaction-cli context --task spec:pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --json` resolveu a autoridade local existente. `/tmp/pose-redaction-cli lint-spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict` passou (7 requisitos, zero seções vazias, zero falhas; trace sem satisfação de implementação). `/tmp/pose-redaction-cli lint-spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --ready-check` passou (`spec.ready=true`, zero falhas). `git diff --check` passou. Esses checks validam o planejamento, não a entrega. Não executar discovery, assessments, full validation, indexação, start, revisão independente ou close como parte deste planejamento.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:264:Review policy schema 5 com `milestone_review_required` e `roadmap_review_required` (`never`, `when-justified`, `always`), recusado por engines anteriores e validado antes de qualquer plano ou escrita (par incompleto, null, tipo, enum, chave duplicada, chave em schema antigo). Capability `closeout-review-policy` no catálogo: instalação nova adota `never`/`never` pelo mesmo produtor de `pose adopt`; `pose adopt closeout-review-policy` mostra a regra atual e a proposta, aceita o par só junto e não se desliga; nenhuma outra capability rebaixa o schema 5; `pose update` não adota. Avaliador único `closeout-review@1` (membros canônicos `xref:<projeto>/spec:<slug>` com aliases e redirects verificados, associações de ADR nas duas direções por metadata ou link local, desconhecido nunca dispensa, proteção pelo baseline quando o escopo muda o contrato de revisão) consumido por review check, verificação de bundle, review plan, closeout state, reached, attention, doctor e MCP. `pose close` de milestone e roadmap publica um recibo imutável em `review-closeouts/`; o escopo só é terminal com ele; recibo corrompido bloqueia e não é sobrescrito; roadmap done sem recibo é completado por novo `pose close`. `always` anula a herança do membro único e `unreviewed_milestones`; rejeição registrada vale sob `never`; roadmaps fechados antes da adoção mantêm a leitura selada. Membros escritos `spec:<slug>` passaram a resolver no closeout state, onde viravam `spec:spec:<slug>`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:272:Rodada 1 (run rrn-7c2315202e585212, Codex gpt-6.1-sol, bundle rvb-08c2ad291964aeda): a run foi recusada pelo motor porque o revisor rodou `pose assess integrate`/`tech-debt`, que escrevem no worktree selado; sua conclusão, decisão changes-requested, trouxe 15 achados bloqueadores, todos tratados no código e cobertos por testes: F1 mandatory-human nunca é dispensado (`mandatoryHumanReview`); F2 repetir o close com recibo exige estado terminal atual; F3 a recuperação de um roadmap done sem recibo segue as regras de um escopo aberto e não fecha sobre revisão registrada; F4 o recibo só vale para a mesma composição canônica e `always` não pode gravar not-required; F5 o fechamento grava uma intenção antes do status, então uma interrupção fica incompleta e só um roadmap done sem recibo nem intenção é histórico; F6 sob adoção o gate vem antes de `enabled=false` e do cutoff legado; F7 prova federada por recibo; F8 preflight e publicação usam a mesma decisão protegida (`CurrentCloseoutDecision`); F9 dispensa exige estado sem bloqueios e a publicação revalida decisão, membros, ADRs e estado na região protegida, antes do status no roadmap; F10 membro transferido é seguido pelo resolvedor até a identidade final; F11 ADR associada é lida e validada como as demais; F12 o review plan falha com recibo corrompido ou divergente; F13 `spec:<slug>` fecha pelo gate do milestone; F14 desconhecido nunca dispensa nem aprova; F15 o doctor só aceita aprovação fresca para a obrigação atual. F8–F10 e F15 têm cobertura por construção, não por teste dedicado.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:276:Rodada 3 (run rrn-057e10b4445fd53d, attestation rva-f27e990acb2ad3be, round 2 do motor, changes-requested): 8 bloqueadores, todos tratados: N1 e N7 a exigência humana vem do plano efetivo (overlays que o plano seleciona, com cutoffs, e o perfil base), montado sem o gate, e o baseline protegido acrescenta a sua exigência humana e não descarta um `always` adotado com `enabled=false`; N2 reached, attention, roadmap reached e doctor perguntam ao verificador aplicável (`reviewCheck`), não só pela ausência de recusa; N3 o schema do recibo declara `exit_gate_digest` e um teste confere os campos emitidos contra o schema; N4 o close de um roadmap fechado antes da adoção é verificação somente leitura, sem recibo (a recuperação só existe com intenção pendente); N5 uma declaração reversa para roadmap inexistente do projeto é desconhecida; N6 o README do inventário de ADR é lido como as demais; N8 o recibo de roadmap vincula os critérios de corte (`ParseRoadmapCriteria`) e repetir o close reexecuta o gate do milestone ou o roadmap check antes de responder.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:290:Rodada 10 (run rrn-8b1997980713c10a, attestation rva-4ce3b608c57b296e, changes-requested): 2 bloqueadores e 1 follow-up, todos tratados; o parcial anterior (R8-N32) é o N36. N34 a projeção da dispensa adotada roda antes do atalho de instância sem bundles: uma instância de tentativas legadas (`review_bundles: false`) projeta a dispensa e o fechamento pelo recibo como uma com bundles; N35 (follow-up, corrigido já) os avisos de start sob a política adotada pedem o fechamento do predecessor pela projeção terminal, não a aprovação ou a dispensa; N36 a coleta de filhos de uma revisão só pula um filho herdado ou dispensado enquanto ele está aprovado: um que caiu vira bloqueio da revisão do pai, que deixa de aprovar.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:294:Rodada 12 (run rrn-da6e5287b19f2087, changes-requested; N40 desfeito na rodada 14): o motor recusou o registro porque o rascunho citou R11-N37 como achado anterior, e uma run recusada não abre achados; a nota da rodada pedia isso, por erro meu. Os achados foram tratados assim mesmo, 2 bloqueadores e 2 follow-ups: N38 sob a política adotada, `unreviewed_milestones` não suprime mais a falha terminal de um filho, nem com a aprovação de uma tentativa legada; N39 `adrs:` e `roadmaps:` são lidos do frontmatter bruto de modo estrito: chave repetida, chave sem valor, fora de lista ou com item vazio deixam a resposta desconhecida, e `[]` explícito declara nenhuma; N40 (follow-up, corrigido já) links em bloco de código, código inline ou comentário não são associações; N41 (follow-up, corrigido já) a emenda D10 não deixa linha em branco no fim do arquivo.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:306:- [open] F1: adotar a closeout review policy no pose-dist e no Harne8 e fechar B31 e B35 sob ela. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:307:- [open] F2: registrar no recibo um snapshot da regra efetiva anterior, para o doctor comparar a transição em vez de declará-la desconhecida. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-13)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:308:- [open] F4: reconciliar os 19 erros de contrato de entrega que `pose check --strict` já reportava antes desta entrega (specs do runtime de worktree, `pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff`, `pose-governance-operation-performance`, `pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches`). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:309:- [open] F3: projetar `adrs:` de roadmap no índice e no MCP `pose_get_roadmap`, hoje lido só pelo avaliador. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-13)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md:310:- [open] F5: reter só o digest das leituras puras de objetos Git imutáveis que um produtor apenas hasheia (o `git show --binary` dos change sets), em vez dos bytes, para o orçamento do read view deixar de crescer com cada commit atribuído; a emenda D10 da ADR de leituras de governança só comprou folga. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:high review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:2:slug: pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:13:delivers: capability:review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:16:# Spec: pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:24:É o follow-up F1 de `pose-federated-source-proof-is-computed-once-per-operation`. No perfil da primeira chamada `pose_closeout_state` sobre o harne8, `resolveReviewGovernanceGuard` pedia `GetDeliveryIntegrity`, que devolve uma cópia profunda do grafo em cache (cerca de 5,5 s de CPU em `copyDeliveryIntegrityGraph`) só para ler os change sets do escopo; e `reviewProcessGroupAvailable` lia todos os `/proc/<pid>/stat` da máquina a cada verificação para saber se o sistema permite observar o fim de um grupo de processos (cerca de 4,3 s), uma propriedade que não muda entre duas verificações de um fechamento.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:38:- R1: The review plan's governance guard shall read the delivery-integrity graph through the cache's in-place view, deriving its paths and base revision inside the view and keeping nothing the graph reaches.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:57:- `pose/review_policy_baseline.go`: o guard deriva caminhos e revisão dentro da view.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:58:- `pose/review_dispatch_unix.go`: a sonda guarda um sucesso por `processGroupProbeTTL`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:61:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_guard_in_place_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:62:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_guard_probe_unix_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:64:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_policy_baseline.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:65:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:70:- capability:review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:72:Composto em produção por todo plano de revisão (o guard) e por toda verificação que declara a contenção do revisor (a sonda). Check permanente `review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/pose -run 'TestReviewGuardReadsTheIntegrityGraphInPlace|TestProcessGroupProbeKeepsASuccessForItsTTL|TestABMProtectedBaseline' -count=1`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:132:- R1 [satisfied] test:TestReviewGuardReadsTheIntegrityGraphInPlace check:review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place.md:153:A primeira tentativa da rodada 1 não chegou ao revisor: o `pose validate --strict` reprovou em `release-test-compile-windows` (`GOOS=windows go vet ./internal/pose`), porque o teste da sonda usava `processGroupVerify` e `processGroupProbe`, que só existem em `review_dispatch_unix.go`. O teste da sonda foi para `review_guard_probe_unix_test.go`, sob a mesma restrição `//go:build !windows`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-falsifier-reconsideration.md:102:- Impossible falsifiers; reviewer judgment, not syntax.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-falsifier-reconsideration.md:156:Delivers optional Expected effect and Falsifier check fields and the falsifier-observed projection. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-state-attention.md:158:Delivers state --attention and pose_obligations with filters and coverage first. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-cli-ergonomics-and-stack-expansion.md:56:- R2: `skill_locale_parity_test.go` shall recognize compound multi-word subcommands across all native CLI verbs (`review`, `assess`, `extension`, `release`, `docs-review`, `state`, `telemetry`, `roadmap`, `rule`, `hook`).\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:2:slug: pose-hierarchical-review-closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:9:components: pose-mcp, cli, lifecycle, reviews, roadmaps, mcp, scaffold\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:12:# Spec: Hierarchical review closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:17:Require a complete, current and scope-appropriate review before a spec,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:18:milestone or roadmap can be considered closed, and make review findings drive a\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:22:POSE already describes a strong review procedure, but review is not a durable\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:24:follow-up disposition without any review attestation. A milestone is considered\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:27:such as “review every spec, milestone and roadmap; fix every gap; do not stop\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:28:until the full scope is reviewed”. Persisting that intent removes prompt\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:34:  judgment; a review consumes check evidence but is not itself a build check.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:35:- Bind every final review decision to a canonical digest of the exact closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:37:- Keep review profiles versioned, explicit and proportional to spec, milestone\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:39:- Keep review artifacts local, diff-reviewable and valid offline.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:42:- Minimize reviewer identity to a configured alias or execution identity; never\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:43:  turn review records into individual productivity metrics.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:50:- Claim that a checklist guarantees reviewer insight or semantic quality.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:53:- Require a different human reviewer for every repository and risk class.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:62:- R1: POSE shall address review scopes with typed refs `spec:slug`,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:65:- R2: Versioned review profiles shall declare stable criterion IDs, applicable\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:68:- R3: A review attempt shall be a first-class immutable artifact containing\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:69:  review ID, scope ref, scope digest, profile/version, reviewer identity,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:71:  and optional superseded review ID.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:77:  risk shall require an owner, rationale, review date and policy permission for\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:79:- R6: Strict closeout shall accept only a current `approved` review by default;\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:83:  `status`, `completed_at` and review references, but include every input whose\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:84:  change invalidates the review.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:90:  member spec shall make the macro review stale.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:92:  outcome, cut criteria and their evidence; any stale child review shall make\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:93:  the roadmap review stale.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:94:- R11: `pose review-check` shall validate review structure, profile coverage,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:95:  finding dispositions, reviewer policy, evidence resolution and digest\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:98:  validation, artifact/surface evidence when applicable, current review and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:101:  its macro review and exit criteria pass; a roadmap shall reject `status: done`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:102:  until all milestone closeouts and its roadmap review are current and approved.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:103:- R14: A macro-review gap shall create or link bounded remediation work inside\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:105:  invalidate the prior macro review and require re-review.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:107:  scope and instruct orchestration to repeat implement, validate, review and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:112:- R17: Reviewer-independence policy shall support same-actor separate review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:115:- R18: CLI JSON and a project-scoped read-only MCP view shall expose review state,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:119:  `pose check --strict` shall reject any `done` scope that lacks a current review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:126:- Compute closeout state without network access and without executing review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:132:- Make repeated `review-check` and `closeout-check` calls idempotent.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:136:- Validate structured refs and never evaluate commands embedded in review text.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:138:- Store reviewer aliases or execution IDs only; prohibit email, personal name,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:139:  prompt contents and unbounded model transcripts in structured review records.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:140:- Require stronger reviewer independence for security-critical modules through\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:146:- Keep current review Markdown reports readable as narrative evidence but do not\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:148:- Warn for legacy `done` scopes without review attestations during\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:150:- Activate strict review closeout by adoption date and scope policy before a\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:153:  behavior when review policy is absent.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:160:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose`: review artifact parser, profile model, canonical\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:162:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli`: `review-check`, `closeout-check`, optional `close`,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:166:- `.pose/review-profiles`, `.pose/policy`, templates, workflows, rules, skills,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:172:- `adr:2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence` for the\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:176:- Add immutable review attempts under `.pose/reviews/` with flat frontmatter and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:181:  review_id: rvw-2026-08-02-001\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:185:  reviewer: agent:review-run-42\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:187:  reviewed_at: 2026-08-02T15:00:00Z\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:200:- Add `pose review-check scope-ref`, `pose closeout-check scope-ref` and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:208:- Store each finalized review attempt as an immutable Markdown artifact; create\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:211:- Generate review projections from artifacts and profiles; allow the later\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:212:  delivery-integrity graph to ingest reviews and `reviewed-by`/`gates` edges\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:213:  without making the review mechanism depend on artifact provenance.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:214:- Derive milestone closure from member spec closeouts, criteria and macro review;\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:221:  review artifact itself.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:229:- A self-review can become ceremonial; independence profiles and separate review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:233:- Macro review can discover work after child specs close; remediation membership\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:235:- Continuous mode can drift in scope; every remediation spec must cite a review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:241:1. Scaffold profiles and review artifacts; project review state and stale\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:243:2. Require spec reviews for newly started specs under opt-in policy.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:244:3. Enable milestone and roadmap macro reviews after member specs expose closure\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:248:5. Make hierarchical review the default for new repository schemas while legacy\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:254:- [x] Record an ADR for immutable review attempts, canonical scope digests,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:258:  review, all-done milestone without macro review, manually done roadmap without\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:259:  outcome review and stale approval after remediation.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:260:- [x] Freeze review artifact, profile, policy and closeout-state schemas with\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:262:- [x] Define the bootstrap review used to close this first mechanism before its\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:266:- [x] Implement review/profile parsers, typed scope validation and immutable\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:270:- [x] Implement `pose review-check` with human and JSON explanations.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:273:- [x] Change milestone readiness from “all specs done” to derived reviewed\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:276:  review workflows.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:280:- [x] Update review/feature/closeout workflows and skills, templates, rules,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:285:- [x] Run negative tests for path escape, evidence execution, forged reviewer\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:288:  revalidates, supersedes the stale review and closes each hierarchy level.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:296:- Context: A review checkbox or prose report can remain apparently valid after\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:298:- Options considered: checkbox in each artifact; mutable latest-review fields;\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:300:- Decision: Store immutable review attempts and require a current digest match\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:302:- Rationale: Freshness becomes falsifiable and history remains reviewable.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:303:- Consequences: Any relevant change requires a new review attempt; digest\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:311:  from spec status only; derive from child closeouts, criteria and macro review.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:312:- Decision: Derive milestone closure from reviewed children plus an approved\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:313:  milestone review.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:316:- Consequences: Adding remediation to a milestone invalidates its macro review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:321:- Context: Users repeatedly restate that agents should continue through review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:322:  findings until an entire scope is reviewed and complete.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:336:rejected or stale reviews. Prove that each hierarchy level stays open, that a\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:346:- Spec readiness: `pose lint-spec pose-hierarchical-review-closeout --ready-check`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:347:- Spec lint: `pose lint-spec pose-hierarchical-review-closeout --strict`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:358:| E2E — hierarchical remediation loop | `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli -run 'HierarchicalCloseoutEndToEnd' -count=1` | Spec, milestone and roadmap close only after fresh reviews in dependency order. |\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:362:- 2026-08-02, planning: current review workflow, report template, spec closeout,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:368:- 2026-08-02, implementation: added profile/policy parsers, immutable review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:372:  overlay for the new review template; the overlay was added and the complete\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:378:- Successes: Runtime and scaffold now separate validation from review, reject\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:389:- R2 [satisfied] check:.pose/review-profiles/spec-closeout.json.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:401:- R14 [satisfied] test:stale review and next-action remediation fixtures.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:404:- R17 [satisfied] check:.pose/policy/review.json independence modes.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:409:- The delivery-integrity graph will reference, not duplicate, review attempts;\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:415:Implemented hierarchical, digest-bound review and guarded closeout across the\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:420:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go` and focused tests.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:421:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go`, strict-check integration and tests.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:422:- MCP catalog/server, docs, review profiles/policy/templates/workflows/skills,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:426:- Passed: focused review/closeout tests, full `go test ./... -count=1`, `go vet`,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:431:- A mechanically complete review can still be shallow; profiles, independence\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-hierarchical-review-closeout.md:432:  policy and evidence quality remain essential review concerns.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:2:slug: pose-review-bundle-convergence\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:7:depends_on: pose-hierarchical-review-closeout, pose-component-aware-review-plans\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:9:components: pose-mcp, cli, reviews, mcp, scaffold, docs\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:10:delivers: surface:review-bundle-cli, contract:review-bundle-mcp, governance:convergent-review-closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:13:# Spec: Convergent review bundles and attestations\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:18:Make POSE review and closeout converge in one bounded cycle by reviewing an\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:23:The component-aware review mechanism detects real gaps, but its current\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:24:freshness model can turn ordinary closeout bookkeeping into repeated review.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:25:The implementation of `pose-component-aware-review-plans` required successive\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:26:provenance, validation, state-refresh and rereview corrections because the\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:28:too mechanical to promote from opt-in/preview to the normal path.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:31:review subject, review it, attach an attestation and close it without creating\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:32:new review inputs. It also keeps POSE useful offline while allowing Harne8's\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:34:targeted rereview.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:37:- Preserve immutable review history and schema-v1/v2 readability.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:38:- Keep deterministic validation separate from technical review judgment.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:46:- Keep reviewer identity to an alias or execution identity and exclude prompt,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:48:- Retain component-aware review as opt-in/preview until every release-blocking\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:55:- Make Harne8 or Conductor mandatory for local review or closeout.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:57:- Claim that a digest, checklist or attestation guarantees reviewer quality.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:62:- Implement the Conductor review workflow in this repository; this spec ships\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:68:- R1: When a typed review scope is prepared, POSE shall resolve a canonical\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:70:  effective review plan, required evidence manifest and child bundle digests\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:75:  patch/tree identities, a current unblocked review plan and every required\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:76:  pre-review validation result; a working-tree-only or unresolved provider SHA\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:77:  shall remain previewable but unsealable.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:83:- R5: The bundle digest shall exclude lifecycle fields, review artifacts,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:84:  reviewer identity, attestation content, timestamps, execution-log prose,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:92:  `.pose/review-bundles/`; its ID shall derive from its SHA-256 payload digest,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:94:- R8: A review attestation shall reference the exact bundle ID and digest,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:95:  reviewer/execution alias, decision, criterion dispositions, tool\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:98:- R9: `review-check` and `closeout-check` shall validate the current attestation\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:103:  invalidate the approved bundle or require a second review attempt.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:105:  consumed review policy or required evidence change, POSE shall create a new\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:113:  an orchestrator can request targeted rereview.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:120:  transitively stale or policy-forbidden partial rereview shall block approval.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:126:  assign reviewers and manage retries, but POSE remains the closeout authority.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:137:- R21: The CLI shall provide `pose review bundle <scope>` for prepare/explain,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:138:  `--seal` for immutable persistence, `pose review attest` for local recording,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:139:  and `pose review verify` for bundle/attestation verification. Equivalent\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:140:  read-only projections shall remain available through `review-plan`,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:141:  `review-check` and `closeout-check`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:146:  `ready-to-seal`, `ready-for-review`, `changes-requested`, `ready-to-close`,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:150:  storing reviewer productivity metrics or attestation bodies.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:156:- R26: The happy path `prepare -> validate -> seal -> review -> attest -> close`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:157:  shall converge without a corrective post-approval mutation or rereview.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:184:  weaken reviewer-independence, evidence, signature or accepted-risk policy.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:186:  log review shall pass before the feature can leave preview.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:189:- R37: Existing schema-v1 and schema-v2 policies, plans and review attempts\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:195:- R39: `pose review record` shall remain a supported compatibility entrypoint.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:196:  Under bundle-enabled policy it shall delegate to the attestation path and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:201:- R41: The feature shall remain opt-in/preview until R26 and every required case\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:212:- R44: Human review diagnostics shall group repeated unmapped or derived-path\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:228:  `review record` compatibility.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:232:- `.pose/policy` and `.pose/review-profiles`: explicit bundle adoption, reuse,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:235:  prepare/validate/seal/review/attest/close operating flow.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:241:- `knowledge:pr15-component-aware-review-provenance` records the independent\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:242:  review, repeated provenance corrections and required-tool enforcement.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:245:- `knowledge:adr-component-aware-review-plans-review` records production\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:246:  false-staleness as an explicit review trigger.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:247:- `adr:2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence` defines\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:249:- `adr:2026-08-12-component-aware-effective-review-plans` defines effective\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:251:- `adr:2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations` defines the fixed-point\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:253:- `knowledge:adr-sealed-review-bundles-review` tracks the decision's production\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:254:  review triggers through the preview and first release.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:255:- `spec:pose-hierarchical-review-closeout` and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:256:  `spec:pose-component-aware-review-plans` are retained historical contracts\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:260:- created: .pose/specs/pose-review-bundle-convergence/spec.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:261:- created: .pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:262:- created: .pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:263:- renamed: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-bundle-convergence.md -> .pose/changelogs/v1.1.0/pose-review-bundle-convergence.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:272:- created: .pose/results/review-bundle-convergence.json\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:273:- created: .pose/reports/2026-08-13-standard-review-bundle-convergence.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:274:- created: .pose/reports/history/standard-review-bundle-convergence.jsonl\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:275:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:276:- created: 