e-mcp profile:cli-surface entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:327:- contract:review-bundle-mcp module:pose-mcp profile:api-contract entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/server.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:328:- governance:convergent-review-closeout module:pose-mcp profile:release-governance entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:372:  \"reviewer\": \"agent:review-execution\",\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:405:result summaries, follow-up bookkeeping, review/attestation files and derived\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:408:review subject does not waive their own correctness requirements.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:411:- Add `pose review bundle <scope> [--json] [--explain] [--seal]`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:412:- Add `pose review attest <bundle-id|path> ... [--apply]`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:413:- Add `pose review verify <scope|bundle-id|path> [--json]`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:414:- Keep `pose review record` as the compatibility adapter specified by R39.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:415:- Add read-only `pose_review_bundle` and extend `pose_closeout_state` with\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:430:9. Keep the feature preview/opt-in until all release blockers pass.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:431:10. Promote it in the next release only after an independent review confirms\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:435:- Add append-only `.pose/review-bundles/<bundle-id>.json` artifacts.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:436:- Retain `.pose/reviews/` as the immutable human-review history; bundle-enabled\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:439:- Add optional review-policy fields for bundle adoption date, classification,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:446:  narrow one lets meaningful changes bypass rereview. Golden include/exclude\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:467:- [x] Consume the two review knowledge artifacts and historical ADR/specs.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:469:- [x] Validate this spec with `pose lint-spec pose-review-bundle-convergence --ready-check`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:480:- [x] Bind review/closeout checks to bundle attestations.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:499:- [x] Run `pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --report --report-task review-bundle-convergence`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:505:- [x] Perform an independent review against the sealed bundle.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:511:### Decision 1 — fixed-point review subject\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:519:- Rationale: This gives review an immutable subject while allowing closeout to\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:526:- Context: Assignment, retries and targeted rereview need durable workflow\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:528:- Options considered: move all review to Conductor; keep all orchestration in\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:548:### Decision 4 — targeted rereview\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:550:- Context: Restarting every criterion after a narrow remediation makes review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:552:- Options considered: always full rereview; trust an orchestrator's affected\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:557:- Consequences: High-criticality policy may still require full rereview.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:579:| Unit | One-cycle convergence | `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run TestReviewBundleCloseoutConvergesWithoutRereview -count=1` | Flow reaches closed with one sealed bundle and one approved attestation. |\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:580:| Unit | Targeted rereview | `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run 'TestReviewBundleDelta|TestReviewAttestationCriterionReuse' -count=1` | Only exact unchanged slices reuse; complete projection remains current. |\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:586:| Compatibility | Legacy schema v1/v2 | `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'TestReviewBundleLegacy|TestReviewRecordCompatibility' -count=1` | Old attempts stay readable; `review record` follows policy mode. |\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:590:| Integration | Strict module matrix | `pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --report --report-task review-bundle-convergence` | Every required matrix check passes with a structured report. |\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:591:| E2E | Source-build fresh repo | `tests/e2e/review-bundle/run.sh` | Prepare, validate, seal, attest, close and recheck finish without stale review. |\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:592:| E2E | Installed home binary | `/home/go/.local/bin/pose version && /home/go/.local/bin/pose doctor --json && POSE_BIN=/home/go/.local/bin/pose tests/e2e/review-bundle/run.sh` | Installed revision matches the validated build and passes the same flow. |\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:595:| Delivery | Artifact provenance | `pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-bundle-convergence --strict` | Declared and Git-observed artifacts match an immutable change set. |\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:596:| Delivery | Surface and contract | `pose surface-check --spec pose-review-bundle-convergence --strict` | CLI reachability and CLI/MCP/governance integration evidence are current. |\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:597:| Governance | History/skills/spec | `pose history-check --strict && pose skills-check --strict && pose lint-spec pose-review-bundle-convergence --strict` | Append-only history, distributed skills and spec lifecycle all pass. |\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:602:- Derived-only state, assessment, report and index refreshes do not stale review.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:635:- Command: `pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --report --report-task review-bundle-convergence`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:638:- Command: `pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-bundle-convergence --strict`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:641:- Command: `pose surface-check --spec pose-review-bundle-convergence --strict`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:649:- 2026-08-13 — implementation landed in `89b100a`; independent review then\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:681:- Independent review corrections: working-tree-only subjects now fail closed;\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:712:  governance:convergent-review-closeout evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:713:  check:review-bundle-convergence.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:733:- R21 [satisfied] surface:review-bundle-cli evidence:e2e\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:737:  commit:89b100a contract:review-bundle-mcp evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:738:  check:review-bundle-convergence.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:745:- R26 [satisfied] source and installed `tests/e2e/review-bundle/run.sh` plus\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:746:  `TestReviewAttestationDoesNotMutateBundleAndConverges` test:review-bundle-e2e.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:750:  `2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations` commit:89b100a.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:756:  successful `govulncheck ./...`; check:review-bundle-convergence.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:763:- R35 [satisfied] trust/independence preservation tests in review plan and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:766:  382-commit gitleaks scan; check:review-bundle-convergence.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:775:- R41 [satisfied] keeping bundle adoption opt-in/preview while source and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:776:  installed-binary convergence cases pass; test:review-bundle-e2e.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:787:- The feature intentionally remains opt-in/preview; promotion is a later\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:798:Delivered the preview/opt-in convergent review flow end to end: canonical\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:805:- Engine: `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go`, review closeout and delivery\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:809:- Distribution: POSE manual, feature/review workflows, skills, docs-site,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:813:- E2E: `tests/e2e/review-bundle/run.sh` for source and installed binaries.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-13-pose-review-bundle-convergence.md:820:- Source and installed `tests/e2e/review-bundle/run.sh`: SUCCESS.\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:1:# ADR: Sealed review bundles and separate attestations\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:4:Accepted (2026-08-13) — implemented by spec `pose-review-bundle-convergence`\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:5:Amended (2026-09-08) by spec `pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals` — see Amendments\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:16:POSE currently binds immutable review attempts to `scope_digest` and, under\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:33:review a transient merge/squash object that is not a durable fetchable ref,\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:34:while POSE needs a stable offline identity for the reviewed content. Harne8's\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:35:Conductor is the appropriate place for reviewer assignment, durable workflow,\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:42:   because path/field exceptions do not define a stable semantic review subject\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:44:2. Freeze the entire repository from review start through closeout — rejected\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:48:3. Move review validity entirely to Harne8/Conductor — rejected because it\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:53:   because the reviewed subject reaches a fixed point without losing offline\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:58:Introduce a versioned immutable `ReviewBundle` as the only new review subject\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:60:scope projection, attributed implementation subject, effective review-plan\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:62:It does not contain lifecycle transitions, reviewer identity, attestation data,\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:73:append-only under `.pose/review-bundles/`. Use canonical patch and sorted\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:84:Record review approval as a separate immutable attestation referencing the\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:91:attestation never changes the bundle. `review-check`, `closeout-check` and\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:96:Permit targeted rereview only by explicit policy: a prior criterion disposition\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:115:behavior for non-adopters. Keep `pose review record` as a compatibility entry\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:116:point. Do not promote bundle-backed component-aware review from preview until\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:123:- Positive: review gains a stable subject; recording approval and closing a\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:128:- Positive: Conductor can implement a humane durable rereview loop without\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:129:  becoming the sole review authority.\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:134:- Positive: grouped diagnostics and phase-aware tools keep the review contract\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:147:  are separated from the review digest, not waived.\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:161:Spec `pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals`.\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:166:is how that stays visible instead of being reviewed as nothing.\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:169:no content to classify and none to read; the reviewable fact is the deletion,\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:171:spends the entire review to tell the reviewer nothing they cannot see — the\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:218:  the first already carries a reviewer's rationale in place of evidence, and the\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:220:- `pose review auto-attest` no longer synthesises a reference. Where the scope\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:238:`reviewEvidenceClassCatalog`, what a profile may demand. Six of nineteen classes\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:340:arrives after it compared the review's timestamp against\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:384:  `allow_criterion_reuse`, `require_signed_attestations`, `reviewer_independence`,\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:403:`critical` accepted risk with no owner, no rationale and no review date; a\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:408:So a project that adopted review bundles — the mechanism this ADR introduced to\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:409:make review *more* rigorous — silently lost a gate it had before, and two policy\n.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md:447:was permitted is a property of the review that happened, so reading it live lets\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-readme-evaluation-path.md:135:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-localization-docs-contract.md:110:- [done] Confirm the first `mkdocs build --strict` CI run (`docs.yml`) against this spec's page edits — not executable in this sandbox (no `pip`/`mkdocs`). Confirmed on run 31148183904: strict build clean, no warnings. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-08-19)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree.md:24:A árvore commitada do pose-dist passou de 256 MiB (256,8 MiB; 88 MiB de review runs e 102 MiB de review bundles). Desde então, todo `pose close` falha em `gitMaterializedChangesForIn` com \"snapshot exceeds 256 MiB\", e toda revisão delegada falha na limpeza do worktree descartável, que tira um `dispatchDiskSnapshot` do mesmo tamanho. Duas specs aprovadas ou em revisão (`pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation`, `pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph`) ficaram sem poder fechar. As duas capturas precisam ler a árvore inteira para responder; um teto abaixo dela só pode reprovar.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree.md:43:- R4: The cleanup of a delegated review's worktree shall bound the bytes it removes by the same budget, computed from the coordinator repository for the worktree's checked-out commit when the worktree is registered, so a clean worktree of a tree past the margin is removed and a worktree grown past the budget is retained.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree.md:61:- `pose/review_adapter_containment.go`: o inventário da limpeza do worktree da revisão delegada usa o mesmo orçamento.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree.md:66:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree.md:129:- Notes: com o teto antigo (só a margem), o teste da árvore inteira reprova com \"snapshot exceeds its budget of 1024 bytes\"; com o orçamento escalonado passa, e um arquivo que cresce 60 KiB além da árvore reprova nas duas capturas. Os fechamentos de `pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation` e `pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph` reprovaram com \"snapshot exceeds 256 MiB\" sobre a árvore de 256,8 MiB do pose-dist.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree.md:158:- [open] F1: decidir a retenção dos registros de revisão, que somam 190 MiB dos 256,8 MiB da árvore do pose-dist e crescem a cada rodada. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-30)\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:4:Accepted (2026-11-02), spec `pose-milestone-review-proportional`.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:8:100 of the 133 milestones with members have exactly one. Reviewing such a milestone repeats the review of its spec: it took 42 milestones and a night to learn that. Of the 34 judged, the two defects worth having came from an adversarial reader with a new falsifier, not from the milestone: the gate of `manifest-tag-integrity` restates R4 of its spec, and its registered check passed with the defect in place. A declared exit check would have passed too.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:12:- A milestone with exactly one local member has no review of its own: its approval is the approval of that spec, once the spec is closed. It inherits a review and nothing else: the acceptance of its edges still has to hold.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:13:- A negative review recorded on the milestone stands, in a bundle or a legacy attempt, and an approval already recorded on it stays as it is.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:14:- While that spec is open, its review answers for the exit gate of the milestone, as a criterion of the plan, so the gate is judged once and not never.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:15:- When that spec turns done it keeps the plan it was sealed with (spec `pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan`): the criterion stays in its plan if the governing sealed bundle carries it, because the plan is an input of the bundle and a plan that lost the criterion at the transition made the bundle the approval was attested over read superseded, and, for an approval backed by a delegated run, no longer governing. A done spec sealed without the criterion gains none, so no approval falls; a done spec whose sealed history cannot be read whole gets a blocker in its plan instead of silently losing the gate. Measured on this repository: 17 done specs gain the criterion, and every one of them verifies the same before and after (closed, fresh, approved).\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:16:- A closeout whose terminal verification stops on an unknown governance read view, with the lifecycle already done, writes no checkpoint and clears the one it holds: the repository carries the state, `--resume` re-plans from it, and a checkpoint recording that stop was read as an open defect by the next reviewer.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:17:- A milestone of several members keeps its integration review, where the review of `community-launch` found what no spec could.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:18:- A roadmap may declare `unreviewed_milestones: <reason>`, and its reached milestones then stand without a review. The reason is sealed with the roadmap, whose own review stays required and is what an external consumer holds for such a milestone.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:22:- One rule answers `review verify`, closeout, the review of a roadmap and the federated proof, because all of them read one verification.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:23:- No bundle or attestation exists for an inherited milestone. `review verify` shows the bundle of the spec and says it is inherited.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:24:- The second look that a late milestone review happened to give is gone for one-member milestones, and belongs to the review of the roadmap.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:29:- Keeping every review: a repetition that costs a bundle of thousands of lines per milestone.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md:30:- Dropping milestone review altogether: it is where several specs meet, and the only place that sees that.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-remediation-lineage.md:76:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-remediation-lineage.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-remediation-lineage.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/schemas/v1/review-bundle.schema.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-remediation-lineage.md:99:- capability:remediation-lineage module:pose-mcp/internal/pose profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-remediation-lineage.md:137:- Contexto consumido: knowledge:adr-sealed-review-bundles-review; não omitir o\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-remediation-lineage.md:173:- `pose review verify spec:pose-abm-remediation-lineage` antes da transição.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-remediation-lineage.md:262:Atestação `rva-0ae8a7981ab2de7e`, `agent:claude-opus-5`, approved; `review-check`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-consolidation-batch-15-authoring.md:91:Gates locais e critérios de saída julgados no [bundle rvb-743f3091a323e9f2](../review-bundles/rvb-743f3091a323e9f2.json), com [atestação rva-4c610fc33c38d11a](../review-attestations/rva-4c610fc33c38d11a.json) de uma execução separada do Codex, mesmo fornecedor/modelo herdado. Sem alegação de identidade autenticada ou revisão entre fornecedores.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-consolidation-batch-15-authoring.md:97:Participantes/amostras/thresholds e provas atuais de runtime/review não existem neste lote.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:38:- R1: Status done e operação idempotente/no-op devem ser distintos de verificação semântica terminal. O plano não deve marcar review/judgment/evidence/verify executados ou satisfeitos apenas porque o lifecycle é done.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:39:- R2: Plan, closeout-check, apply/resume e consumidores CLI/MCP devem usar o mesmo verificador do contrato aplicável ao scope, com blockers, limitações e próximos passos suportados; P02 com review devido ausente não deve aparecer terminal em uma superfície e recusado na outra.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:41:- R4: Done com prova suficiente deve manter idempotência e retorno no-op fiel; done com verificação insuficiente deve revelar lacuna/reparo sem reabrir, sobrescrever ou fabricar review automaticamente. Contexto desconhecido/ilegível não deve certificar terminal.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:67:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:72:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:92:- [x] Reproduzir done sem review e definir contrato compatível.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:101:- Knowledge: knowledge:adr-sealed-review-bundles-review, knowledge:pose-b07-implementation\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:115:| V1 — P02 done sem review devido após adoção | Plano não certifica terminal/steps verificados; mesmo blocker do closeout-check. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:120:| V6 — Prova/contexto ilegíveis e paridade CLI/MCP | Limitação/blocker fiel; não fabricar terminal, receipt ou review. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:126:| Done sem review, legacy/cutoff, válido, histórico ilegível | `cd pose-mcp && go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run TerminalVerification -count=1` | mesmo veredito entre state/plan/CLI/MCP; sem escrita ou review fabricado |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:155:Implementado o verificador terminal compartilhado, com lifecycle distinto, prova e limitações explícitas e no-op sem mutação. A dependência de amendments foi fechada em `94b4f4b` antes do start B11; seus R1–R3 e histórico foram preservados. Fechada nativamente em 2026-10-25, com matriz estrita 152/152, composição sem findings e review aprovada; consulte o [relatório](../reports/2026-10-24-b11-terminal-verification.md).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:159:No-op de lifecycle não garante conclusão atual. A implementação precisa distinguir contrato histórico aplicável de exigência nova e não reescrever status/review para sanar lacuna. A dependência de amendments está done; B11 consome apenas seu assessment e não cria journal ou baseline paralelos. O novo estado `not-run` é breaking para consumidores do plano; atualizar clientes antes de adoção. A verificação é limitada ao contrato aplicável, não comprova materialidade ou execução histórica sem receipt.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-closeout-terminal-verification.md:163:- [open] Acrescentar cenário raw-done-terminal ao corpus adversarial genérico; regressões permanentes e produtor registrado já cobrem R1–R8. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-design-delta-batched-git-reads.md:74:  is regenerated before sealing the governed review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-design-delta-batched-git-reads.md:91:Implementation validated and closed through the governed review gate on 2026-10-01. Canonical strict validation passed 48/48 checks at f41b5aa; review bundle `rvb-8629f7c6a90b26ec` was fresh and approved before `pose close`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegation-surface, pose-delegated-review-completion-signal\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:14:# Spec: A general task can be delegated to another agent\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:20:Let a person or an agent hand any task to another agent through `pose delegate task`, with the access it needs, the same lifecycle as every delegated run, and no path from a task to a gate.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:24:Decided by the [delegation ADR](../adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md). The personal launchers survive mostly because they also delegate work that is not a review: implementing, fixing, committing and pushing with another vendor's agent. Without a native task purpose they cannot retire, and the work they run stays unrecorded and unobservable by POSE's own commands.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:32:Scheduling or queueing tasks; tasks across projects; reviewing what a task changed (that is a review of its own bundle).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:38:- R1: `pose delegate task <prompt-file|->` shall run the chosen agent with the prompt on stdin in `--cd <dir>` (default: the current directory).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:42:- R5: Without `--record`, the run shall be kept under the user's state directory for the project — prompt, raw and normalized events, final message, stderr, argv, removed variable names, exit code, label — with owner-only permissions; with `--record`, under `.pose/delegate-runs/`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:44:- R7: Every reader of review runs, attestations, closeouts and gates shall ignore task runs, and `pose review attest --run` shall refuse a task run.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:66:Task front end, access templates, record location and permissions, exclusion from review readers, default continuation message.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:82:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:83:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_task.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:84:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_task_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:85:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:86:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_handoff.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:87:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:88:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:89:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:98:- capability:delegation-task module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_task.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:102:`pose delegate task`; policy keys `purposes.task.default_access`, `agents.<name>.outside_git_args`, `add_dir_args`, `no_network_args` and `resume.commands`, and the template placeholders `{outside_git}`, `{add_dirs}` and `{no_network}` (D3); record location; `pose delegate resume --prompt` for tasks; `wait` exits 0 for a task its agent completed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:109:- [x] Exclusion from every review and gate reader\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:111:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:126:- Selected option: every review reader ignores task runs and attestation refuses them\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:128:- Consequences: a task that reviews something has to be run as a review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:136:- Consequences: an agent without the fragments cannot take those flags, and says so; existing review templates are unchanged\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:141:- Minimal option: record tasks under `.pose/review-runs` with a purpose field every reader filters\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:142:- Selected option: task runs are stored apart (state directory, or `.pose/delegate-runs` with `--record`), read only by the lifecycle commands, with their own identifiers (`tat-` attempts, `trn-` runs) and no attempt reservation or bundle; attestation and provenance refuse a task run by name\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:143:- Rationale: a reader that forgets the filter would turn a task into evidence; storage the review readers never open cannot\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:144:- Consequences: a task has no bundle budget; its continuation budget is the attempt's, as for reviews\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:145:- Falsifier: a review reader, a gate or a closeout that lists a task run\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:151:A fake agent runs a task with each access level, inside and outside a Git repository; `full` warns and is never defaulted; `--no-network` with `write` is refused; the record lands in the state directory with owner-only permissions, and under `.pose/` only with `--record`; `attest --run` refuses a task run and `review verify` ignores it; a limited task resumes with the default message.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:170:Delivered `pose delegate task` on implementation head `f19a1c723ac66020e6215ad746640cdb892305b3`, milestone `task` of roadmap `delegation`: prompt input and real working directory, access templates and explicit fragments, private records outside governance storage, final stdout and agent exit status, structured JSON, observation, cancellation, continuation, handoff and launching-session routing. Tasks never become review evidence. Full launcher parity remains the retirement milestone's responsibility.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:172:Independent review was performed by maintainer-authorized `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review` (Codex/OpenAI), another vendor than implementer Claude/Anthropic (`agent:claude-opus-5-5`, session `f2a4d9f2-d557-4064-ae96-6ed52bb47cd2`). The engine-required `agent:independent-` prefix is a declaration, not authenticated proof. Local attestations are unsigned; cognitive independence is not observable. The seal declares implementation `anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`; its warning about the absent Anthropic session reference in the sealing environment is expected and retained.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:174:Sealed bundle: [rvb-0d0c180fd61d0b2b](../review-bundles/rvb-0d0c180fd61d0b2b.json). Approved attestation: [rva-4e82abf0154dfd55](../review-attestations/rva-4e82abf0154dfd55.json). `review verify` confirmed fresh, approved review before the guarded native close. The independent review used the backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:180:- Twenty-three isolated negative mutations were detected and restored. Probes from rounds 1–3 were rerun, including overlapping credentials, anchored/equal/conflicting sessions, stderr limits, safe failure records and the shared review classifier without task-only channels. No blocker remained in round 4.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-task.md:188:F2 is a future hardening item: the external state path accepts a symbolic ancestor while its leaf and record files remain owner-only; no cross-user disclosure was demonstrated. F3 is a parity gap retained for the retirement work: task does not accept `--detach`. Neither item waives an R1–R10 acceptance requirement. The owner and review triggers below are the operational handoff.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-release-prepare-guards-claimed-fragments.md:70:2026-10-10, independent review (agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review, fallback reviewer): low severity. With `--allow-moved-claims` prepare froze without naming the claims, and the help did not show the flag. Prepare now prints `release.allowed.moved-claim=` for each, the test asserts it, and the help lists the flag.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:6:optional worktree runtime (B35) was delivered in three slices, each reviewed independently, and\n.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:33:Propose these boundaries for review, without choosing wire/schema details yet:\n.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:106:expiring operational review in knowledge:adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:192:  `pose_action_fulfil`, `pose_review_attest`), which revalidate authority, assurance,\n.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:194:  (`pose_delegate_*`) or request a gate (`pose_validate_*`) carry their own catalog\n.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:212:  the runs alive at once, abandoned ones included, are capped so that repeated\n.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:221:  not carry (the `--reviewer` execution identity when a mechanical attestation is\n.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:266:- **Slicing.** B35 is delivered in three specs, each reviewed on its own:\n.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:277:The three slices are done and each was reviewed independently: `pose-optional-worktree-runtime`\n.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:286:- **Hosted operations.** The runtime hosts five read checks (`review-check`, `closeout-check`,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-seeds-an-answerable-maintainer.md:22:When `pose update` creates `.pose/policy/actions.json` and opens configuration-review requests to the `maintainer` role, the project shall have a way to name its maintainer as part of that step, and answering an unanswerable request shall say why.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-seeds-an-answerable-maintainer.md:30:The engine must not invent a principal: a name from git is a suggestion, confirmed by preview and apply, as `pose identity add` already does.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-seeds-an-answerable-maintainer.md:49:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/configuration_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-seeds-an-answerable-maintainer.md:73:2026-10-10, independent review (agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review): medium severity. `setup` marked `identity.maintainer` done for a principal with a registered key holding only `reviewer`, while nobody held `maintainer`. The step now asks for a maintainer whenever that role is empty under agency readiness or open role requests; `TestSetupWantsAMaintainerEvenWhenYouHoldAnotherRole` fails on the previous step.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:2:slug: pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:7:depends_on: pose-abm-review-soundness\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:11:delivers: governance:review-tool-deferred\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:24:Evitar que reviews de specs sem delivery target sejam forçados a fabricar\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:35:review; não relaxar `review-complete`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:48:`pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go` e teste de contrato CLI.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:51:- governance:review-tool-deferred module:pose-mcp profile:structural-delta entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:54:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:55:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:56:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:66:- [x] Rodar suíte e review final.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:80:- Consequences: uma disposição inválida ainda falha em `review verify`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:87:| Full CLI/review behavior; R2/R3 | `go test ./internal/cli ./internal/pose -run 'Review|Closeout' -count=1` | target-bearing gates remain strict |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:94:2026-09-19: focused parser regression, full Go suite, vet, build and review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:96:2026-09-19: sealed review bundle `rvb-fa979be05b5ed2ad` and approved\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:101:- R2 [satisfied] <review evaluator keeps target-bearing required tools strict> evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:108:deferred before scope evaluation, while final review verification remains the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:113:run the final review verification gate. This boundary is covered by the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-tool-deferred-without-delivery.md:114:existing target-bearing review tests and the sealed validation evidence.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-abm-capability-adoption.md:72:ABM capability follow-ups, pilot report, review policy (only after decision).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-abm-capability-adoption.md:82:- modified: .pose/policy/review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-abm-capability-adoption.md:147:A shadow on five disposable clones at ce17db6 (report `.pose/reports/pose-abm-capability-adoption.md`) measured each capability against an unadopted baseline. Contract nodes had no observable effect in this corpus. Atomic start added 39 closeout-restricting `start-reconciliation` obligations, one per spec already in progress, with no command to record a legacy baseline and no adoption cutoff; that stops its rollout without invalidating the code. Causality closeout stamped its contract on all 39 prepared bundles; its attestation cost was not measured. No implementation was added. The three adoption decisions are open as action requests act-7d587a8e4f3bf0fc, act-fa1d72f029d567a0 and act-08a9fd2d9a0e50bb, addressed to human:oseias with the agent's recommendation (adopt, defer, defer); the review policy changes only after each answer.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-abm-capability-adoption.md:155:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-abm-capability-adoption.md:159:- [done] Resolved by the adoption cutoff (spec pose-atomic-start-adoption-cutoff), chosen by the maintainer over a baseline command. Original item: atomic start needs a baseline command for specs already in progress, or an adoption cutoff, before it can be adopted: the shadow measured 39 closeout-blocking reconciliations with no remedy (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-01)\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-bounded-release-compatibility-policy.md:65:  path is a reviewed one-line change with a checksum pin.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md:32:- R1: Inventariar cada rota CLI/MCP pertinente como domínio direto, wrapper de CLI, planejamento read-only, write admitido ou handoff externo, com a classe declarada e mantida igual ao catálogo por teste. A fonte única de uma operação é uma só: para as operações read-only e limitadas cuja semântica já mora no pacote CLI (`suggest`, `followups`), é a função do comando, que o wrapper executa em processo, deixando de spawnar o binário, com evidência de contagem; mover essa semântica para o pacote de domínio é follow-up. Os gates (`check`, `skills-check`, `lint-spec`) e o harness externo (`delegate`) mantêm a fronteira de processo, sem promessa genérica de eliminar spawn.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md:71:Executar após B12/B14/B34 e reutilizar closeout/context/orchestration existentes. Store wrappers em cli.go têm timeout fixo e delegam à CLI; não copiar cmd handlers inteiros para uma segunda implementação. Inventariar routes/context flags, catálogo/registry/docs/scaffold/locales e consumidores, completar artifacts e classification de compatibilidade antes de start. knowledge:adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review acompanha a proposta, que permanece Proposed. CLI como adapter de fonte única é preservada pela extração para domínio; acertar a fronteira de validação externa antes de qualquer tool nova. B35 consome esta API depois; não impor runtime para obter paridade standalone.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md:76:- Proposal: [Shared domain and optional worktree runtime](../adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md), status Proposed; knowledge:adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md:105:- Spawns, counted (`CLISpawnAttempts` and `CLIInProcessRuns`): of the ten CLI-wrapper routes, two (`pose_suggest`, `pose_get_followups`) no longer start the binary; `pose_check`, `pose_skills_check` and `pose_lint_spec` still do, by design, and the five `pose_delegate_*` routes drive `pose delegate`, a legitimate external harness. No latency or efficiency gain is claimed, and stdio is not offered as an IPC channel.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md:107:- An in-process run cannot be killed: on a deadline it finishes in the background, writes nothing, and the caller gets an execution failure with no verdict. A caller that has already cancelled never starts the command, a completion that races a cancellation is discarded, and the runs alive at once, abandoned ones included, are capped at four, so repeated timeouts cannot accumulate work; the work of one run (`followups` reads the follow-ups of the corpus) is bounded by the corpus, not by a ceiling, and a ceiling is the follow-up below.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md:124:- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head, and the suites of `internal/pose`, `internal/cli` and `internal/mcpserver`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md:125:- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review by a different vendor, concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md:134:- [open] Move the semantics of `suggest` and `followups` from the CLI package into the domain package so both adapters render one function, then drop the registry. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md:135:- [open] Resolve the root as the CLI dispatcher does before an in-process run, or reject a root that is not a project root. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md:136:- [open] Give `followups` an enforced ceiling on the corpus it compares, or a kill path, so the in-process admission rests on bounded work and not only on a cap of concurrent runs. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md:137:- [open] Decide whether the gates (`check`, `skills-check`, `lint-spec`) can run in process with a kill path, and measure the spawn count and latency per operation on the real corpus. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md:74:Executar após B07/B12/B14/B15/B31/B32/B33/B34. Reusar o host MCP quando admissível, mas não tomar stdio de outro cliente nem confundir event cursor/active context com snapshot/checkpoint. A [proposta de runtime](../adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md) e knowledge:adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review exigem resolver IPC local por plataforma, identity/handshake/ownership/fallback e limites antes do código; o path worktreeruntime é proposta de organização a reconciliar. Respeitar ADR scoped Git batch, active-context disclosure, obligations D14 e boundary de validation orchestration. Runtime é host opcional do domínio, não scheduler/Harness/conductor novo; nenhum transporte/command/default será adotado pela escrita. Completar schema/versionamento, CLI flags/registry/catalog/docs/locales e budget/benchmark inventory antes do start.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md:79:- Proposal: [Shared domain and optional worktree runtime](../adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md), emenda de 2026-11-09 (transporte, identidade, fatiamento); knowledge:adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md:125:- Result: registrado pela evidência de validação selada; revisão delegada independente concluída com `pose review conclude`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md:133:- [open] Answer a peer of another user with a reason before closing the connection, so that the client reports it instead of a bare EOF. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md:134:- [open] Put the build's `vcs.modified` and the capabilities the runtime offers in the identity, so that two dev builds of one version do not handshake as compatible. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md:135:- [open] Keep the stderr of a detached `serve` in a log in the endpoint directory, so that a start whose serve dies reports why. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md:136:- [open] Named pipe com ACL do dono para o Windows, que hoje roda sempre standalone. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md:137:- [open] Exercer em teste o par com UID diferente (dois usuários). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-read-view-streamed-object-digests.md:24:Em 2026-11-13, fechando `pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit`, todo `pose index` do pose-dist passou a ser recusado: os change sets de todas as specs leem `git show --binary` de 2.451 commits (492 MB), e com os arquivos da geração a operação passou do orçamento de 512 MiB de entrada capturada. A emenda D10 da ADR de leituras de governança elevou o orçamento para 1 GiB, o que só comprou folga: o corpus cresce a cada commit atribuído, e o próximo estouro bloqueia de novo toda geração de índice, fechamento e revisão do repositório. É uma lacuna de consistência do motor: um limite de segurança que o uso normal do próprio POSE derruba.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-read-view-streamed-object-digests.md:28:- O read view continua sem cache entre operações (ADR governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views): o ganho vem de não reter os bytes, não de reaproveitá-los entre execuções.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-read-view-streamed-object-digests.md:187:- [open] F1: evitar que `pose index` leia o patch de cada commit atribuído várias vezes (medido: cerca de 2,4 leituras por commit dentro da operação de construção, além da prova de fechamento das entradas), e medir se o I/O restante pede um registro imutável de digest por commit, versionado, em vez da releitura. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-12-13)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-request-resolution.md:7:depends_on: pose-review-attribution-roles, pose-action-requests\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-request-resolution.md:30:Reuse the review authority contracts and their explicit limits. Corrections are\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-request-resolution.md:68:- Resolution input is untrusted; signatures verified with the existing review authority verifier.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-request-resolution.md:121:- Context: MCP exposes only read, gate and external-event tools; review sealing and attestation import are CLI writes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-request-resolution.md:131:- Decision: `.pose/policy/actions.json` maps roles to principals; signing pins, the human-authority grant and the audience stay in the review policy.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-action-request-resolution.md:176:Delivers resolve, cancel, waive and invalidate with roles, digests, revisions, idempotency and verified claims as specified. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-21-action-effects-select-material-destinations-independently-of-origin.md:44:prospective and requires compatibility review before any release/adoption.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-compat-fixture-delivery-example.md:30:  strict check, idempotent reapply and user-data preservation assertions active.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-standalone-dogfood.md:52:- Process theater emerges if artifacts are created after implementation or never reviewed.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-standalone-dogfood.md:64:- [x] Define minimum artifact ownership and review rules for this repository: \"Dogfooding governance\" section in `CONTRIBUTING.md`; module ownership in `.pose/indexes/module-metadata.json` (`pose-mcp`, `mcp-enforce` → `@pose-maintainers`, criticality high). ([reference](https://dora.dev/capabilities/platform-engineering/))\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-standalone-dogfood.md:97:- R3 [deferred-integration: spec:pose-governance-gate-activation] — the quarterly audit is scheduled for 2026-10-01 and has not run yet; reviewing its first output is R6 of the spec that owns this trace\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-standalone-dogfood.md:105:Ownership and review rules for the standalone instance (`CONTRIBUTING.md`,\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-standalone-dogfood.md:123:- [spawned: pose-governance-gate-activation] Review the first quarterly audit run (2026-10-01) and disposition its findings. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-state-followup-origins.md:33:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/docs_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-state-followup-origins.md:40:knowledge:module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance to avoid\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-state-followup-origins.md:41:unrelated index refresh invalidating reviews. Revert the isolated fix to roll back.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-state-followup-origins.md:69:- R2 [satisfied] <state tests preserve spec references; direct review confirms capability labels are not promoted to pointers> evidence:unit\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-state-followup-origins.md:81:Governed review verified fresh and approved: bundle `rvb-430eb0b3ec8ffa5e`,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-flat-spec-amendments.md:152:Delivers per-spec journals for flat specs through the store resolver. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-dora-adoption-metrics-explicit-events-and-unavailable-state.md:75:  since activation) and Task Success (done / (done+abandoned+blocked),\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-dora-adoption-metrics-explicit-events-and-unavailable-state.md:103:  guarantee (a reflection test over the JSON schema), not a code-review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-target-and-node-scoping.md:63:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/source_coverage_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-target-and-node-scoping.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/configuration_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-target-and-node-scoping.md:94:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-21-b08-review-r1.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-target-and-node-scoping.md:96:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-21-b08-review-r2.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-target-and-node-scoping.md:155:| V1 — destinos, todas as fases, gates e stale apply | `cd pose-mcp && go test ./internal/pose -run 'ActionTarget|Governed|AdoptedEffects|StartPreview' -count=1` | Somente destino/phase/mode pertinentes restringidos; write recompõe. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-target-and-node-scoping.md:168:com uma capability e zero findings, e review verificado. Consulte o\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-target-and-node-scoping.md:198:[relatório de revisão](../reports/2026-10-21-b08-review-r2.md). O comando nativo\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-target-and-node-scoping.md:213:- [open] Revisar o versionamento e a comunicação da mudança breaking antes de publicar ou adotar B08 em outra instância; este lote não publica release nem muda policy. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-10-29)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-target-and-node-scoping.md:214:- [open] Acrescentar ao corpus adversarial um exemplo de subject existente mas semanticamente inadequado, preservando a distinção entre binding declarado e adequação da decisão humana; este lote não promete inferir essa adequação. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-21)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-lint-spec-flat-layout-followup-resolution.md:6:depends_on: pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-report-coverage-that-rests-on-inference.md:76:- modified: .pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-report-coverage-that-rests-on-inference.md:180:- [open] Revisit the declared-subtree contract once `inferred-coverage` has been observed in real repositories — the four approaches and why each was set aside are in the ADR amendment, and the missing input was how much anyone actually relies on the inference (owner:unowned crit:low review:2027-06-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-4-release-readiness.md:6:depends_on: review-check-names-a-negative-verdict\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-4-release-readiness.md:19:Publish 6.0.4 so that the report of a negative review verdict on a closed scope\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-4-release-readiness.md:24:On 6.0.3, `pose review-check` and `pose check --strict` say `no review attempt\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-4-release-readiness.md:25:exists` for a closed scope whose newest review requested changes, while `pose review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-4-release-readiness.md:93:  scope's changes-requested review as a missing record.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-4-release-readiness.md:146:negative review verdict on a closed scope.\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:1:# ADR: Immutable hierarchical review and closeout evidence\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:4:Accepted (2026-08-02) — spec `pose-hierarchical-review-closeout`\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:11:without a durable review of the exact scope being closed. Review prose existed,\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:12:but was neither immutable nor bound to the reviewed inputs. The new contract\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:13:must work offline, remain reviewable in Git, support proportional independence\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:20:2. Store a mutable `review_status` on each spec/roadmap — rejected because edits\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:24:   deterministic without collapsing review into a build check.\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:28:Store versioned review profiles under `.pose/review-profiles/` and immutable\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:29:attempts under `.pose/reviews/`. Address scopes with `spec:<slug>`,\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:32:review artifact itself, but include child closure digests at macro levels.\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:35:their own current approved review. Never infer review approval from narrative\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:41:implementing the mechanism is reviewed with the newly shipped profile before\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:52:- Trade-off: remediation creates a new review attempt rather than editing the\n.pose/adr/2026-08-02-immutable-hierarchical-review-and-closeout-evidence.md:56:- Neutral: deterministic checks remain necessary evidence; review remains a\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:35:- R2: A closure deve incluir conforme o escopo specs/subjects, action requests/answers/journals, review bundles/provas/results, policy/authority/contratos, curadoria, matriz/tests/fontes usados na evidência, descriptor/conjunto de índices, roots federadas/refs Git pertinentes e arquivos untracked relevantes. Alteração material de qualquer input observado deve invalidar a identidade aplicável; documentar inputs excluídos com justificativa, sem hash universal fictício.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:42:- R9: CLI/MCP/Attention/review/closeout devem consumir a mesma read view e divulgar geração, binding, freshness, coverage e limitations no mesmo escopo. Preservar legados com limites/versionamento explícitos; não retroinventar geração ou chamar snapshot histórico de current. Declarar budgets de bytes, trabalho, retries e ciclo/profundidade federados.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:52:- created: .pose/reports/2026-11-06-pose-b34-global-review-view-budget.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:53:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_scope_operation_view_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:54:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_scope_operation_view_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:59:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_fixture_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:60:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:61:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_mcp_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:62:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_wait_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:63:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:64:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:85:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:86:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:87:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:88:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:106:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegated_review_capability_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:110:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:128:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attribution.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:129:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:141:- created: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/governance_review_read_view_parity_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:146:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:164:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/release_review_r2_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:165:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:166:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:167:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:168:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:169:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:171:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:172:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_executable_budget_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:173:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_write_scope.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:180:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegated_verdicts_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:188:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:189:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_domain_preflight_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:191:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/update_preview_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:202:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/milestone_review_proportional_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:205:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_current_fixture_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:206:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:207:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_read_view_retention_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:215:Knowledge consumido neste plano: `knowledge:pose-b06-source-coverage-closeout`, `knowledge:pose-b07-implementation` e `knowledge:adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:225:3. **Review e closeout.** Fazer `WithReviewOperationView` reutilizar a primitiva de observação e os limites existentes, sem alegar snapshot transacional. Integrar views e coverage a review/closeout. Antes de qualquer gate ou efeito de start/close/ação/seal/attestation que reutilize avaliação, revalidar closure e authority no ponto de escrita, sob os locks pertinentes e com CAS/fencing B14 quando aplicável. `ObligationSnapshotChanges` sozinho não é essa proteção e atualmente não tem callers de produção. Não usar resposta read-only como autorização persistente.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:262:- Rationale: O `reviewOperationView` já prova que reuso de catálogo pode manter leitores vivos e auditar entradas observadas; estender essa seam conserva semântica dos producers, em vez de duplicar parser ou fazer hash universal.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:271:- Decision: Serializar writers cooperativos por root com um guard explícito, adquirido antes de recomputar a avaliação e mantido até publicação/receipt. Usar a ordem root canônica → recurso, reaproveitar locking B14 e manter CAS do destino e descriptor B15. Propagar o lease por `Store`/`Files`, sem estado global por goroutine; migrar e testar cada publisher participante. Produzir vetor de roots e recusar gate quando closure/fencing necessário não está disponível. Não criar um coordenador global entre roots nem prometer contenção de writers externos.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:311:| obrigatório — V3: Gate real de start, ação e closeout/review revalida closure/authority sob locks pertinentes; mudança antes do efeito; replay de proof/predecessor. | `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run 'GovernanceWriteGuard\\|GovernanceReadView(Start\\|Action\\|Review\\|Closeout)\\|ActionRequest\\|Start\\|ReviewCloseout' -count=1` | Com writers POSE concorrentes, conflito ou efeito impedido; nenhum efeito se baseia só em `ObligationSnapshotChanges`/metadata. Caso de writer externo sem fencing fica explicitamente fora da garantia e não recebe prova fabricada. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:328:- Em 2026-11-07, após registrar a revisão editorial e atualizar o índice sem gravações concorrentes, `review run-proof` confirmou a prova completa e a diferença de fornecedor. `closeout-check` passou com `lifecycle_done=true`, `review_approved=true`, `terminal=true` e `next_action=none`. O check estrutural global `pose check --strict` passou com 35 avisos históricos e nenhum erro, no conteúdo funcional e editorial atual. Restam somente o commit dos registros, o scan final do intervalo e a publicação; nenhum resultado remoto é alegado.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:332:- Em 2026-11-06, as correções F1/F2 da revisão independente foram commitadas em `4054d6be`: a auditoria final do registro de roots passou a atingir os metadados consumidos pelos gates, e a auditoria reutiliza os bytes imutáveis já capturados. As contraprovas falharam na versão anterior e passaram com race (3,225 s). A matriz canônica passou 189/189 no checkpoint `df7da2f0` (354,5 s de wall), incluindo integração B34 com race. A revisão Claude Opus 5.5 `rrn-7759994b4172a7a7` aprovou o bundle `rvb-84f1b7779fb959da`; a conclusão nativa registrou a atestação `rva-7fba31ed67c77cca`. Os drafts e registros recusados por formato/evidência foram preservados. Review verify e review-check confirmaram aprovação atual; `pose close` aplicou `done` em 2026-11-06. O revisor examinou código e evidência selada, sem executar comandos Bash negados pela contenção. A verificação estrutural final e a publicação ficam registradas somente após seus resultados.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:338:- Em 2026-11-06, após o índice final `gen-3acfce7ed391ed59`, artifact-check e surface-check passaram sem errors. O check estrito global falhou com 381 erros: 245 ações genéricas de fresh-review, 135 mensagens de path escape e uma closure desconhecida por record/metadata budget. A investigação nativa Sol medium `trn-78de82fe660bb649` identificou agregação dos closeouts independentes numa única view e perda de causa em `artifactPathWithin`; os erros não provam 381 reviews quebrados. A entrega permanece in-progress; os 189 checks do commit de código anterior não qualificam a correção desse caminho global.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:340:- Em 2026-11-06, a matriz canônica do código `5c9f1a96` passou com 189/189 checks em 1.052,2 s. O índice real da build normal passou e publicou `gen-dbc32ae488133b00` antes da atualização final dos resultados. Os perfis Sol medium e Claude Code Opus 5.5 foram cadastrados e reconhecidos nas instâncias; preview não é execução de review. O fechamento continua condicionado aos gates atuais e à revisão independente.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:345:- Após a correção do ownership das fixtures detached, os quatro testes de cleanup/barreira passaram em cinco repetições (`-count=5`, 27,777 s), e a seleção adjacente de delegação CLI/MCP, espera, observação e hooks passou com `-race`. O novo controle de dois supervisores inicialmente tentou abrir reviews concorrentes sem resultado terminal do predecessor e foi recusado em cinco repetições; a fixture foi corrigida para reter os supervisores nos hooks após seus runs terminais, preservando a ordem legítima de tentativas. Esses resultados focados não substituem a nova matriz completa. Não houve alteração de código de produção ou da semântica de `delegate wait` nessa correção.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:346:- Em 2026-11-05, a matriz nativa estrita no HEAD `ba458666948ab8c911eedac0ae5064dfc4048263` executou 189 checks: 188 aprovados e um reprovado, em 996 s. Todos os checks especializados passaram, incluindo a integração B34 com race; a suíte completa terminou em 342 s, sem timeout, mas `TestTheWaitAcknowledgementNeverTouchesAnExistingEntry` falhou no cleanup da fixture com `directory not empty`. O pacote domínio passou em 340,992 s e MCP em 5,691 s. A execução não qualifica a entrega completa. A investigação identificou que o terminal do run precede a saída do supervisor detached, que ainda pode escrever durante auto-conclude/hook; a correção deve aguardar seu término real antes de remover a fixture, preservando a semântica de `delegate wait`. O resultado canônico registra a reprovação; nenhuma falha de cleanup será ignorada.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:348:- Em 2026-11-04, a sexta rodada focada congelada compilou os três pacotes e executou 247 testes/subtestes aprovados e 88 falhas. A seleção passou a executar também os testes CLI anteriormente bloqueados pela compilação, portanto não é comparável por contagem à rodada anterior. Persistiram falhas de contexto do default root sem ID explícito, cold start de índices, closeout/review e um novo print direto; logs: `/tmp/b34-focused-frozen-6.jsonl` e `/tmp/b34-focused-6-failures.txt`. Nenhum requisito é qualificado por essa rodada incompleta.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:352:- Em 2026-11-04 (UTC), a terceira rodada focada congelada executou domínio, CLI e MCP com `-count=1 -timeout=5m`: 179 testes aprovados e 15 falhas. Os casos novos de bindings, consumo de índices e guards de ações federadas passaram; a integração projeção/review, os doubles de diretório e os controles positivos de closeout ainda falharam. Log: `/tmp/b34-focused-frozen-3.jsonl`. A rodada não qualifica o target composto.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:353:- Em 2026-11-04 (UTC), a segunda rodada focada congelada registrou 161 testes aprovados, mas falhou em compatibilidade de review view, coverage de phase readiness e limite de impressão direta do CLI. O pacote MCP passou. Log: `/tmp/b34-focused-frozen-2.jsonl`. As correções posteriores e novos casos de índices ainda não estão qualificados por essa rodada.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:391:- R2 [satisfied] check:governance-read-view-integration test:TestGovernanceReadViewGitCapturesAndAuditsExactCommand test:TestGovernanceReadViewIndexConsumptionChecksBoundInputsOnlyWhenUsed test:TestGovernanceReadViewOperationSharesInputByteBudgetAcrossRoots check:delegated-run-provenance-integration test:TestRunProvenanceExecutableHasIndependentMeasuredBudget test:TestRunProvenanceExecutableBudgetBoundaryAndLinks. Sources and semantic federated index inputs use the captured closure; unrelated unused roots remain outside its coverage.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:398:- R9 [satisfied] capability:governance-read-view-generation evidence:integration check:governance-read-view-integration test:TestGovernanceReadViewParityAcrossCLIAndMCPEntryPoints test:TestGovernanceReadViewScopeGlobalGateSerialAndParallelPreserveApprovals. Shared domain projection and review views disclose additive schema-v1 bindings, freshness and coverage; legacy inputs remain readable with explicit uncertainty and budgets.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:417:- [open] Substituir a classificação `federated-roadmap` por substring de erro por erro tipado, preservando código/receipts e controles negativos (revisão Claude F3). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:418:- [open] Evitar reexecução integral da matriz por checkpoints administrativos de índice/resultados, vinculando equivalência ao material validado e preservando rejeição de evidência stale e checkout incompleto. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-12-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-generation-bound-query-cursors.md:99:Aplicar os gates do `review-plan` e as rules vigentes. Durante a correção, executar regressões focadas no delta e nos controles afetados; no fechamento, registrar evidência canônica atual que cubra o módulo. Uma validação global que já contenha seus resultados pode responder também ao componente quando coverage/proveniência nativas comprovarem isso, sem repetir a suíte apenas por haver dois IDs de ferramenta. Preservar todos os checks obrigatórios e repetir o que uma mudança material invalidar.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-generation-bound-query-cursors.md:133:- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-generation-bound-query-cursors.md:134:- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review by a different vendor, concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-generation-bound-query-cursors.md:145:- [open] Give the list collections an index so that `limit` bounds the read, parse and copy work instead of only the page size, then measure it against the corpus. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-process-inventory-tolerates-exit.md:6:depends_on: pose-delegated-adapter-containment\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-process-inventory-tolerates-exit.md:60:`internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go`, `internal/pose/start_lock_linux.go`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-process-inventory-tolerates-exit.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-process-inventory-tolerates-exit.md:83:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-process-inventory-tolerates-exit.md:99:The real sequence on a real process: open its `stat`, kill and reap it, read. The inventory run while processes exit continuously. The gate fails on the previous predicate.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-process-inventory-tolerates-exit.md:110:A process that exits between opening its `stat` and reading it reads as gone, in the group inventory and in the probe of a lock's owner. Other read errors still fail closed. Independently reviewed by Codex in one round: the predicate and the lock change hold, and all three new tests fail without the fix.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-process-inventory-tolerates-exit.md:118:- [open] F1: keep the underlying termination error in the failure, so that the next incident can be told apart from the other causes that fit within a second (review finding 1). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-process-inventory-tolerates-exit.md:119:- [open] F2: force the read error through both call sites with a seam, including an active owner and unknown on permission (review finding 2). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/adr/2026-09-11-release-archival-is-attested-by-the-ledger-never-written-into-specs.md:44:list sits in the spec's Technical Plan, and the sealed review bundle digests that\n.pose/adr/2026-09-11-release-archival-is-attested-by-the-ledger-never-written-into-specs.md:45:section as semantic review input. Cutting 5.0.5 changed the Technical Plan digest\n.pose/adr/2026-09-11-release-archival-is-attested-by-the-ledger-never-written-into-specs.md:51:workflow, which asks for member specs to be terminal, with current review,\n.pose/adr/2026-09-11-release-archival-is-attested-by-the-ledger-never-written-into-specs.md:75:   Technical Plan, so the conflict with sealed review stays.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-recovery-and-close-scope-consistency.md:25:Achado ao investigar o aviso persistente do harne8 (113 avisos do gate, todos \"review input closure is unknown: index generation does not bind input …\"), 2026-11-10:\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-recovery-and-close-scope-consistency.md:28:2. Mesmo corrigido isso, o `pose index` do harne8 falhava com \"module discovery walk: governance read view budget exceeded\": o limite de 10 000 entradas da varredura de módulos foi cruzado por 7 319 arquivos rastreados do submódulo `pose-dist` (1 652 bundles e 1 597 atestados de review, 525 specs, …) mais os 2 833 do próprio harne8; o `.pose` de cada projeto não contém módulo e cresce a cada fechamento, então uma instância grande nunca mais atualizaria seus índices. A mensagem era só o nome do orçamento.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-recovery-and-close-scope-consistency.md:141:- Result: registrado pela evidência de validação selada; revisão delegada independente concluída com `pose review conclude`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-index-recovery-and-close-scope-consistency.md:149:- [open] Fazer o gate de commit recusar, no modo estrito, um commit que muda um índice sem o descritor da geração. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:51:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-22-b28-pending-review-r1.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:76:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/suggest_review_regression_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:77:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-pose-b28r2-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:78:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-pose-b28r3-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:79:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-pose-b28r4-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:80:- created: .pose/results/b28r4-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:81:- created: .pose/results/b28r3-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:83:- created: .pose/results/b28r2-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:90:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-pose-b28-d7ebc300-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:91:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-pose-b28-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:92:- created: .pose/results/b28-d7ebc300-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:178:- [open] O doctor recomenda instalar uma extensão para uma regra ilegível. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:180:- [open] Dizer o alias e a origem explícitos também na saída humana de `pose suggest`. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:181:- [open] Aceitar na CLI MCP o alias de caixa (`Go`) que a CLI já aceita. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:182:- [open] Corrigir os executores de mutação das unidades b14/b15. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:183:- [open] Documentar o estado `unreadable` das referências de `pose suggest`. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:184:- [open] Classificar link quebrado de workflow/skill como perda e não como indisponibilidade. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:185:- [open] Ampliar o filtro da integração B28 para os consumidores novos. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:186:- [open] Diferenciar task-map ausente de ilegível na mensagem de `pose suggest`. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:187:- [open] Não recusar prosa válida que contém newline JSON escapado. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:188:- [open] Remover a menção a \"6.x\" do texto do dry-run de `pose migrate`. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-distributed-instructions-parity.md:189:- [open] Trocar o shell interpolado e a heurística de duas substrings dos executores `b14-mutations.py` e `b15-mutations.py`. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-knowledge-consumption-traceability.md:16:show when governed knowledge influences work and offer optional human-reviewed semantic retrieval.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-knowledge-consumption-traceability.md:28:- R2: Usage signals shall inform review without extending TTL automatically.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-knowledge-consumption-traceability.md:52:- Popularity can preserve stale knowledge unless owners still review it.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-knowledge-consumption-traceability.md:87:- R2 [satisfied] usage projection informs review without touching expires_at; check:test (TestKnowledgeUsageProjection)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-knowledge-consumption-traceability.md:112:  reviews — the projection informs but never extends TTL by design.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-knowledge-consumption-traceability.md:117:- [spawned: pose-governance-gate-activation] Cite knowledge refs from the feature/bugfix workflows and skills so citation becomes routine, then review usage in the first quarterly audit. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-10-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-atomic-start-adoption-cutoff.md:44:- R5: A start record under `.pose/starts/` shall be classified in the review subject as a governance record, so a spec started with `pose start --apply` can be sealed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-atomic-start-adoption-cutoff.md:62:Start status, review policy reader, effective governance, manuals.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-atomic-start-adoption-cutoff.md:69:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-atomic-start-adoption-cutoff.md:71:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-atomic-start-adoption-cutoff.md:72:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_start_record_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-project-identity-file.md:53:- The file is a governance path in the review subject, so changing the identity is reviewed.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-mcp-conductor-harness-trust-boundary-for-safe-validation-orchestration.md:22:   unreviewed local code execution, with no approval step and no isolation.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-mcp-conductor-harness-trust-boundary-for-safe-validation-orchestration.md:25:   guarantee) undesigned and untested until it's too late to review cheaply.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-mcp-conductor-harness-trust-boundary-for-safe-validation-orchestration.md:57:  `conductor_run_*` already delegates state to Conductor. The in-process\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-command-parity.md:25:`pose review record`, `pose review-check` or `pose close` — the exact gate\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-command-parity.md:98:- modified: .agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-command-parity.md:109:- **Multi-word commands are enumerated by hand.** `review record` and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-command-parity.md:169:  `new-knowledge` (pose-bugfix, pose-feature, pose-review), `report`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-command-parity.md:175:  `review record` and `review-check`. `skills-check --strict` reports 0/0.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-command-parity.md:219:- [done] The multi-word command list (`review record`, `assess snapshot`, …) is maintained by hand and under-reports when a new two-word verb appears — a guard failing quiet is the wrong direction. Consider deriving it from the CLI's own dispatch table at test time, which would also fix the same weakness in the manual parity check's command discovery. Done in `pose-parity-reads-the-cli-surface`: there is no table, so the dispatch is read from the CLI's source; it yields 13 groups where the list had 8, one of which (`roadmap`) is not a command. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-v7-4-1-version-alignment.md:23:`pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records` lets a scope that carries the signed legacy ledger `pose adopt` writes be sealed; Harne8 needs it to close `harne8-adopt-pose-v7-2-0`. One unreleased fragment, `fixed` and not breaking, makes it a patch release.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-obligation-projection.md:20:Provide one deterministic, read-only aggregation of obligations from readiness, review,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-obligation-projection.md:52:- R1: The aggregation shall not modify specs, reviews, state or policy; a test hashes the tree before and after.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-obligation-projection.md:178:Delivers the read-only projection with producers, coverage, correlation, snapshot and filters. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-artifact-provenance-ledger.md:7:depends_on: pose-hierarchical-review-closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-artifact-provenance-ledger.md:27:prose into reviewable provenance and supplies the artifact side of the combined\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-artifact-provenance-ledger.md:33:- Keep the spec as the reviewed source of artifact claims and generated indexes\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-artifact-provenance-ledger.md:154:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-artifact-provenance-ledger.md:191:- Add artifact policy under `.pose/` as reviewed source data; keep generated\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-artifact-provenance-ledger.md:271:- Context: A declaration is reviewable intent; Git is evidence of repository\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-artifact-provenance-ledger.md:318:- 2026-08-03, review remediation: made spec parsing independent of the process\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-artifact-provenance-ledger.md:330:- Failures: the first full-suite review found assessment mirror drift; the\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-artifact-provenance-ledger.md:353:  can use the deterministic backfill proposal and review ambiguous ownership\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-artifact-provenance-ledger.md:383:- Mature repositories need reviewed orphan-policy migration; warnings are not\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:2:title: A delegated reviewer is an adapter that turns a sealed bundle into a draft\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:8:# A delegated reviewer is an adapter that turns a sealed bundle into a draft\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:13:reviewer for pose-mcp specs, and the review of `pose-native-attestation-issuer`\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:14:was delegated to another vendor's agent (Codex, gpt-6.1-sol) through a\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:19:- the implementer wrote the reviewer's prompt, so the reviewed party steered\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:20:  the review;\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:21:- under declared assurance, `different-actor` is satisfied by the reviewer\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:23:  comment says so (`review_closeout.go`);\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:24:- nothing recorded the reviewer runs, so a rejection could be dropped by\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:25:  running the review again or switching models;\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:33:2. **An engine adapter**: POSE generates the review brief from the sealed\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:34:   bundle, runs a configured reviewer command on a disposable copy, and\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:36:3. **An action request only**: the engine opens a \"review by another actor\"\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:47:- **Brief from the bundle.** The review request is generated from the sealed\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:52:  (`.pose/policy/reviewers.json`); POSE ships examples for Codex and Claude\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:54:- **Disposable copy.** The reviewer runs on a worktree at the sealed commit;\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:57:  run record under `.pose/review-runs/` and the reviewer's conclusion. When\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:66:  review policy says so: criteria marked as requiring a person (risk\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:67:  acceptance, public contracts, or whatever the project chooses), reviewers\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:68:  in conflict, a reviewer asking for a business decision, or the run budget\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:74:  issuer; `different-actor` is read from that record, not from a reviewer\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:78:- **Opt-in.** A catalog capability, `delegated-review`, off by default.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:83:   its checks; a person is involved only where review policy escalates. The\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:86:   reviewer recording on their own as unverified.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:90:4. **Scope:** reviews, independent adjudications and smoke runs from the\n.pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md:96:  adopt `delegated-review`; until then it stays, documented as a declaration.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-locale-obligation-flags.md:26:Origin: the open follow-up of `pose-locale-coverage-contract` (crit medium, review 2026-10-10), prioritized by the maintainer on 2026-10-09. The gate treated `pose surface-check --strict` and `pose surface-check` as the same command, and only one of them is the doctrine.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-locale-obligation-flags.md:46:- Five skills differed when the comparison was first run: the pt-BR `pose-review` asked for `pose validate` \"proportional to risk\" where the source requires `pose validate --strict`, and the English `pose-feature`, `pose-knowledge`, `pose-recurrence-escalation` and `pose-spec-closeout` omitted obligation flags their translations taught. Each was aligned to the stricter or more explicit side.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-locale-obligation-flags.md:59:- modified: locales/pt-BR/.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-locale-obligation-flags.md:64:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-locale-obligation-flags.md:105:The locale coverage gate compares `command --strict|--apply|--seal` per code span in both directions. Five skills were aligned: pt-BR `pose-review` now requires `pose validate --strict`, and the English `pose-feature`, `pose-knowledge`, `pose-recurrence-escalation` and `pose-spec-closeout` name the obligation flags their translations already taught.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-locale-obligation-flags.md:109:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-seal-names-carried-forward-evidence.md:28:What it does not do is say so. A reviewer reading a sealed bundle sees a list of\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-seal-names-carried-forward-evidence.md:46:  reviewer's judgement, and it is judgement they could not previously make.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-seal-names-carried-forward-evidence.md:66:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go` — the seal-time warning\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-seal-names-carried-forward-evidence.md:71:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-seal-names-carried-forward-evidence.md:72:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-seal-names-carried-forward-evidence.md:75:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-seal-names-carried-forward-evidence.md:113:  cannot be regenerated against a head that moved past it. The reviewer needs to\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-seal-names-carried-forward-evidence.md:167:- [open] Carry the carried-forward warning into review verify, so it is visible when reading an attestation rather than only when sealing (owner:unowned crit:low review:2027-01-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:2:slug: pose-abm-progressive-review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:6:depends_on: pose-abm-review-soundness, pose-abm-review-authority, pose-abm-design-basis, pose-abm-structural-delta\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:10:delivers: governance:abm-progressive-review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:13:# Spec: Progressive review from explicit obligations\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressi