dation.json`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:279:the candidate `artifact-check --spec pose-abm-progressive-review --strict` exited 0\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:284:convergence) into `.pose/results/abm-progressive-review-validation.json`, and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:285:candidate `surface-check --spec pose-abm-progressive-review --strict --results`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:301:`surface-check --spec pose-abm-progressive-review --strict --results\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:302:.pose/results/abm-progressive-review-validation.json` passed: one target, seven\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:360:pose-abm-progressive-review --strict` passed against the policy's own results path\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:366:- `review auto-attest` reported five pendencies — compatibility, documentation,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:375:  the conclusion is the reviewer's answer, the ref says what was in front of them.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:379:`review verify` reports fresh, approved, zero blockers. `review-check` and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:380:`closeout-check` are terminal, and `close spec:pose-abm-progressive-review` applied\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:396:### Explicit review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:413:  contract; `review-plan` and `review-attestation` schemas publish the new fields as\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:428:- security: one finding, raised and fixed in this review. The protected baseline\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:437:  check. Also reviewed and found sound: reviewer-supplied mapping values are quoted\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:471:- R8 [satisfied] governance:abm-progressive-review evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:472:  check:abm-progressive-review-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:476:  published. Portal composition is harne8-abm-review-experience by this spec's scope.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:487:against overlays and author metadata, and a governance change is now reviewed under\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:493:review-experience by this spec's own scope. Every requirement then received the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:494:explicit review recorded above, and the security finding it raised was fixed before\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:499:All four increments are implemented, reviewed explicitly and closed through the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:509:`high-criticality-review` and `structural-materiality` ship installed and inert, as\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-progressive-review.md:510:the constraints require. The `proportional-review` milestone gate, the roadmap and\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-adapter-containment, pose-delegated-review-run-continuity, pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:14:# Spec: `pose delegate` is the one surface for delegated executions\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:20:Give every delegated execution one command tree, one vocabulary, one policy file and one run record, so a person and an agent start, inspect and continue a delegated run the same way whatever its purpose.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:24:Decided by the [delegation ADR](../adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md). The engine's delegated review already reserves attempts, contains the reviewer, continues interrupted runs and proves provenance, yet no review has run through it: execution operations are scattered across `pose review dispatch`, `resume` and `status`, beside the commands that govern the review subject, and the personal launchers that fill the gap stay in use. This spec builds the frame every later delegation spec plugs into.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:32:Routing between vendors (`pose-delegation-routing`); handoff (`pose-delegation-handoff`); detach, wait, heartbeat and live watch (`pose-delegated-review-completion-signal`, amended by the ADR); general tasks (`pose-delegation-task`); MCP (`pose-delegation-mcp`).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:38:- R1: `pose delegate` shall offer the purposes `review`, `adjudicate`, `smoke` and `task` and the lifecycle commands `ls`, `watch`, `wait`, `resume`, `handoff`, `cancel` and `agents`; with no argument it shall print its help, and an unknown subcommand shall exit 2.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:40:- R3: `review`, `adjudicate` and `smoke` shall run through the delivered dispatch path — sealed bundle or target, generated brief, disposable worktree, attempt ledger, containment — with `read` access; any other `--access` shall be refused with exit 2.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:42:- R5: `pose review dispatch`, `pose review resume` and `pose review status` shall keep their behaviour and exit codes, print one line on stderr naming the `pose delegate` replacement, and be absent from the help listing.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:44:- R7: `pose update` shall convert `reviewers.json` schema 1 into `delegation.json` schema 2 deterministically, each adapter becoming an agent whose command is its `read` template, and shall show the conversion in its preview; the engine shall read schema 1 while schema 2 is absent and shall refuse when both files exist.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:50:- R13: `pose delegate cancel <run>` shall stop the run through its supervisor and record it `failed` with the cause `cancelled`; the attempt shall stay consumed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:51:- R14: `pose delegate agents` shall list each configured agent with vendor, model, whether its CLI is on the path, and the reset instant of its last recorded usage limit.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:65:- Instances with `reviewers.json` keep working until they run `pose update`; the aliases stay for one minor version after this spec is released.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:87:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:89:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:90:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:91:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:92:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:93:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:94:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:97:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:98:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:99:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:107:- modified: docs-site/docs/review-and-trust.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:111:- capability:delegation-surface module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:115:New command tree `pose delegate`; `delegation.json` schema 2; normalized event schema 1; deprecated aliases.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:125:- [x] First independent review: changes requested (B01–B10, F01–F03), all addressed with regression tests that fail on the reviewed commit\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:126:- [x] Second independent review: changes requested (B02, B06, B07, B09 partial; N01–N02 new blockers; N03 follow-up), all addressed with regression tests that fail on the reviewed commit\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:127:- [x] Third independent review: changes requested (N01 partial; N04 follow-up, fixed in the same change), both addressed with regression tests that fail on the reviewed commit\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:128:- [x] Fourth independent review: changes requested (N05 new blocker; N04 residual follow-up, fixed in the same change), both addressed with regression tests that fail on the reviewed commit\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:129:- [x] Fifth independent review and native closeout: approved by agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review; N05 and residual N04 fixed, no remaining findings\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:135:- Minimal option: `pose review dispatch --kind`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:136:- Selected option: purposes as subcommands of `pose delegate`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:138:- Consequences: `pose review` stops starting runs\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:154:- Consequences: `.pose/review-private/active/` holds runtime markers; a marker whose owner is proven dead is reported, never cancelled\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:160:- Selected option: schema 2 accepts `{output}`, `{session}` and `{effort}` only as whole argv elements; a schema 1 adapter that interpolates one into an argument is not converted, and `pose update` warns and keeps `reviewers.json`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:184:- Selected option: archive the converted `reviewers.json` outside `.pose/policy` and name it in `migrated_from`; a run recorded before the conversion keeps its policy baseline when the directory, with the archived file in the place of `delegation.json`, reproduces the recorded digest and `delegation.json` is exactly the conversion of that archive\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:185:- Rationale: the conversion changes the policy's form, not its meaning, and R7 promises that recorded runs keep verifying; the baseline of every run is the digest of the whole policy directory, which the conversion necessarily changes. Found by the first independent review (B01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:193:- Rationale: R2 gives the flags one meaning across the tree, so a person or an agent can add `--agent` or `--label` to any command without learning which accept it. Found by the first independent review (B07)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:201:Each subcommand parses and rejects as specified; a review run through `pose delegate review` and through the alias produces identical records apart from `label` and `purpose`; a schema 1 fixture migrates to the expected schema 2 bytes and both files together are refused; a fake agent receives none of the listed variables; recorded Codex and Claude streams normalize to the same event sequence; `--dry-run` reserves nothing.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:224:Delivered milestone `surface` of roadmap `delegation`: the `pose delegate`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:225:command tree and vocabulary, review/adjudicate/smoke over the existing dispatch,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:229:versioned JSON. Deprecated review aliases retain their behavior and exit codes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:233:### Independent review and evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:235:Approved on 2026-10-26 by the maintainer-authorized reviewer\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:236:`agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review` (Codex/OpenAI), reviewing implementation\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:241:repository are unsigned. Another vendor performed this review; the declaration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:246:entries, with specific judgments on R1–R14 and D1–D8. Native `review verify`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:255:manuals and two docs-site pages were reviewed against runtime, with en/pt-BR\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:257:`capability:delegation-surface` at `pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:269:check summaries are retained locally under `.review-work/round5/`, as requested,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-surface.md:292:No new follow-up or unresolved review finding remains. All findings from the\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-manual-distribution-merge.md:172:- [spawned: pose-machinery-distribution-contract] Rules, workflows, templates and skills still reach an instance only under `pose upgrade --force`, which overwrites local edits wholesale. Machinery needs the same distinction between engine-owned and instance-owned content that the manuals now have, so a plain upgrade can deliver them safely. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-07)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-external-milestone-members.md:19:Let milestone closeout, review and readiness accept members qualified with\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-external-milestone-members.md:25:\"xref:proj.pose-dist/spec:pose-abm-review-soundness\"`: closeout, lifecycle,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-external-milestone-members.md:26:scope digest, review plan, bundle children and readiness all read each member\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-external-milestone-members.md:47:`review_closeout.go` (`milestoneMember`, `externalMemberDone`), `review_bundle.go`,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-external-milestone-members.md:48:`review_plan.go`, `readiness.go`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-external-milestone-members.md:52:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-external-milestone-members.md:53:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-external-milestone-members.md:54:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-external-milestone-members.md:70:- [x] Run the matrix, review and close.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-external-milestone-members.md:86:then from the review plan, then with `no immutable attributed change set`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-external-milestone-members.md:95:executor reviews were resealed and reattested.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-federated-external-milestone-members.md:106:Milestones owning another project's specs close, review and report readiness through federated acceptance, failing closed without a resolver.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-causality-closeout-adoption-cutoff.md:62:Review policy reader, bundle sealing, review plan overlay selection, effective governance, manuals.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-causality-closeout-adoption-cutoff.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-causality-closeout-adoption-cutoff.md:70:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-causality-closeout-adoption-cutoff.md:71:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:74:- R7: The payload change shall be recorded as an amendment to the sealed-review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:78:- The existing review suite passes.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:85:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go` — the sealed plan and criterion\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:87:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go` — tool scoping\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:88:- `.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md` — the payload\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:94:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:95:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:96:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:97:- modified: .pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:147:- Context: review found the implementation contradicted this spec's own\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:214:- R2 [satisfied] <reviewCriterionComponents resolves the criterion's profiles through the sealed selection and the blocker names the components; TestCriterionRejectsEvidenceFromAnotherComponent seeds a second delivery target and a foreign result, and asserts the rejection>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:216:- R4 [satisfied] <reviewToolEvidenceBlocker compares the evidence module against tool.Component through moduleMatchesTarget>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:218:- R6 [satisfied] <reviewCriterionEvidenceBlockers returns early when the criterion demands no class, asserted by TestCriterionWithNoDemandedClassIsNotScoped, which strips the classes from a criterion the plan really scopes and then checks the scope is still live for the same criterion with its classes; auto-attest uses pickScoped for criteria and tools, asserted by TestAutoAttestPicksEvidenceFromTheRightComponent validating its own output>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:219:- R7 [satisfied] <the sealed-review-bundles ADR carries a 2026-09-09 amendment stating the payload gains plan.selected_profiles, why re-reading the selection was rejected, the bounds of the rule and the compatibility consequence>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-evidence-scoped-to-component.md:238:- [done] Decide whether root-level evidence should satisfy a component-scoped criterion, or whether module coverage needs a stricter definition here. Decided in `pose-component-evidence-is-not-inherited-upward` (ADR amendment 2026-09-09): root keeps answering, a containing module keeps answering, and a directory inside the component stops answering for it — the upward prefix was partial coverage read as complete. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-12-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:2:slug: pose-review-approval-follows-children\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:6:depends_on: pose-review-subject-later-removal\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:11:delivers: capability:review-approval-follows-children\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:21:The integration approval of a milestone or roadmap stands only while the review of each child stands, and retained verification picks the bundle matching picks, whatever the seal times say.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:25:Independent review of `pose-review-subject-later-removal` found two faults in what eighteen milestone seals are about to rely on. A child rejected after its parent was approved leaves the parent `closed`, fresh and approved (SR-R1-05, high). A bundle that replaced another governs while inputs match, but after drift retention scans by seal time and can return the replaced one (SR-R1-07, medium).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:36:- Retiring recorded approvals: a parent recovers when its child's review does, with no reseal.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:42:- R1: Preparing a milestone or roadmap shall report a blocker for each child whose review does not stand: not approved, not fresh, with lost attestation history, or, when the parent's lifecycle is done, not closed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:43:- R2: Verification of a parent, current or retained, shall not report it approved while a child of its bundle does not stand, and shall name the child. Closeout and `pose review-check` shall agree. A store without a federated resolver cannot judge a federated manifest and retains as closeout does; with a resolver a changed manifest still stales the scope.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:45:- R4: Bundle selection shall honour replacement lineage everywhere a governing bundle is chosen — current and legacy coordinated matching, retention, the latest negative review, effective governance, the supersession delta and the governance replay: every replacement comes before what it replaces and takes the newest place of its chain, whatever the seal times, equal ones included. A `replaces` counts only between bundles of the same content.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:46:- R5: A replaced bundle's approval shall not be retained nor stop the search for a negative review; its negative review still counts.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:51:- A public verification, `review-check` or closeout verifies each scope at most once. The memo lives for that call only and is keyed by project and resolver.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:59:- A closed parent whose child's review no longer stands stops verifying approved, which is the point. The changelog says so.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:65:`internal/pose/review_bundle.go`, `internal/pose/review_closeout.go`, `internal/pose/review_reuse_provenance.go`, the manuals.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:69:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:70:- created: .pose/starts/pose-review-approval-follows-children.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:71:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-approval-follows-children.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:72:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.amendments.jsonl\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:73:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reuse_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:87:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_approval_follows_children_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:91:- capability:review-approval-follows-children module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:95:A parent's verification, review check and closeout report a child that no longer stands.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:102:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:118:- R1 [satisfied] capability:review-approval-follows-children evidence:integration check:review-approval-follows-children-integration test:TestParentApprovalFollowsAChildsRejection test:TestChildMustBeClosedUnderADoneParent report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:5894a604f0700f63fda71578de62eb000035a6f9 — Preparation blocks on a child that does not stand.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:119:- R2 [satisfied] check:review-approval-follows-children-integration test:TestParentApprovalFollowsAChildsRejection test:TestParentApprovalRecoversWithItsChild test:TestParentApprovalFollowsLostChildHistory test:TestParentStandsWithoutAResolverOverAFederatedChild report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:5894a604f0700f63fda71578de62eb000035a6f9 — Verification, review-check and closeout refuse a parent over such a child and name it; it recovers with the child.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:120:- R3 [satisfied] check:review-approval-follows-children-integration test:TestRoadmapApprovalFollowsItsDescendants report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:5894a604f0700f63fda71578de62eb000035a6f9 — A roadmap does not stand over a milestone whose spec does not.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:121:- R4 [satisfied] check:review-approval-follows-children-integration test:TestReviewBundleLineage test:TestRetentionHonoursReplacementLineage test:TestLegacyCoordinatedMatchingFollowsLineage test:TestSealedBranchLineage test:TestForgedReplacementRetiresNothing test:TestEffectiveGovernanceFollowsLineage test:TestGovernanceReplaySelectsAsVerificationDoes report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:5894a604f0700f63fda71578de62eb000035a6f9 — One lineage order serves every reader of a governing bundle.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:122:- R5 [satisfied] check:review-approval-follows-children-integration test:TestReplacedApprovalIsNotRetained test:TestReplacementsRejectionIsNotOverriddenByWhatItReplaced test:TestReplacedRejectionStillCounts test:TestLatestNegativeSkipsAReplacedApproval report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:5894a604f0700f63fda71578de62eb000035a6f9 — A replaced approval is not retained and stops no search; its negative review counts.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:123:- R6 [satisfied] check:review-approval-follows-children-integration test:TestChildCycleEndsInARefusal report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:5894a604f0700f63fda71578de62eb000035a6f9 — A sealed cycle ends in a named refusal.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-review-approval-follows-children.md:129:A milestone's or roadmap's approval now stands only while each child's review does, in preparation, verification, `review-check` and closeout, transitively, and recovers with the child with no reseal. One lineage order serves every reader of a governing bundle, an edge counts only between bundles of the same content, and a sealed cycle ends in a refusal. Old and new verification agree on all 22 real milestone and roadmap scopes, `check --strict` passes, and the 18 milestones about to be sealed prepare with no blocker. Independently reviewed by Codex over four rounds.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-roadmap-gate-scopes-milestones-and-external-members.md:25:is terminal with a fresh approved review, yet `pose close` refuses it with\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-roadmap-gate-scopes-milestones-and-external-members.md:37:external member keeps every federated blocker (status, trust, source review,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-roadmap-gate-scopes-milestones-and-external-members.md:43:review eligibility of `pose close`, or the federated traversal.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-roadmap-gate-scopes-milestones-and-external-members.md:66:`review_closeout.go` (milestone close) and focused tests.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-roadmap-gate-scopes-milestones-and-external-members.md:72:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-roadmap-gate-scopes-milestones-and-external-members.md:92:- [x] Run module checks, review and close.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-roadmap-gate-scopes-milestones-and-external-members.md:97:`pose close` requires an approved review before any gate, so the regressions\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-roadmap-gate-scopes-milestones-and-external-members.md:116:`review_closeout.go`, and its baseline was lowered accordingly.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-roadmap-gate-scopes-milestones-and-external-members.md:121:self-attest. The commit superseded the foundation reviews again, since\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-roadmap-gate-scopes-milestones-and-external-members.md:122:`surface_check.go` and `review_closeout.go` are artifacts of those specs; the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-26-pose-roadmap-gate-scopes-milestones-and-external-members.md:137:`pose close` still requires an approved review before any gate, so the close\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-requirement-trace-contract.md:13:intent-to-closure chain. Constraint: links must be explicit and reviewable —\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-requirement-trace-contract.md:20:   is invisible in review diffs of the spec itself.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-requirement-trace-contract.md:25:   one reviewable document, diff-friendly, offline, parsed by the same\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-requirement-trace-contract.md:46:  tool is an additive catalog change (golden regenerated and reviewed per\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-requirement-trace-contract.md:57:  point — the reviewable link is the artifact.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-requirement-trace-contract.md:59:  review owns quality, the gate owns existence and consistency. The legacy\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:25:Three scripts that CI and local validation run (`tests/quickstart/first-governed-loop.sh`, `tests/journeys/install-and-upgrade.sh`, `tests/import/migration-guides.sh`) create directories with `mktemp -d` and never remove them. One of them is the 42 MB `pose` binary they build. On a maintainer's machine, where `/tmp` is a RAM-backed tmpfs, 275 such directories (about 7 GB) accumulated within hours of consecutive validations and review runs, filled the quota and, with the memory they took, contributed to background reviews being stopped for lack of memory. The system's age-based cleanup (10 days) cannot keep up with that rate.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:41:- R3: A check shall fail when a script under `tests/`, `scripts/`, `examples/` or `install.sh` that calls `mktemp` neither uses the helper in its plain form (sourced and initialized on their own lines before the first `mktemp`) nor is pinned by the SHA-256 of the whole file after a reviewer read its own EXIT trap, so a new script cannot forget the cleanup and a pinned script cannot change without a new review. The check is a regression guard for that omission, not an analysis of arbitrary shell, and it shall be able to fail: it shall be shown failing against the scripts as they were.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:70:`tests/hygiene/temp-cleanup.sh` checks, statically, two rules over every tracked script that mentions `mktemp`. A script not in `tests/hygiene/temp-cleanup.pins` must use the helper in its plain form: `tests/lib/tempdir.sh` sourced on a line of its own, then `pose_test_tmp_init` on a line of its own, both at the start of the line and both before the first `mktemp`. The ten scripts that clean up with an EXIT trap of their own (`install.sh`, `scripts/verify.sh`, `examples/demo/record.sh` and seven test scripts) are listed in the pins file with the SHA-256 of the whole file: a change to one fails the check until a reviewer has read its allocation and trap again and run `bash tests/hygiene/temp-cleanup.sh --repin`, and a pin whose script no longer calls `mktemp` is stale. Dynamically, it checks that the helper leaves a sandbox `TMPDIR` empty after success, a failed assertion, an error under `set -e`, an unset variable, TERM and INT (delivered to a probe started with default signal dispositions, whose exit status 130 or 143 proves the signal ended it), including read-only and `0000` entries, each case proving by a marker that its setup ran, and shown failing against the helper with the previous `chmod -R u+w`; that a script without the helper does leave its directory (so the checks can fail); and that the quickstart script, run with a sandbox `TMPDIR`, leaves it empty. It runs in CI and as a required integration check of the matrix.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:72:What the static rules do not claim: they read lines, not shell. A new script that follows the plain form and then defeats the helper with unusual syntax (a word split by a continuation, `declare -i TMPDIR`, a conditional init written across lines) passes them; the helper's own behaviour is established by the dynamic cases and by review of each new script. Eleven rounds of independent review showed that deciding cleanup from the text of arbitrary shell does not converge, so the check was reduced to the omission it can decide: forgetting the helper, and changing a pinned script unreviewed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:79:- [x] Strict validation, different-actor review and closeout.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:99:Independent review round 13 on `534653c6` passed global strict validation (137/137), explicit `pose-mcp` strict validation (134/134), `go vet ./...`, `go test ./... -count=1`, ShellCheck at warning severity, and `TestLocalVerifyCoversCurrentCIGates`. The registered `test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files-integration` producer executes `tests/hygiene/temp-cleanup.sh`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:101:Independent helper probes reached setup markers, removed restricted 0500/0400/0000 descendants, and cleaned up on success, assertion failure, set-e error, unset variable, INT (130) and TERM (143). Old-permissions and missing-signal-handler controls make the gate fail. The three real scripts leave their caller TMPDIR empty with absolute paths, relative paths, CDPATH unset or exported as dot, and the reviewed binary/previous options.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:103:The revised R3 gate rejects original scripts, seven invalid helper forms in a newly tracked script, changes to each of the ten pinned files, deleted/no-longer-allocating pinned scripts and a nonexistent pin. A valid helper form and an explicitly reviewed re-pin pass. All review mutations were restored. The original quickstart without the helper leaves a directory, proving the empty-TMPDIR check can fail.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:105:The demo succeeds and cleans up after a failed build. The actual clean-environment Docker measurement executes the installed pose 7.4.1 and staged quickstart/helper successfully (12.486 seconds for the measured command path), leaving its host TMPDIR empty. A Docker removal failure no longer skips host cleanup; the previous measurement script leaks under the same injected failure. Compact results and hashes of full external outputs are recorded in [independent review evidence](../results/test-scripts-temp-cleanup-independent-review.json).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:119:The helper owns an absolute temporary root, exports TMPDIR and removes restricted descendants on the exits and signals required by R1. The three scripts adopt it without changing their assertions. CI, local verification and the validation matrix execute the hygiene gate. The revised R3 enforces the plain helper form or a reviewed whole-file SHA-256 pin; the demo uses one root, and the clean-environment producer stages the helper and survives Docker cleanup failure.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:121:Maintainer-authorized independent review by `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review` (Codex/OpenAI, a different vendor from the Claude/Anthropic implementer) approved round 13. Identity and separation are declared; pose-dist attestations are unsigned. Bundle `rvb-6167567bf3fa6ac4` and attestation `rva-5358c584e2a8bd4f` bind the review. Native review verification, guarded close, strict spec lint and strict check passed. See the [review report](../reports/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-temp-cleanup-review.md) and [compact evidence](../results/test-scripts-temp-cleanup-independent-review.json).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:129:R3 deliberately reads lines rather than analyzing arbitrary shell. Unusual syntax or later helper sabotage can pass the plain-form rule; each new script and re-pin requires reviewer inspection. A pin detects whole-file changes and does not authenticate who reviewed them. The `agent:independent-` prefix remains an engine-required declaration until `pose-delegated-review-run-provenance` replaces it, rather than signed session provenance.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-17-pose-test-scripts-remove-their-temp-files.md:133:No outstanding corrective follow-up remains for this delivery. New scripts and changed pins continue through the review obligations of R3.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-proportional-next-action.md:33:- R2: Apresentar separadamente obrigação de pessoa, review/judgment de agente competente, input, operação externa/ambiente e orientação advisory. Advisory não deve aparecer como gate obrigatório; waiting em fase futura não deve causar interrupção atual. Preservar IDs, satisfaction, effects e coverage do domínio; nenhum blocker conhecido no recorte não é autorização universal.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-proportional-next-action.md:39:- R8: Qualificar decisão humana material, review por agente independente, input tipado e operação externa com evidência adequada em jornadas CLI/MCP: retomada ocorre na fase/target correto, negativos permanecem, policy exceptions têm pergunta/opções e nenhuma answer aplica policy ou publica silenciosamente. Encaminhamento de review usa capability/fulfillment quando efetivamente disponível; ausência tem diagnóstico, não pessoa obrigatória por fallback.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-proportional-next-action.md:53:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-proportional-next-action.md:59:- modified: .pose/workflows/review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-proportional-next-action.md:90:| V2 — Agente reviewer, pessoa requerida, advisory e fase futura | Destinatário/executor/efeito corretos; nenhum pedido humano cosmético ou interrupção indevida. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-proportional-next-action.md:95:| V7 — Decisão humana/review por agente/input/external operation em CLI/MCP | Retomada pertinente com prova e outcomes corretos; exceptions por policy, sem apply oculto. |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-3-release-readiness.md:6:depends_on: retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-3-release-readiness.md:19:Publish 6.0.3 so that the precedence fix for retained reviews ships as an\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-3-release-readiness.md:130:it, since Tasks is part of what its review sealed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-review-run-continuity\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:12:delivers: capability:delegated-run-continuity\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:15:# Spec: A delegated review that is interrupted is resumed, not restarted\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:21:Let a delegated review that stopped before it finished (the reviewer's usage limit was reached, the process timed out or died, the host was lost) continue from where it stopped, on the same sealed commit and brief, as one attempt, instead of being restarted from nothing or mistaken for a completed review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:25:Origin: the B06 consolidation reviews (2026-10-17). A review of a large diff takes tens of minutes of reviewer time. The reviewer's usage limit was reached during the programme, and the work was picked up by hand: the session was resumed with a personal launcher flag once the maintainer reported that the limit had reset, and nobody could say whether the half-finished run counted against the attempt budget or as a rerun. The engine knows none of this: `pose-delegated-review-dispatch` records an interruption as a failed run, and `pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger` would refuse \"rerun without reason\" on a bundle whose only run was interrupted. The cost of an interruption should be the time to the reset, not the review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:29:Reuses the run record, the attempt reservation and the exclusive publisher of the ledger and state-consistency work; adds no runner. Vendor-specific behaviour (how a session is named, how a limit is worded) lives in the adapter declaration, never in the engine. Nothing here makes an interrupted run a review. Implementation authorized by continuation on 2026-10-25, baseline `3fa69b6`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:33:Resuming across a changed sealed bundle (that is a new attempt, carrying prior findings: `pose-delegated-review-round-protocol`); choosing a different vendor on the maintainer's behalf; waiting for a limit that has no stated reset.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:40:- R2: An adapter shall declare, in `.pose/policy/reviewers.json`, how its limit is recognised (exit codes and output patterns, and how the reset instant is read), how its session identifier is captured, and its resume command template. An adapter that declares none shall never have an interruption classified as `usage-limit`, and its interrupted runs shall be reported `unknown` and not resumable.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:41:- R3: `pose review resume <run>` shall continue a resumable run on a worktree at the same sealed commit, with the same brief (digest compared), the same adapter and the vendor session captured by the interrupted run, and shall record the continuation as a new run linked `resumes: <run>` under the same attempt.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:44:- R6: The draft and findings of an interrupted run shall be preserved in the run record by digest and disclosed as partial, and shall never be accepted as the review or counted as a rejection; only the draft of the run that reaches `completed` is the review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:45:- R7: `pose review resume <run> --wait-until-reset[=<max>]` shall sleep until the recorded reset instant (plus a bounded jitter) and then resume, shall never poll the vendor, and shall refuse when there is no recorded reset or the reset is later than `<max>`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:47:- R9: `pose review status` shall show, for every interrupted run, its cause, whether it is resumable, the reset instant and the time left to it; `pose doctor` shall report an attempt whose last run is `interrupted` and not resumed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:67:Run-state model and the supervisor's classification, adapter policy reader, `review resume`, `review status`, ledger accounting of resumes, doctor and insights.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:71:- created: .pose/adr/2026-10-25-continue-delegated-runs-under-one-immutable-attempt.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:76:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:79:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:80:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:90:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:91:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:92:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:93:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:94:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:95:- created: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/review_run_continuity_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:96:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:97:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:98:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:99:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:100:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:106:- capability:delegated-run-continuity module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:110:New run states and fields; new `review resume` subcommand; additions to `reviewers.json` (`limit`, `session`, `resume`).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:124:- ADR: [Continue under one immutable attempt](../adr/2026-10-25-continue-delegated-runs-under-one-immutable-attempt.md)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:125:- Knowledge: knowledge:pose-b07-implementation, knowledge:adr-sealed-review-bundles-review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:128:- Rationale: a reason-bearing rerun is exactly what the ledger exists to make rare and visible; an interruption is not the reviewer's verdict and must not be priced like one\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:136:- Rationale: independence is evidence about who reviewed; changing reviewer silently changes the evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:137:- Consequences: a limit can stop a review until the reset or a human decision\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-run-continuity.md:175:Filesystem/Git anchors remain trusted. Private session loss prevents recovery. A claim without a captured run/result remains explicit pending evidence, not an automatic host-loss recovery or permission to relaunch. No review authority, vendor identity authentication, new runner, policy adoption or adapter containment is introduced.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-closeout-names-the-missing-trailer.md:60:`internal/pose/review_bundle.go`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-closeout-names-the-missing-trailer.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-closeout-names-the-missing-trailer.md:83:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-closeout-names-the-missing-trailer.md:111:With no attributed change set the bundle reports that cause alone, with its fix: the `POSE-Spec:` line, `pose index` and `pose artifact-check`. The evidence gap that follows from it is no longer a second reason, as issue #208 asked. The test was seen failing with both messages on the previous code. A bundle with no change set stays unsealable, and a milestone of external members keeps its evidence gate. Independently reviewed by Codex in four rounds, with no blocker.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-01-pose-closeout-names-the-missing-trailer.md:119:- [covered: pose-evidence-gate-means-validation] F1: For a spec with a change set, `assess-design` evidence fills the list, so the empty-evidence blocker does not establish that validation ran. Decide whether it should distinguish them (review R2-F9).\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-reserve-delegated-attempts-before-launch-and-witness-immutable-runs.md:1:# ADR: Reserve delegated attempts before launch and witness immutable runs\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-reserve-delegated-attempts-before-launch-and-witness-immutable-runs.md:4:Accepted (2026-10-25), spec `pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger`.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-reserve-delegated-attempts-before-launch-and-witness-immutable-runs.md:7:Existing runs are content-addressed, but deletion leaves no trace in a scan of surviving files, and a preview's cached run count races another dispatch. B14 provides the exclusive synced publisher. The accepted delegated adapter ADR separates drafts from verified attestations; B17/B19 own signatures and governed conclusions, and run continuity is a following spec.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-reserve-delegated-attempts-before-launch-and-witness-immutable-runs.md:10:Before launching a valid dispatch, reserve an immutable ordinal slot per bundle under `.pose/review-attempts/`, using authoritative PublishFile ExpectAbsent. The content-addressed attempt ID includes a nonce; one contender wins a slot, losers refuse without launching or retrying. Re-read current runs and reservations at execution, enforce per-adapter quota including reservations, and require a bounded explicit reason whenever any completed run exists for the unchanged bundle, across adapters/kinds. An incomplete reservation blocks another attempt and is never auto-deleted or declared completed. An immutable result receipt links its final run after dispatch finishes. No mutable in-flight state or lock-order dependency is introduced; crashes remain explicit incomplete records for the continuity spec.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-reserve-delegated-attempts-before-launch-and-witness-immutable-runs.md:12:Before publishing a run/transcript, publish its immutable content-hash witness under `.pose/review-run-ledger/`. Use the same exclusive synced publisher for all three files; retries of identical bytes are idempotent, conflicting bytes refuse. A witness whose run or transcript is missing/corrupt is a visible incomplete history, not discarded. Validate record bounds and identities before reading; bounded inventories refuse rather than truncate. Legacy schema-1 runs stay readable without new fields or invented receipts. New optional fields do not change their historic identity.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-reserve-delegated-attempts-before-launch-and-witness-immutable-runs.md:19:Breaking stricter rerun admission; add --reason without changing existing positional API callers (optional trailing reason). Failed attempts consume quota; incomplete reservations require explicit inspection. Existing legacy records remain declared history. No journal cleanup, silent repair, proof fabrication or infinite retry. Rejected alternatives: surviving-file scans lose deletions; holding a lock through a long reviewer process leaves brittle ownership; a mutable counter loses crash evidence; automatic migration would invent past reservations. Future continuity reuses attempt IDs/receipts rather than introducing another quota.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-checks-route-to-the-runtime-by-default.md:20:Com o runtime do worktree rodando, compatível e disposto, `review-check`, `closeout-check`, `artifact-check` e `surface-check` rodam nele sem o chamador pedir, com a saída e o código de saída de sempre e o fallback standalone.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-checks-route-to-the-runtime-by-default.md:24:O runtime só atende quem usa `pose runtime run`; o ganho (cerca de 25 s para cerca de 10 s no `review-check`) não chega a quem digita `pose review-check`. A decisão de rotear por padrão toca o contrato de cada comando e a saída com cor num terminal.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-lint-validates-remediation-references.md:3:status: abandoned\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-lint-validates-remediation-references.md:22:Report a malformed `remediates:` value when the spec is linted, not only when its review bundle is sealed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-lint-validates-remediation-references.md:32:- R1: `pose lint-spec` shall validate each `remediates:` entry with the parser the review bundle uses and fail with the expected form (`spec:<slug>@<category>`) and the accepted categories.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-lint-validates-remediation-references.md:33:- R2: `pose review bundle --seal` shall keep its own check.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-lint-validates-remediation-references.md:48:- Decision: abandon the spec.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-init-is-install.md:26:Walked for the 7.0.0 review: `pose init` in an empty repository creates fifteen empty directories and says \"Run: pose check\"; that check fails with seven errors and `pose new-spec` fails with \"template not found\". The README's first delivery starts with `pose init --wizard --yes`, so a person following it from a bare repository gets a broken instance. Part of roadmap pose-v7-onboarding-and-consolidation (milestone entry-and-update).\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:2:slug: pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-conclusions\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:12:delivers: capability:review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:15:# Spec: The review brief states the rules the conclusion is checked against\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:21:A delegated reviewer that follows the brief writes a conclusion the attestation preflight accepts, whichever agent runs it.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:25:Reviews by Claude Opus 5.5 were refused four times by the preflight although the review itself was sound: judgment criteria passed without a conclusion, evidence given as file and line, a criterion disposed as a finding without the id of a filed finding, a structural fact answered nowhere, tools answered `not-run`, a disposition that does not exist, with the required `artifact-check` and `surface-check` never run because the profile allowed no shell, and, once it could run them, tool evidence given as a bare command line where the engine wants `<class>:<ref>` and a sealed ref of the classes `surface-check` lists. The brief of `review-brief/3` named only `rationale` for not-applicable, `<class>:<ref>` for evidence and no `mappings` at all. Codex had stumbled on the same rules earlier in this repository and learned them from notes the implementer carried between rounds, and it reads `AGENTS.md` and the skills of the checkout, which `claude --safe-mode` does not. The gap is the brief, not the agent.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:31:- The reviewer's access does not widen beyond read-only commands.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:36:- Giving the reviewer a way to write, assess or validate.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:42:- R1: The brief of the current template shall state, for a run asked to conclude, each rule the four functions of the attestation preflight that judge a draft's criteria, tools, findings and evidence check before it records the conclusion (`validateBundleAttestationWith`, `reviewCriterionEvidenceBlockers`, `evaluateReviewToolCoverageIn`, `reviewToolEvidenceBlocker`): a passed judgment criterion carries a rationale; the evidence of a passed criterion is one of the refs listed under Sealed evidence; a criterion disposed as a finding carries the id of a finding of the draft; structural facts are answered as mappings by the criterion that asks for them; a not-applicable carries a rationale and is refused where the bundle seals evidence of the class the criterion asks for; every required criterion and tool is answered; a tool disposition is passed, failed, not-used or deferred, a required tool is run and passed, a recommended tool not run is not-used with a rationale, the evidence of a tool is a class:ref (a sealed ref of a class the tool lists, otherwise command: and the command run), and an approving draft leaves no finding open (each is a follow-up with action, owner and review_by, or the draft requests changes); and a draft that breaks one is refused whole.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:43:- R2: A test shall tie each message those four functions can refuse a conclusion with to the words of the brief that state its rule, or exempt it with the reason a reviewer cannot break it, so that a rule added to the preflight without a sentence in the brief fails the build.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:44:- R3: The template shall be versioned: `review-brief/7` is current (it adds the refusal of a draft that dispenses with every required criterion, and `/6` added the severities a follow-up can be accepted at, the deferred answer of a tool that needs the review complete, the component scoping of evidence, what a mapping's basis is and the one line outside the block that is read), `review-brief/5` (the identifiers of the findings a later round accounts for), `/4` and `/3` still render exactly as before, so a run briefed with it still verifies, resumes and concludes.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:45:- R4: The delegation profile of the Claude reviewer shall allow, in its fresh, resumed and resumed-read commands, the required tools of a review plan (`pose artifact-check`, `surface-check`, `review-check`, `closeout-check`) and `git status` and `git ls-files`, and no verb that writes or runs a program: `pose assess`, `pose validate`, any `pose` verb that records, `git commit|push|add|checkout|reset`, `go build|install`, and the verbs whose flags write a file or run one (`git log|diff|show --output`, `go test -exec -c -o`, `go vet -vettool`, `pose lint-spec --json-out`), which a prefix allow-list cannot exclude by flag.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:54:- The allowed commands are the required tools of the review plan and two Git reads that take no flag that writes. The profile pre-approves those commands; Claude Code also runs, without asking, the commands it classifies as read-only itself (`cat`, `ls`, `find`, `git diff`, `git log`), and refuses a write (`touch` was refused in a probe). A prefix allow-list cannot exclude a flag, so a verb with a write or exec flag is not pre-approved; the reviewer reads the code with its read tools and relies on the sealed evidence for tests. The run safety record states that the worktree is not isolated from the filesystem, so no containment is claimed.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:58:- Runs briefed with `review-brief/3` conclude as before. New runs are briefed with `/4`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:64:`internal/pose/review_brief.go`, `internal/pose/review_conclusions.go`, `.pose/policy/delegation.json`, the manual.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:68:- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:69:- created: .pose/starts/pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:70:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:74:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:75:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:76:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_versions_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:78:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:87:- capability:review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:91:The review brief template moves from `review-brief/3` to `review-brief/7` (`/4` stated the rules, `/5` the identifiers of prior findings, `/6` the accepted-risk severities and four more, `/7` that a draft cannot dispense with every required criterion); the reviewer profile `claude-opus-5-5` allows the required tools of a review plan and two Git reads.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:95:- [x] Find why the Claude reviewer's drafts were refused and the Codex reviewer's were not\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:98:- [x] Allow the read-only commands of a review to the Claude profile\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:100:- [ ] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:106:- Minimal option: keep telling each reviewer in the note file\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:114:- Minimal option: leave the Claude reviewer without a shell\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:116:- Rationale: a reviewer that cannot run anything cites file and line, which the preflight refuses, and cannot reproduce the tests it is asked to judge; Codex runs under a read-only sandbox and can\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:131:- R1 [satisfied] test:TestTheBriefStatesEveryRuleThePreflightEnforces check:review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:138:- The brief states the rules in words; it does not validate a draft before the run ends. A reviewer that ignores it is still refused by the preflight, as before.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md:142:### Isolation of the secondary agents, reviewed at the e\n... 341438 bytes omitted ...\no, sem engine paralelo. Confrontar regra atual de exclusividade por spec e aliases antes de escolher outra identidade; não admitir segunda atribuição por novo registro de tentativa. Fixar sintaxe de seleção e contrato do manifest com compatibility/migration preview antes de start, conforme [ADR proposto](../adr/2026-10-14-release-temporal-evidence-and-attempt-lineage.md) e knowledge:adr-release-temporal-evidence-review. Não copiar requirements inteiros para outro ledger, nem impor policy/gates retrospectivos.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-release-scope-selection-and-exclusivity.md:74:- Proposal: [Temporal evidence and attempt lineage](../adr/2026-10-14-release-temporal-evidence-and-attempt-lineage.md), status Proposed; knowledge:adr-release-temporal-evidence-review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-release-scope-selection-and-exclusivity.md:91:| V5 — Preview seguido de mudança da fila/authority ou prepare concorrente | Revalidação/CAS; conflito e efeitos divulgados, sem overwrite. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-release-scope-selection-and-exclusivity.md:93:| V7 — CLI/MCP, legacy queue e history/migration preview | Mesmo domínio/scope e compatibility deliberada, sem reescrita de cut. |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-release-recovery-verification.md:205:- [open] The liveness check verifies that the installer downloads and the binary runs, but not the checksum or the Sigstore signature of what it downloaded; a daily job that also verified identity would be stronger. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/adr/2026-10-02-release-version-source-is-declared-by-the-project.md:34:describes as \"update and review the authoritative version\".\n.pose/adr/2026-10-02-release-version-source-is-declared-by-the-project.md:39:and updates it in reviewed work before planning, as the workflow already says. The\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:19:1. Embedding conditional contributor reminders into key AI agent skills (`pose-bugfix`, `pose-review`, `pose-spec-closeout`, `pose-recurrence-escalation`, `pose-feature`) and core workflows (`bugfix.md`, `review.md`, `feature.md`, `refactor.md`) in English and Brazilian Portuguese (`pt-BR`).\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:45:- R5: Key skills (`pose-bugfix`, `pose-review`, `pose-spec-closeout`, `pose-recurrence-escalation`, `pose-feature`) shall include explicit guidance instructing agents to stage synthetic reproductions under `.pose/contributions/` if Contributor Mode is active.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:46:- R6: Core task workflows (`bugfix.md`, `review.md`, `feature.md`, `refactor.md`) shall document the contributor feedback step.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:71:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:74:- `.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:80:- `.pose/workflows/review.md`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:101:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:103:- modified: .agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:108:- modified: locales/pt-BR/.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:113:- modified: .pose/workflows/review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:117:- modified: locales/pt-BR/.pose/workflows/review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:127:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:132:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.pose/workflows/review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:136:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-contributor-mode-workflow-and-cli-hints.md:141:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/.pose/workflows/review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-06-pose-project-binding-consistency.md:25:The release review found that setting POSE_DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID skips conflicting entries in POSE_PROJECT_ROOTS. Setup separately reads only the project file, so it can describe a conflicting configuration as ready. Both violate the identity spec's refusal contract.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-06-pose-project-binding-consistency.md:29:Preserve agreeing declarations and environment-only identities. Reuse the existing resolver; no identity migration. Context consulted: knowledge:multirepo-review-continuation.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys.md:13:# Spec: Say when a review policy key is not read\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys.md:18:Report a key in the review policy that the engine does not model, recovering\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys.md:22:`pose-adoption-stamp-stays-readable` made the review policy decoder ignore keys\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys.md:53:- R1: `pose doctor` shall report any top-level key in `.pose/policy/review.json`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys.md:67:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go` — the derived key list\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys.md:76:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys.md:158:- R1 [satisfied] <doctor's review.policy-keys compares the raw document's top-level keys against ReviewPolicyKnownKeys; the test asserts both misspellings are named>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys.md:165:  `reviewer_independence` is not caught.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys.md:167:  reads; this covers the review policy alone.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-doctor-reports-unread-policy-keys.md:175:- [done] Extend the unread-key finding to the delivery, artifact and capability policies, which have the same silent-default exposure. Done in `pose-policy-keys-and-release-surface-coverage`, and to docs, release and state as well — seven policies, keys derived from the structs, with a check that fails if a shipped policy is neither held to its keys nor exempted in writing. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-12-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-open-backlog-reconciliation.md:7:depends_on: pose-review-assurance-disclosure\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-open-backlog-reconciliation.md:54:- R1: Every remaining requirement of the twelve non-terminal specs shall be classified as implementation, evidence, review, acceptance, adoption or external operation, with the source consulted.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-open-backlog-reconciliation.md:56:- R3: Each open follow-up shall be classified as material implementation, evidence review/acceptance, adoption/pilot, external or human operation, accepted/deferred residual, duplicate or satisfaction candidate, or missing intent/owner.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-open-backlog-reconciliation.md:87:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-authority.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-open-backlog-reconciliation.md:92:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-open-backlog-reconciliation.md:95:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-review-assurance-disclosure.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-open-backlog-reconciliation.md:105:- Over-closing to shrink numbers; guarded by evidence-plus-authority rule and review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-open-backlog-reconciliation.md:128:Read each spec and its evidence; record per-requirement classification; review the\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-open-backlog-reconciliation.md:164:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-11-the-cli-has-one-rendering-layer-and-its-printed-lines-are-a-contract.md:131:- Positive: presentation becomes one reviewable surface with one vocabulary; a\n.pose/adr/2026-09-11-the-cli-has-one-rendering-layer-and-its-printed-lines-are-a-contract.md:136:  review diligence.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:2:slug: pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:12:delivers: capability:claude-sandboxed-review\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:40:- R4: Seleção é exclusiva de review, mantém compatibilidade na ausência do perfil e aplica a mesma contenção na retomada; comandos inválidos são recusados antes da execução.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:44:Adicionar `review_profile.command` e `review_profile.resume_command` opcionais por agente. Projetar somente no adaptador de review; clonar Resume antes de substituir seu comando. A policy atual adota o perfil Claude com sandbox obrigatório e Bash sem Edit/Write. O wrapper deriva scratch privado do output do motor, configura Go/TMPDIR e nega escrita no cwd selado e no Git comum físico. O motor prepara apenas diretórios vazios de staging Claude no checkout descartável antes do snapshot; arquivos continuam sujeitos à mesma checagem. A limpeza Go fica dentro do sandbox. O módulo é de criticidade high. Assessment de 2026-11-12: 114333 LOC de produção, 109213 de testes, um TODO; conteúdo reaproveitado. knowledge:delegated-conclusions-round4 orienta preservar recusas e provas, sem transformar task em atestação.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:48:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:49:- created: .pose/adr/2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:50:- created: .pose/starts/pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:54:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:55:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:57:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/claude_sandboxed_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:58:- created: .pose/reports/claude-review-sandbox-qualification.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:59:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:67:- capability:claude-sandboxed-review module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:71:Schema 2 ganha `review_profile` opt-in. Perfil ausente não muda o adaptador; parsers antigos estritos recusam a chave. Review continua com acesso read ao sujeito e scratch descartável para execução. Não ampliar as capacidades declaradas do backend trusted-process.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:86:- Selected option: perfil específico de review, conforme ADR `2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:94:Executar obrigatoriamente as camadas abaixo, em série nas operações que capturam Git/índices. Fakes comprovam seleção/recusa, nunca isolamento do SO. Rollback: retirar `review_profile` explicitamente da policy e reverter a extensão opcional; não reescrever runs nem tratar revisão restrita como reexecução de testes.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:98:| Seleção review, compatibilidade task/adjudicate/smoke e resume sem mutação | `LC_ALL=C go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run 'TestSandboxedReview' -count=1` | Seleção correta, ausência preservada, inválidos recusados e ambos comandos protegidos |\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:100:| Linux real, scratch permitido, source/sentinel/Git recusados, subprocessos | `pose delegate task /tmp/pose-sandbox-qualification-prompt.md --agent claude-opus-5-5 --access read --cd /tmp/pose-sandbox-qualification --json` em instância descartável com o comando de revisão projetado | Tool calls reais e erros do SO; hashes preservados; relatório público sanitizado |\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:101:| Review governado reexecuta rastreio e vet | `pose delegate review spec:pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox --agent claude-opus-5-5 --json` após bundle/evidência válidos | Run nativo com comandos, resultados e conclusão independente; sem alterações no checkout |\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:103:| Segurança e governança | `govulncheck ./...` no módulo; `pose lint-spec pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox --strict`; `pose artifact-check --spec pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox --strict`; `pose surface-check --spec pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox --strict` | Sem vulnerabilidade alcançável nova, diff sem segredos, claims reconciliados e composição comprovada |\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:107:- R1 [satisfied] test:TestSandboxedReviewClaudeEnforcesFreshAndResumedShellBoundaries test:TestSandboxedReviewStagingIsMaterializedBeforeIntegrityAndFilesStillCount check:claude-sandboxed-review-integration report:claude-review-sandbox-qualification\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:108:- R2 [satisfied] test:TestSandboxedReviewDependencyFailuresNeverLaunchClaude test:TestSandboxedReviewWrapperKeepsScratchPrivateAndPropagatesStartupFailure check:claude-sandboxed-review-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:109:- R3 [satisfied] check:claude-sandboxed-review-integration report:claude-review-sandbox-qualification\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:110:- R4 [satisfied] test:TestSandboxedReviewSelectsOnlyReviewAndKeepsResumeConfiguration test:TestSandboxedReviewOmissionPreservesLegacyAdapter test:TestSandboxedReviewRefusesIncompleteOrUnsafeCommands test:TestSandboxedReviewRepeatedTypedInitKeepsOneIdentityButRejectsConflicts test:TestSandboxedReviewSessionCodecPreservesUnambiguousChannelsExactly check:claude-sandboxed-review-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:120:Perfil Claude exclusivo de review, com sandbox de shell obrigatório, scratch privado, negação de escrita no checkout e Git comum físico, mesmas proteções no resume e recusa explícita sem dependências. Staging vazio é preparado antes do snapshot; arquivos continuam contados pela integridade. A captura aceita init tipado repetido da mesma sessão, preservando bytes originais para proveniência e redação. Qualificação real Linux, testes determinísticos e revisão governada aprovados. Não há alegação de isolamento do processo Claude inteiro nem qualificação de outras plataformas.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:128:- [open] F1: derivar o staging Claude de um sinal explícito do adaptador projetado no DispatchPlan, vinculado à proveniência, em vez de reler a policy no dispatch; o comportamento atual falha fechado. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-13)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:129:- [open] F2: usar erro sentinel e errors.Is para ambiguidade de captura, evitando dependência da mensagem textual; alteração dessa mensagem hoje volta a recusar captura. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-13)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox.md:130:- [open] F3: adicionar regressão e documentação para IDs init conflitantes em canal originalmente não ambíguo, fixando a recusa mais estrita já implementada. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-13)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-cyclonedx-sbom.md:32:- Keep generation reproducible and diff-reviewable.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-cyclonedx-sbom.md:43:- GoReleaser, dependency metadata, NOTICE review and release assets.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-cyclonedx-sbom.md:52:- Generated license fields may be incomplete and need review policy.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-cyclonedx-sbom.md:66:- [x] Add direct-dependency and license-completeness policy checks: `verify.sh` fails when a direct production dependency parsed from `pose-mcp/go.mod` is missing from the SBOM; license completeness is reviewed against `NOTICE` per the ADR policy (no absence-of-risk claim). ([reference](https://cyclonedx.org/specification/overview/))\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-cyclonedx-sbom.md:112:- Generated license fields may be incomplete; the NOTICE review policy owns\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-cyclonedx-sbom.md:118:- [done] Inspect the first snapshot rehearsal's SBOMs: confirm syft resolves the replaced `mcp-enforce` module path and review detected licenses against NOTICE. Inspected the published v0.18.2 SBOMs: syft resolves the `mcp-enforce` replace path but not its version, and 26 of 27 components carry no license, so there is nothing to reconcile against NOTICE. Recorded as F5. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-08-14)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-shellcheck-ci-gate.md:171:- [open] The missing-`cd` defect was valid shell and invisible to static analysis. The durable answer is reproducing a gate's exact command locally before cutting, which is process rather than tooling — consider whether the release workflow can execute the verification legs against a snapshot before a tag exists. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-02)\n.pose/adr/2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:1:# ADR: sandboxed Claude review commands\n.pose/adr/2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:4:Accepted (2026-11-12), implementation decision for `pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox`. Runtime qualification remains a delivery gate.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:6:Qualification-driven additions below were decided on 2026-11-13; they are not represented as pre-implementation decisions. @pose-maintainers owns requalification on CLI/platform/codec changes and review by 2026-12-13.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:10:Governed review projects an agent's `commands.read` and `resume.command`. The existing restricted Claude profile cannot safely permit arbitrary Go test flags through a prefix allow-list. The task sandbox permits editing and cannot be substituted for a review. The trusted-process containment ADR deliberately does not promise filesystem isolation of the Claude process itself.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:14:Add an optional `review_profile` to a schema-2 delegation agent, containing a fresh `command` and, when the agent supports resume, `resume_command`. Select it only for governed `review`. Copy the resume configuration before projection. Omission preserves byte-identical legacy adapters; older strict parsers refuse the unknown field. Validate both commands and session placeholders before dispatch. No runtime fallback to `read` or task commands is allowed after selecting this profile. Existing command digests, policy baselines and provenance verification bind the selected adapter without a parallel ledger.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:26:References: [Claude sandbox](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sandboxing), [settings](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings-reference), [trusted-process decision](2026-10-25-bound-trusted-reviewer-execution-and-disclose-unavailable-isolation.md).\n.pose/adr/2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:28:The first governed qualification exceeded the residual cleanup inventory with its Go build cache. Keep engine cleanup limits unchanged; instruct the reviewer to run `go clean -cache` as the final Bash command inside the mandatory sandbox. Reject outer-wrapper cleanup of the adapter-controlled path: a test could replace it with a symlink to host data. The engine still verifies cleanup with its unchanged owned-resource bounds; instructions alone never certify successful cleanup. Cleanup failure still fails the run; no broader filesystem isolation is implied. Capture failures retain only a closed-vocabulary stage/reason, never withheld raw output.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:30:Real-worktree qualification found that Claude automatically adds the origin Git common directory to its shell write permissions. Explicitly resolve its physical path with git rev-parse and deny it on fresh/resume; resolution failure refuses launch. Synthetic directories named shared-git do not qualify this boundary. Native post-run integrity checks do not certify origin refs/tags/objects; prevention comes from this explicit OS denial, measured in a disposable real Git worktree and checked again by the governed reviewer.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:2:slug: pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:6:depends_on: pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:9:delivers: contract:review-bundle-doc-only-specs\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:18:Ensure `pose review bundle --explain`, `pose review bundle --seal`, `pose review auto-attest`, and `pose close` succeed seamlessly for documentation-only, governance, and ADR specs that have no code delivery targets:\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:19:1. Persist the updated delivery-integrity index when `pose artifact-check` reconciles a spec's change set and ensure `pose review bundle` dynamically creates `.pose/indexes/delivery-integrity.json` if absent.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:20:2. Add precondition `delivery-target-declared` to the `validate` tool in the base review profile `spec-closeout.json` and in `ReviewPlan` tool construction, skipping required validation evidence when a spec has no code modules or delivery targets.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:24:Unblocks initial repository setup, governance milestones, ADR reviews, and pure documentation deliverables in POSE without requiring dummy code modules or failing on missing validation evidence.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:28:- Retain strict integrity and review verification gates across all commands.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:35:- R1: `cmdArtifactCheck` and `cmdReviewBundle` shall persist and ensure `.pose/indexes/delivery-integrity.json` exists so subsequent review bundle operations resolve change sets cleanly.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:49:- `.pose/review-profiles/spec-closeout.json`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:50:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:51:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:53:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:54:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:57:- contract:review-bundle-doc-only-specs module:pose-mcp profile:api-contract entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:64:- modified: .pose/review-profiles/spec-closeout.json\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:65:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:66:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:69:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:88:- R1 [satisfied] contract:review-bundle-doc-only-specs check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewBundleSealAndCloseoutForDocOnlySpecWithNoDeliveryTargets evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:89:- R2 [satisfied] contract:review-bundle-doc-only-specs check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewBundleSealAndCloseoutForDocOnlySpecWithNoDeliveryTargets evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:90:- R3 [satisfied] contract:review-bundle-doc-only-specs check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewBundleSealAndCloseoutForDocOnlySpecWithNoDeliveryTargets evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:91:- R4 [satisfied] contract:review-bundle-doc-only-specs check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewBundleSealAndCloseoutForDocOnlySpecWithNoDeliveryTargets evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:98:- contract:review-bundle-doc-only-specs -> pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:108:- Supported review bundle sealing, auto-attestation, and spec closeout for doc-only and governance specs.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-doc-only-specs.md:109:- Fixed change set persistence between artifact-check and review bundle.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-03-pose-debt-marker-lexical-precision.md:67:- created: .pose/reports/2026-08-03-pose-debt-marker-lexical-precision-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-03-pose-debt-marker-lexical-precision.md:127:  actual Portuguese source comments during the parent-repository review.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-03-pose-debt-marker-lexical-precision.md:137:  review, publication and independent verification gates passed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-adapter-containment\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:6:depends_on: pose-git-and-dispatch-snapshot-integrity, pose-cli-mcp-operation-results, pose-delegated-review-dispatch\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:11:delivers: capability:delegated-adapter-containment\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:24:B18 / D06 e T3-06. Consultar o [plano autoritativo](../results/pose-implementation-plan.json) e a [análise de delegação](../reports/2026-10-11-pose-front-03-delegated-review.md). Completar os mecanismos existentes sem duplicar as fundações done.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:49:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:50:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:51:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:52:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:53:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_windows.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:54:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:55:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:56:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:57:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:58:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:59:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:71:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-adapter-containment.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:72:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:73:- created: .pose/adr/2026-10-25-bound-trusted-reviewer-execution-and-disclose-unavailable-isolation.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:74:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:75:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:76:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:77:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_adapter_containment_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:78:- created: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/review_adapter_containment_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:83:- capability:delegated-adapter-containment module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:91:Reutilizar B07/B12/B16/B17, `knowledge:pose-b07-implementation` e a decisão [trusted-process](../adr/2026-10-25-bound-trusted-reviewer-execution-and-disclose-unavailable-isolation.md). Não criar sandbox ou issuer paralelo. Resolver policy e capacidades antes de reserva/spawn; capturar streams e output com limites; registrar cleanup no OperationResult dentro do run imutável antes de publicá-lo. Preservar snapshot/digests e quota. Não apagar evidência automaticamente.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:111:Usar fixtures sintéticas e snapshot fixo. Plano V1–V8 definido antes do código; regressões reais correspondentes constam no trace. Validação canônica final no commit `93bd352`: 156/156 checks strict em 254.6s, incluindo `delegated-adapter-containment-integration`, no caminho de policy `.pose/results/delivery-validation.json`. Race final passou nos três consumidores; govulncheck e secret scan sem achados. [Relatório](../reports/2026-10-26-b18-adapter-containment.md).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-delegated-adapter-containment.md:151:- R9 [satisfied] capability:delegated-adapter-containment evidence:integration check:delegated-adapter-containment-integration test:TestAdapterContainmentCLIRealDispatchAndDisclosure test:TestAdapterContainmentMCPReportsFailedCleanupWithoutApproval\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:2:slug: pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:12:delivers: capability:review-brief-templates-are-immutable\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:15:# Spec: A review brief template version never changes its text\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:21:A change to the text a review brief template renders takes a new template version, and the build fails when it does not.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:25:A run records the digest of the brief it was sent and its proof signs it, so the text a template version renders is part of what that version means. `review-brief/4` changed its text three times under one version while the conclusion rules were being stated, and the runs briefed with its earlier texts could no longer be re-rendered: their approvals failed verification (\"brief/template/notes/transmitted bytes differ\") until the retention of delegated approvals stopped re-rendering the brief for a done scope. Nothing guarded the rule that a version is immutable; the mistake was caught by measuring, not by the build. This closes the follow-up of `pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:41:- R1: Every review brief template version in use (the current one and every earlier one a run may have been briefed with) shall have a recorded digest of the text it renders from fixed bundles that carry every kind of content a brief renders: bare, with implementer notes, structural facts (one shared with another spec) and a tool scoped to a component, and as the second round with its predecessor run and bundle, an unreadable draft and an open finding, and as a third round with nothing open; with a renamed entry, an optional criterion and notes that carry a fence.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:57:- The recorded digests are those of the versions as they render today. Runs briefed with an earlier text of `review-brief/4` are already verified as sealed by the retention of delegated approvals, which does not re-render the brief.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:63:`internal/pose` tests and `testdata`, the ADR on delegated review conclusions, the manual.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:67:- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:68:- created: .pose/starts/pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:69:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:71:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_versions_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:72:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:80:- capability:review-brief-templates-are-immutable module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:92:- [ ] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:108:The test was written, then a sentence of `review-brief/4` was edited to see it fail with the message naming the version, and reverted to see it pass.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:115:- R1 [satisfied] test:TestEveryReviewBriefTemplateVersionRendersWhatItRenderedWhenItWasPublished check:review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:125:- The digest of `review-brief/4` is the text as it renders today; the two earlier texts it had before are not recorded and are not needed, since a done scope's approval is verified as sealed.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:126:- The recording is made with `UPDATE_BRIEF_GOLDEN=1` and keeps every digest already in the file; changing one by hand is visible in review.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:133:Each review brief template version in use has a digest of what it renders from a fixed bundle, recorded in `testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json`; the build fails when a version renders other text, saying that a change takes a new version, and when a version has no digest; recording never rewrites a digest already there. Left out: the adjudication and smoke templates.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:136:- pose-mcp/internal/pose (review_brief_versions_test.go, testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:137:- POSE.md and its pt-BR and scaffold copies; the validation matrix gains `review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration`\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:140:- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head, and the suites of `internal/pose`\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:141:- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review (Claude Opus 5.5, independent by model) concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:144:- A text change that also changes the version constants and the digests in one commit passes by design: the guard asks for a new version, not for a reviewer.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md:148:- [open] Cover the adjudication and smoke brief templates and the versioned delegation handoff renderers with the same golden digests, rendered from a fixed script, fixed questions and a fixed predecessor run. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-spec-amendment-history.md:16:record material intent and acceptance-criteria changes as append-only reviewed amendments.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-spec-amendment-history.md:28:- R2: Each event shall identify affected IDs, rationale, author/reviewer and timestamp.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-spec-amendment-history.md:61:- [x] Confirm baseline and fixtures against [OpenSpec](https://github.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec): no amendment mechanism existed; git history shows diffs but not materiality, rationale or review; context resumed from knowledge:contract-baseline-handoff.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-spec-amendment-history.md:64:- [x] Define material-change taxonomy and amendment schema: `.pose/specs/<slug>/amendments.jsonl` (schema 1) with `baseline|added|withdrawn|semantic|editorial`, affected R-IDs, rationale, pseudonymous author/reviewer aliases, RFC3339 timestamp and post-change hash per ID (ADR `2026-07-19-append-only-spec-amendment-history`). ([reference](https://github.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec))\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-spec-amendment-history.md:87:- R2 [satisfied] events carry IDs, rationale, author/reviewer aliases and RFC3339 timestamp, enforced by LoadAmendments; check:test (TestAmendValidation, TestAmendList)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-spec-amendment-history.md:112:- Rationale truthfulness is owned by review, not the gate.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-spec-amendment-history.md:116:- [spawned: pose-governance-gate-activation] Record baselines for the active-roadmap specs as they enter execution, making the gate effective beyond fixtures. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-23)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-review-completion-signal\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-dispatch, pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger, pose-delegation-surface\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:15:# Spec: A delegated run can be watched and announces that it finished\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:21:Let whoever started a delegated run (a person, an agent, a CI step, a runner such as Harne8's Conductor) start it without holding the process, follow it live, and be woken by a plain process exit when it reaches a terminal state, with the result in the exit code and in one machine-readable line.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:25:Origin: the B06 review rounds (2026-10-17). The lead agent launched the reviewer as a background process and expected to be resumed when it ended. On the later rounds it was not: the launching command returned at once, the host saw a finished task, and the real review ran unobserved until the maintainer reported that it had finished. The behaviour the lead needs exists in every host as \"a tracked process exits\", but nothing in POSE offers a process whose lifetime equals the review's, so each launcher reinvented it, and got it wrong in a different way.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:27:Amended on 2026-10-26 by the [delegation ADR](../adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md): the commands move under `pose delegate` and cover every purpose, and the spec gains the live watch, the run listing and the picker that the personal watch launcher provides today (R9–R12), so that launcher can retire.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:35:Push notifications to chat or email; resuming an interrupted run (`pose-delegated-review-run-continuity`); choosing the reviewer.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:41:- R1: `pose delegate <purpose> --detach` shall start the run under a supervisor that survives the caller's terminal, shall return the run identifier and the paths of its record at once, and shall exit 0 without waiting.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:42:- R2: `pose delegate wait <run> [--timeout <d>]` shall block until the run is terminal and shall exit with a code that distinguishes `approved` (0), `changes-requested` or `rejected` (10), `failed` (20), `interrupted` (30), `stalled` (40) and `timeout of the wait` (50), after printing one line of JSON (`--json`) or text with the run, state, decision, resumable flag and reset instant. Usage errors exit 2.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:43:- R3: `pose delegate wait` shall be a plain foreground process whose lifetime is the review's, so that a host tracking the process is woken by its exit; it shall not poll the network and shall not depend on a host-specific feature.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:46:- R6: `pose delegate ls [<run>|<bundle>]` and the MCP tool `pose_delegate_status` (`pose-delegation-mcp`) shall report the state without blocking, including heartbeat age, so a caller can tell a running run from a stalled one; the MCP tool shall never block longer than its own bounded timeout.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:49:- R9: `pose delegate watch <run|label>` shall follow the run's normalized events live and stop by itself at the terminal transition; `--no-follow` shall print what was recorded so far and exit; `-v` shall add the tail of each tool output, bounded by `--lines <n>` (default 12); `--json` shall stream the normalized events as NDJSON.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:51:- R11: In a terminal, `watch` with no argument shall follow the only active run and otherwise open a picker — fzf when it is on the path, with a live preview of the run under the cursor refreshed at a configurable interval (0 turns it off), a numbered menu without it; outside a terminal, an ambiguous or missing reference shall exit 2 and list the candidates.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:52:- R12: `pose delegate ls` shall list attempts by their latest run with state, purpose, agent, label, turns, age, last step and heartbeat age; colours shall follow `NO_COLOR` and be off when the output is not a terminal, in `ls` and in `watch`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:57:- A killed `pose delegate wait` or `watch` leaves the run running.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:66:- A foreground `pose delegate` run, and the deprecated `pose review dispatch`, keep their present behaviour and exit codes; `--detach`, `wait`, `watch` and the extended `ls` are additions.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:72:Supervisor, run record heartbeat and terminal marker, `pose delegate wait`, `ls` and `watch`, the picker, the MCP status tool, the `on_terminal` policy key.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:76:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:77:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:85:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_observation_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:86:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_observation_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:88:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_routing_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:92:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:93:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:95:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:96:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:97:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_wait.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:98:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_wait_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:99:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_detach_unix.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:100:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_detach_windows.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:101:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:111:- capability:delegation-observation module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:115:`pose delegate <purpose> --detach`, `pose delegate wait`, `ls` and `watch`, `pose_delegate_status`, `on_terminal`; documented exit codes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:125:- [x] First independent review: changes requested (B01–B09; F01–F04), B01–B09 and F02–F04 addressed with regression tests that fail on 2e015c4; F01 (redacted live events a failed capture later withholds) stays a disclosed follow-up of D7\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:126:- [x] Second independent review: B01–B07, B09 and F02–F04 accepted as fixed and the exact gitleaks entry accepted; B08 partial and the new follow-up N01 addressed with regression tests that fail on 939c5ab; F01 stays disclosed under D7\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:127:- [x] Third independent review (Claude Sonnet 5.5, same vendor, another model): B08 and N01 accepted as fixed; the new blocker N02 and the follow-ups F-R3-01, F-R3-03, F-R3-04, F-R3-06, F-R3-08 and F-R3-10 addressed, with regression tests that fail on 9377ac7 where the behaviour is testable; F01, F-R3-02, F-R3-05, F-R3-07 and F-R3-09 stay follow-ups for the closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:128:- [x] Fourth independent review (Claude Sonnet 5.5, same vendor, another model) and closeout: N02, F-R3-01, F-R3-03, F-R3-04, F-R3-06, F-R3-08 and F-R3-10 accepted as fixed with no blocker; F01, F-R3-02, F-R3-05, F-R3-07, F-R3-09 and the new F-R4-01 to F-R4-05 are the open follow-ups of the Final Report\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:134:- Minimal option: document that a caller should poll `review status`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:135:- Selected option: a blocking `review wait` whose exit is the signal\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:136:- Rationale: every agent host and CI system already wakes on a process exit; polling makes each caller invent an interval, and a short-lived launcher is how the review was lost on 2026-10-17\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:138:- Falsifier: a host that tracks processes and is not woken, or a wait that exits while the review still runs\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:144:- Rationale: a pid is reused; a heartbeat alone cannot tell a slow reviewer from a dead one\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:145:- Consequences: a long silent reviewer step must still heartbeat from the supervisor, not from the vendor\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:201:- R6 [deferred-integration: spec:pose-delegation-mcp] The ls half is delivered and verified by test:TestPreviewCarriesVerboseAndLsReadsLiveProgress and check:delegation-surface-integration; the MCP tool pose_delegate_status that this requirement names is delivered by pose-delegation-mcp and is not claimed as satisfied here.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:207:- R12 [satisfied] check:delegation-surface-integration test:TestDelegateWatchReplaysTheChain test:TestPreviewCarriesVerboseAndLsReadsLiveProgress report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:213:Milestone `observation` of roadmap `delegation`: `pose delegate review|adjudicate|smoke --detach` starts the run in a session of its own, in the caller's directory, and returns its attempt once the attempt is handed back (a run that cannot hand back does not start its agent; a route that must wait for a usage-limit reset is not detached); `pose delegate wait` ends with the run and exits 0, 10, 20, 30, 40, 50 or 2; the running process rewrites a heartbeat and a run whose heartbeat is stale and whose process is provably gone is recorded `stalled` through an exclusive claim; the terminal record is published before the marker goes; `pose delegate watch` replays an attempt's chain with resume markers and follows the redacted live events until the record is published, with a picker and colours only on a terminal; `on_terminal` runs once under containment and its failure never changes the run's state; `ls` shows heartbeat age, stall and hook failure; the four manuals and the help catalogue describe it. R6 is delivered for `ls` only: the MCP tool `pose_delegate_status` is delivered by `pose-delegation-mcp`, deferred and not satisfied here. The guarantees of `pose-delegation-surface` and `pose-delegation-routing` (dispatch, ledger, continuity, provenance, containment, routing) were not weakened. Opened on 2026-10-18 under roadmap `delegated-review` from the operating experience of the B06 review rounds (see Origin); moved on 2026-10-26 to milestone `observation` of roadmap `delegation`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:215:### Independent review and evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:217:Maintainer-authorized reviewer `agent:independent-claude-sonnet-5-5-review` (Claude Sonnet 5.5, Anthropic), the same vendor and another model than the implementer, Claude Opus 5.5 (`agent:claude-opus-5-5`, session `f2a4d9f2-d557-4064-ae96-6ed52bb47cd2`). The `agent:independent-` prefix is a declaration required by the engine; by the rule of 2026-10-09 another model satisfies `different-actor` and another vendor would be preferred. Identity is declared and this instance's attestations are unsigned. Rounds 1 and 2 were Codex (OpenAI); rounds 3 and 4 were this reviewer.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:219:Bundle `rvb-5535a3591b6decad`, attestation `rva-197bace721068608`, sealed with `--lead anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`; the seal's absence of an Anthropic session reference in the reviewing environment is expected, no implementation execution digest was invented, and the approval is a declared review, not a signed vendor receipt.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:221:Round 4 of `a8ce8cf97acb89815cc8440f028ec319c63ec1c3` accepted N02 (a detached run read a relative `--note-file` from the project root), F-R3-01, F-R3-03, F-R3-04, F-R3-06, F-R3-08 and F-R3-10 as fixed, and kept B08 and N01 fixed and the earlier rounds' closed items closed. N02, F-R3-01 and F-R3-06 have regression tests that fail when the production line is reverted; F-R3-03, F-R3-04, F-R3-08 and F-R3-10 have none (F-R4-01). The round-3 probes were re-executed, a variant of N02 from a subdirectory, a symlinked directory and with an absolute path passes, and four concurrent watchers of a 150-event stream show no loss or duplicate. Full report, probes and mutation logs are kept locally under `.review-work/round4/` (deliberately untracked). Residual-risk handoff: knowledge:delegation-observation-round4.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:235:- [open] F01: redact the live view with what the record will withhold, or withhold the live events of a capture that later fails; disclosed under D7. See knowledge:delegation-observation-round4. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-25)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:236:- [open] F-R3-02: test the SIGTERM, grace and SIGKILL path of a stopped supervisor and make the fallback reach the agent's own group. See knowledge:delegation-observation-round4. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-25)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:237:- [open] F-R3-05: stop or announce the agent, and clear the live file and marker, of a run recorded `stalled`. See knowledge:delegation-observation-round4. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-25)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:238:- [open] F-R3-07: fire `on_terminal` for the deprecated alias and for stalled runs, or narrow the manual wording. See knowledge:delegation-observation-round4. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-25)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:239:- [open] F-R3-09: retry once a marker read that races a rewrite before listing a loss. See knowledge:delegation-observation-round4. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-25)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:240:- [open] F-R4-01: add regression tests for F-R3-03, F-R3-04, F-R3-08 and F-R3-10. See knowledge:delegation-observation-round4. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-25)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:241:- [open] F-R4-02: show a pending hook state and report a lost hook outcome earlier than six minutes. See knowledge:delegation-observation-round4. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-25)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:242:- [open] F-R4-03: document in the four manuals how a relative `on_terminal` command is resolved. See knowledge:delegation-observation-round4. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-25)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:243:- [open] F-R4-04: show the live events of a stalled run in `watch` and print the `--detach` paths relative to the caller. See knowledge:delegation-observation-round4. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-25)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md:244:- [open] F-R4-05: name or select the review regression tests so the delegation integration check and the race selection run them. See knowledge:delegation-observation-round4. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-25)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:2:slug: pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:9:delivers: contract:review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:18:Prevent `pose review bundle --explain` and `pose review bundle --seal` from failing with hard errors when overlay review profiles reference rule IDs provided by uninstalled extensions (such as `backend-go` or `frontend-react`):\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:21:3. Allow bundle sealing, review attestation, and spec closeout to proceed unimpeded on projects without all optional rule extensions installed.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:24:Eliminates blocking failures on fresh projects (`pose init` on empty repositories or repositories without all language extensions) where default overlay profiles reference extension rules, restoring smooth review bundle workflows.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:29:- Zero regressions in existing review bundle and plan test suites.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:37:- R2: Overlay profiles whose selectors do not match the review scope context shall be skipped without evaluating or blocking on missing rules.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:38:- R3: Overlay profiles whose selectors match the review scope context shall compose criteria normally and record uninstalled rules as warnings in `plan.Warnings`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:50:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:51:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:52:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:55:- contract:review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation module:pose-mcp profile:api-contract entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:62:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:63:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:64:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:69:- [x] Increment 3: Add unit and regression tests in `review_plan_test.go` covering unmatched and matched overlay profiles with uninstalled extension rules.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:81:- R1 [satisfied] contract:review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewPlanOverlayProfilesWithUninstalledExtensionRulesDegradeToWarnings evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:82:- R2 [satisfied] contract:review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewPlanOverlayProfilesWithUninstalledExtensionRulesDegradeToWarnings evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:83:- R3 [satisfied] contract:review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewPlanOverlayProfilesWithUninstalledExtensionRulesDegradeToWarnings evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:84:- R4 [satisfied] contract:review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewPlanOverlayProfilesWithUninstalledExtensionRulesDegradeToWarnings evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:91:- contract:review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation -> pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:101:- Enabled graceful degradation for uninstalled rule extensions in review profiles.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-overlay-uninstalled-rules-graceful-degradation.md:102:- Verified review bundle planning and sealing on projects with uninstalled extension rules.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-only-the-signing-gate-is-read-live.md:24:flipped today cannot re-judge a review recorded years ago. One gate is\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-only-the-signing-gate-is-read-live.md:35:Both are the kind of change that passes review by looking consistent.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-only-the-signing-gate-is-read-live.md:167:- [open] Read the validator with the AST rather than a regular expression, so a policy field reached through a local variable is seen too (owner:unowned crit:low review:2027-03-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-sdd-migration-acquisition.md:47:  dry-run inspection, import, review of what was imported, and the first\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-sdd-migration-acquisition.md:152:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-authority-fixture-clock.md:7:depends_on: pose-abm-review-authority\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-authority-fixture-clock.md:47:`pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_authority_test.go` e este registro.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-authority-fixture-clock.md:50:- governance:authority-fixture-clock module:pose-mcp profile:structural-delta entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_authority_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-authority-fixture-clock.md:54:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_authority_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-authority-fixture-clock.md:100:2026-09-19: sealed review bundle `rvb-5e01174a8bdc7801` and approved\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-install-gate-failure-recovery-notice.md:168:  review:2026-10-15)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-review-capability\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-conclusions, pose-delegated-review-run-provenance, pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger, pose-delegation-routing, pose-delegation-handoff, pose-delegated-review-round-protocol, pose-delegated-review-action-fulfillment, pose-delegation-mcp\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:12:delivers: capability:delegated-review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:15:# Spec: Delegated review as an adoptable capability\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:21:Make delegated review a catalog capability that `pose init` offers with yes as the default, with documentation, a skill and agent examples, so a project adopts it like any other contract, and so a project that declines it still reaches delivery with an honest record.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:25:The maintainer asked for this to become POSE's standard way to hand reviews, attestations and similar work to a secondary agent, without the mechanisation turning into a rubber stamp.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:27:Origin: the 2026-10-09 review of `pose-native-attestation-issuer` by Codex through a personal launcher; it found three real defects in three rounds and exposed what the engine lacks (ADR `2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter`, roadmap `delegated-review`).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:29:Amended on 2026-10-26 by the [delegation ADR](../adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md): the capability is offered at init instead of opt-in only, runs through `pose delegate`, and when it is off a plan that requires `different-actor` degrades to a disclosed same-actor review (R1–R5 reworded, R8–R11 added).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:33:Offered by `pose init`; an existing instance stays as it is until it adopts the capability; adopting it rewrites no earlier review record. The B17 delegated_review signed-run-proof barrier remains live: an older prefix-only approval can cease satisfying current verification after adoption. Requirements follow the maintainer's decisions recorded in the 2026-10-09 ADR and amended by the 2026-10-26 ADR. `mandatory-human` is never degraded.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:39:- R1: `pose adopt delegated-review` shall turn on the run-backed independence rule, dated the day it is applied, and refuse without a review-capable agent, explicit executor-attested provenance, a loadable conclusions issuer and its exact attestation pin with project/audience binding. The B17 signed-run-proof barrier stays live for older approvals without rewriting their records.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:40:- R2: The documentation shall describe the contract under `pose delegate`, the Codex and Claude Code agent examples, routing and its fallback steps, the degradation of R10 and every safeguard of both ADRs.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:41:- R3: A `pose-delegate` skill shall tell an agent when to delegate a review and when a task, that it must not write the reviewer's prompt, that a rejection is answered by a change, not a rerun, and how to act on `next_actions`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:42:- R4: An end-to-end journey shall seal a fixture with a seeded defect, delegate its review to a fake agent, have the engine record the rejecting run, fix, run the next round on the new bundle and close with no manual step; a second journey escalates a person-required criterion to an action request; a third, with the capability off, closes with a disclosed same-actor review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:43:- R5: When a `pose delegate review` run passes every check — brief generated from the sealed bundle, disposable copy unchanged, run record intact and signed, `different-vendor` or `different-model` independence against the implementation recorded in the bundle, conclusion complete and accepted by the attestation preflight, no earlier rejection on an unchanged bundle — the engine shall record the attestation from the run with no further step; a rejecting conclusion shall be recorded and block the scope until the bundle changes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:44:- R6: Review policy shall declare which criteria require a person, and the engine shall turn each escalation — such a criterion, reviewers in conflict, a reviewer asking for a business decision, or the run budget exhausted without approval — into an action request with the question and options ready, answered as a confirmation or approval; nothing else waits on a person.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:47:R5 and R7 are delivered by [`pose-delegated-review-conclusions`](2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md) (phase B19, amendment of 2026-10-27 to the delegation ADR); this spec traces them to it and qualifies them in the integrated journeys of R4.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:48:- R8: A fresh `pose init` shall offer delegation with yes as the default answer; on yes with supported CLIs found on the path it shall provision project-specific native executor signing, pin it only for attestations, write `delegation.json` with those agents, and enable `delegated_review: true` last, dated that day. A refusal, EOF, non-interactive init or zero supported CLIs shall record false without a delegation policy, key or pin. Existing governance is preserved even if its schema stamp is missing; partial publication retains recoverable artifacts and distinguishes unconfirmed durability.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:49:- R9: `pose update` shall never turn the capability on; while it is off, it shall print one suggestion naming `pose adopt delegated-review`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:50:- R10: An explicit false `delegated_review` decision shall allow new plans requiring `different-actor` to accept `same-actor-separate-execution`, with `delegated-review-disabled` sealed into the plan and attestation and disclosed by verification and closeout. Legacy omission preserves prior behavior; mandatory-human and stronger protected baselines are unchanged, including signed run proof for an agent review of the disabling change itself. Disabling preserves pins and history and does not reconstruct proof or erase rejection or budget state.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:51:- R11: While the capability is on and routing finds no available agent for a review after its fallback steps, the engine shall raise the escalation of R6 with the question ready, and shall not degrade as R10 does.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:57:Catalog entry, `pose init` and `pose update` prompts, independence degradation in the review plan and its disclosure, docs page, skill, journey tests.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:61:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:62:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-review-capability.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:63:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-review-capability.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:66:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:67:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:69:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_assurance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:70:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_review_adoption.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:71:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_review_adoption_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:74:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:77:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegated_review_capability_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:78:- created: .agents/skills/pose-delegate/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:79:- created: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.agents/skills/pose-delegate/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:84:- modified: docs-site/docs/review-and-trust.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:92:- created: locales/pt-BR/.agents/skills/pose-delegate/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:93:- created: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/.agents/skills/pose-delegate/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:95:- created: .pose/adr/2026-10-29-make-delegated-review-adoption-explicit-and-recoverable.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:99:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.amendments.jsonl\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:105:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_policy_baseline.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:107:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/delegate_tools.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:108:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/delegate_tools_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:110:- created: .pose/reports/delegation-adoption-review-round1.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:112:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_review_escalation.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:113:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:114:- created: .pose/reports/delegation-adoption-review-round2.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:117:- created: .pose/reports/delegation-adoption-review-round3.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:121:- capability:delegated-review module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_review_adoption.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:134:The contract is ADR `2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter`, accepted on 2026-10-09 with the maintainer's decisions: the engine records a verified run, people by exception through policy, agent independence by differing vendor or model (different vendor preferred), and reviews, adjudications and smoke runs from the first delivery.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:136:The [delegation ADR](../adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md), accepted on 2026-10-26, amends it: delegation is offered by `pose init` with yes as the default instead of being opt-in only; with the capability off, `different-actor` degrades to a disclosed `same-actor-separate-execution` so one agent of one vendor can reach delivery; the implementation identity comes from the sealed bundle; runs go through `pose delegate`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:138:The [adoption ADR](../adr/2026-10-29-make-delegated-review-adoption-explicit-and-recoverable.md) clarifies absence versus refusal, machine-only signing bootstrap and recoverable publication. Maintainer decision `act-31f0849a7ec6712c` selected the live B17 barrier on 2026-10-29; this spec promises immutable historical records, not grandfathered proof exemptions.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:143:- Selected option: degrade to a disclosed same-actor review when the capability is off; escalate, never degrade, when it is on and no agent is available\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:144:- Rationale: an instance that declined delegation has no second actor to name, and requiring one only invites a declared reviewer nobody verified; an instance that adopted it has promised independence, so a missing agent is a question for a person, not a silent downgrade\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:145:- Consequences: the review record of a declining instance always shows the limitation\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:150:- Minimal option: treat a missing delegated_review key as a new refusal\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:153:- Consequences: capture delegated-review-disabled in the sealed plan and derived record/closeout assurance; omission keeps previous digests unchanged. The protected review of a disabling change seals delegated_run_proof_required, retains independent routing and automatic verified conclusion for that review only, and cannot accept a prefix-only agent approval merely because live delegation is now off\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:166:- Minimal option: exclude the client alias from the review subject\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:170:- Falsifier: an unsafe alias seals or the supported alias disappears from the review subject\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:175:- Selected option: bound the upgrade journey by the newest reviewable capability, excluding needs-setup, while retaining published checksum-verified releases, actual configuration decisions and idempotent update assertions\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:176:- Rationale: CapabilitiesToReview deliberately does not ask a configuration decision before prerequisites exist; delegated-review introduces a newer needs-setup entry, not a new automatically decidable adoption\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:177:- Consequences: the production adoption/update contract is unchanged; the registered journey continues exercising a real review instead of inventing a decision or falsely failing when none is owed\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:180:Review context: knowledge:delegation-routing-round3; knowledge:delegated-conclusions-round4; knowledge:delegation-mcp-round5. B19 conclusions and B20 fulfillment are already done. B21 qualifies their composition; no new phase checkpoint is introduced. The 2026-10-26 ADR's init offer supersedes the older batch-10 wording about off-by-default interactive opt-in. Disabling the capability preserves runs, attempts, rejections, issuer pins and earlier approvals; it does not cancel an execution or restore a spent budget.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:197:| Update preview/apply and capability-off suggestion | `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli -run 'DelegatedReviewCapability|UpdatePreviewParity' -count=1` | One suggestion, never activation; preview and apply agree |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:201:| Final source and delivery contracts | `pose artifact-check --spec pose-delegated-review-capability --strict` and `pose surface-check --spec pose-delegated-review-capability --strict` | Attributed paths reconcile and production entrypoint has current integration evidence |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:203:Additional required checks: full Go suite and vet; focused race tests for delegation/adoption; Windows/Darwin builds; secret scan; distributed manual and skill parity. Review, native closeout and CI must pass before declaring done. Failures and retries are preserved rather than silently replaced in the review report.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:207:- R1 [satisfied] Exact trust validation, dated idempotent adoption, protected floor and the retained live barrier: test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityValidatesTheExactExecutor test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityAdoptsAndExplicitlyTurnsOff test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityProtectsTheAdoptedFloor test:TestRunProvenanceLiveOptInDoesNotGrandfatherPrefix evidence:integration check:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:208:- R2 [satisfied] The operating manuals, native help and docs-site describe routing, signing, recovery and limitations; distributed locale/skill guards cover parity: test:TestLocaleCoverage test:TestSkillsCheckDiscoveryAndBoundedWorkflowFixture file:docs-site/docs/review-and-trust.md evidence:integration check:pose-mcp/go/test\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:209:- R3 [satisfied] The distributed pose-delegate skill distinguishes governed review from task, native briefs from labelled notes, remediation from reruns and authorized next actions: file:.agents/skills/pose-delegate/SKILL.md test:TestClaudeSkillLinksMatchAgentsSkills test:TestSkillsCheckDiscoveryAndBoundedWorkflowFixture evidence:integration check:pose-mcp/go/test\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:210:- R4 [satisfied] Native CLI journeys reject a source-seeded defect, preserve rejection, accept the changed bundle automatically and close; person/MCP and explicit-off journeys cover the exceptions: test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityRejectFixApproveAndClose test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityEscalatesThroughMCP test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityOffClosesWithDisclosure test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityDisablingChangeStillConcludes evidence:integration check:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:211:- R5 [satisfied] B19 conclusions compose through the same verified writer and rejection history: test:TestConcludeReviewRunRecordsTheAttestation test:TestConcludeReviewRunRecordsARejection test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityRejectFixApproveAndClose evidence:integration check:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:212:- R6 [satisfied] Person, unavailable/insufficiently independent agents and the B20 business/budget/conflict paths use native authority-bound decisions: test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityPersonAndSameModelEscalate test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityEscalatesThroughMCP test:TestDelegatedReviewRequestEscalatesToAPerson evidence:integration check:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:213:- R7 [satisfied] B19/B20 per-kind destinations remain distinct and runner-independent: test:TestDelegatedReviewRequestPerKind evidence:integration check:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:214:- R8 [satisfied] Accepted, refused, headless, missing CLI, repeated/missing-stamp, linked governance and partial-publication cases use the public init and native issuer machinery: test:TestDelegationInitAcceptedOfferCreatesOnlyExecutorTrust test:TestDelegationInitRefusalAndHeadlessCreateNoSigningArtifacts test:TestDelegationInitDoesNotBootstrapOverExistingGovernance test:TestDelegationInitPolicyPublicationFailureRetainsRecoverableState test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityValidatesTheCapturedConfiguration evidence:integration check:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:215:- R9 [satisfied] Update emits one suggestion while preserving disabled policy; adoption preview is mutation-free: test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityUpdateOnlySuggests test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityAdoptPreviewAndOff evidence:integration check:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:216:- R10 [satisfied] Only explicit refusal relaxes new eligible plans, with sealed/read-time disclosure and unchanged protected/human floors: test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityDisclosesOnlyAnExplicitRefusal test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityOffClosesWithDisclosure test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityDoesNotRelaxAProtectedBaseline evidence:integration check:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:217:- R11 [satisfied] Unavailable agents open one decision without a run; routing skips same-model candidates and tries independent ones first: test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityUnavailableAgentEscalatesWithoutSpawn test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityRoutesPastASameModelAgent test:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityEscalatesThroughMCP evidence:integration check:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:223:B21 composes catalog adoption, fresh-init consent and native machine signing, recoverable activation, explicit-off disclosure, protected-baseline proof, independent routing, authorized CLI/MCP escalation and verified automatic conclusions. Existing instances are not automatically adopted. Maintainer action act-31f0849a7ec6712c selected the live B17 proof barrier; the adoption ADR and amendments record that choice and its protected-disabling-review consequence.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:227:Claude Opus 5.5 supplied cross-vendor source reviews and accepted the journey/matrix and narrow alias-sealing corrections without blockers. The additional alias is sealed as governance with exact canonical link bytes; external or mismatched targets and symbolic ancestors fail closed. Low source findings are F2–F5 below; F1 records the pre-existing global coverage limitation. Other client aliases remain intentionally unsupported until a concrete contract exists; the cosmetic D5/D4 ordering is retained. Neither observation justifies broadening this delivery. Native bundle, attestation and guarded closeout record the formal acceptance; publication and CI remain independently observable GitHub operations, not inferred from local validation. This delivery does not close either roadmap or retire the personal launchers.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:229:Native closeout sealed bundle rvb-541e52f960dcffe4, recorded reviewer-authored attestation rva-20765d4a2f4c0355 and applied the guarded transition to done on 2026-10-29. The first attestation preview refused two cross-component evidence references and wrote nothing; the same reviewer corrected those producer-less tool rows to not-used with substantive rationale. The strict external docs build and pose-mcp-owned upgrade journey remain truthful inspected context, not invented component producers. Identity and independence remain declared; attribution names the Claude reviewer as preparer/concluder and agent:codex as applier.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:233:A trusted local executor can emit a complete canned judgment. Native proof authenticates the executor declaration and bound artifacts, not substantive review cognition or a vendor receipt; the adversarial disclosure test guards that boundary. The technical-debt assessment has zero uncovered markers but reports incomplete coverage for two pre-existing legacy spec sources; it is not evidence of global completeness.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:239:- [open] F2: Improve the missing-agent diagnostic for a protected disabling review before any current bundle is sealed; it currently fails closed without opening an escalation in that off-capability case. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:240:- [open] F3: Refine the automatic-conclusion hint for an off-capability legacy review run whose bundle is absent; preserve source-loss diagnostics without suggesting that ordinary off-capability work owed an automatic conclusion. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:242:- [open] F1: Reconcile the empty follow-up bullets in the legacy specs pose-instance-engine-version-tracking and pose-knowledge-durable-reference-type; the current followups/technical-debt producers correctly report partial global coverage until those sources are repaired. This does not waive any B21 requirement or claim global completeness. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:244:- [open] F4: Document or support sealing tracked client skill aliases on Windows checkouts with core.symlinks=false; the current regular-file representation fails closed and requires a checkout that preserves symlinks. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md:245:- [open] F5: Add a subject-builder regression for client skill alias dirty changes, rename and removal; the current direct classification/digest regressions and native sealed delivery cover the present path, but not future builder refactors. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:31:| Evidence classes no check may emit | reading `review_plan.go` | edit a profile |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:32:| \"no immutable attributed change set\" | reading `review_bundle.go` | run `pose index` |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:33:| Submodule fails the subject classifier | reading `review_bundle.go` | ~30 lines |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:44:   validation matrix accepts nine classes; the shipped review profiles reference\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:65:- Removing `pose review auto-attest`. That command fabricates evidence for\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:67:  between a judged review and a stamped one collapses. Removing it deletes a\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:71:  fixed in `pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes`; the criterion side\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:81:  review profile that no registered check is permitted to emit, naming the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:85:  collected for a review.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:120:  a profile it does not use, or a check whose results feed no review, and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:169:  log, a merged pull request and a published review reply in the adopting\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:199:  `review.evidence-vocabulary` miss the unproducible class, the class check\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:210:- R1 [satisfied] <doctor.go: review.evidence-vocabulary, scoped to the profiles .pose/policy/review.json selects; tests assert warn on a selected profile naming a class outside ValidEvidenceClasses, ok when every class is producible, and ok when the offending profile is on disk but unselected> surface:diagnose-invisible-governance-failures evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:215:- Closed after v1.8.0 shipped: `review.evidence-vocabulary` reported every\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:220:  check now reads `.pose/policy/review.json` and inspects only the profiles\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:226:  `pose review auto-attest` to invent a ref. The diagnostic makes it visible;\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-diagnose-invisible-governance-failures.md:235:- [done] Decide the fate of pose review auto-attest, which fabricates evidence for criteria whose classes have no producer. Decided: it stays and refuses. `AutoAttestReviewBundle` no longer invents a reference for either criteria or tools — where the scope carries validation evidence it errors and names what to run, and where it does not it records not-applicable with the reason. The fabrication the question was about is gone. (owner:unowned crit:high review:2026-10-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:2:slug: pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:10:delivers: capability:review-plan-producible-evidence-classes\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:18:Stop the review planner from requiring evidence classes that no registered\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:20:truthfully instead of `pose review auto-attest` being the only path that\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:36:pose review attest: review tool validate (component site) requires evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:42:check does not have, or to run `pose review auto-attest`, which fills the gap\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:46:mechanism that completed a review was the fabricating one. A gate whose sole\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:49:produces are indistinguishable, in the record, from reviewed ones.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:52:project that owns its review profiles and reconciles the classes there still\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:72:- R1: A synthesised review tool shall take its evidence classes from the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:74:- R2: A review plan shall not carry an evidence class outside\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:87:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go` — `buildReviewTools`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:90:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:91:- renamed: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md -> .pose/changelogs/v1.7.12/pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:92:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:93:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:97:- capability:review-plan-producible-evidence-classes module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:143:Assert the invariant directly — no tool in a planned review may name a class\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:167:  fixture decoupled: it hardcoded `evidence:validation:review-plan` and built\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:178:- R1 [satisfied] <review_plan.go — profileEvidence(\"validate\") replaces the literal at both synthesis sites>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:179:- R2 [satisfied] <review_plan.go — producible() filters in add(), so every tool is covered, not just validate; asserted by TestReviewPlanToolsOnlyDemandProducibleEvidenceClasses>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:180:- R3 [satisfied] <a dropped class appends \"review tool X drops evidence class Y: no registered check may emit it\" to plan warnings, threaded through buildReviewTools into plan.Warnings>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:193:- [done] Apply the same producible filter to criterion evidence classes so auto-attest stops inventing refs. Delivered by `pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary` and the auto-attest specs after it, not by a filter: validateReviewContractRefs holds a schema-v2 criterion's classes to ValidEvidenceClasses, so `evidence class \"validation\" ... is not one a registered check may emit` refuses the profile at load, and both halves of auto-attest now refuse rather than invent a ref. Verified against the engine, not read. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-12-07)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md:194:- [open] Derive tool evidence classes from the module's registered checks once the planner can reach the matrix (owner:unowned crit:low review:2026-12-07)\n.pose/adr/2026-10-18-git-state-that-cannot-be-read-is-unknown-and-a-worktree-is-judged-by-its-content.md:18:  review worktree, and judged the run by `git status --porcelain` text: a path made\n.pose/adr/2026-10-18-git-state-that-cannot-be-read-is-unknown-and-a-worktree-is-judged-by-its-content.md:19:  `assume-unchanged` or `skip-worktree` by the reviewer, a link, or a quoted name could\n.pose/adr/2026-10-18-git-state-that-cannot-be-read-is-unknown-and-a-worktree-is-judged-by-its-content.md:21:- Any file under `.pose/indexes/`, `.pose/results/` or `.pose/review-bundles/` was\n.pose/adr/2026-10-18-git-state-that-cannot-be-read-is-unknown-and-a-worktree-is-judged-by-its-content.md:22:  \"derived\", so a review could rewrite the validation matrix or sealed evidence and still\n.pose/adr/2026-10-18-git-state-that-cannot-be-read-is-unknown-and-a-worktree-is-judged-by-its-content.md:34:D2. The review worktree is judged by content, not by Git's account of it:\n.pose/adr/2026-10-18-git-state-that-cannot-be-read-is-unknown-and-a-worktree-is-judged-by-its-content.md:41:and the policy are not regenerated by a review.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-18-git-state-that-cannot-be-read-is-unknown-and-a-worktree-is-judged-by-its-content.md:64:dispatch, if a review can rewrite the validation matrix, the policy or a sealed record and\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:22:O runtime opcional da fatia 1 passa a rodar, para quem pede, os checks de leitura do projeto (`review-check`, `closeout-check`, `artifact-check`, `surface-check`, `roadmap-check`), com resultado tipado e fallback standalone, e a guardar entre um comando e o seguinte a saída das leituras do Git que são funções puras de ids de objeto ou do commit do HEAD.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:26:Fatia 2 da B35 (emenda do ADR de 2026-11-09), reescrita pela medição que as duas specs de engine anteriores fizeram: o cache de grafos da B33 não ajudava (o custo estava em recalcular a vinculação das entradas e em rodar o Git duas vezes), e depois delas o `review-check` deste repositório leva cerca de 25 s, dos quais cerca de 14 s são os 242 `git log -1 -- <path>`. Um processo residente que guarda essas leituras, chaveadas pelo commit, responde o segundo `review-check` em cerca de 10 s, com a mesma saída.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:82:- [x] Medir: o segundo `review-check` no runtime contra standalone, com a saída comparada\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:111:- A medição (cerca de 25 s standalone, cerca de 10 s o segundo `review-check` no runtime, saída idêntica) foi feita à mão com o binário real, não num teste.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:120:O runtime hospeda `review-check`, `closeout-check`, `artifact-check`, `surface-check` e `roadmap-check` por `pose runtime run`, com resultado tipado, digest de ambiente, fallback standalone e sem repetir o que pode ter rodado (R7, R10), e guarda entre comandos as leituras puras do Git por commit (R5); o segundo `review-check` deste repositório levou cerca de 10 s contra cerca de 25 s standalone, com a mesma saída.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:127:- Result: registrado pela evidência de validação selada; revisão delegada independente concluída com `pose review conclude`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:135:- [open] Test the admission of a memo hit's bytes against an operation's input budget when the budget is nearly spent. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:136:- [done] Put the user and global Git configuration in the memo key (the key holds the digest of the effective configuration, read once per operation). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:137:- [covered: pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement] Admissão, orçamento e proteção das consultas curtas contra checks pesados, com medições fixadas (fatia 3, `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement`). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-1