d draft spec is reported as a delivery-contract error on every other spec (148 in this repository) instead of once on itself (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-10-13)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-release-doc-discovery-and-sbom-parser.md:76:Implementation validated and closed through the governed review gate on 2026-10-01. Canonical strict validation passed 48/48 checks at f41b5aa; review bundle `rvb-3b6f52e24b22f0d3` was fresh and approved before `pose close`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegation-task, pose-delegated-review-capability, pose-delegation-task-detach-and-state\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:41:- R4: A documentation check shall fail when an active document, skill or help text of the distribution names `pose review dispatch`, `pose review resume`, `pose review status` or a personal launcher, outside deprecation notes and historical records.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:72:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:74:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:75:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:76:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_task.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_task_detach_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_subject_capabilities_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:88:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegated_review_request_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:89:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegated_verdicts_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:90:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_routing_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:91:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:92:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:94:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_adapter_containment_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:95:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_attempt_ledger_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:96:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:97:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:98:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:107:- capability:delegation-task module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_task.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:111:Parity matrix schema 1 (`.pose/parity/delegation-launchers.json`); removal of `pose review dispatch|resume|status`, which now exit 2 naming their replacement; `pose delegate review|adjudicate|smoke` discloses the run's containment (`delegate.safety`, `safety` in `--json`); the `launcher-parity` check of the validation matrix.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:134:- Selected option: remove `pose review dispatch`, `resume` and `status` in this spec, so the release that carries the passing parity check is the one without them (the maintainer's decision of 2026-10-29)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:136:- Consequences: a user of 7.4.x who runs `pose review dispatch|resume|status` after the upgrade gets an unknown-command error with no release that printed a deprecation first; the changelog marks it breaking and names each replacement\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:147:- R1 [satisfied] check:launcher-parity test:TestLauncherParityMatrixCoversEveryLauncherCapability report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:badde66753299900be9f6d8f56b5ef8e346700a7 — `.pose/parity/delegation-launchers.json` schema 1 has one row per capability of the ADR's \"Retirement by parity\" section, 21 in all, each with its `pose delegate` command and covering tests.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:152:- R6 [satisfied] check:delegation-surface-integration test:TestTheRemovedReviewAliasesNameTheirReplacement test:TestAdapterContainmentCLIDisclosesItBeforeTheRun test:TestRunContinuityDoctorStatusAndPending report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:badde66753299900be9f6d8f56b5ef8e346700a7 — `pose review dispatch|resume|status` are removed in this spec, ahead of the release that carries it (D2); `pose delegate` keeps what they gave: the brief without an agent, containment before the run, a pending continuation answered with exit 0.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:158:Milestone `retirement` of roadmap `delegation`, on implementation head `badde66753299900be9f6d8f56b5ef8e346700a7`: the versioned parity matrix and its check (R1–R3), the active-document check (R4), the operator's retirement section (R5) and the removal of `pose review dispatch`, `resume` and `status` (R6, D2, the maintainer's decision of 2026-10-29: removed in this spec although no release printed their deprecation; the changelog marks it breaking). Closing the matrix took capabilities the launchers had and POSE lacked: `pose delegate task --session <id> --agent <name>` continues a session POSE never recorded, and the alias removal kept three guarantees of `dispatch` and `review resume` in `pose delegate` — the brief when no agent can run, the containment disclosed before a run starts, a reserved continuation answered as pending with exit 0. `.pose/parity/` is classified as review governance. `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch.go` is kept as the home of the removed aliases' answer rather than deleted: five done specs declare it as a current artifact, and POSE has no record of a later spec removing a file an earlier one created (a sealed first closeout, `rvb-b02c94d7b79d4088` and `rva-0b2e83cc88087b2b`, failed `check --strict` on its deletion and is kept as history). The personal launchers outside the repository are not touched: retiring them is the operator's step the manual describes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:160:Independent review: eight rounds by Codex `gpt-6.1-sol` (OpenAI, reasoning medium), a different vendor than the implementer Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic). Rounds 1–7 requested changes (PG-R1-01..10, R2-01..07, R3-01..03, R4-01..02, R5-01..03, R6-01..03, R7-01..03), each fixed in its own commit; most hardened the active-document reader, which ended reading Go strings through the type checker, under each release configuration's files as `go list` selects them. Round 8 approved. Reports are local review evidence under `/tmp/pose-roadmaps-evidence/parity/` (untracked); the native bundle and attestation are the sealed record.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:170:The check proves that a row's command and tests exist, not that they exercise the capability; review of the cited tests is the defence (corpus known-gap `parity-row-cites-an-unrelated-test`). The Go reader resolves constants within a package: a fragment imported from another package, text in a cgo preamble, and configurations the release does not build are not read (known gaps `imported-fragment-completes-a-replaced-command`, `cgo-preamble-text-reaches-usage`). Exact removal notes are an allowlist kept by hand.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:174:- [open] F1: harden the release-definition reader before the release adopts another representation or a source-selecting setting: reject every unmodelled line, multiline lists and empty dimensions, and model or refuse source-selecting environment variables and build directories (PG-R8-01, consolidating PG-R7-03). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:175:- [open] F2: detect incomplete package enumeration beyond what the gate refuses today, document vendor, nested-module and generated-source boundaries, and pin or validate the toolchain whose version tags select files (PG-R8-02). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:176:- [open] F3: read configurations the release does not build (other GOOS/GOARCH, custom tags) before shipping one, and check generated operator output (PG-R6-02). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:177:- [spawned: pose-delivery-later-removal] F5: let a done spec's `removed:` claim satisfy the existence of a path an earlier spec declared current, so removing a file does not require keeping it (`review_dispatch.go` here).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-parity-gate.md:178:- [open] F4: resolve string fragments imported from other packages of the module and add a reader or runtime check before a cgo preamble supplies operator text (PG-R5-02, PG-R5-03; corpus known gaps). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-federated-source-proof-is-computed-once-per-operation.md:7:depends_on: pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-federated-source-proof-is-computed-once-per-operation.md:96:- Context: o perfil da primeira chamada depois da spec `pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation` pôs cerca de 37 s em `federatedSourceProof`, com 64 provas e 39 distintas.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-federated-source-proof-is-computed-once-per-operation.md:147:- [open] F1: reduzir o custo de cada prova distinta, medido no mesmo perfil: verificação dos filhos do bundle (cerca de 8,5 s), parse e cópia do grafo de integridade (cerca de 8 s e 5,5 s), carga e validação da política de delegação (cerca de 4,3 s) e a sonda de grupo de processos `verifyReviewProcessGroup` a cada verificação (cerca de 4,3 s). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-24)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-public-claims-onboarding.md:147:- Context: review reproduced the printed command against a fresh install and it\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-public-claims-onboarding.md:234:- [open] Have the template's version_claims modes derive from the contract schema so a new mode cannot be documented in only one place (owner:unowned crit:low review:2026-12-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-extension-catalog-resolution.md:110:  instead of already sitting reviewed on disk (unlike a local package\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-2-release-readiness.md:6:depends_on: review-verify-retains-completed-scopes\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-2-release-readiness.md:20:closed scope's approval under `review verify` and federated acceptance.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-2-release-readiness.md:25:adoption gates, because every upstream review it consumes reads as unapproved after\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-2-release-readiness.md:27:have to pin an unreleased runtime or renew every upstream review.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-2-release-readiness.md:90:idempotent reapply and preservation.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-v6-0-2-release-readiness.md:150:closed scope's approval under `review verify` and federated acceptance.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-18-pose-closeout-read-view-covers-the-federated-corpus.md:87:- [open] F1: registrar o commit do motor, o digest do binário e os comandos exatos no relatório de medições na próxima regeneração. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-18)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-18-pose-closeout-read-view-covers-the-federated-corpus.md:88:- [open] F2: explicitar no ADR que a reprodução de provas e a pré-verificação da travessia do índice compartilham o teto de observações. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-18)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-scaffold-ships-a-neutral-dor-policy.md:26:On 2026-10-09 the maintainer adopted the Definition of Ready in pose-dist (`7eeca305`, configuration review of 7.1.0). `.pose/policy/dor.json` was still synced verbatim into the embedded scaffold, so the drift guard turned CI and Security red on main (red signals #136 and #137), and a regenerated scaffold would have shipped `adopted_at: 2026-10-09` to every new instance, gating its specs from another repository's date. `changelog.json`, `review.json` and `actions.json` had already been fixed the same way.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-scaffold-ships-a-neutral-dor-policy.md:53:No material decision: the file joins the existing self-referential list, as `changelog.json`, `review.json` and `actions.json` did.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-scaffold-ships-a-neutral-dor-policy.md:74:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-run-verification-pins-brief-inputs.md:21:Verify a delegated run's provenance against the brief inputs it was dispatched with, so records retained after the seal do not change the re-rendered brief and break verification of an approved run.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-run-verification-pins-brief-inputs.md:24:Retaining the exhausted attempts of an earlier bundle after a later bundle was approved made `review verify` fail with `run provenance: brief/template/notes/transmitted bytes differ`, because the previous-round section of the re-rendered brief changed. The records had to be kept outside the repository.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-run-verification-pins-brief-inputs.md:27:A brief must still be bound to what the reviewer actually received; only inputs recorded at dispatch may stand in for a re-render.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-run-verification-pins-brief-inputs.md:37:- R3: Retaining earlier bundles' runs after an approval shall leave `review verify` and `pose close` of the approved scope unchanged.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-material-equivalence-reuse.md:54:- R5: Closeout plan and review verify shall render reused/invalidated with input bindings.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-material-equivalence-reuse.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-material-equivalence-reuse.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-material-equivalence-reuse.md:151:Delivers per-criterion input contracts and the reuse explanation on verify. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-recoverable-closeout-plan.md:32:Recoverable operation with checkpoints and idempotent reapplication; no ACID promise\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-recoverable-closeout-plan.md:42:Publishing on spec close; auto-approving review or editing policy.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-recoverable-closeout-plan.md:52:- R1: `pose close spec:<slug> --plan` shall preview the ordered steps with reasons and the pending judgments; `--apply` executes mechanical steps; `--resume` continues from the last checkpoint.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-recoverable-closeout-plan.md:83:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-recoverable-closeout-plan.md:98:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-recoverable-closeout-plan.md:99:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_subject_capabilities_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-recoverable-closeout-plan.md:109:- Hidden automation surprising operators; preview first, explicit apply.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-recoverable-closeout-plan.md:154:- R1 [satisfied] surface:recoverable-closeout-plan evidence:integration test:TestClosePlanPreviewsWithoutWriting check:closeout-plan-integration test:TestAnInterruptedCloseoutResumesWithoutDuplication\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-recoverable-closeout-plan.md:165:Delivers close --plan, --apply and --resume with checkpoints. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-commit-gate-refuses-index-without-descriptor.md:25:O harne8 ficou meses com 113 avisos porque o commit `e1593bde` regenerou `spec-graph.json` e `roadmaps.json` sem o `generation.json`, e nada no gate disse isso: cada review closeout dizia só \"input closure is unknown\". O gate agora nomeia a causa no primeiro commit que a cria, e o remédio funciona (spec `pose-index-recovery-and-close-scope-consistency`).\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-commit-gate-refuses-index-without-descriptor.md:116:- Result: registrado pela evidência de validação selada; revisão delegada independente concluída com `pose review conclude`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-commit-gate-refuses-index-without-descriptor.md:123:- [open] Um `pose check` rodado enquanto o `pose index` publica pode ver uma divergência passageira e recomendar `pose index`: dar à mensagem o estado de publicação em andamento. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-commit-gate-refuses-index-without-descriptor.md:124:- [open] Um hook de commit do harne8 que rode o `pose` com os roots explícitos, para que os avisos `unknown-project` das xref para `proj.pose-dist` deixem de aparecer. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-retroactive-attribution-record.md:65:- Validate the full repository and request independent review.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-retroactive-attribution-record.md:94:The implementation verifies the maintainer's signature and applies the 19 historical dispositions. The independent review and CI are pending.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-changed-scope-validation.md:116:- [open] Seed dependsOn edges for this repository's real modules (pose-mcp, mcp-enforce) once cross-module coupling needs scoped validation. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-10-16)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-amendment-history-holds-before-close.md:26:On 2026-10-10 two specs (pose-dist's `pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records` and Harne8's `harne8-adopt-pose-v7-2-0`) recorded their first `pose amend` event as `semantic` or `added` with no baseline. Their atomic start records held a baseline, but the amendment log did not, so every node present since the start read as \"added without an amendment event\". The amendment gate in `lint-spec` runs only on done specs, so the failure appeared only after `pose close`, and an independent reviewer had to unwind an approved close.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-amendment-history-holds-before-close.md:59:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-amendment-history-holds-before-close.md:76:- [x] Separate review and native closeout.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-amendment-history-holds-before-close.md:83:- Knowledge: knowledge:adr-sealed-review-bundles-review, knowledge:pose-b07-implementation\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-amendment-history-holds-before-close.md:113:Implemented and natively closed on 2026-10-24 the existing R1–R3 as the prerequisite of B11, under current continuation authorization. Readonly context resolved `proj.pose-dist`; assessment freshness reused. The first amendment copies only recorded start state; existing journals stay append-only. Lint warns during execution and close checks before transition and again under the shared lifecycle lock. No release, policy adoption, parent gitlink update or remote publication. Final strict validation passed 151/151 at HEAD `8a35140`; sealed review and guarded closeout are recorded in [implementation evidence](../reports/2026-10-24-amendment-history-before-close.md).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-amendment-history-holds-before-close.md:117:Explicit `--baseline` retains its existing current-state semantics; review must judge materiality. Cooperative locking cannot prevent arbitrary filesystem edits. Append/Sync failure is surfaced without truncation; inspect partial journals explicitly. No journal remains opt-out. B11 still owns semantic terminal verification and plan/transport parity; this prerequisite does not claim that delivery.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-amendment-history-holds-before-close.md:123:- [open] Extend the generic adversarial corpus with first-amendment/start and preclose-history cases; permanent regression producer already covers R1–R3. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:2:slug: pose-milestone-review-proportional\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:11:delivers: capability:milestone-review-proportional\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:15:# Spec: Milestone review is proportional to its members\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:21:A milestone of one member is approved when its spec is, a milestone of several keeps its review, and an old roadmap can say why its milestones were not reviewed.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:25:Reviewing the 42 reached milestones took a night and 145 thousand lines of bundles, and 100 of the 133 milestones with members have one member, whose review repeats the review of its spec. The ADR `.pose/adr/2026-11-02-a-milestone-of-one-member-is-that-member.md` records why no condition is attached.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:29:- `review verify`, closeout, the review of a roadmap and the federated proof give one answer.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:30:- A negative review recorded on a milestone stands.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:31:- Edges still bind: a milestone inherits a review, not the acceptance of what it depends on.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:43:- R1: Under a review policy with bundles, a milestone with exactly one local member, closed and approved, whose federated acceptance holds, shall read approved and closed with no bundle of its own, and say where the approval comes from.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:44:- R2: A negative review recorded on such a milestone, in a bundle or a legacy attempt, or an attempt history that cannot be read, shall keep it unapproved, and a recorded approval shall stay as it is.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:45:- R3: A milestone with an external member or with several members shall owe its review as before.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:46:- R4: The review plan of an open spec that is the only member of a milestone of a live roadmap shall carry a required judgment criterion holding the exit gate of that milestone, one criterion per gate.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:47:- R5: A roadmap that declares `unreviewed_milestones` with a reason shall treat a milestone whose members are all terminal as standing, in verification and closeout, one member or many, with the reason sealed and readable in the bundle of the roadmap, whose own review stays required and is what an external consumer holds.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:48:- R6: The review of a roadmap shall seal over inherited and declared milestones, and `pose state --attention` shall not list them as reached, while a milestone that does not stand stays listed.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:56:- This drops a review, so it comes with an ADR. A milestone gains approval only from a closed, approved spec or from a reason the roadmap declares and its review seals.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:66:`internal/pose/review_bundle.go`, `internal/pose/review_plan.go`, `internal/pose/roadmaps.go`, `internal/pose/obligation_projection.go`, the closeout skill.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:70:- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:71:- created: .pose/starts/pose-milestone-review-proportional.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:72:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-milestone-review-proportional.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:75:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:76:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:87:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/milestone_review_proportional_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:89:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_approval_follows_children_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:90:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:95:- capability:milestone-review-proportional module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:99:`review verify` of a one-member milestone reports the bundle of its spec. Roadmap frontmatter gains `unreviewed_milestones`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:104:- [x] Carry the exit gate into the review of the spec\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:105:- [x] Let a roadmap declare unreviewed milestones\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:108:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:114:- Minimal option: reviewers attest one-member milestones in bulk\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:115:- Selected option: no review, as the ADR records\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:116:- Rationale: the review repeated its spec, and a condition on a declared check would have passed over the defect that argued for it\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:118:- Falsifier: a defect found in a one-member milestone that the review of its spec could not have seen, with its exit gate in hand\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:126:- Falsifier: a gate that a reviewer of the spec cannot judge\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:130:- Minimal option: review every old multi-member milestone\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:131:- Selected option: a reason declared in the roadmap and sealed by its review\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:132:- Rationale: an old roadmap needs an honest record, not a retroactive review\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:133:- Consequences: a roadmap can skip reviews by writing a reason, which its reviewer reads\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:144:- R1 [satisfied] capability:milestone-review-proportional evidence:integration check:milestone-review-proportional-integration test:TestOneMemberMilestoneInheritsItsSpec test:TestAMilestoneDoesNotInheritAnOpenOrUnapprovedSpec test:TestAnApprovedOpenSpecIsNotInherited test:TestAPolicyWithoutBundlesKeepsItsOwnAnswer test:TestAMilestoneInheritsNoAcceptance test:TestCloseOfAnInheritingMilestonesSpecNamesTheRoadmap report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:117c1c0068b7851841228686f6e0445640c4da08\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:145:- R2 [satisfied] check:milestone-review-proportional-integration test:TestANegativeReviewOfAMilestoneStands test:TestARecordedMilestoneApprovalStays test:TestARecordedLegacyRefusalStands report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:117c1c0068b7851841228686f6e0445640c4da08\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:146:- R3 [satisfied] check:milestone-review-proportional-integration test:TestOtherMilestonesOweTheirReview report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:117c1c0068b7851841228686f6e0445640c4da08\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:147:- R4 [satisfied] check:milestone-review-proportional-integration test:TestTheSpecAnswersForTheExitGate test:TestEachExitGateHasItsOwnCriterion report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:117c1c0068b7851841228686f6e0445640c4da08\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:148:- R5 [satisfied] check:milestone-review-proportional-integration test:TestARoadmapDeclaresUnreviewedMilestones test:TestTheReasonIsSealedByTheRoadmap test:TestARetainedRoadmapDoesNotCoverADeclarationItNeverRead test:TestADeclarationRescuesATerminalSingleton test:TestAnExternalConsumerHoldsTheRoadmapOfADeclaredMilestone report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:117c1c0068b7851841228686f6e0445640c4da08\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:149:- R6 [satisfied] check:milestone-review-proportional-integration test:TestRoadmapSealsOverInheritedMilestones test:TestRoadmapSealsOverADeclaredMilestone test:TestAttentionKeepsWhatDoesNotStand test:TestAttentionKeepsLegacyRefusals test:TestALegacyApprovalDoesNotEraseABundleRefusal test:TestALaterLegacyApprovalReplacesALegacyRefusal test:TestReachedListsAnUnapprovedSingleton report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:117c1c0068b7851841228686f6e0445640c4da08\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:155:A milestone of one local member has no review of its own: it stands on the closed, approved review of its spec, through the one verification that `review verify`, closeout, the review of a roadmap and the federated proof read, and `approval_origin` says so. It inherits a review and nothing else: its edges still have to hold, and a refusal recorded on it, in a bundle or a legacy attempt, stands. An open spec answers for the exit gate of its milestone. A roadmap can declare why old milestones stand unreviewed, and its bundle seals that reason, so a retained approval does not cover a declaration it never read. Of 171 milestone and roadmap scopes here, none fell and 16 rose, each judged correct by the reviewer. Independently reviewed by Codex in three rounds, which found ten blockers between them, from a failed acceptance erased by inheritance to a legacy approval hiding a recorded refusal.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:159:The review of a one-member milestone that happened to come later is gone, and the review of the roadmap is where a second look now belongs. The exit gate is a judgment, which a reviewer can answer as not applicable with a rationale. `pose state --attention` reads records and does not verify, so its list can differ from a verification on a stale approval. A policy without bundles keeps its own answer.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:163:- [open] F1: Add a representative cost measure of roadmap preparation, with distinct members and gates: reviewed sizes took up to two seconds and no budget exists (review R2-F2). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-milestone-review-proportional.md:164:- [open] F2: Add a milestone-gate case to the adversarial corpus and a journey test of the gate criterion on a fresh install (review R2-F3). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-suite-history-promise-per-step.md:56:Implementation validated and closed through the governed review gate on 2026-10-01. Canonical strict validation passed 48/48 checks at f41b5aa; review bundle `rvb-4c25f3ec247a586d` was fresh and approved before `pose close`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-validation-matrix-dead-test-patterns.md:25:`go test -run` exits 0 when a pattern, or one alternative of it, matches nothing, so a check that names a missing test reports evidence it never produced. On 2026-10-30 four checks carried such alternatives: `review-bundle-convergence` (`ReviewPlanActionableToolPhases`), `spec-authority-transfer-negative-gates` (`TestSpecTransferBoundary`), `material-reuse-integration` (`reuse`, which Go's case-sensitive match never hits) and `atomic-start-cutoff-integration` (`PreviewStart`, `ApplyStart`, names of production methods, not tests). Four of them were never test names; their intended coverage is already matched by other alternatives of the same checks.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-validation-matrix-dead-test-patterns.md:83:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-validation-matrix-dead-test-patterns.md:95:- R1 [satisfied] check:test test:TestValidationMatrixRunPatternsNameExistingTests report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:5d2e5d87e45dcaec699f986b663336b448e88f90 — The five dead alternatives are gone; each of the four checks selects the same tests as before (52, 9, 17, 3), confirmed independently by the reviewer.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-validation-matrix-dead-test-patterns.md:103:Five -run alternatives that named no test removed from four checks, and a source-level guard that keeps new ones out under a narrow, explicitly modelled grammar and refuses the rest. Independently reviewed by Codex over eight rounds (203 differential cases against `go test` in the last sweeps; reports kept outside the checkout).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-validation-matrix-dead-test-patterns.md:107:The guard judges declarations, not runs: `pose-validate-refuses-empty-go-checks` fails at run time a check of which Go reports that no test ran, while skips, `-short`, `TestMain` control flow and dynamic subtests stay unjudged. Two review fixtures fail outside a Git repository ancestry (F1).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-validation-matrix-dead-test-patterns.md:111:- [open] F1: make the review-bundle fixtures (`componentReviewFixture`, `reviewBundleFixture`) initialise their own Git repository, so `review-bundle-convergence` and `material-reuse-integration` do not depend on an enclosing repository of the temporary directory (reviewer F4, rounds 1–2). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-13)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:7:depends_on: pose-abm-progressive-review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:21:and `structural-causality`, which its reviews have been sealed under since the ABM\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:48:`engineering-judgment`, `high-criticality-review` or `structural-materiality`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:71:- modified: .pose/policy/review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:76:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.pose/policy/review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:93:`pose-abm-progressive-review`, which is closed and whose sealed review is bound to\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:107:| Adoption recorded | `pose update --no-self` then read `.pose/policy/review.json` | Both contracts dated 2026-09-20 |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:109:| Overlays and closeouts intact | `pose closeout-check spec:<done-slug>` | `review_approved=true`, `terminal=true` |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:110:| Previous engine reads it | `pose review-plan <scope>` with the installed 5.0.8 binary | Exit 0 with a resolved plan |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:123:- `overlay_profiles` unchanged at `backend-review@1`, `frontend-review@1`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:124:- `pose-abm-progressive-review`, `pose-abm-structural-delta` and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:125:  `pose-abm-review-soundness` all report `review_approved=true` and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:127:- The installed 5.0.8 binary resolves a review plan against the reordered policy,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:136:`review-check` fresh and approved; `closeout-check` terminal.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:157:- R1 [satisfied] `.pose/policy/review.json` carries `explicit_judgment_adopted_at`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:162:  `review_approved=true` and `terminal=true`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:163:- R4 [satisfied] the installed 5.0.8 binary resolves a review plan against the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:171:This repository now declares the two contracts its reviews were already sealed\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:179:recording the adoption here. `.pose/policy/review.json` is not in\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:180:`SelfReferentialPolicyFiles`, so this repository's live review policy is the template\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:182:`component_aware_adopted_at: 2026-08-13`, `review_bundles_adopted_at: 2026-08-14` and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption.md:189:`review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances`, which also explains why the neutral\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-governed-effect-enforcement.md:55:- R5: Preview modes shall report the would-be refusal with reason codes and write nothing.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-governed-effect-enforcement.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-governed-effect-enforcement.md:85:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-governed-effect-enforcement.md:157:- R3 [satisfied] test:TestAStartPreviewTakenBeforeARequestIsStaleAtApply check:governed-effects-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-governed-effect-enforcement.md:159:- R5 [satisfied] <the fresh preview reports action-request-pending and writes nothing> test:TestAStartPreviewTakenBeforeARequestIsStaleAtApply check:governed-effects-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-governed-effect-enforcement.md:165:Delivers opt-in enforcement of action request effects on close, start apply and release prepare. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-continue-delegated-runs-under-one-immutable-attempt.md:1:# ADR: Continue delegated runs under one immutable attempt\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-continue-delegated-runs-under-one-immutable-attempt.md:4:Accepted (2026-10-25), spec `pose-delegated-review-run-continuity`.\n.pose/adr/2026-10-25-continue-delegated-runs-under-one-immutable-attempt.md:15:Interrupted drafts remain partial and cannot authorize review effects. Attempts and resumes have separate counters. Wait only for a declared bounded reset, with bounded jitter and no vendor polling; revalidate after the wait. Explicit cross-adapter dispatch carries `limit-of:<run>` and discloses both runs. Filesystem/Git anchors remain the ledger trust boundary. A claim without a result remains an explicit incomplete operation; restarting the same predecessor never launches another process. Rejected alternatives: a reason-bearing new attempt double-counts recovery; mutable predecessor updates erase evidence; automatic vendor fallback changes declared independence.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-residual-triage-and-risk-acceptance.md:6:depends_on: pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read, pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof, pose-writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication, pose-residual-nature-commitment-and-effect, pose-open-backlog-reconciliation\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-residual-triage-and-risk-acceptance.md:33:- R2: Projetar preview por item/intenção com estado antes/depois, razão, evidência pertinente, autoridade, compromisso/efeito e gatilho de reconsideração. Reusar fontes canônicas e B24; candidato sem decisão adequada permanece aberto, inclusive destino done inadequado ou evidência incompleta. Não criar backlog paralelo ou spec por TODO.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-residual-triage-and-risk-acceptance.md:34:- R3: Aplicar somente decisões explicitamente sustentadas pela autoridade e evidência exigidas para seu escopo. Revalidar snapshot/diff/inputs e autorização vigente antes do writer; mudança concorrente recusa aplicação stale com diagnóstico. Preview não altera fontes, commitments ou dispositions.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-residual-triage-and-risk-acceptance.md:39:- R8: Qualificar preview/apply, concorrência, replay, erro parcial e risco vencido em CLI/MCP usando mesmo domínio; preservar layouts flat/folder, aliases/proveniência e coverage de fontes. Inventariar contratos/schemas/compatibilidade antes do código; nenhuma consulta escreve triagem ou eleva candidato a decisão.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-residual-triage-and-risk-acceptance.md:86:| V3 — Preview e fonte alterada entre preview/apply | Zero writes no preview; conflito stale recusado sem overwrite. |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:2:slug: pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:6:depends_on: pose-abm-review-soundness\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:10:delivers: contract:review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:14:# Spec: The review bundle seals evidence for the components its plan validates\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:19:Make a sealed review bundle carry the current validation evidence of every\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:25:`conductor` and also changes `harness`, `contracts` and `scripts`. Its review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:30:`review verify` blocked on \"cites evidence from conductor\". A multi-component\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:31:spec with one target could not be reviewed honestly, and the only way out was\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:50:`pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go` (`reviewBundleEvidence`).\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:53:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:54:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:55:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:56:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:59:- contract:review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence module:pose-mcp profile:api-contract entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:62:Pass the plan to `reviewBundleEvidence` and add the components of its\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:65:may add evidence, which supersedes its review until it is reattested.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:72:- [x] Run the matrix, review and close.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:77:the modules it will hold the reviewer to, so those are the modules whose\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:78:evidence the reviewer must be able to cite.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:85:| Harne8 consumer | `pose review bundle spec:harne8-abm-governed-execution --json` | Evidence from conductor, contracts, harness and scripts. |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:106:A review bundle seals the current evidence of the modules its plan validates\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-review-bundle-seals-planned-component-evidence.md:112:supersedes its review until reattested.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-project-id-from-any-directory-name.md:154:2026-09-29, review. Reading the diff against the install path found two gaps in the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-project-id-from-any-directory-name.md:168:`agent:claude-opus-5-5`, approved with five explicit judgments; `review-check`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-extension-signing-clean-tree.md:155:- [covered: pose-release-clean-tree-attribution] Make the release workflow fail loudly and early on an unexpectedly dirty tree, naming the step that dirtied it, instead of letting goreleaser report it after the expensive gates have already run. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-02)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-launch-proof-demo.md:138:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-06-pose-launch-proof-demo.md:142:- [open] Record the demo from `examples/demo/record.sh`, trimmed under 60 seconds, so it can be embedded (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-01)\n.pose/adr/2026-09-07-one-canonical-documentation-address.md:42:   non-canonical host, so the split cannot silently reappear.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-07-one-canonical-documentation-address.md:68:*abandon* rather than to adopt. It also scales: `docs.harne8.com/POSE/`,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-parity-reads-the-cli-surface.md:182:- R5 [satisfied] <loadCLISurface fails when `check`, `review` or `release` is absent, or when review or release yield no subcommands>\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-verifier-extension-install-cwd.md:128:  only the install leg failing. The block review also removed a dead assignment\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-verifier-extension-install-cwd.md:167:  different mistake. The block is now small and reviewed, but the pattern says\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-verifier-extension-install-cwd.md:172:- [done] `pose extension install` takes no target directory and silently uses the current one. It caused a manual mis-install and then this gate defect. Consider an explicit target argument. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-02)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-review-run-provenance\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-dispatch, pose-native-attestation-issuer, pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read, pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof, pose-historical-trust-and-review-reuse, pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:12:delivers: capability:delegated-run-provenance\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:21:Satisfy `different-actor` for a delegated review from evidence — the run record — instead of the `agent:independent-` reviewer prefix.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:25:Under declared assurance the engine accepts `different-actor` when the reviewer is named `agent:independent-…`; on 2026-10-09 the reviewing agent had to adopt that literal prefix to be accepted. Anyone can type it, and the engine's own comment calls it a declaration.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:27:Origin: the 2026-10-09 review of `pose-native-attestation-issuer` by Codex through a personal launcher; it found three real defects in three rounds and exposed what the engine lacks (ADR `2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter`, roadmap `delegated-review`).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:31:Honest labelling: a machine-attested run is disclosed as such, never as a person. The contract and delegated adapter ADR are accepted. Implementation authorized by continuation on 2026-10-25, baseline `3e4c26d`. Preserve existing R1–R4 and add the prospective P1–P6 deltas as R5–R10 before start; do not adopt the capability, authenticate a person or apply a draft automatically here.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:38:- R2: An attestation produced from a run shall reference the run; the verifier shall read the reviewer's vendor and model from the referenced run record.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:39:- R3: `different-actor` shall be satisfied by a run whose vendor or model differs from the implementation principal's declared vendor and model, per the contract spec's answer; the `agent:independent-` prefix shall no longer satisfy it in instances that adopt `delegated-review`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:40:- R4: Review assurance shall disclose a run-backed review as `machine-attested`, distinct from `declared` and from a person's signed confirmation.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:43:- R6: A verifier shall require explicit executor-attested trust and known normalized implementation/reviewer vendor/model, disclose their source, and never present a signed executor declaration as a vendor receipt or cognitive independence.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:44:- R7: A proof shall distinguish the brief body and exact transmitted bytes, raw and redacted transcript/output digests, and output completeness; incomplete or truncated output shall not establish a completed review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:47:- R10: Domain, CLI, MCP, verify and Attention shall share proof/disclosure for same vendor/model, differing model or vendor, prefix-only, unknown baseline and tampered issuer/config/output cases; machine-attested review shall never satisfy a human requirement.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:57:- created: .pose/adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:62:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:65:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:66:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:74:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:75:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:77:- created: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_assurance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:82:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:83:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:84:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:85:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:86:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:87:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:88:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:94:- capability:delegated-run-provenance module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:107:- ADR: [Native signed run proofs](../adr/2026-10-25-bind-delegated-review-authority-to-native-signed-run-proofs.md)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:108:- Knowledge: knowledge:review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof, knowledge:adr-sealed-review-bundles-review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:110:- Rationale: Signing post-hoc configuration cannot prove which inputs the executor used; a reviewer prefix cannot authenticate separation.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:111:- Consequences: Legacy runs remain declared. Explicit opt-in requires proof for different-actor agent reviews; catalog adoption and governed draft application remain later capability scope.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-run-provenance.md:117:Adversarial tests: a prefix-only reviewer is refused under the capability; a run by the implementer's own model is refused; a tampered run record fails its signature.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-agency-readiness-pilot.md:82:- modified: .pose/policy/review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-agency-readiness-pilot.md:162:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-agency-readiness-pilot.md:166:- [open] Run the slice as a person in pose-dist and record the friction in this report before any adoption beyond pose-dist and Harne8 (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-05)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-agency-readiness-pilot.md:167:- [spawned: pose-attention-within-a-second] Bring Attention close to its 1 s target on large corpora; Harne8 reads take 30 to 37 s (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-22)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-agency-readiness-pilot.md:168:- [open] Exercise authority transfer with an open action request under the adopted capability (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-15)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-dependency-digest-pinning.md:39:hiding. `actions/dependency-review-action@v5`, set by the Node 24 bump earlier\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-dependency-digest-pinning.md:48:  version comment is unreviewable.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-dependency-digest-pinning.md:55:  decision with its own review burden.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-dependency-digest-pinning.md:76:- Readability is preserved by the version comment; a reviewer never has to\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-dependency-digest-pinning.md:89:  referenced tag resolved to at pin time, except `dependency-review-action`,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-dependency-digest-pinning.md:190:  packages pinned. `actions/dependency-review-action@v5` did not resolve — no\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-dependency-digest-pinning.md:242:- [covered: pose-dependency-pin-refresh] Decided: Dependabot, not a warning check — a check that reports a stale pin only moves the manual edit that already was not happening. Original item: digest pins do not refresh themselves: upstream security fixes now arrive only when someone updates a SHA by hand, and nothing reports that a pin has fallen behind. Decide between Dependabot on the actions and Docker ecosystems, or a check that compares each pin against its tag's current target and warns. This is the cost this spec deliberately accepted and it should not stay unmanaged. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-02)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-dependency-digest-pinning.md:243:- [open] Nothing verifies that the version comment beside a SHA names the version that SHA actually is, so a wrong comment misleads every future reviewer while the pin itself stays valid. The same resolution the `pose-action-runtime-currency-gate` draft needs would settle this too — consider folding the two checks together rather than building both. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-release-boundary-rehearsal.md:32:`contract_adoptions` to the review policy, which v1.8.1 refused outright: its\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-release-boundary-rehearsal.md:61:  load a review policy this engine writes.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-release-boundary-rehearsal.md:173:- Decision: `review-plan` against a scope that does not exist.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-release-boundary-rehearsal.md:178:  `review-plan` loads the policy before resolving the scope, so it reaches the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-release-boundary-rehearsal.md:209:  previous tag fails with `invalid schema-v2 review policy: json: unknown field\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-release-boundary-rehearsal.md:242:- [open] Consider asserting the archive layout against what `.goreleaser.yaml` actually produces, rather than against the name `extractPoseBinary` expects — the fixture and the extractor agree by construction here (owner:unowned crit:low review:2026-12-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-review-contract\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:15:# Spec: Delegated review contract\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:21:Accept the delegated-review ADR with the maintainer's answers to its four open decisions, and reconcile the roadmap's specs with them before any implementation.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:25:The ADR proposes that a delegated reviewer is an adapter turning a sealed bundle into a draft. Four choices change what the later specs build: who records the attestation, whether an agent run can satisfy `different-actor`, whether a different vendor is required, and the initial scope.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:27:Origin: the 2026-10-09 review of `pose-native-attestation-issuer` by Codex through a personal launcher; it found three real defects in three rounds and exposed what the engine lacks (ADR `2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter`, roadmap `delegated-review`).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:39:- R3: Each spec of roadmap `delegated-review` shall be amended where an answer differs from the assumption it was written under, before it starts.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:49:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:50:- created: .pose/adr/2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:51:- created: .pose/roadmaps/delegated-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:52:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-review-contract.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:53:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:54:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:55:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:67:The contract is ADR `2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter`, accepted on 2026-10-09 with the maintainer's decisions: the engine records a verified run, people by exception through policy, agent independence by differing vendor or model (different vendor preferred), and reviews, adjudications and smoke runs from the first delivery.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-contract.md:79:- R3 [satisfied] evidence:manual <brief R4/R6, dispatch R5/R7, capability R4-R7 amended to the answers before any spec started; brief R4 corrected after the independent review found it still let the reviewer record>\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-extension-catalog-lifecycle.md:124:- [spawned: pose-machinery-distribution-contract] Publish a first real, signed reference extension (e.g. a community skill) end-to-end through the release-signing pipeline to prove the full chain outside unit tests. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-extension-catalog-lifecycle.md:125:- [spawned: pose-machinery-distribution-contract] Consider a lightweight `pose extension search <catalog-dir>` once a first real catalog directory convention is adopted by an operator. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-18)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-check-worker-count-is-the-machines.md:70:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-check-worker-count-is-the-machines.md:145:Sealing the review then refused, and the refusal was correct: `unclassified review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-check-worker-count-is-the-machines.md:163:`review-check` fresh and approved; `closeout-check` terminal. `surface-check --strict`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-check-worker-count-is-the-machines.md:182:  lives in now classifies as governance so a spec that changes it can be reviewed\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-check-worker-count-is-the-machines.md:201:  cores (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-21)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-mcp-protocol-completeness.md:118:- [open] Revisit the resources/prompts boundary only if a concrete, ADR-worthy use case emerges (e.g. an approved semantic-search adapter) — do not extend it incrementally. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:7:depends_on: pose-review-assurance-disclosure, pose-obligation-contract\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:53:- R1: The corpus shall include the 6.3.0 `human:oseias` attestations and fail if any render reads as human review while the schema stays valid.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:57:- R5: Each new gate added by this program shall add its cheapest-formal-satisfaction case to the corpus before its spec closes; the review template gains that question for governance changes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:75:Test corpus under pose testdata, review template for governance changes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:82:- modified: .agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:83:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:93:The review template planned in the draft (`.pose/templates/review.md`) is the\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:94:parsed legacy review-attempt format, so the cheapest-formal-satisfaction\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:95:question went into the review skill instead, where governance changes are\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:96:reviewed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:148:- R4 [satisfied] <cases drive refusals and recovery: declined-approval-satisfies, closeout-plan-fills-judgment, stale-preview-authorizes-apply> test:TestAdversarialCorpus check:adversarial-corpus\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:149:- R5 [satisfied] <one case per later gate; the cheapest-formal-satisfaction question is in the pose-review skill> test:TestAdversarialCorpus check:adversarial-corpus test:TestDelegatedCorpusCasesStillExist check:adversarial-corpus-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:153:Seven cases were added for the gates delivered later in the program (R5): a stale start preview, a code change that keeps a judgment, a minimal surface without trace, a stale assessment, an unpinned and a calendar premise trigger (all enforced), and an unobserved falsifier check (known-gap). The transfer gate's case is `delegated` to `TestTransferRefusesARequestOpenedAfterThePreview`, whose fixture lives in the pose package; the corpus checks that the test still exists. Disabling the premise validation made both premise cases fail, as they must.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus.md:157:Delivers the corpus with one case per gate of the program, including delegated and known-gap cases. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/adr/2026-11-14-governance-association-links-are-read-with-a-commonmark-parser.md:8:Spec `pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit` (R3) makes a roadmap's\n.pose/adr/2026-11-14-governance-association-links-are-read-with-a-commonmark-parser.md:9:closeout review depend on its ADR associations: `adrs:` on the roadmap,\n.pose/adr/2026-11-14-governance-association-links-are-read-with-a-commonmark-parser.md:62:  drops but makes ordinary prose and examples require review, and still\n.pose/adr/2026-11-14-governance-association-links-are-read-with-a-commonmark-parser.md:76:- Follow-up F6 of the closeout review policy spec (links shown as code\n.pose/adr/2026-11-14-governance-association-links-are-read-with-a-commonmark-parser.md:79:  contract and is reviewed as one.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-specs-ergonomics-and-discovery.md:42:- R5: Update `review_bundle.go`, `check.go`, and `lintspec.go` to seamlessly classify and validate date-prefixed and flat spec layouts.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-authority-claim-project-is-not-the-audience.md:8:remediates: spec:pose-abm-review-authority@defect-fix\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-authority-claim-project-is-not-the-audience.md:22:Give the two bindings of a signed authority claim their own meaning: `project` names the project the decision governs and is compared with a new `authority_project` in the review policy; `audience` names the verifier installation meant to accept it and stays compared with `authority_audience`. Both review claims and action-request claims follow the same rule.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-authority-claim-project-is-not-the-audience.md:26:pose-abm-review-authority left open that `Project` and `Audience` were both compared with `authority_audience`, so one field was redundant and a claim could not say which project it governs apart from which verifier it was issued to. With one Harne8 installation serving several projects, the audience is shared, and only a project binding stops a claim issued for one project from being replayed in another. No instance has adopted `verified`, and the Harne8 issuer is not built yet, so 7.0.0 is the moment to settle the contract it will implement. The maintainer chose this in Decision 5 (A-extended, alternative b).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-authority-claim-project-is-not-the-audience.md:30:The project binding comes from the review policy, which the protected baseline covers, never from the environment or the directory name, which a verifier run can change. Verified mode stays opt-in.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-authority-claim-project-is-not-the-audience.md:40:- R1: The review policy shall accept `authority_project`; verified identity assurance shall require it to be a valid project id, as it requires `authority_audience`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-authority-claim-project-is-not-the-audience.md:41:- R2: A review authority claim shall be refused when its `project` differs from `authority_project` or its `audience` differs from `authority_audience`, each with its own reason; a claim whose project and audience are both right shall pass.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-authority-claim-project-is-not-the-audience.md:42:- R3: An action-request claim shall follow the same rule, and shall be refused when the review policy declares no `authority_project`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-authority-claim-project-is-not-the-audience.md:61:Review policy reader, review authority verification, action-request claim verification, manuals.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-authority-claim-project-is-not-the-audience.md:67:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-authority-claim-project-is-not-the-audience.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-authority-claim-project-is-not-the-audience.md:70:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_authority_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-authority-claim-project-is-not-the-audience.md:92:Signed fixture claims for review and action requests with the right binding, a foreign project under the same audience, and a foreign audience; a verified policy without `authority_project`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:2:slug: pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:9:delivers: contract:review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:24:Prevents a single corrupted or modified review artifact from poisoning review verification, closeout checks, and status reporting for all other unrelated specs in the project.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:37:- R3: `ListReviewAttempts(scope)` shall skip unmatching scope review attempts on parse errors when `scope != \"\"`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:48:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:49:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:50:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:51:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:54:- contract:review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing module:pose-mcp profile:api-contract entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:61:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:62:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:63:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:64:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:83:- R1 [satisfied] contract:review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing check:isolation test:TestListReviewBundlesScopeIsolationFromUnrelatedCorruptedBundle evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:84:- R2 [satisfied] contract:review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing check:isolation test:TestListReviewBundlesScopeIsolationFromUnrelatedCorruptedBundle evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:85:- R3 [satisfied] contract:review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing check:isolation test:TestReviewVerifyScopeIsolationFromUnrelatedCorruptedBundle evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:92:- contract:review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing -> pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:102:- Scoped review bundle, attestation, and attempt listing functions isolate parse and integrity errors to the affected scope.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing.md:103:- Unrelated specs retain fully independent review verification and closeout.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-instance-engine-version-tracking.md:175:`projectRootAt(dir)` that `projectRoot()` itself now delegates to) and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-policy-keys-and-release-surface-coverage.md:29:for the review policy, because that is where the decoder had to be relaxed. The\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-policy-keys-and-release-surface-coverage.md:84:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go` — the derivation helper\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-policy-keys-and-release-surface-coverage.md:96:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-policy-keys-and-release-surface-coverage.md:100:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-09-07-pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-policy-keys-and-release-surface-coverage.md:157:  change nobody can review.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-policy-keys-and-release-surface-coverage.md:195:- R1 [satisfied] <policyKeyChecks holds review, delivery, artifacts, capabilities, docs, release and state to keys taken from their own structs by PolicyKnownKeys; TestDoctorReportsUnreadKeysInEveryModelledPolicy fires one warn per file> surface:policy-keys-and-release-surface-coverage evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-policy-keys-and-release-surface-coverage.md:219:- [done] Give changelog.json and dor.json named policy types, and reconcile what they ship with what is read. Done in `pose-changelog-and-dor-policy-types`: `categories` now governs the valid set in all three places it was written out, dor.json ships an explicit empty `adopted_at` saying the gate is opt-in, and both are held to their keys — the exemption list is empty (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-12-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-policy-keys-and-release-surface-coverage.md:220:- [done] Cover the remaining command surfaces the audit found at zero: review-check, history-check, docs-sync, docs-review, contribute-submit, roadmap-check and the spec-readiness helpers in check.go. Done in `pose-remaining-command-surfaces-coverage`: all twelve off zero, `internal/cli` 71.2% to 72.9%, and the roadmap-check fixture surfaced an early return that makes the gate report zero criteria and pass — recorded there as crit:high (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-12-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:2:slug: pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:8:components: cli, pose, review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:9:delivers: surface:review-policy-v2-migration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:19:1. Ensure `pose update` idempotently migrates managed review policy (`.pose/policy/review.json`) and review profiles from schema v1 to schema v2 (`component_aware: true`, `review_bundles: true`, typed overlay profiles).\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:20:2. Ensure engine component discovery remains active for path classification during review bundle preparation even when a repository is on a schema v1 policy.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:21:3. Ensure `pose review verify` honors `review_bundles=false` and recorded reviews (`pose review record`) consistently with `pose review-check` and `pose close`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:24:Prevents legitimate subproject paths from being rejected as unclassified on older repositories or when review bundles are disabled, and ensures smooth, automated upgrades to schema-v2 review policies.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:27:- Zero breaking changes to existing review commands.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:35:- R1: `cmdUpdate` and `seedAbsentInstanceConfig` shall idempotently upgrade `.pose/policy/review.json` from schema_version 1 to 2, enabling `component_aware` and `review_bundles`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:36:- R2: `cmdUpdate --dry-run` shall report when a review policy migration from v1 to v2 is pending.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:37:- R3: `reviewBundleSubject` shall resolve discovered repository components when `plan.Components` is empty, ensuring legitimate subproject paths are classified as `implementation`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:38:- R4: `VerifyReviewBundle` shall check recorded reviews via `ReviewCheck` when `policy.ReviewBundles == false` and no sealed bundles exist, reporting state `ready-to-close` / `closed` appropriately.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:51:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:52:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:55:- surface:review-policy-v2-migration module:pose-mcp profile:cli-surface entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:64:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:65:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:68:- [x] Increment 1: Keep component discovery active in `reviewBundleSubject` (R3).\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:69:- [x] Increment 2: Support `review_bundles=false` and recorded reviews in `VerifyReviewBundle` (R4).\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:71:- [x] Increment 4: Add regression tests for policy migration and recorded review verification (R1, R4).\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:83:- R1 [satisfied] surface:review-policy-v2-migration check:delivery-integration test:TestUpdateMigratesReviewPolicySchemaV1ToV2 evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:84:- R2 [satisfied] surface:review-policy-v2-migration check:delivery-integration test:TestUpdateMigratesReviewPolicySchemaV1ToV2 evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:85:- R3 [satisfied] surface:review-policy-v2-migration check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewBundleSubjectClassification evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:86:- R4 [satisfied] surface:review-policy-v2-migration check:delivery-integration test:TestPoseCloseWithLiveGitTrailerNoReport evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:93:- surface:review-policy-v2-migration -> pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:103:- Implemented `migrateInstanceReviewPolicy` in `cmdUpdate` and `seedAbsentInstanceConfig` to upgrade schema v1 review policies to v2.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:104:- Added dry-run notification for pending review policy migrations.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:105:- Kept component discovery active in `reviewBundleSubject` for path classification on v1 policies.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-policy-v2-migration-and-verify-compat.md:106:- Updated `VerifyReviewBundle` to evaluate recorded reviews via `ReviewCheck` when bundles are disabled.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-component-evidence-is-not-inherited-upward.md:79:- modified: .pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-component-evidence-is-not-inherited-upward.md:118:  contained directory does not). Recorded as an amendment to the sealed review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-component-evidence-is-not-inherited-upward.md:181:- [done] Have a check declare the subtree it actually walked, so containment is read from the run rather than inferred from the module path — it is the durable answer to both directions, and the downward one is still an inference. Answered in two steps rather than one. `pose-report-coverage-that-rests-on-inference` makes the inference visible now, at no cost and refusing nothing; the declared-subtree contract is deferred with its four approaches recorded in the ADR amendment, because this repository offers no case to calibrate it against — every match here is by equality or by the root. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2027-01-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-dispatch\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:12:delivers: capability:delegated-attempt-ledger\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:15:# Spec: Every delegated review attempt stays on the record\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:21:Keep every delegated review run, rejections included, so a review cannot be retried until it approves.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:25:Nothing on 2026-10-09 would have stopped the implementer from discarding the reviewer's \"changes required\" and running another reviewer. The three rejections that found real defects were valuable precisely because they stood.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:27:Origin: the 2026-10-09 review of `pose-native-attestation-issuer` by Codex through a personal launcher; it found three real defects in three rounds and exposed what the engine lacks (ADR `2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter`, roadmap `delegated-review`).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:31:Append-only; no command deletes or rewrites a run. The delegated review contract is done and the ADR's maintainer decisions are accepted. This scope does not adopt delegated-review, authenticate adapter identity or apply a draft as an attestation. Implementation authorized by continuation on 2026-10-25, baseline `2c0bb3e`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:37:- R1: Runs under `.pose/review-runs/` shall be append-only and content-addressed, and `pose history-check` shall treat a rewritten or deleted run as a violation.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:39:- R3: `pose review verify` shall disclose earlier rejecting runs for the same scope next to the approving one.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:50:- created: .pose/adr/2026-10-25-reserve-delegated-attempts-before-launch-and-witness-immutable-runs.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:55:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:58:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:59:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:72:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_attempt_ledger_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:74:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:75:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:77:- created: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/review_attempt_ledger_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:79:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:80:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:82:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:88:- capability:delegated-attempt-ledger module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:101:- ADR: [Durable attempts and immutable witnesses](../adr/2026-10-25-reserve-delegated-attempts-before-launch-and-witness-immutable-runs.md)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:102:- Knowledge: knowledge:pose-b07-implementation, knowledge:adr-sealed-review-bundles-review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger.md:132:Implemented durable ordinal reservations, immutable run witnesses, rerun admission, verify disclosure and declared draft metrics across text/JSON/HTML/MCP. No delegated-review policy, vendor identity proof, automatic attestation, run continuation or adapter containment is adopted. Native close completed on 2026-10-25 after 153/153 canonical checks, artifact reconciliation (35/35), composition with zero findings, and approved attestation `rva-83cfa3925739793c` on bundle `rvb-da193121009a577e`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-spec-format-migration-command.md:23:3. **Idempotence & Predictability**: `--dry-run` previews every file move, and already-migrated specs are detected and skipped without errors.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-qualified-artifact-resolution.md:64:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-qualified-artifact-resolution.md:85:- created: .pose/reports/2026-09-21-qualified-artifact-resolution-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-qualified-artifact-resolution.md:102:Version new metadata through existing schema/capability mechanisms. Preview\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-qualified-artifact-resolution.md:117:- [x] Obtain explicit review and guarded closeout; no additional follow-ups; refresh assessments as the closeout operation.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-qualified-artifact-resolution.md:123:- Prefer the existing Store/roots/review contracts over a second authority or resolver.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-qualified-artifact-resolution.md:147:- `pose review verify spec:pose-qualified-artifact-resolution` and `pose closeout-check spec:pose-qualified-artifact-resolution` before `pose close spec:pose-qualified-artifact-resolution`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-qualified-artifact-resolution.md:179:- R8 [satisfied] TestQualifiedArtifactTypedRoadmapsAndContractNegotiation proves opt-in schema 3/version 1 and rejects unsupported metadata. Installed pose 5.0.8 was exercised on an isolated schema-3 fixture and refused it with unsupported review policy schema 3; historical policies/bundles are untouched.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-qualified-artifact-resolution.md:189:[technical review](../reports/2026-09-21-qualified-artifact-resolution-review.md).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-governed-capabilities-default-on-new-instances.md:22:Ship agency readiness, contract nodes, atomic start and causality closeout (with the structural overlay) adopted in every new instance, dated the day it was installed, and give an existing instance one command to turn each on or off with its adoption date instead of editing the review policy by hand.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-governed-capabilities-default-on-new-instances.md:26:The maintainer decided, while resolving the adoption requests of pose-abm-capability-adoption, that these capabilities are the product's default and not a per-repository experiment: a new project should start governed by them, while a project already under way decides when, so nothing it has in flight is re-judged. Today the distributed review policy adopts none of them, so the decisions recorded for pose-dist reach no other project, and adopting one by hand means knowing which version key, date key and overlay entry go together.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-governed-capabilities-default-on-new-instances.md:30:Install adopts only when the review policy did not exist before that install; `pose update` never adopts anything, including when it seeds a missing policy. Every date is the instance's own. The distributed policy file stays neutral: the adoption is an install-time decision that is logged, not a file that carries another repository's choices. Turning a capability off is as explicit as turning it on.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-governed-capabilities-default-on-new-instances.md:40:- R1: When `pose install` creates the review policy, it shall adopt agency readiness, contract nodes, atomic start and causality closeout with the structural-materiality overlay, dating atomic start, causality closeout and the overlay with the install day, and shall log each adoption.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-governed-capabilities-default-on-new-instances.md:41:- R2: `pose install` over an existing review policy, and `pose update` in every case, shall adopt nothing.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-governed-capabilities-default-on-new-instances.md:42:- R3: `pose adopt <capability>` shall preview the review-policy keys it would set, and with `--apply` write them, dated today or `--date YYYY-MM-DD`; `--off` shall preview and remove the same keys; the result shall be refused when the policy reader would reject it; an unknown capability shall be refused with the known ones listed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-governed-capabilities-default-on-new-instances.md:49:- Install and adopt write the review policy atomically.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-governed-capabilities-default-on-new-instances.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/progressive_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-governed-capabilities-default-on-new-instances.md:99:Install into empty and pre-configured targets, update over a target without a review policy, and drive `pose adopt` on and off through the reader, asserting the written keys and the refusals.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-governance-stats-local-freshness.md:36:Do not change what counts as fresh, or the review verification itself.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-governance-stats-local-freshness.md:66:- [x] Run the matrix, review and close.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-governance-stats-local-freshness.md:103:the review history.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-harne8-control-plane-integration.md:29:- R3: Portal and GraphForge shall consume policy-filtered projections for portfolio and review.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-harne8-control-plane-integration.md:111:- [open] Add an MCP-exposed variant of evidence reconciliation once a real Harness integration exists to validate the wire shape against — `pose reconcile-evidence` ships CLI-only in this release, consistent with every other locally-testable contract this roadmap built. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-10-19)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:2:slug: pose-update-configuration-review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:13:delivers: capability:configuration-review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:22:When `pose update` finds capabilities new since the last configuration review, it scaffolds a configuration-review spec for this engine version and opens one action request per capability — adopt, decline or defer, with the recommendation and the day-to-day effect — addressed to the maintainer role. Nothing is adopted until the maintainer answers; an answered request is applied with `pose adopt --request <act-id> --apply` or by `pose setup`, and the decision records the request it came from.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:30:Idempotent: one review spec per engine version, never duplicated, never re-asking a capability that has an open request or a recorded decision. An update with nothing new writes nothing. The spec and requests are questions; only an answer changes policy.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:40:- R1: `pose update` shall, when capabilities are new, create `.pose/specs/<date>-pose-configuration-review-<version>.md` listing each with its effect, introduction version and recommendation, and open one decision request per capability (options adopt, decline, defer; recommended adopt when the catalog turns it on in new instances), restricting the review spec's closeout, addressed to the `maintainer` role.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:42:- R3: `pose adopt --request <act-id> [--apply]` shall apply an answered review request: adopt turns the capability on, decline and defer record the decision with the answer's reason and the request id; an open, cancelled or foreign request shall be refused.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:43:- R4: `pose setup` shall list review requests waiting for an answer and answered ones not yet applied, and at a terminal apply an answered one after confirmation.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:51:- An answer applies policy only through the request's authority rules, so the review inherits role checks and signature verification.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:55:- Existing instances only see a review when an update brings something undecided.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:61:Update, a review spec template, action requests opened by the engine, `pose adopt --request`, setup.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:65:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:66:- created: .pose/starts/pose-update-configuration-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:67:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/configuration_review.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:68:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/configuration_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:78:- renamed: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-update-configuration-review.md -> .pose/changelogs/v7.0.0/pose-update-configuration-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:82:- capability:configuration-review module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:92:An older instance updated: the review spec and one request per new capability appear, a second update adds nothing, answers are applied through `pose adopt --request`, and the strict check passes throughout.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:102:- R1 [satisfied] test:TestConfigurationReviewAsksOncePerCapabilityAndChangesNothing check:configuration-review-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:103:- R2 [satisfied] test:TestConfigurationReviewAsksOncePerCapabilityAndChangesNothing check:configuration-review-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:104:- R3 [satisfied] test:TestConfigurationReviewAppliesOnlyAnsweredRequests check:configuration-review-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:105:- R4 [satisfied] test:TestConfigurationReviewAppliesOnlyAnsweredRequests test:TestSetupAnswersAndAppliesAReviewRequestAtATerminal check:configuration-review-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-update-configuration-review.md:115:The update writes the review spec (localized) and one decision request per undecided capability, idempotently; `pose adopt --request` applies answered requests with their reason and id; `pose setup` lists open and answered requests and, at a terminal, answers as the maintainer (signing under verified assurance) and applies.\n.pose/adr/2026-07-19-signed-extension-packages-as-data-only-directories.md:97:  remains a distinct, separately-reviewed decision.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-sbom-license-inventory.md:163:- [covered: pose-sbom-license-coverage-gate] Assert a minimum license coverage in the artifact-identity gate, so an SBOM that silently stops resolving licenses fails the release instead of shipping empty. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-02)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-followup-dispositions-accept-qualified-refs.md:26:Decision 5 of the backlog reconciliation confirmed that two pose-abm-review-authority follow-ups are covered by `harne8-action-request-confirmation-channel`, a Harne8 spec. Qualified references resolve everywhere else in POSE — dependencies, targets, roadmap members — but `lint-spec` reads a disposition target only as a local slug and refuses the qualified one as \"a missing spec\", so a follow-up owned by another project can only stay falsely open.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-proof-presence-channel-parity.md:6:depends_on: pose-historical-trust-and-review-reuse, pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read, pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof, pose-native-attestation-issuer, pose-signed-action-answers\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-proof-presence-channel-parity.md:82:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-23-b03-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-proof-presence-channel-parity.md:140:| CLI resolve/show/identity/doctor e preview sem assinatura/toque | `go test ./internal/cli -run ActionPresence -count=1` | Mesmo contrato do domínio, scope divulgado, preview not-evaluated e zero escrita. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-proof-presence-channel-parity.md:141:| MCP preview/apply/show e catálogo | `go test ./internal/mcpserver -run 'ActionPresence|Catalog' -count=1` | Sem resolução persistida nas recusas; todos os proofs fornecidos verificados; schema coerente. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-proof-presence-channel-parity.md:167:- R7 [satisfied] test:TestActionPresenceCLIIssuerAndHistoricalParity; test:TestActionPresenceMCPPreviewAndApplyParity; test:TestActionPresenceCLIPreviewAndMigrationBeforeSigner\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-proof-presence-channel-parity.md:180:[parecer real](../reports/2026-10-23-b03-independent-review.md).\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-requirement-evidence-traceability.md:20:- Keep links explicit and reviewable; never infer compliance from file proximity.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-requirement-evidence-traceability.md:74:- ADR `.pose/adr/2026-07-19-requirement-trace-contract.md` (Accepted): in-spec trace subsection over a separate trace file and over proximity inference; staged migration (legacy done specs warn, new specs fully enforced via template); additive MCP catalog change reviewed through the golden diff.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-requirement-evidence-traceability.md:109:- Mechanical link coverage can be mistaken for evidence quality — review\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-requirement-evidence-traceability.md:114:- [spawned: pose-governance-gate-activation] Flip the legacy done-without-trace warning to an error once the 10 pre-contract specs gain trace sections or are archived. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-23)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-effective-governance-projection.md:7:depends_on: pose-legacy-contract-cutoffs, pose-review-assurance-disclosure\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-effective-governance-projection.md:57:- R5: The projection shall not write policy nor widen review criteria; a test asserts no file changes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-effective-governance-projection.md:75:State builder, review policy and capability readers, MCP state tool, manual.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-effective-governance-projection.md:161:Delivers the governance section on state and pose_project_state. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-v7-legacy-cleanup-plan.md:84:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attribution.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-v7-legacy-cleanup-plan.md:147:- R3 [satisfied] <unknown review policy keys are reported as risks> test:TestMigrateDryRunInventoriesLegacyWithoutWriting check:migrate-dryrun-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-v7-legacy-cleanup-plan.md:153:Measured at 9c3a038 (`pose migrate v7 --dry-run`, 0.5 s): 318 flat and 3 dated folder specs, no undated folder and no blocked spec, 5 legacy review policy adoption keys, no unknown key, 1307 sealed bundles (483 without `governing_contracts`), 1301 declared-identity attestations (1285 without attribution or supplement), no incomplete transfer. A first run reported 10 incomplete transfers because it read each transfer's status as the source project; the ten ABM transfers are `activated` on this, the destination side. The predicate now uses the current project and its role in the plan. R2's apply half is deliberately not built in 6.x: `--apply` is refused and the plan lists what a 7.0 apply must carry (revision guard, per-class checkpoint, gate rehearsal). The help catalog entries for five earlier commands were updated in this commit because the catalog lagged their flags.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-v7-legacy-cleanup-plan.md:157:Delivers the dry-run inventory and the measured plan; no apply in 6.x. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-transfer-preserves-obligations.md:30:Preserve the existing context and revision guard; moving a file never delegates\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-transfer-preserves-obligations.md:54:- R5: Transfer preview shall list requests that are transferable, local-only or invalidated by the move.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-transfer-preserves-obligations.md:72:Spec transfer preview/apply/resume, action request journal remapping.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-transfer-preserves-obligations.md:94:- Remapping errors; preview lists every effect before apply.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-transfer-preserves-obligations.md:143:- R5 [satisfied] <the plan lists each request as invalidate-in-source or history-only; none is transferable by design> test:TestTransferRefusesARequestOpenedAfterThePreview check:transfer-actions-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-transfer-preserves-obligations.md:149:Delivers request dispositions in the transfer plan and invalidation at source retirement. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:2:slug: pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:8:components: pose-mcp, cli, review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:9:delivers: surface:review-bundle-classification\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:18:Fix issue #31 where `pose review bundle spec:<slug> --seal` fails with `unclassified review subject path` on valid project conventions (`docs/decisions/`, `.pose/roadmaps/`, root `.pose/*.json`, and component source trees like `agent/`, `conductor/`), and ensure `pose artifact-check` properly honors recorded change-set ranges from history reports.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:21:Unblocks seamless review bundle sealing and closing ceremonies across diverse project repository structures, ADR directory conventions (`docs/decisions/` alongside `.pose/adr/`), roadmap definitions, and custom component hierarchies without forcing manual overrides or recording workarounds.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:36:- R1: `loadReviewRepoEntries()` in `review_plan.go` shall gracefully synthesize repo entries from `.pose/indexes/repo-map.json` (if present), `.pose/indexes/module-metadata.json`, `.pose/state/components/*.json`, and top-level directory discovery so that declared spec components (e.g., `components: conductor, agent`) resolve to real `ReviewPlanComponent` paths even when `repo-map.json` is absent.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:37:- R2: `reviewBundlePathClass()` in `review_bundle.go` shall classify `docs/decisions/` as `governance` and `docs/` as `documentation`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:38:- R3: `reviewBundlePathClass()` shall classify `.pose/roadmaps/`, `.pose/templates/`, `.pose/rules/`, `.pose/adr/`, `.pose/knowledge/`, and root governance manifests (`.pose/docs.json`, `.pose/docs-review.jsonl`, `.pose/release-policy.json`, `.pose/project.json`, `compatibility.json`) as `governance`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:39:- R4: `reviewBundlePathClass()` shall classify paths under any matched `ReviewPlanComponent` path root as `implementation`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:51:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:52:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:54:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:58:- surface:review-bundle-classification module:pose-mcp profile:cli-surface entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:65:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:66:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:73:- [x] Increment 2: Update `reviewBundlePathClass()` with ADR, roadmap, and governance manifest conventions (R2, R3, R4).\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:75:- [x] Increment 4: Add unit tests, verify strict checks, seal review bundle, and attest.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:89:- R1 [satisfied] surface:review-bundle-classification check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewBundleComponentDiscoveryAndGovernancePaths evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:90:- R2 [satisfied] surface:review-bundle-classification check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewBundleComponentDiscoveryAndGovernancePaths evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:91:- R3 [satisfied] surface:review-bundle-classification check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewBundleComponentDiscoveryAndGovernancePaths evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:92:- R4 [satisfied] surface:review-bundle-classification check:delivery-integration test:TestReviewBundleComponentDiscoveryAndGovernancePaths evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:93:- R5 [satisfied] surface:review-bundle-classification check:delivery-integration test:TestArtifactCheckHonorsRecordedChangeSets evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:100:- surface:review-bundle-classification -> pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:110:- Resolved issue #31: Enhanced `loadReviewRepoEntries()` in `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go` to synthesize review components across `.pose/indexes/repo-map.json`, `.pose/indexes/module-metadata.json`, `.pose/state/components/*.json`, and top-level directory discovery.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths.md:111:- Expanded `reviewBundlePathClass()` in `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go` to properly classify ADR directories (`docs/decisions/`), roadmaps (`.pose/roadmaps/`), governance manifest files (`.pose/*.json`), and discovered component trees (`agent/`, `conductor/`, etc.).\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did.md:6:depends_on: pose-roadmap-reviews-findings\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did.md:21:The engine says what took effect wherever `pose-roadmap-reviews-findings` left a consumer behind, and it finds a repository and its hooks the way git does.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did.md:63:`internal/pose/capability_catalog.go`, `internal/pose/spec_trailers.go`, `internal/cli/maintenance.go`, `internal/cli/doctor.go`, `internal/cli/setup.go`, `internal/cli/adopt.go`, `internal/cli/configuration_review.go`, `internal/cli/issuer.go`, `internal/cli/init_delegation.go`, `internal/cli/state.go`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did.md:71:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did.md:78:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/configuration_review.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did.md:84:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_review_adoption.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did.md:103:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did.md:134:Implemented R1–R6 with focused integration tests. Hooks are resolved by git, updates refuse an empty `.git`, and policy publication continues to its second document after an unsynced first one. Callers report published policies with a warning. State validation preserves an unconfirmed publication through skipped and failed attempts and distinguishes partial publication durability. Lost-log markers report an unfinished effect. A separate Codex review found two blockers: failed refreshes hiding warnings and unsynced delegation activation bypassing its final configuration check. Both now have deterministic regression cases. Strict validation at `1bf72b3d` passed all 186 checks. Bundle `rvb-f9f0d2a54ece5d09` was approved by `rva-15bc11c3b166a389`, from a separate Codex execution using the same vendor and inherited model. Native verify and review-check passed before the governed transition to done. The isolated mutation corpus detected all 13 guard removals; no compilation failure was counted as a detected mutant.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did.md:142:F1, F2, F3 and F6 of `pose-roadmap-reviews-findings` are covered here. F4 (inventory proof) and F5 (fixture teardown race) remain open in that spec.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did.md:144:- [open] Upgrade `golang.org/x/net` from v0.60.0 to at least v0.62.0 for GO-2026-6866 and GO-2026-6860. The closeout govulncheck reports no affected symbols or imported packages; these two advisories are module-only and predate this change. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/adr/2026-09-19-structural-delta-delivery-profile.md:11:O producer `assess-design` já observa `structure` no subject selado de review,\n.pose/adr/2026-09-19-structural-delta-delivery-profile.md:22:essa classe é derivada pelo review bundle a partir do subject canônico, não por\n.pose/adr/2026-09-19-structural-delta-delivery-profile.md:30:  inventar um subject de review nem duplicar o producer.\n.pose/adr/2026-09-19-structural-delta-delivery-profile.md:32:  pertencendo ao review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-release-publication-evidence-replay.md:6:depends_on: pose-historical-trust-and-review-reuse, pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity, pose-release-lifecycle-closure, pose-reproducible-release-verification\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-release-publication-evidence-replay.md:38:- R7: Formalizar adoção/versionamento prospectivos e migration preview de contratos temporais antes do código, conforme ADR proposto. Knobs tag_pattern/require_verification expõem supported/configured/adopted/effective e limites, sem anunciar enforcement que não existe ou impor novo gate retrospectivo indiscriminadamente.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-release-publication-evidence-replay.md:74:Executar após B04/B38. Reusar ProjectRelease/GetReleaseStatus/LoadReleaseEvents, snapshot/tag integrity e independent verification. Confrontar os decoders atuais, contratos de identity/assets e consumidores open-next/scripts; completar paths dos schemas e report producers antes de start. O [ADR temporal proposto](../adr/2026-10-14-release-temporal-evidence-and-attempt-lineage.md) e knowledge:adr-release-temporal-evidence-review registram a proposta, não adoção; reconciliar/aceitar decisão de compatibilidade e schema antes do código. B39 define validade/lineage, B41 a persistência recuperável e B40 a seleção integrada, evitando ciclo nativo entre B39/B41.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-release-publication-evidence-replay.md:79:- Proposal: [Temporal evidence and attempt lineage](../adr/2026-10-14-release-temporal-evidence-and-attempt-lineage.md), status Proposed; knowledge:adr-release-temporal-evidence-review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-release-publication-evidence-replay.md:98:| V7 — Policy knobs, legacy/cutoff e migration preview | Suporte/compatibilidade/efeito observados, sem enforcement retrospectivo silencioso. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-governance-residual-diagnostics.md:17:without changing which policy is authoritative or invalidating completed reviews.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-governance-residual-diagnostics.md:30:  sealed bundle, including when a completed scope's review is retained.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-governance-residual-diagnostics.md:40:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-governance-residual-diagnostics.md:41:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-governance-residual-diagnostics.md:42:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-governance-residual-diagnostics.md:76:  is regenerated before sealing the governed review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-governance-residual-diagnostics.md:94:Implementation validated and closed through the governed review gate on 2026-10-01. Canonical strict validation passed 48/48 checks at f41b5aa; review bundle `rvb-c084508355446fe8` was fresh and approved before `pose close`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-review-conclusions\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-round-protocol, pose-delegated-review-run-provenance, pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger, pose-delegated-adapter-containment, pose-review-approval-domain-preflight, pose-delegation-routing\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:11:delivers: capability:delegated-review-conclusions\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:14:# Spec: The engine records a delegated run's validated conclusion\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:20:Let the engine turn a delegated run that passes every check into its governed conclusion — the attestation of a review, the decision record of an adjudication, the evidence of a smoke run — with no manual step, and keep a rejection blocking until the bundle changes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:28:R1 and R2 are R5 and R7 of [`pose-delegated-review-capability`](2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-capability.md), verbatim; the capability keeps them and traces them to this spec. Recording a conclusion never bypasses the attestation preflight, the review plan or `mandatory-human`. Escalations to a person (capability R6) and adoption (capability R1, R8–R11) are not part of this phase.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:38:- R1: When a `pose delegate review` run passes every check — brief generated from the sealed bundle, disposable copy unchanged, run record intact and signed, `different-vendor` or `different-model` independence against the implementation recorded in the bundle, conclusion complete and accepted by the attestation preflight, no earlier rejection on an unchanged bundle — the engine shall record the attestation from the run with no further step; a rejecting conclusion shall be recorded and block the scope until the bundle changes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:39:- R2: An `adjudication` or `smoke` run that passes the same checks shall record its verdict where its origin expects it (the adjudicated spec's decision record, the smoke target's evidence), under the same rules. Delivered by [`pose-delegated-verdict-destinations`](2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md): no such destination exists yet, and defining them is a feature of its own (decision D2, the maintainer's choice of 2026-10-27).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:59:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:60:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:62:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-review-conclusions.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:63:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:64:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:65:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:66:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:67:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:70:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:74:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:75:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:76:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:77:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_conclude.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:78:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_conclude_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_handoff.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:90:- capability:delegated-review-conclusions module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_conclude.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:95:- [ ] Adjudication and smoke destinations: moved to `pose-delegated-verdict-destinations` (D2)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:97:- [x] Independent review and native closeout: round 4 approved implementation 153d54bb2690bbe6b96d8da9760b1f97b6502728; bundle rvb-07212529dbde2aa2, attestation rva-ac02fc0441f45356.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:105:- Minimal option: a person runs `pose review run-sign` and `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign` with the criteria and tools as flags\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:106:- Selected option: the conclusion is typed in the run's pose-draft block — `criteria` and `tools` beside the findings, which the brief of template `review-brief/3` asks for, and `action`, `owner` and `review_by` on a follow-up to accept it as a risk — and the engine signs the run's proof and the attestation with the native issuer the delegation policy names (`conclusions.issuer`, the key outside the project) or `--issuer`, recording it through the same domain writer and preflight as every attestation. It records on its own as a review run completes only when review policy `delegated_review` is true and the issuer is set; otherwise `pose review conclude <run>` does it on demand. The maintainer chose this on 2026-10-27\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:107:- Rationale: one writer and one preflight keep the conclusion to the bar every attestation meets; a typed conclusion leaves nothing for the engine to answer on the reviewer's behalf\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:108:- Consequences: a criterion or tool the draft does not answer is refused by the preflight, never filled in; runs briefed with `review-brief/1` and `/2` keep verifying with their template; whoever signs it, an attestation of a run briefed with `review-brief/3` states that run's conclusion — criteria, tools that state a conclusion, and findings — or verify refuses it, so the manual `review attest --run --run-proof --sign` path is bound as the engine's is (review round 1, B1)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:114:- Selected option: move R2 to `pose-delegated-verdict-destinations`, which defines where each verdict goes (the adjudicated spec's decision record, the smoke target's surface evidence) and records it under the same rules; the maintainer chose this on 2026-10-27\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:115:- Rationale: neither destination exists, and defining them is a feature of its own; the review conclusion needs none of it\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:128:- R1 [satisfied] Native engine records the signed review attestation and rejecting conclusion through the shared admission: test:TestConcludeReviewRunRecordsTheAttestation test:TestConcludeReviewRunRecordsARejection check:pose-mcp/go/test commit:153d54bb2690bbe6b96d8da9760b1f97b6502728\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:129:- R2 [deferred-integration: spec:pose-delegated-verdict-destinations] Delivered by `pose-delegated-verdict-destinations` under D2; adjudication and smoke destinations remain in that draft and are not claimed implemented by this spec.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:131:- R4 [satisfied] Replay, supersession, concurrent conclusion and interrupted reservation recovery preserve one governed conclusion: test:TestConcludeReviewRunRecordsTheAttestation test:TestConcludeReviewRunConcurrently test:TestConcludeReviewRunRecoversAReservation check:pose-mcp/go/test report:2026-10-28-delegated-conclusions-round4.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:137:Delivered R1, R3 and R4 in implementation commit `153d54bb2690bbe6b96d8da9760b1f97b6502728`: the engine signs and records a review run's typed conclusion through the shared attestation writer and preflight, records rejecting conclusions, preserves refusal reasons, and serializes replay/recovery with a process-owned lock. Recovery requires an authenticated matching attestation and complete readable history. Explicit `review conclude` and the dual opt-in automatic delegate hook reach the production path for capability:delegated-review-conclusions. D2 assigns R2 delivery to `pose-delegated-verdict-destinations`; those draft destinations and capability adoption are not claimed delivered here.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:139:### Independent review and evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:141:Reviewer `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review`, declared Codex/OpenAI, reviewed the Claude/Anthropic implementation in a new execution. Identity is declared and the local attestation is unsigned; synthetic fixture signatures do not authenticate this review or prove cognitive independence. Knowledge consumed: knowledge:delegated-rounds-legacy-status and knowledge:module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:143:Sealed bundle `rvb-07212529dbde2aa2`, digest `sha256:07212529dbde2aa2f8e1c04648b6b7aa6876489a9816feaefe47f439f7a64252`; plan `sha256:3abb8224d37f53956931a291e816b8fe0fedd1a5b715979873bce2d3482585d4`; attestation `rva-ac02fc0441f45356` approved all required coverage with explicit judgment and accepted low finding `f-r4-01`. Native `review verify` and `review-check` reported fresh/approved, and `close` applied the guarded transition on 2026-10-28 UTC after the requirement trace was supplied.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:145:Current canonical strict validation passed 158/158 checks at the implemented commit. Independent full Go suites in C and pt_BR.UTF-8, vet, focused race tests, Windows/Darwin cross-builds and gitleaks passed. Reused rounds 1–3 probes include separate processes and actual SIGKILL recovery, repeated five times with one published proof and attestation per run; mutation counterexamples demonstrate the lock, reservation, typed-binding and Coverage protections. The obsolete preview/apply equality assertion remains intentionally in the historical probe source; current preview explicitly defers admission and recovery preview changes no bytes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:147:Strict artifact-check reconciled 28 claims with 31 attributed paths and no errors; broad orphan warnings were reviewed. Strict surface-check connected the declared capability and production entrypoint to fresh module-wide integration evidence; the separate-process probes exercise the conclusion path on Linux. The shared ADR structural fact is explicitly mapped to R1. Assessment coverage losses and seal warnings are disclosed in report:2026-10-28-delegated-conclusions-round4.md. Native results: `.pose/results/delivery-validation.json`; local probes/overlays/logs: `.review-work/round4/` (untracked).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:151:Accept the bounded low operability risk `f-r4-01` below. The unsupported-platform sentinel fails immediately, while other permanent backend errors can still wait two minutes and lose their cause as apparent contention. Failure remains closed; the injected EOPNOTSUPP probe published no proof or attestation. Linux process locking and owner death were exercised; Windows and Darwin were compiled, not run. Assessment tech-debt coverage remains incomplete for two pre-existing invalid specs, and broad integration consumer gaps are not asserted as new regressions. No production, tests, policy, matrix, capability or adoption configuration was changed by the reviewer. Handoff: knowledge:delegated-conclusions-round4.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md:155:- [open] f-r4-01: distinguish permanent filesystem/backend lock errors from contention and retain the original cause; injected EOPNOTSUPP currently waits until the deadline and reports another owner, with no governed effects. See knowledge:delegated-conclusions-round4. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-closeout-delivery-assurance-convergence.md:21:GitHub Issue [#30](https://github.com/oseiaspereira88/pose/issues/30) identifies a critical structural false negative in the closeout flow: `pose close spec:<slug>` fails with a generic `delivery assurance gate failed: action-mismatch` error even after `pose artifact-check --spec <slug> --strict`, `pose closeout-check`, and `pose review-check` all report clean, approved states with valid `POSE-Spec: <slug>` commit trailers.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-closeout-delivery-assurance-convergence.md:36:- Modifying cryptographic review bundle sealing or review attestation schemas.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-closeout-delivery-assurance-convergence.md:70:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go`: Update `cmdClose` to provide rich error diagnostics on delivery assurance failures.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-closeout-delivery-assurance-convergence.md:72:- Unit and integration test suites: `artifact_integrity_test.go`, `surface_check_test.go`, and `review_closeout_test.go`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-closeout-delivery-assurance-convergence.md:78:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-closeout-delivery-assurance-convergence.md:116:- [ ] Update `cmdClose` error reporting in `review_closeout.go` to emit structured, actionable diagnostic messages.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-closeout-delivery-assurance-convergence.md:160:- Scope: `internal/cli/artifact_integrity_test.go`, `internal/cli/surface_check_test.go`, `internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go`, `internal/pose/delivery_integrity_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-closeout-delivery-assurance-convergence.md:194:- `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-closeout-delivery-assurance-convergence.md:216:- [done] Document the `POSE-Spec: <slug>` trailer workflow in `AGENTS.md` and `.pose/workflows/feature.md` (Issue #29). Both carry it, in both locales: `AGENTS.md` under \"Commit trailer\" and `feature.md` as the commit step. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-09-21)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-23-pose-covered-followup-anchor-verification.md:6:depends_on: pose-review-bundle-scope-isolated-listing\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-consolidation-batch-4-authoring.md:95:Gates locais e critérios de saída julgados no [bundle rvb-d180c55a8451366f](../review-bundles/rvb-d180c55a8451366f.json), com [atestação rva-31049b372c3a9572](../review-attestations/rva-31049b372c3a9572.json) de uma execução separada do Codex, mesmo fornecedor/modelo herdado. Sem alegação de identidade autenticada ou revisão entre fornecedores.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-review-dispatch\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-brief\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:12:delivers: capability:delegated-review-dispatch\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:15:# Spec: Dispatch a delegated review to a configured adapter\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:21:Run a configured reviewer command on a disposable copy of the sealed commit and record the run and its draft, replacing personal launcher scripts.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:25:The 2026-10-09 launcher had to solve per run what the engine should solve once: the reviewer's sandbox made `.git` read-only, a validation was killed for lack of memory, and the implementer chose model and flags by hand.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:27:Origin: the 2026-10-09 review of `pose-native-attestation-issuer` by Codex through a personal launcher; it found three real defects in three rounds and exposed what the engine lacks (ADR `2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter`, roadmap `delegated-review`).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:31:POSE depends on no vendor CLI. The repository the user works in is never written by a reviewer run. Requirements follow the maintainer's decisions recorded in the accepted ADR on 2026-10-09.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:37:- R1: `.pose/policy/reviewers.json` shall declare adapters: a command template, the vendor and model it runs, a timeout and an execution budget; POSE ships examples for Codex (`codex exec`) and Claude Code (`claude -p`) and enables none.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:38:- R2: `pose review dispatch <bundle> --via <adapter>` shall create a disposable worktree at the bundle's sealed commit, pass the brief on stdin, and remove the worktree afterwards.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:39:- R3: A run shall be recorded under `.pose/review-runs/` with adapter, vendor, model, start and end time, exit code, brief digest, transcript digest and the reviewer's draft attestation or findings.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:40:- R4: A run that changes the sealed commit's files, exceeds its timeout or budget, or exits non-zero shall be recorded as failed, never as a review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:41:- R5: Dispatch alone shall not record an attestation; recording a run's conclusion is the engine's verified step, specified by `pose-delegated-review-capability`, and runs only when the run passes every check there.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:43:- R7: `pose review dispatch` shall accept every brief kind (`review`, `adjudication`, `smoke`) with the same run record.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:49:Adapter policy reader, worktree lifecycle, process runner with timeout, run record writer, and the `review dispatch` subcommand.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:53:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:54:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-review-dispatch.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:55:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:56:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:57:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:58:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:59:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:61:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:62:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_windows.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:66:- capability:delegated-review-dispatch module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:77:The contract is ADR `2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter`, accepted on 2026-10-09 with the maintainer's decisions: the engine records a verified run, people by exception through policy, agent independence by differing vendor or model (different vendor preferred), and reviews, adjudications and smoke runs from the first delivery.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:87:2026-10-10, first real run: `pose review dispatch spec:pose-ci-avoids-anonymous-rate-limits --via codex --apply` with the example Codex adapter (gpt-6.1-sol, read-only) ran on a worktree at aa29027d, received the generated brief and returned a full review — a decision, a judgment per planned criterion with file and line evidence, and one medium defect in that spec. The run was recorded as failed because the worktree showed `.pose/assessments/technical-debt.md` and `.pose/state/technical-debt.json` modified: the reviewer ran the `assess tech-debt` tool the plan requires, which regenerates derived state. The change check now ignores derived state (`.pose/assessments`, `.pose/state`, `.pose/indexes`, `.pose/results`, `.pose/review-bundles`, `.pose/review-runs`, `.pose/reports/history`) and still fails a run that edits anything else; the test covers both.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:91:2026-10-10, independent review (agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review, fallback reviewer): medium severity. The timeout killed only the adapter's process; a child holding stdout (the shape of `codex exec` and `claude -p`) kept the dispatch waiting until it ended. The adapter now runs in its own process group, the group is killed on timeout and after the run, and `WaitDelay` releases the pipes. `TestReviewDispatchTimeoutKillsTheAdaptersChildren` took 30s on the previous code and fails; it now returns in under a second.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:93:2026-10-10, second independent review (agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review, fallback reviewer): medium and low. (A) With `WaitDelay`, an adapter that exited 0 leaving a child on its output was recorded as failed; a run whose process succeeded and only hit `ErrWaitDelay` now completes, its leftover killed with the group. (B) For a rename, only the destination was checked, so moving sealed content into derived state passed; both paths are checked. `TestReviewDispatchJudgesTheRunNotItsLeftovers` fails on the previous code.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:97:- R1 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-dispatch evidence:integration test:TestReviewDispatchRunsAndRecordsAdapters\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:98:- R2 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-dispatch evidence:integration test:TestReviewDispatchRunsAndRecordsAdapters\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:99:- R3 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-dispatch evidence:integration test:TestReviewDispatchRunsAndRecordsAdapters\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:100:- R4 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-dispatch evidence:integration test:TestReviewDispatchRunsAndRecordsAdapters test:TestReviewDispatchTimeoutKillsTheAdaptersChildren test:TestReviewDispatchJudgesTheRunNotItsLeftovers\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:101:- R5 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-dispatch evidence:integration test:TestReviewDispatchRunsAndRecordsAdapters\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:102:- R6 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-dispatch evidence:integration test:TestReviewDispatchRunsAndRecordsAdapters\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:103:- R7 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-dispatch evidence:integration test:TestReviewDispatchRecordsEveryBriefKind\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:109:`pose review dispatch` runs a configured reviewer adapter on a disposable worktree at the sealed commit with the brief on stdin, records completed and failed runs with their transcripts under `.pose/review-runs/`, and records no attestation.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:113:- The worktree is disposable but the reviewer process runs with the user's permissions: an adapter can still write outside the worktree. The example adapters run read-only (`codex exec -s read-only`, `claude --permission-mode plan`).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-dispatch.md:114:- Runs are append-only by convention here; immutability and the rerun rule are spec `pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:24:In the Harne8 batch of 2026-11-22, every material change to one module required the whole 72-check matrix again. Each run took about 35 minutes with three jobs. Intermittent failures in unrelated suites made roughly one run in three useless. A hooks change confined to `scripts/` needed four full runs in one review round. The canonical record is all-or-nothing today. `--changed-from` already selects the affected modules, but it writes a partial record that cannot replace the canonical one in `results_path`, so closeout still needs the full run.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:30:Caching individual command outputs, hashing arbitrary inputs of a check, carrying across a matrix or engine change, and changing how review bundles seal evidence beyond reading the per-check head.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:166:- 2026-11-22: review round 1 (rrn-0dd98c4aab8b5918, Codex) found F1 (high). A base that validated a dirty working copy could be carried. The record now has `material_clean`, and a base without it, or with an unavailable material binding, is refused. `TestCarryRefusesABaseThatValidatedADirtyWorkingCopy` reproduces the sequence. It failed with the check mutated out and passes with it.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:167:- 2026-11-22: review round 2 (rrn-1c033e4c349d7794) confirmed R1-F1 fixed and found four new issues. N1: a rename's source path was missing from the changed set. N2: a self-contained root module was exempt from its own files. N3: quoted, newline-delimited Git names lost their owner. N4: modified engine builds at one revision shared an identity. All four are fixed, each with a regression test that failed when its fix was mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:168:- 2026-11-22: review round 3 (rrn-3461f6ff36909419) confirmed N1–N4 fixed and found two more issues. N5: a deleted dependency left its self-contained dependents carried. N6: module metadata that did not decode was ignored. Both are fixed, each with a regression test that failed when its fix was mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:170:- 2026-11-23: review round 4 (rrn-4b28f2ff95acf9c4) found N7–N10.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:176:- 2026-11-23: review round 5 (rrn-b07ee93779a65e40) found N11–N14.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:182:- 2026-11-23: review round 6 (rrn-88e0428bda9bc9c7) found N15 and N16. N15: a discovered ancestor dependency missed changes in nested modules. N16: declared dependencies reached through symlinks. Both are fixed, each with a regression test that failed when its fix was mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:183:- 2026-11-23: review round 7 (rrn-85704a129332a685) found N17–N19.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:188:- 2026-11-23: review round 8 (rrn-0375009e985e6a3d) found N20–N23.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:194:- 2026-11-23: review round 9 (rrn-dfc7e3348240ce19) found N24–N26.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:199:- 2026-11-23: review round 10 (rrn-29af03286365811e) found N27–N29. N27: the case probe failed open on an unusable first entry. N28: dependencies outside the repository were accepted. N29: the ADR and this summary misdescribed the self-contained fallback. All three are fixed; N27 and N28 have regression tests that failed when their fixes were mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:200:- 2026-11-23: review round 11 (rrn-c0b4006e2a8ff303) found N30–N32.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:205:- 2026-11-23: review round 12 (rrn-abb61f059dc6d700) found N33–N35.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:210:- 2026-11-23: review round 13 (rrn-f6546af4c9e5625e) found N36–N38 and the follow-up N39.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:215:- 2026-11-23: review round 14 (rrn-db44fd7f02f7b981) found N40 and N41, and N42 restated F2. N40: submodule and hidden-index conditions were checked only at the end. N41: start cleanliness was sampled after the plan inputs were read. One predicate, `validationMaterialClean`, now runs at the pin before the plan is read and again at the end. `TestValidateConditionClearedDuringTheRunIsNotClean` failed with the start predicate mutated back to status only.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:216:- 2026-11-23: review round 15 (rrn-16091dd78a12cc0b; the first attempt rrn-7d33ba9fc274421f stopped on the sandbox's read-only scratch) found N43 and N45, and N44 restated F2. N43: submodule movement was not witnessed. N45: an all-carried run ignored a signal. The movement witness now covers every submodule's reflog, and a signal sets the run-level `cancelled`, which bases refuse. Both regression tests failed when their fixes were mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:217:- 2026-11-23: review round 16 (rrn-328651cf23a32126) found N46–N48, and F2 was restated.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:222:- 2026-11-23: review round 17 approved in rrn-6741de0e146e3777, but the conclusion was refused for a round-prefixed finding id. The repeat rrn-243366b14aa5fea4 was concluded as changes-requested in rva-b084f3e3849f1ed5 with N50: the metadata was verified and then reread from disk. The carry now selects with one snapshot read from the pinned commit. `TestCarrySelectsWithThePinnedMetadataSnapshot` failed with a disk reread mutated back in. The other repeated finding is F2.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:223:- 2026-11-23: review round 18 (rrn-5ed84b0f66cce29b, attestation rva-f39a887e59b3aaaa) found N52: an unreadable metadata blob read as absent. N53 restated F2 and N54 restated F1. Absence now comes from the pinned tree, and a listed blob that cannot be read is an error. `TestCarryRefusesAnUnreadableMetadataBlob` failed when the old fallback was mutated back in.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:224:- 2026-11-23: review round 19 (rrn-fc6566de3c7eedf0) approved, but the conclusion was refused at preflight because decision D1 named no requirement. Each decision now states its basis: D1 rests on R3, R4 and R7, D2 on R2 and R10, D3 on R6.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:225:- 2026-11-23: the round-20 run showed that the rule refusing any base with an unavailable material binding refused every real base: a clean record of this repository holds 77 bindings the engine cannot compute. `material_clean` is the witness, and that rule was removed. The round-20 delegation also failed before running because the reviewer note exceeded 16 KiB, so the note was condensed.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:226:- 2026-11-23: review round 21 (rrn-20db50998dd91866) found no code defect. Its run failed because `pose assess` wrote inside the sealed checkout. Its draft found N57: the manual still stated the removed rule. All four manual copies were corrected. The dogfood after round 21 carried five of six modules from a clean base with zero changed files; `pose-mcp` ran because of its high-criticality policy.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:227:- 2026-11-23: review round 22 approved (rrn-41f73b6e7465d0bb, attestation rva-c09024015650a57b). `pose close` then refused with `undeclared-delivery`, because the spec declared no delivery target. The spec now declares `capability:validate-carries-unchanged-checks`, whose entrypoint is the `validate` command.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:264:- [open] F1: cover with an end-to-end test that a review bundle sealed over a carried record judges the carried head (seal, verify and closeout-check on a fixture). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:265:- [open] F2: `--carry --report` lists carried checks as executed commands without their `carried_from` head and time; exclude them from the executed summary and label reused results (review round 13, N39). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-adaptive-assessment-freshness.md:166:Delivers binding-based freshness, assess discover --if-stale and the advisory assessment obligation. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-delivery-surface-assurance.md:40:- Keep qualitative review possible through a referenced, versioned report, but\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-delivery-surface-assurance.md:96:  delivery refs, named validation checks or versioned manual-review reports;\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-delivery-surface-assurance.md:172:  - C3: manual-review:.pose/reports/ui-audit.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-delivery-surface-assurance.md:217:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-delivery-surface-assurance.md:360:- 2026-08-03, review remediation: required Git-observed artifacts for delivery\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-delivery-surface-assurance.md:383:- Failures: review found four semantic gaps; each was remediated and covered by\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-delivery-surface-assurance.md:391:- R3 [satisfied] test:TestSurfaceCheckFailsUnreachableDelivery; report:.pose/reports/2026-08-03-pose-delivery-surface-assurance-review.md.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-delivery-surface-assurance.md:401:- R13 [satisfied] check:skills-check-strict; report:.pose/reports/2026-08-03-pose-delivery-surface-assurance-review.md.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-delivery-surface-assurance.md:406:  review responsibility documented by the new workflow and skill.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-02-pose-delivery-surface-assurance.md:432:  review remain necessary.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-class-producers-reads-the-disjunction.md:19:Report a review criterion none of whose accepted evidence classes is produced,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-class-producers-reads-the-disjunction.md:34:`a11y` was named because `frontend-review` demands it. That profile is selected\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-class-producers-reads-the-disjunction.md:122:  reviewing it — the first because a follow-up said to act, the second while\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-class-producers-reads-the-disjunction.md:149:  reduced it to one criterion, `frontend-review/frontend-accessibility (a11y)`;\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-class-producers-reads-the-disjunction.md:179:- [open] Resolve profile selection through the component-aware planner rather than by reading the language selector, so a profile that cannot apply for any reason is skipped and not only for an absent language (owner:unowned crit:low review:2027-03-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-release-signing.md:117:- [covered: pose-release-signing-rejection] The rejection path is now exercised on every CI run by tests/release/verify-negative.sh, and signing has run on four real releases. Original item: run a workflow_dispatch snapshot rehearsal after merge and confirm sign + verify pass in the release environment. Still pending: dispatching the Release workflow was denied by the automation session; a maintainer has to run it. Tracked on `pose-first-release-evidence-confirmation`. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:high review:2026-08-14)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-structured-validation-results.md:118:- [spawned: pose-governance-gate-activation] Adopt --sarif in the CI security surface once code-scanning upload is wired for validation results. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-10-16)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-calendar-dates-tolerate-utc-stamping.md:50:- R3: Knowledge artifacts apply the same tolerance to `last_reviewed_at` against\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-calendar-dates-tolerate-utc-stamping.md:127:`review-check`, and was replaced before closing.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-calendar-dates-tolerate-utc-stamping.md:134:- R3 [satisfied] surface:lifecycle-date-order evidence:integration check:calendar-date-skew-integration test:TestCompletionOneDayBeforeUTCCreationIsZoneSkew — `pose maintenance` warns on `last_reviewed_at` through the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:36:- R1: Produce a read-only deterministic preview with operation ID, source/destination qualified identities, expected revisions, requirement map, impacted references and digest. No preview creates a destination spec or changes lifecycle.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:42:- R7: Keep existing executor reviews bound to their original subjects. A parent adoption commit never impersonates implementation attribution; migrated subjects that change semantics require fresh evidence under the owning authority.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:55:Build a confined migration service over the existing authorized project roots and shared artifact resolver. Freeze the CLI contract as `pose spec-transfer preview|apply|resume|status`; preview emits a deterministic plan, apply requires its digest and explicit authorization for both project IDs, and resume accepts only a verified operation receipt. MCP exposes read-only status for one already-authorized project. No command commits or pushes.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:57:Use review-policy schema 4 with `spec_authority_transfer_version: 1` as the opt-in capability boundary. Do not stamp it during `pose update` or enable it in consumer projects. A transfer must fail closed unless both roots explicitly adopted the capability.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:69:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:96:until the complete module matrix, attribution, review and closeout gates pass.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:100:Version new metadata through existing schema/capability mechanisms. Preview\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:115:- [x] Obtain explicit review and governed closeout; disposition follow-ups and refresh assessments.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:121:- Prefer the existing Store/roots/review contracts over a second authority or resolver.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:136:| Preview, requirement mapping, history, frontmatter, folder companion files and CLI; R1/R2/R5/R7 | `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'TestSpecTransfer(Preview|RequirementMap|ApplyPreservesHistory|ApplyPreservesSourceFrontmatter|PreservesFolder|CLIEndToEnd)' -count=1` | Preview is read-only and stable; every requirement is accounted for; transferred metadata and old evidence stay intact. |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:138:| Authorization, stale revisions, changed reference inventory, redirect cycles/missing targets, capability and confinement; R5/R6/R8 | `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'TestSpecTransfer(Negative|PreviewBlocks|ResumeBlocks|ResolverRejects|ApplyPreservesHistory|PreservesFolder|RewritesRoadmap)|TestSpecAuthorityTransferPolicySchema' -count=1` | Unauthorized roots, CAS conflicts, changed source-reference inventory, invalid redirect chains, unsupported policy and symlink/traversal escapes fail closed. |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:147:- `pose review verify spec:pose-spec-authority-transfer` and `pose closeout-check spec:pose-spec-authority-transfer` before `pose close spec:pose-spec-authority-transfer`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:151:2026-09-24: accepted ADR and predecessor confirmed; risk-based test plan and exact artifact inventory recorded. Implemented the transfer engine, CLI, resolver redirect and MCP status. Preview/apply/recovery, negative-gate, redirect-cycle, historical-subject and authorized-status test families pass on Git fixtures. Follow-up hardening preserves unknown source frontmatter and blocks resume when new source references appear after an interruption. `go test ./...`, `go vet ./...`, all four named scenario commands, and the strict module matrix pass (21/21 checks). `pose check --strict` and `pose lint-spec --strict` pass; check reports 11 existing non-blocking warnings. `pose artifact-check --strict` passes with existing repository-wide orphan warnings; `pose surface-check --strict` passes (1 target, 21 results, 0 findings). `pose docs-check` reports no docs manifest, so the opt-in docs contract is absent; `pose assess integrate` reports 56 unobserved provider contracts, including the new status tool. Human review and governed closeout remain pending.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:153:2026-09-24 autonomous review: sealed bundle `rvb-165fc70dcb37c601`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:155:`pose close` completed the spec; the earlier pending-review note records the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:156:state before this review.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:159:- R1 [satisfied] check:spec-authority-transfer-integration test:TestSpecTransferPreviewIsDeterministicAndReadOnly — repeated previews have the same digest and leave both Git roots unchanged; sibling and nested-submodule roots are covered.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:164:- R6 [satisfied] check:spec-authority-transfer-integration test:TestSpecTransferRewritesRoadmapMembershipAndKeepsOtherObligations test:TestSpecTransferPreviewBlocksUnscannedProjects test:TestSpecTransferResumeBlocksChangedReferenceInventory — only inventoried ownership references change; unresolved roots and newly introduced source references block the operation.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:165:- R7 [satisfied] check:spec-authority-transfer-integration test:TestSpecTransferApplyPreservesHistoryAndRewritesApprovedReferences — the source history and existing review subjects remain bound to their original revisions.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-spec-authority-transfer.md:171:The transfer engine, CLI and MCP status contract passed review and governed spec closeout. No consumer project has adopted schema 4 and no real project transfer has been executed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:21:Let any project that installs only POSE sign review attestations and reviewer authority claims, so `signed-attestations` and `verified-identity` can be adopted without Harne8, while an external issuer such as the Harne8 Conductor stays trusted alongside the native one.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:25:Found while adopting 7.1.0 on 2026-10-09: the engine verifies Ed25519 attestation envelopes from issuers pinned as `<issuer>#sha256:<key-digest>` in `trusted_attestation_issuers` and `human_authority_issuers`, but POSE has no way to create an issuer key, compute its pin or sign an attestation. The only emitter is Harne8's Conductor, which signs after an authenticated person confirms through its endpoint. Harne8 had to defer both capabilities, and a repository without Harne8 can never adopt them. Action answers already have a native path (`pose identity add` and `ssh-keygen -Y sign`); review attestations do not.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:32:- Trust is pinned explicitly in review policy; a self-declared issuer or key is never trusted alone (the current envelope rule).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:34:- MCP does not sign with a key on the agent's behalf: it returns the canonical bytes to sign and accepts the signed envelope, as `pose_review_attest` does now.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:45:- R2: `pose issuer pin <name|public-key> [--attestations] [--human-authority] [--apply]` shall add `<name>#sha256:<digest>` to the chosen policy lists as a preview first, keeping every pin already there.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:46:- R3: `pose review attest <scope> ... --sign <issuer>` shall complete the attestation as recording would, sign its canonical bytes with the issuer key and record the envelope, which `pose review verify` accepts under `require_signed_attestations`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:47:- R4: The native issuer shall sign a reviewer authority claim the same way, so `verified-identity` reads a human reviewer from a native claim.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:69:`pose-mcp/internal/cli` (new `issuer` command, `review attest --sign`), `pose-mcp/internal/pose` (issuer key store, signing beside `VerifyReviewAttestationEnvelope`, authority-claim signing), capability prerequisite messages, docs.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:85:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:102:- [x] `review attest --sign` and native reviewer authority claims\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:120:- Context: an authority claim names one audience and one project, the ones review policy declares.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:134:2026-10-09, independent review (agent:gpt-6.1-sol, Codex): changes required, high severity. `POSE_ISSUER_HOME` accepted a directory inside the project and `issuer init` wrote the private key there (for example `<project>/.pose/issuers/`), one `git add -A` from publication, against R1. Every key operation now takes the project root and refuses a key directory inside it, symlinks resolved, before anything is written; `TestNativeIssuerKeyIsRefusedInsideTheProject` covers the direct path, a symlink into the project, and signing from such a directory.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:136:2026-10-09, second independent review (agent:gpt-6.1-sol): two more defects. High: the key directory was checked but the `<issuer>.key` file could be a symlink to a key inside the project, and loading followed it. Medium: two rotations in the same second archived to the same file and `rename` silently replaced the earlier retired key. The key file is now read with `Lstat` and refused when it is a symlink or has another hard link (Unix; Windows has no link count), and a retired key is archived with a hard link that fails instead of replacing, numbered when the name is taken. `TestNativeIssuerKeyFileMustNotBeALink` and `TestRotationsInTheSameSecondKeepEveryRetiredKey` failed on 7932776b and pass now.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:138:2026-10-09, third independent review (agent:gpt-6.1-sol): one low-severity defect. A valid issuer name containing `.retired-` (for example `ops.retired-backup`) was read as a retired key by `issuer list` and disappeared from it. Listing now reads the issuer from the key file and treats only `<issuer>.key` as current; `TestIssuerNameContainingRetiredIsListed` failed on 24b54a69 and passes on 5a590598.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:140:2026-10-09, fourth independent review (agent:gpt-6.1-sol): medium severity. A FIFO named `<x>.key` in the key directory blocked `issuer list` and `issuer pin`, because the file was read before its type was checked. Listing now opens only regular files, and loading refuses any non-regular key file before reading; `TestIssuerSpecialFileIsNeverOpened` blocked on e440104a and passes now.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:156:`pose issuer init|pin|list|rotate` and `pose review attest --sign <issuer> [--authority …]`: a project with POSE alone signs review attestations and reviewer authority claims, and native and external issuers coexist in the same policy lists.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-native-attestation-issuer.md:161:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-governance-wait-rework-observability.md:41:A personal productivity tracker; a universal target of fewer reviews; promising speedup\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-governance-wait-rework-observability.md:56:- R4: Rework caused by subject change shall be separated from operational error or review conflict when evidence exists; unknown causes are not attributed to user or engine.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-governance-wait-rework-observability.md:84:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-governance-wait-rework-observability.md:85:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-governance-wait-rework-observability.md:162:Measured on this repository at 6e5f4d9 with `scripts/bench-governance.sh 1`: `state --attention` 1.9 s, `check --strict` 83.7 s, `index` 60.0 s, delivery index 5.09 MB. The pre-batch engine (133478d) takes the same 82.8 s for `check --strict` as the current one, so the batch did not regress it; the cost predates this roadmap. On the same corpus `stats governance --rework` reported 1307 sealed bundles over 206 scopes: 477 superseded because the subject changed, 571 because the review plan changed, 17 for intent or plan, 33 for evidence, 3 unknown; of 1301 attestations, 8 extra ones followed an attestation invalid against today's policy and 36 have no recorded cause.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-governance-wait-rework-observability.md:166:Delivers --waits, --rework, --outcomes and the benchmark script, as dimensions without a score. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-delivery-integrity-index-compaction.md:61:byte-identical, because sealed review bundles and `deliveryEvidenceCurrent`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-delivery-integrity-index-compaction.md:123:`pose surface-check`, `pose review bundle --seal`, `pose closeout-check`,\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-delivery-integrity-index-compaction.md:136:in `cli/index.go`, `cli/artifact_integrity.go` and `cli/review_closeout.go` call\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-delivery-integrity-index-compaction.md:148:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-workflow-event-ref-contract.md:34:the injection one line below it, unnoticed by the same review.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-workflow-event-ref-contract.md:36:Two escapes from human review, on the same pattern, in one day. That is the\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-workflow-event-ref-contract.md:195:- [open] The scanner recognises the YAML forms this repository happens to use. If the workflows ever adopt anchors, flow mappings or unusual block indicators, the contract silently narrows. Revisit whether `gopkg.in/yaml.v3` — already in go.sum as an indirect dependency — is worth promoting for the workflow contracts, which would remove the whole class of blind spot. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-attention-lists-only-open-obligations.md:85:- Consequences: an invalidated answer reappears in `for_actor`, as it is open again.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-attention-lists-only-open-obligations.md:115:Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-package-manager-distribution.md:74:- ADR `.pose/adr/2026-07-19-package-manager-channels-generated-not-hosted.md` (Accepted): manifests are generated deterministically from `checksums.txt` + release tag (`pose release-package-manifests`), not hosted in a maintained tap/registry — Homebrew installs directly from the formula attached to the GitHub release (`brew install --formula <url>`, zero publication lag, no upstream review dependency); WinGet ships as a generated manifest artifact submitted to `winget-pkgs` by a maintainer (non-zero, tracked publication lag). Rejected: owning a Homebrew tap or submitting to homebrew-core (extra sync/credential surface, upstream review dependency not yet justified by volume); adding Scoop/Nix now (out of scope for R1's \"at least one Windows channel\", left as a small future extension of the same generator).\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-package-manager-distribution.md:104:- Residual risk: compromised channel credentials could redirect trusted package names — mitigated by the generator having no persistent credentials of its own (it only reads `checksums.txt`, already produced by the signed/verified release) and by WinGet publication requiring a maintainer-reviewed PR into `winget-pkgs` rather than an automated push; Homebrew has no credential at all since it installs directly from a release-pinned URL. `winget-pkgs` submitter account compromise remains an upstream risk outside this repository's control.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-package-manager-distribution.md:109:- [spawned: pose-package-channel-delivery] Confirm the first real `package-channels.yml` clean-host run on the first tagged release (brew/winget unavailable in this sandbox). Attempted on v0.18.2 and found the gate has never run (trigger never fires) and fails immediately when dispatched (`go run` from a non-module root). Tracked as F1+F2 on `pose-first-release-evidence-confirmation`. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-08-19)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-package-manager-distribution.md:110:- [open] Submit the first generated WinGet manifest to `winget-pkgs` and record the observed publication lag in `package-channels.md`. No longer blocked by F1+F2 — `pose-package-channel-delivery` gave the gate a trigger that fires and a command that runs, and `pose-package-channel-workflow-safety` made its checkout safe — but still waiting on the first tagged cut to actually emit a manifest, since neither change has run in a release yet. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-09-18)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-package-manager-distribution.md:111:- [open] Revisit Homebrew tap ownership once install volume justifies the maintenance cost over the formula-URL install. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-10-19)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-21-pose-contributor-mode-protocol.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-docs-asset-parity.md:184:- [open] The document list is enumerated by hand, which is the same gap shape that left `tests/release/` outside shellcheck for three failed releases. Consider extracting download URLs from all of `docs-site/docs/` and `README.md` by glob instead of by list. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-scaffold-self-referential-policy-fix.md:28:tree instead of the target's. A finished spec's `review bundle --seal` failed\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-scaffold-self-referential-policy-fix.md:50:  to the already-existing local alternative (`pose review attest`/`auto-attest`).\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-scaffold-self-referential-policy-fix.md:68:  naming `pose review attest`/`pose review auto-attest` as the supported\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-scaffold-self-referential-policy-fix.md:226:- Scope: both modules, plus the repo's own delivery/surface/review-plan\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-scaffold-self-referential-policy-fix.md:297:  not a gap this bugfix should close; `pose review attest`/`auto-attest`\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:21:`pose review run-proof` e os leitores de veredito que citam o emissor de uma run usam a mesma pergunta que o fechamento usa para um escopo done (a prova como foi dada), e a expiração nesse caminho está decidida e escrita no manual.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:25:`pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift` fez o fechamento reter a aprovação de um escopo done (`VerifyReviewRunProofAsSealed`), mas `pose review run-proof`, o emissor lido em `verifiedVerdictOf` e o emissor lido na recuperação de uma conclusão interrompida ainda chamavam `VerifyReviewRunProof`, que pergunta se a run ainda governa o repositório agora e se a prova expirou. Dois leitores discordavam sobre a mesma run depois de uma deriva rotineira: o fechamento dizia aprovado e `run-proof` falhava.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:38:- R1: `VerifyReviewRunProofForReading` responde a prova como foi dada quando o escopo do bundle da run está done e a pergunta viva caso contrário; `pose review run-proof`, o emissor de `verifiedVerdictOf` e o da recuperação de conclusão usam essa função.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:46:`pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go`, `delegated_verdicts.go`, `review_conclusions.go`, `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance.go`, o manual (`POSE.md` e `locales/pt-BR/POSE.md`, com as cópias de `scaffold/dist`).\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:53:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:54:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:55:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:56:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:70:Nova função pública `VerifyReviewRunProofForReading`; `pose review run-proof` passa a responder a prova como foi dada para um escopo done.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:121:- Result: registrado pela evidência de validação selada; revisão delegada independente concluída com `pose review conclude`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:128:- [open] Testar com uma prova de TTL lida depois da expiração: o leitor selado aceita e o vivo recusa (R2 hoje tem o código e o manual, sem teste comportamental). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:129:- [open] Fazer `verifiedVerdictProof` (adjudicação e smoke) perguntar a mesma pergunta selada para escopos done. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-planning-and-release-narrative-reconciliation.md:6:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-contract, pose-v7-legacy-cleanup-plan\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-planning-and-release-narrative-reconciliation.md:42:- R5: Claims de review/release/runtime/migração devem ser vinculados ao comportamento/consumer e versão/canal efetivamente disponíveis, incluindo limites: envelope não é approval, run não é conclusão governada, ledger não é suficiência, MCP não prova runtime residente e apply ausente não deve ser anunciado.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-planning-and-release-narrative-reconciliation.md:65:- modified: .pose/roadmaps/delegated-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-10-pose-skill-index-parity.md:161:- [covered: pose-locale-coverage-contract] The parity work has now been extended twice after a miss — first from manuals to skills, then from skill entries to the skill index — each time because someone noticed by reading. Rather than adding a check per document, consider enumerating the translated files under `locales/` and requiring each to have a declared comparison, so a new translated document is guarded by default instead of when it is missed. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-verdict-destinations\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-conclusions\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:11:delivers: capability:delegated-verdict-destinations\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:20:Give the verdict of a delegated adjudication and of a delegated smoke run a governed destination, and let the engine record it there under the rules a review conclusion follows.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:24:R2 of [`pose-delegated-review-conclusions`](2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md) asks for these verdicts to be recorded \"where the origin expects them\" — the adjudicated spec's decision record, the smoke target's evidence — and neither destination exists. The maintainer chose on 2026-10-27 to deliver review conclusions first and to define these destinations in a spec of their own.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:28:The same checks as a review conclusion apply: an intact, signed run of a current bundle, a complete typed verdict, idempotence, refusals recorded with their reason. A verdict never becomes an approval of another scope.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:32:Review conclusions (delivered by `pose-delegated-review-conclusions`); turning the capability on.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:40:- R3: A verdict that fails a check, is incomplete or does not parse, shall record no governed effect and keep its reason, as a review conclusion does.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:46:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:47:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:48:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:49:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:50:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:51:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:52:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:53:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:54:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:60:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:61:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:62:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:63:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegated_verdicts_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:71:- capability:delegated-verdict-destinations module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_conclude.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:78:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:87:- Consequences: a spec's adjudications are read beside it, not in it; a question the current bundle's verified adjudication says does not hold fails `lint-spec` and refuses `close`; an adjudication of an earlier bundle is kept but no longer gates either. Every record is admitted on read under what its conclusion required: its proof signed by the issuer it names, the independence its plan requires, and a verdict answering exactly what was asked (review round 1)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:95:- Consequences: `smoke` joins the closed vocabulary of evidence classes; no profile demands it until an instance adds it. A smoke result names the target and the spec it observed and is evidence of that target only; its head, time and provenance come from the run, its bundle and the current index, never from the document's bytes, so it is current only while the run's bundle governs its scope (review round 1)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:101:- Selected option: `pose review conclude` and the automatic conclusion handle adjudication and smoke runs under the same checks, lock, refusals and idempotence as a review conclusion, plus one more check: the verdict answers exactly what the brief asked — every question, every delivery target, nothing else\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:117:- R3 [satisfied] Exact typed coverage, proof/issuer/kind, independence and supported schema are required; refusal publishes no effect and busy lifecycle reservations remain recoverable: test:TestSmokeVerdictRefusesAnUnaskedTarget test:TestVerdictsMeetThePlansIndependence test:TestVerdictRecordsVerifyLikeTheConclusion test:TestSmokeResultsRefuseAnUnsupportedSchema test:TestAdjudicationSurvivesADeadLifecycleLock check:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-provenance-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:125:### Independent review and evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:127:Reviewer `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review`, maintainer-authorized Codex/OpenAI execution, reviewed the Claude/Anthropic implementation, Claude Opus 5.5 session `f2a4d9f2-d557-4064-ae96-6ed52bb47cd2`. The engine-required `agent:independent-` prefix is a declaration; local attestations are unsigned and synthetic fixture signatures do not authenticate vendor or cognitive independence. The bundle was sealed with explicit lead `anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`; the warning about the absent Anthropic session reference in this Codex environment is expected.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:129:Bundle `rvb-57cfad060c87c98c`, digest `sha256:57cfad060c87c98c276dccc710cad452a7e4d3b0e02a663971d2c17c2eef8f01`, plan `sha256:ada579c8ed38d9afb2242c9df934c7929e415080e315a1e5edac8d4660ad8b1c`; approved attestation `rva-89954037e256fc74`. Native verification and review-check confirmed a fresh approved review before the guarded close. Independent full Go suites passed in C without session markers and in pt_BR.UTF-8; vet, Windows/Darwin builds, focused race, gitleaks and govulncheck passed. Current global strict validation passed 158/158 checks; module validation passed 155/155 on the implemented commit.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:131:Independent adversarial probes and mutation counterexamples reconciled the prior independence, provenance/target, exact coverage, closeout, concurrency, schema, issuer and real-child-process crash-recovery findings. F04 is resolved by the native CLI regression: removing its consumer or either target-selection filter compiles but fails its assertions. That test substitutes the loader boundary; actual smoke-document verification remains covered in the pose package. Local review evidence, including real process exit after lock acquisition and native recovery followed by one verified same-run verdict, remains in `.review-work/round5/` as requested. The canonical committed validation results and sealed review records carry the native evidence.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:135:The first round-5 global validation passed 157/158 checks but failed the install/upgrade journey with `contract-nodes is not on after the answer was applied`. Its full output was preserved. The simultaneous module validation passed that check, the maintainer reported eleven successful focused runs, and the authorized fresh global validation passed all 158 checks. This is recorded as an intermittent check observation, not a finding attributed to this diff. No production or test fix was made by this reviewer.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-verdict-destinations.md:139:No unresolved review finding remains for this spec. Evidence establishes admission, persistence, provenance and CLI composition over fixtures; it does not prove an external service was physically exercised. Windows and Darwin were compiled rather than executed. Integration's pre-existing observational consumer gaps and tech-debt's incomplete scan of two pre-existing invalid specs are disclosed without claiming complete source coverage or new regressions. Declared reviewer identity and unsigned attestation are existing assurance limits.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-trace-test-refs-resolve.md:33:Judging whether the cited test is adequate to the requirement; that remains the review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-trace-test-refs-resolve.md:40:- R2: An unresolved ref shall fail `lint-spec` and `pose close` while the spec is open, and shall be reported as a warning on a done, superseded or abandoned spec.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-trace-test-refs-resolve.md:56:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-trace-test-refs-resolve.md:57:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-trace-test-refs-resolve.md:110:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-history-quiet-tolerated-verdict.md:58:  is regenerated before sealing the governed review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-history-quiet-tolerated-verdict.md:69:Implementation validated and closed through the governed review gate on 2026-10-01. Canonical strict validation passed 48/48 checks at f41b5aa; review bundle `rvb-c3d705febef1baac` was fresh and approved before `pose close`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:2:slug: pose-abm-review-soundness\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:19:Stop the engine from approving, on a reviewer's behalf, criteria that no registered check\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:24:concluding anything, which makes the whole review record weaker evidence than it appears.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:67:disagree about what a reviewer still owes.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:78:planned criterion changes the plan digest, so an open review is re-prepared under the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:88:CLI reference, the review-plan schema and the embedded scaffold.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:91:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:92:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/abm_review_soundness_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:93:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:94:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:97:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:98:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:99:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:100:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:101:- modified: pose-mcp/schemas/v1/review-plan.schema.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:102:- modified: .agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:107:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:124:validation result set, the validate report and the sealed bundles this review went\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:147:Every open review is re-prepared, because the plan digest changes. Accepted: re-adopting\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:149:effect of it. A scope whose plan is entirely judgment now needs a reviewer before it can\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:243:- Date: 2026-09-19 (R8 added during implementation, after the first hand-answered review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:253:- Notes: the characterization file from the originating review was copied into the tree,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:262:- Warnings: adding `kind` changes the plan digest, so open reviews are re-prepared.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:278:The first review in this repository that had to be answered by hand was also the first to\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:283:reviewer's only options were to cite another component's result, which is false, or to\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:306:- Open reviews are re-prepared under the new plan digest. Completed scopes are exempt, but\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:310:- A profile author can still ask for judgment everywhere and make review expensive. The\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:311:  engine does not police proportionality; that is the progressive-review contract.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:315:- [covered: pose-review-assurance-disclosure] Outputs now state the identity as declared and the separation as not verified; requiring verified identity by default is decided with the Harne8 confirmation channel. Confirmed by the maintainer on 2026-10-05 (pose-open-backlog-reconciliation, Decision 5). Original item: Reviewer authority is still satisfied by a declared prefix, so `different-actor`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-review-soundness.md:317:  crit:high review:2026-10-03)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-security-validation-release-api-auth.md:66:- R1 [satisfied] The current Security step binds `github.token`; review of the validation, journey-test and shell inheritance path is recorded in report:.pose/reports/2026-10-14-security-validation-release-api-auth.md; the original binding is commit:2255621cc82fa348ee2419b892296b96ea7b276e.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-security-validation-release-api-auth.md:74:The configuration correction is present and its local structural evidence is recorded in [the report](../reports/2026-10-14-security-validation-release-api-auth.md). The maintainer waived corrected GitHub runner confirmation on 2026-11-03; runtime verification on that runner is not claimed. Keep this spec `in-progress` until the principal completes the remaining review and native closeout gates.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:17:Prepare the single 6.0.0 release requested by the maintainer, with reviewed\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:24:Use knowledge:module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance when\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:25:refreshing source reviews. Derived index changes do not change reviewed code.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:33:  judgment against current sealed evidence; preserve historical review records.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:51:- created: .pose/reports/2026-09-28-abm-dependency-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:52:- created: .pose/results/abm-dependency-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:72:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:73:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_release_archive_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:107:paths outside the ledger. Retain historical review sidecars unchanged. Register\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:113:- [x] Complete explicit source reviews and reconcile their evidence.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:116:- [x] Validate and review the technical candidate; apply the canonical closeout gate.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:152:- R1 [satisfied] report:.pose/reports/2026-09-28-abm-dependency-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:157:- R6 [satisfied] integration:pose-mcp/go/release-review-archive-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:171:preview notes. Remaining release operations use the existing lifecycle:\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-v6-release-readiness.md:179:- [open] Make the temporary Git fixture cleanup deterministic for the existing 500-commit attribution test; the observed CI cleanup race must not recur (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-10-28)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-community-claims-hold.md:25:The integration review of `community-launch` found the public gate passing a README that named v0.0.1 as the latest release, a README carrying per-release text and a hardcoded tool count that its own spec forbids, a quickstart timing measured on v7.0.0 and presented as current, and a demo that prints \"legitimately closed\" with no close having run.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-community-claims-hold.md:29:- The demo keeps fitting under a minute, with its reviewer stated as the script.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-community-claims-hold.md:44:- R4: The demo shall block a delivery, have it reviewed, close it through `pose close`, and fail unless the spec reads done and `pose review verify` approves it.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-community-claims-hold.md:96:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-community-claims-hold.md:104:- Rationale: the release cut criteria of `community-launch` ask for a delivery that is blocked and then legitimately closed, and a wording cannot redefine that; the first attempt at this spec tried and was refused in review\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-community-claims-hold.md:105:- Consequences: the script stands in for the reviewer and says so in the conclusion it records; a check of the matrix runs it\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-community-claims-hold.md:106:- Falsifier: a reader who takes the scripted review for an independent one\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-community-claims-hold.md:125:`pose public-claims` now reads a release as a reader meets it: tag links, the label of a release link, badges and sentences that say latest or current, with or without the `v` and keeping a prerelease suffix. Past releases stand only in a marked block of a declared surface. The READMEs hold no per-release text and no count of what ships, the quickstart claims no budget until a current measure exists, and the demo blocks a delivery, has it reviewed and closes it through the gate in under three seconds of machine time, checked by the matrix. Independently reviewed by Codex in four rounds: the first refused a wording change in place of a real close.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-community-claims-hold.md:129:The reviewer of the demo is the script, and it says so. A bare version in prose is treated as history, so a stale version with no word saying it is current passes. The gate covers declared surfaces only.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-community-claims-hold.md:133:- [open] F1: Measure the quickstart on a clean container and restore a dated budget; Docker was off during this spec. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-community-claims-hold.md:134:- [open] F2: Record the demo under 60 seconds and embed it, and publish a scoped contributor task and the Discussions space, which `community-surfaces` still owes. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-community-claims-hold.md:135:- [open] F3: Decide whether the landing page of Harne8 and the old docs host are surfaces of this gate, which `single-public-truth` still owes. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-engine-reads-raw-history.md:25:`pose release check --strict` accepted a tag with no release snapshot in its tree once `git replace` pointed its commit at a valid release: the tag and its object did not move, and the check returned `valid:true` with no gaps. `pose-history-readers-read-raw` gave the engine one raw reader, and the release helpers and about forty other calls never went through it. The review of milestone `manifest-tag-integrity` found this with a falsifier, after the review of the spec had not.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-engine-reads-raw-history.md:38:- `.git/shallow`, handled by `pose-review-reads-raw-history-and-roots-diff`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-engine-reads-raw-history.md:91:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-engine-reads-raw-history.md:114:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-engine-reads-raw-history.md:130:The falsifier of the milestone review as an integration test, domain and CLI, seen failing first, and a scan of the sources.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-engine-reads-raw-history.md:142:A replace ref can no longer supply the release snapshot of a tag: `pose release check` refuses it in the domain and in the CLI. Every Git reading in the Go sources of the engine goes through the raw reader, and a test that reads the syntax tree of the whole module refuses a new direct start, a starter taken as a value and a program the source does not name, with each exception bound to one start in one function. `pose report --git-stage` keeps writing to the index the operator selected. Independently reviewed by Codex in four rounds: the first found two calls in the ready check that a text pattern had missed and a write sent to the wrong index, the next two tightened the rule.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-engine-reads-raw-history.md:150:- [open] F1: Disarm executable Git configuration on observational gate calls, starting with `core.fsmonitor`, which still runs on a raw `git status` (review round 1 F2). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-engine-reads-raw-history.md:151:- [open] F3: Add a raw-history row to the adversarial corpus, with the launch forms and the operation of an exception. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-engine-reads-raw-history.md:152:- [open] F2: Decide which shipped scripts a raw-history rule should reach, starting with `tests/hygiene/temp-cleanup.sh` (review round 1 F4). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:40:`go.mod` as a real module, which invalidates the review attestation of\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:53:- No change to the provenance-digest/review-attestation mechanism itself\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:66:  `module-metadata.json` changes from invalidating unrelated specs' review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:97:  `.pose/policy`, `.pose/review-profiles`, or `.pose/indexes/{spec-graph,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:146:  policy, review-profile, spec, roadmap, report or knowledge file is ever\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:189:  (index/module-metadata/policy/review-profiles seeding factored out of\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:228:- created: .pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:326:  provenance digest and supersedes unrelated specs' review attestations.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:329:  digest so a module-metadata change only invalidates reviews whose scope\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:337:  exists to provide) that deserves its own spec, review and explicit\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:342:  removed or reclassified) still invalidates every closed spec's review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:483:  module-metadata change still invalidates unrelated closed specs' review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:521:- [open] Narrowing the provenance digest so a purely-additive `module-metadata.json` change does not invalidate unrelated closed specs' review attestations (Decision 2's accepted boundary) — worth its own spec if the review-reseal cascade this causes proves costly in practice beyond this one fixture-discovery case. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:522:- [open] A configurable per-repository exclusion list for module discovery, if a real case ever needs more than the hardcoded `testdata`/`fixture`/`fixtures` names this spec adds (Non-goals). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-16-pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes.md:523:- [open] A full Android/Kotlin validation profile (`validation-matrix.json` checks) now that discovery classifies the domain correctly — same deferred-scope pattern `pose-validation-scanner-consolidation` used for Cloudflare Workers. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegation-surface, pose-delegated-review-run-provenance\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:20:Choose the agent of a delegated run from the identity of whoever produced the subject, fall back in a declared order when the preferred agent is unavailable, and record the independence each run achieved.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:24:Decided by the [delegation ADR](../adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md). Today `--via` is mandatory and the implementation identity is a static declaration in `reviewers.json`, with a fixed execution. When the leading agent changes from one scope to the next, \"the other vendor\" has no answer, and the reviewer is compared with the policy file instead of with whoever implemented. A vendor out of quota is discovered only by a failed run.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:32:Continuing a stopped run with another agent (`pose-delegation-handoff`); relaxing `different-actor` when the capability is off (`pose-delegated-review-capability`).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:38:- R1: `pose review bundle --seal` shall record the implementation identity — principal, vendor, model, execution digest and its source (`detected` or `declared`) — in the bundle payload.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:43:- R6: An agent shall be unavailable when its CLI is not on the path, when its last run recorded a usage limit whose reset instant is in the future, or when its optional `probe` command fails within its bounded timeout; `pose delegate agents` shall show `available`, `limited until <instant>` or `missing`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:47:- R10: For `pose delegate task`, the implementation shall be the launching session's identity, determined as in R2 and R3.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:48:- R11: A `review` run with `same-model` independence shall never satisfy `different-actor`; `pose review verify` and the closeout shall disclose the achieved independence of the run behind each attestation.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:67:Bundle sealing and payload schema, routing resolver, availability reader, run record (`routing`, `independence_achieved`), assurance disclosure, `pose delegate agents`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:77:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_routing_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:82:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:83:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:84:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_assurance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:87:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:88:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:89:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_routing_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:90:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:91:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:92:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:94:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:103:- modified: docs-site/docs/review-and-trust.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:107:- capability:delegation-routing module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:120:- [x] First independent review: changes requested (B01–B08, F01–F05), all addressed; B04 by correcting D5, whose claim that a probe never stales a recorded run was wrong\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:121:- [x] Second independent review: B01–B08 and F01–F05 accepted as fixed (B04 by the corrected D5, B08 by both layers); changes requested for B09, with F06 and F07, all addressed with regression tests that fail on ca7aab5\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:122:- [x] Third independent review and native closeout: B09, F06 and F07 fixed; prior closures preserved; F08 and F09 accepted as low residual risks with owned follow-ups\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:147:- Consequences: resealing content a bundle already holds returns the bundle that governs it, with its identity, so a reviewer closing out never becomes the implementation; only a declared `--lead` naming another identity than the governing bundle's seals anew, and that seal names the bundle whose identity it replaces, so it governs whatever the seal instants or the ids say and a historical identity declared again is a new seal; a run compared with a replaced identity stops governing, and a run routed against an identity its bundle does not record does not start\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:155:- Consequences: sealing from a terminal or CI without `--lead` gives a bundle routing treats as of unknown vendor and attested review cannot use; the seal says so\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:156:- Falsifier: an attested different-actor review whose implementation vendor no seal recorded\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:161:- Selected option: default `max_wait` 5h, bounded at 24h; a probe is an argv with a 10s default and 60s bound, no placeholder, outside the adapter the review path verifies\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:168:- Minimal option: implement the task identity inside `pose delegate task`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:178:R10 is delivered as the session-identity determination the seal uses (D6); its caller in `pose delegate task` is deferred to `pose-delegation-task`, and the trace records it as such rather than as an executed task path. Fixture sessions with each vendor's markers seal bundles with the expected identity; `--lead` overrides and is labelled; a fake agent set with one vendor limited and one CLI missing routes through each fallback step in order; `wait` starts after a recorded reset and is skipped beyond `max_wait`; a same-model run is disclosed and refused as `different-actor`; an earlier bundle still reads the policy identity.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:185:- R4 [satisfied] check:delegated-run-provenance-integration test:TestRunProvenanceReadsTheSealedImplementation report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:187:- R6 [satisfied] check:delegation-surface-integration test:TestDelegationAvailabilityReadsPathRunsAndProbe test:TestAvailabilityReadsTheLastRunByInstant test:TestPreviewDisclosesNamedRoutingAndLimitedFollowsTheState report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:190:- R9 [satisfied] check:test test:TestNamedRunsRecordTheirRouting test:TestPreviewDisclosesNamedRoutingAndLimitedFollowsTheState report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:192:- R11 [satisfied] check:delegated-run-provenance-integration test:TestRunProvenanceReadsTheSealedImplementation test:TestRunProvenanceSameModelAndUnknownBaselineRefused report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:198:Milestone `routing` of roadmap `delegation`: sealed implementation identity with declared/detected source, legacy reading, ordered availability-aware routing and bounded cancellable waiting, per-run routing and achieved independence, and shared assurance disclosure. The prior dispatch, ledger, continuity, provenance and containment guarantees remain in force. R10 delivers the shared detector; integration into a running `pose delegate task` remains deferred to `pose-delegation-task` under D6.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:200:### Independent review and evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:202:Maintainer-authorized reviewer `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review` (Codex/OpenAI), a different vendor from implementer Claude/Anthropic, session `f2a4d9f2-d557-4064-ae96-6ed52bb47cd2`. The `agent:independent-` prefix is a declaration required by the engine; identity is declared and this instance's attestations are unsigned.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:204:Bundle `rvb-d7d135d12bc26b47`, attestation `rva-0440231118d1df1d`. Sealed explicitly with `--lead anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`; the seal's warning about the missing Anthropic session reference in the reviewing environment is expected. No implementation execution digest was invented. The native approval is declared review, not a signed vendor receipt.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:206:B09, F06 and F07 are fixed; B01-B08 and F01-F05 retain their earlier dispositions, including the D5 correction and both B08 layers. Round-2 probes pass; two old round-1 assertions remain superseded by the already accepted contract decisions. Full report, reproductions and mutation logs are retained locally under `.review-work/round3/` (deliberately untracked). Residual-risk handoff: knowledge:delegation-routing-round3.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:212:Strict artifact reconciliation matched 33 claims with 33 observed paths. Fresh capability composition, integration assessment, rule selection, design/debt assessment and native review verification were executed. Security scans found no known vulnerabilities or leaks in the reviewed change set. The docs-site matrix declares no checks; its documentation was manually reviewed, with that tool disposition disclosed rather than borrowed evidence. Both strict spec lint and all-spec lint passed; the strict structural check passed with preexisting warnings. The delegation roadmap remains nonterminal because later milestones are still draft; closing this spec does not close the whole roadmap.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:216:F08 is a low disclosure defect: `agents --lead` can label an unknown vendor independent, but that boolean does not govern routing, recorded independence or run-backed authority. F09 is a low helper serialization defect: canonicalizing a policy loses an explicitly empty fallback list; existing production writers do not rewrite an existing schema-2 policy. Acceptance expires at review on 2026-11-25, or earlier if such a writer is introduced. The handoff records synthetic recipes and boundaries.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:222:- [open] F08: make `pose delegate agents --lead` disclose unknown vendor conservatively in text and JSON; the current independent_of_lead boolean is not consumed by routing or approval. See knowledge:delegation-routing-round3. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-25)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md:223:- [open] F09: preserve absent versus explicitly empty routing.on_unavailable in canonical policy serialization before adding an existing-schema-2 rewrite consumer, also preserving declared agent order. See knowledge:delegation-routing-round3. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-25)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-dependabot-runtime-repair.md:61:- Rationale: only the derived runtime manifest needs automation; the PR keeps normal CI and maintainer review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-02-pose-dependabot-runtime-repair.md:86:A trusted default-branch workflow repairs only derived runtime evidence for eligible Dependabot action pins. PR review and existing security gates remain required.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-18-pose-ci-go-1-26-11.md:63:The six workflows now select Go 1.26.11. Local workflow contract and vulnerability scans passed. Independent review and CI are pending.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-monorepo-validation-advisory.md:38:framing suggests — a root manifest whose own script explicitly delegates\n.pose/specs/2026-08-15-pose-monorepo-validation-advisory.md:179:      delegates via npm, expected); `pose validate --workspace foo`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-release-stability.md:26:configuration example must be reviewable, and the Windows package check must\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-release-stability.md:61:- The bundle shall retain the bytes of `.env.example` for security review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-release-stability.md:83:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-release-stability.md:84:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-release-stability.md:93:The generated contributor instructions and review-bundle path classification\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-v6-2-0-release-stability.md:111:These targets identify contributor guidance and immutable review classification.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-upgrade-compatibility-lab.md:65:- [ ] Exercise dry-run, apply, reapply and preservation assertions. ([reference](https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/))\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-upgrade-compatibility-lab.md:78:**Strategy:** validate the upgrade engine against a populated instance (dry-run accuracy, apply/reapply idempotency, preservation of locale/user-modified/populated content), an explicit-remediation negative case, and a symlink-escape security case — all network-free; real N-minus pairs are deferred to the network-dependent release gate.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-upgrade-compatibility-lab.md:88:- R3 [satisfied] dry-run proven byte-for-byte non-mutating, apply proven to change only `schema-version` on a populated instance, reapply proven a strict no-op; check:test (TestUpgradeDryRunIsAccurateAndNonMutating, TestUpgradeApplyIsIdempotentAndPreservesInstanceContent)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-upgrade-compatibility-lab.md:93:- `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli/... -run 'Upgrade' -v -count=1` — SUCCESS (5 tests: dry-run non-mutation, apply+idempotent-reapply+preservation, newer-instance explicit remediation with zero partial mutation, symlinked-managed-dir rejection with zero write-through and zero schema advance, plus the pre-existing legacy-instance compatibility test).\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-upgrade-compatibility-lab.md:104:- Delivered scope: `cmdUpgrade` (previously zero unit-tested) now has full R2/R3 coverage against a populated instance — pt-BR locale content, a real spec, a real knowledge note, a hand-edited managed file — proving dry-run non-mutation, apply-changes-only-schema-version, idempotent reapply, and preservation; a new `ensureManagedDirSafe` helper closes a real symlink-escape gap in the three managed directories `pose upgrade` creates; `tests/release/compat.sh` gained the same populated-fixture depth for real N-minus pairs (R1) plus an idempotency/preservation assertion it previously lacked.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-upgrade-compatibility-lab.md:110:- [spawned: pose-release-cycle-debt-closure] Confirm the first real `check_upgrade_pair` run in `tests/release/compat.sh` once `compatibility.json.supported_upgrades` gets its first entry, and record the result. Superseded in part by `pose-compat-gate-candidate-integrity`: the support window now starts at 0.18.2, so the awaited entry is no longer 0.9.0 but the release after 0.18.2. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:high review:2026-09-04)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-review-brief\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-contract\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:12:delivers: capability:delegated-review-brief\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:21:Generate the request a delegated reviewer receives from the sealed bundle itself, so the implementer no longer writes the reviewer's prompt.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:25:On 2026-10-09 the implementing agent wrote every prompt the reviewing agent received, which lets the reviewed party frame — or steer — the review. Everything a reviewer needs is already in the sealed bundle.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:27:Origin: the 2026-10-09 review of `pose-native-attestation-issuer` by Codex through a personal launcher; it found three real defects in three rounds and exposed what the engine lacks (ADR `2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter`, roadmap `delegated-review`).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:37:- R1: `pose review brief <bundle|scope>` shall render the scope, the change set diff reference, the plan's pending criteria and tool dispositions, the material structural facts and the sealed evidence, from the sealed bundle only.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:40:- R4: The brief shall state the reviewer's boundaries: report defects with file and line, do not change the repository, do not record an attestation — the engine records a verified run's conclusion (ADR decision 1).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:42:- R6: The brief shall have three kinds — `review` (a spec's sealed bundle), `adjudication` (an independent verdict on a recorded question, such as a pilot's outcomes, with the evidence it names) and `smoke` (a scripted run of a delivered surface with its expected observations) — each with its own versioned template and the same boundaries.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:48:A brief renderer in `pose-mcp/internal/pose` over `ReviewBundle`, a versioned template, and the `review brief` subcommand with `--json`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:52:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:53:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-review-brief.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:54:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-review-brief.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:55:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:56:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:57:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_brief.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:58:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:63:- capability:delegated-review-brief module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:68:- [x] `pose review brief` with `--note-file` and `--json`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:73:The contract is ADR `2026-10-09-delegated-review-is-an-adapter`, accepted on 2026-10-09 with the maintainer's decisions: the engine records a verified run, people by exception through policy, agent independence by differing vendor or model (different vendor preferred), and reviews, adjudications and smoke runs from the first delivery.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:79:Golden test: the same bundle renders identical bytes; a fixture with a seeded defect is reviewed from the brief alone in the adoption milestone's journey.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:83:2026-10-10: `pose review brief spec:pose-v7-3-0-version-alignment` renders the scope, the range bb938fc6..42ee510e with its seven attributed paths, every planned criterion with its kind and evidence classes, the plan's tools and the sealed evidence, from `rvb-b0ae3428882f27f6` alone. The seeded-defect review named in this spec's validation strategy belongs to the capability milestone's journey, where a reviewer run exists.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:85:2026-10-10, independent review (agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review, fallback reviewer): low severity. The smoke brief repeated the review criteria instead of scripting a run. It now lists each delivery target of the spec with its entrypoint under \"Surfaces to run\", the spec's requirements under \"Expected observations\", and asks for observations per surface and per requirement.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:89:- R1 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-brief evidence:unit test:TestReviewBriefIsRenderedFromTheBundleDeterministically\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:90:- R2 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-brief evidence:unit test:TestReviewBriefIsRenderedFromTheBundleDeterministically\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:91:- R3 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-brief evidence:unit test:TestReviewBriefLabelsImplementerNotes\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:92:- R4 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-brief evidence:unit test:TestReviewBriefIsRenderedFromTheBundleDeterministically\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:93:- R5 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-brief evidence:unit test:TestReviewBriefRefusesStaleBundlesAndHasThreeKinds\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:94:- R6 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-brief evidence:unit test:TestReviewBriefRefusesStaleBundlesAndHasThreeKinds test:TestSmokeBriefScriptsTheDeliveredSurfaces\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:100:`pose review brief` renders the request a delegated reviewer receives from the sealed bundle, in three kinds, with fixed boundaries and implementer notes fenced in a labelled section.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-delegated-review-brief.md:104:- The brief does not inline the diff or the spec text: the reviewer reads them from the repository at the named range, which the dispatch milestone gives it as a disposable worktree.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-live-policy-reads-through-aliases.md:16:Close the regex blind spot in the sealed-review security regression guard.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-live-policy-reads-through-aliases.md:59:  is regenerated before sealing the governed review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-01-pose-live-policy-reads-through-aliases.md:71:Implementation validated and closed through the governed review gate on 2026-10-01. Canonical strict validation passed 48/48 checks at f41b5aa; review bundle `rvb-6bf323b456383c97` was fresh and approved before `pose close`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:25:Follow-up F5 of `pose-delegation-parity-gate`: removing `pose review dispatch` meant deleting `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch.go`, which five done specs declare as current; `check --strict` refused, and the file was kept only to hold the removed aliases' answer. POSE knew how a release archives a file, not how a later spec removes one, so any removal of a file an earlier spec created forced either keeping it or rewriting a closed spec's history.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:43:- R5: `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch.go` shall be removed, the removed aliases' answer moved back into the review command, and the five done specs that declare it shall pass `check --strict` through R1.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:62:Delivery-integrity graph (existence rule, removal witnesses, edges), the CLI that builds its inputs from Git, the review command, the manuals.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:84:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:85:- removed: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:104:- [x] Remove review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:106:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:122:A Git fixture with spec A creating a file, spec B deleting it later and declaring `removed:`: A's existence passes and the graph has the edge; spec C declaring `modified:` after the removal still fails; B's removal unobserved, B on a branch not containing A's change, and A removing its own file all keep the finding. Then the real removal of `review_dispatch.go` passes `check --strict`. Each rule is shown failing on revert.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:130:- R5 [satisfied] check:delivery-later-removal-integration test:TestTheRemovedReviewAliasesNameTheirReplacement report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:f88e5ca847d0233f9a88b950f87f789114430936 — `review_dispatch.go` is removed at 839a738767642caef0aea0432c28bdf96d886397; the real index records that removal superseding the six specs that declare the file, and `check --strict` passes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:137:Follow-up F5 of `pose-delegation-parity-gate`: a later spec's observed removal satisfies the existence of a path earlier specs declare current, when every earlier change to the path precedes the deletion in Git; `review_dispatch.go` is removed. Attribution reads raw object history engine-wide (no replace refs or grafts). Independently reviewed by Codex over seven rounds (reports kept outside the checkout); 37 mutations of the rule killed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:141:Other history readers of structural review still honour replace refs (F1). A trailer change set beginning at the repository root does not resolve, so a valid removal of a root creation is refused (F2). Git work has no aggregate budget (F3). `index --verify` does not bind Git or recorded history, so an indexed witness is as fresh as its generation (F4). A shallow clone refuses every removal; a full-history checkout is required for the exemption.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:145:- [covered: pose-history-readers-read-raw] F1: align the history readers of structural review (`review_path_attribution.go`, `review_bundle.go`, `git_spawn_cache.go`, `git_batch.go`, `design_delta.go`) with raw object history, correct caches keyed by object ID, and say how to regenerate evidence (LR-R4-02). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:146:- [covered: pose-history-readers-read-raw] F2: resolve a trailer change set whose first commit is the repository root without `root^`, with collector and graph coverage (LR-R4-03). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:147:- [open] F3: give removal history reads cancellation, batching and an aggregate subprocess and memory budget, with a Git-call-count test and a wide-history benchmark (LR-R1-09). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:148:- [covered: pose-removal-witness-freshness] F4: bind the Git and recorded-history inputs of removal witnesses to index generation freshness, or report their freshness as unknown (LR-R1-10). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delivery-later-removal.md:149:- [open] F5: build the deletion-order fixture of `TestLaterRemovalHistoryShapes` deterministically instead of a bounded SHA search (LR-R6-02). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph.md:24:A spec `pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation` mediu, na primeira chamada `pose_closeout_state` de um servidor MCP no harne8, 1.116 comandos `git log -1 --format=%H -- <path>` somando 81 s: cada um percorre o histórico do pose-dist (3.528 commits) até achar o último commit que tocou o arquivo. Com o commit-graph com caminhos alterados (`git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths`), cada consulta cai de 47 ms para 2 ms, sem mudar a saída do Git, e a primeira chamada cai de 136 s para 59 s. É manutenção do repositório, que o motor não faz sozinho numa leitura de governança; o `doctor` é o lugar onde o POSE já recomenda e aplica remediações seguras.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph.md:102:- Context: o follow-up F1 da spec `pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation`; o maintainer pediu para escrever o commit-graph nos checkouts dele e seguir com o F1.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph.md:154:- [open] F1: medir e reduzir o `pose doctor` no harne8, que passa de 900 s em Go, sem processo Git filho, já com o binário anterior a esta spec. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-23)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:18:Make what a review profile may demand and what a registered check may emit the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:24:- `reviewEvidenceClassCatalog` — sixteen names a profile could declare.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:28:satisfy — `contract`, `integration-test`, `lint`, `manual-review`,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:48:  check declare `manual-review` as its evidence class.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:64:- R1: A review profile declaring an evidence class outside `ValidEvidenceClasses`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:80:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go` — profile contract validation\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:81:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go` — the filters this removes\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:87:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:88:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:89:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:100:  loading it, which fails review planning rather than degrading it. That is the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:102:  hard stop on update, and `pose doctor`'s `review.evidence-vocabulary` has\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:132:  and it would let `pose validate` accept `manual-review` as a check's evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:185:- Notes: all eight packages pass, including every review test with both filters\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:214:- [done] Decide whether lint, typecheck, security-scan and contract should be emittable classes rather than reported as build. Decided yes, in `pose-emittable-analysis-evidence-classes` (ADR amendment 2026-09-09): all four join the closed vocabulary, `go vet` moves to `lint` and a `go build ./...` check restores the Go stack's `build` producer. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-12-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-one-evidence-class-vocabulary.md:215:- [open] Consider whether the evidence-class vocabulary should be extensible by an instance rather than compiled in (owner:unowned crit:low review:2027-03-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-remaining-command-surfaces-coverage.md:25:`review-check`, `history-check`, `docs-sync`, `docs-review`, `contribute\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-remaining-command-surfaces-coverage.md:158:- R2 [satisfied] <TestTheseCommandsRefuseAnInvocationTheyCannotServe requires exit 2 and the message for six usage paths; the review-check, roadmap-check and contribute-submit tests each add a refusal of their own> surface:remaining-command-surfaces-coverage evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-remaining-command-surfaces-coverage.md:178:- [done] `roadmap-check` returns before loading any roadmap when `.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json` is absent, so it reports zero cut criteria and exits 0 — a gate reading as met because the path that would fail is never reached; roadmap criteria include check: and manual-review: refs that need no delivery profile. Fixed in `pose-roadmap-check-reaches-its-gate`: neither an absent profile index nor an absent specs directory skips the evaluation, so every criterion gets the verdict it deserves and an unresolved delivery ref blocks as it should. (owner:unowned crit:high review:2026-11-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-remaining-command-surfaces-coverage.md:179:- [open] Cover what the audit found and this spec did not: the assess trio, the install and self-update helpers, runServeMCP, parseSinceDate, inferSuggestDomain, siblingSpecStatus and hasOpenChild (owner:unowned crit:low review:2027-01-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-consolidation-batch-2-authoring.md:96:Gates locais e critérios de saída julgados no [bundle rvb-600e9e49de40e63c](../review-bundles/rvb-600e9e49de40e63c.json), com [atestação rva-08d7378a329f5dca](../review-attestations/rva-08d7378a329f5dca.json) de uma execução separada do Codex, mesmo fornecedor/modelo herdado. Sem alegação de identidade autenticada ou revisão entre fornecedores.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:2:slug: pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:10:delivers: capability:review-subject-and-scope-precision\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:13:# Spec: Precision in the review subject and its component scope\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:18:Correct two defects in work shipped days earlier, both found by review of the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:27:**A gitlink under a classified path is unsealable.** `pose-review-subject-submodule-classification`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:32:    if sha, ok := reviewBundleGitlinkSHA(s.Root, path); ok { ... }\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:38:the lookup never runs. The digest step then calls `reviewBundleFileDigest` on a\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:44:**Overlay evidence classes leak across components.** `pose-review-plan-producible-evidence-classes`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:59:- `reviewBundlePathClass` stays a pure function of the path. Being a gitlink is\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:66:- Reviewing a submodule's contents. The reviewable unit remains the pointer that\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:67:  moved; the tree behind it has its own repository and its own review.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:92:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go` — gitlink resolution and precedence\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:93:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go` — per-component evidence scoping\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:96:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:97:- renamed: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md -> .pose/changelogs/v1.8.0/pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:98:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:99:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:100:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:101:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:105:- capability:review-subject-and-scope-precision module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:134:- Options considered: (a) call Git inside `reviewBundlePathClass`; (b) call it\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:141:  over the subject's own paths, so the cost is bounded by what is being reviewed\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:180:  fixture failing on `review subject path api/dep cannot be read`. Making the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:194:- R1 [satisfied] <review_bundle.go — the gitlink map is consulted before the shape class is honoured; TestReviewBundleClassifiesSubmoduleUnderAMappedComponent covers a submodule under a mapped component>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:195:- R2 [satisfied] <reviewBundleGitlinks issues one `git ls-files --stage --` over the subject's candidate paths, replacing the per-path lookup>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:196:- R3 [satisfied] <review_plan.go — profileEvidence filters overlays by the components their selection matched; TestReviewPlanScopesOverlayEvidenceToItsMatchedComponent asserts each component keeps only its own overlay's classes>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision.md:211:- [open] Review whether other synthesised tools should be component-scoped like validate, rather than only the one this defect exposed (owner:unowned crit:low review:2026-12-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:26:On 2026-10-09 four instances (Harne8, pose-dist, audio-relay, storageclose) were declared adopted on 7.1.0 because `pose update --no-self --dry-run` printed only `instance already at schema v1` and `DRY-RUN — no changes applied`. The real update then merged machinery into AGENTS.md, POSE.md, skills and the spec template, stamped `engine_version`, seeded `.pose/project.json` and opened a configuration review with up to eight decision requests. Every instance had stayed stamped by 6.1.0 since its earlier update; only `pose version` revealed it, and `doctor` and `check --strict` passed silently. Three adoption specs recorded a false conclusion as a result.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:36:- R1: `pose update --dry-run` shall list every file it would merge or create, the `engine_version` change, and each configuration-review request it would open, with the same wording the real run prints.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:59:> - created: .pose/adr/2026-10-22-update-preview-records-the-shared-execution-in-an-operation-scoped-view.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:60:> - created: .pose/reports/2026-10-22-b29-update-preview-design-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:64:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/update_preview_confinement_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:72:review directory guards before metadata inspection. Run focused Go tests, full\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:73:strict validation, race tests and fresh CodeQL, then obtain a fresh sealed review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:88:- created: .pose/adr/2026-10-22-update-preview-records-the-shared-execution-in-an-operation-scoped-view.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:89:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-22-b29-update-preview-design-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:90:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/update_preview_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:95:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/configuration_review.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:132:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/docs_review.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:157:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attribution.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:158:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:159:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:160:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:161:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_path_attribution.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:162:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:163:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reuse_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:164:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_structure.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:171:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-22-b29-update-preview-implementation.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:174:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/update_preview_linux_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:175:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/update_preview_facts_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:177:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:185:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/update_preview_composition_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:186:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/update_preview_release_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:188:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/release_review_regression_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:190:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-23-b29-pending-review-r1.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:214:- Decision: Use the shared apply/preview execution context and in-memory operation-scoped view described in [the prospective ADR](../adr/2026-10-22-update-preview-records-the-shared-execution-in-an-operation-scoped-view.md). Preserve the current running-engine/no-self preview boundary and normal apply semantics; include force install, discovery, requests, index computation and final governance reads.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:215:- Rationale: One execution algorithm with projected reads eliminates reconstruction and second-planner drift. Partial preview cannot satisfy R1/R2.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:229:| Operation view read-after-write, alias/link replacement, exclusive/atomic/direct-write distinction and failure injection | `go test ./internal/... -run 'UpdateOperation|UpdatePreview' -count=1` | No physical preview mutation, coherent staged reads, typed failures and exact net effects. Register exact final tests/check before collecting. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:231:| Running-engine update parity, force/nonforce, EN/pt-BR, current/stale/schema migration, requests and policy/profile seeding | `go test ./internal/cli -run 'UpdateDryRun|UpdatePreview|Upgrade|Machinery|ConfigurationReview' -count=1` | Preview/apply share semantic events and per-request content, actual resulting state matches intended effects; no false no-op. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:232:| Original discovery and adversarial filesystem/permission layouts | `go test ./internal/cli -run 'UpdateDryRun|UpdatePreview|Discovery' -count=1` | Existing symlink corpus, execute-only directory with named child, external/broken links, ignored/submodule/nested modules and unknown relevant reads exercised in unprivileged fixtures. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:233:| End-to-end no-write audit and force projected gate | `go test ./internal/cli -run 'UpdatePreview.*(Subprocess|NoWrites|Force|Parity)' -count=1` | Actual command preview produces no filesystem effects, including external targets and transient staging/locks; projected final gate sees planned governance state. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:235:| Go API, races and platform builds | `go test ./...`; `go vet ./...`; `go test -race ./internal/pose ./internal/cli` | Existing production behavior preserved; no shared global preview state; existing cross-platform build checks retained. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:237:At the time this prospective plan was recorded, no replacement test above had executed. Current implementer results and exact selectors are recorded in [the implementation report](../reports/2026-10-22-b29-update-preview-implementation.md); the registered required check is `update-preview-integration`. Native global evidence, immutable attribution and independent final review remain with the parent.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:243:2026-10-10, independent review (agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review, fallback reviewer): medium severity. `pose update --dry-run --force` reported \"the update would fail\" because the copy held an empty `.git` and `--force` runs install, which refuses a directory git does not recognise; the real `--force` update succeeded. The copy is now `git init`-ed; `TestUpdateDryRunWithForceRunsOnTheCopy` covers it (reproduced on audio-relay before the fix).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:245:2026-10-10, independent review (agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review): medium severity. The copy skipped symlinks, so with `.pose/policy` symlinked the dry-run predicted 23 files and 12 requests the real update does not create. The copy now follows symlinks as the update reads through them (cycles broken, broken links skipped); `TestUpdateDryRunFollowsASymlinkedPolicy` fails on the previous copy.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:247:2026-10-10, second independent review (agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review): medium severity. Following links turned them into plain directories, hiding the update's refusals: with `.pose/templates` symlinked the dry-run returned 0 and the real update 1. The copy now keeps links as links, pointing at copies of their targets (inside the shadow, or next to it for targets outside the instance), so the update meets the same links and nothing it writes reaches the instance; `hashTree` reads through links to compare content. `TestUpdateDryRunMeetsTheLinksTheUpdateMeets` fails on the previous copy.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:249:2026-10-10, third independent review (agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review, fallback reviewer): two medium findings and one low. (1, 2) A directory reached through a link and by its own path (`.claude/skills -> ../.agents/skills`) was copied twice, and the second pass failed on the links and read-only files the first wrote, where the update succeeds; the copy is now idempotent. `TestUpdateDryRunCopiesALinkedDirectoryOnce` fails on the previous copy. (3) Action request ids hash the second they are opened, so the copy's file names were not the update's, and `TestUpdateDryRunListsWhatTheUpdateChanges` failed about 1 in 300 runs; the dry-run now counts the requests it would open instead of naming them, and the test compares counts (40 consecutive runs pass).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:251:2026-10-10, fourth independent review (agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review, fallback reviewer): medium severity. The \"already copied\" shortcut took a directory as copied because its path existed, which a link to one file inside it had created first; with `.pose/policy -> ../config/policy` and an alias to one policy file, the dry-run predicted 31 changes and 12 requests against the update's 9 and 8. The shortcut is gone: a linked directory is always copied, and the copy skips what is already there. `TestUpdateDryRunCopiesADirectoryAfterALinkIntoIt` fails on the previous copy.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:253:2026-10-10, fifth independent review (agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review, fallback reviewer): medium severity. A link to a directory that contains it (`.pose/self -> .`, `.agents/up -> ..`) made the copy reach the same link again and fail with \"file exists\", where the update succeeds; the self case regressed in 5e2579af. Such a link is now linked to the copy of its target without copying the target into itself, and a link already recreated is left alone. `TestUpdateDryRunLinksADirectoryThatContainsTheLink` fails on the previous copy.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:255:2026-10-10, sixth independent review (agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review): high severity. A broken link was recreated with its original target, so with `.pose/rules/security.md` pointing at a missing absolute path the dry-run created that external file and still said nothing was applied. A broken link is now recreated still broken, at the same missing path inside the shadow when the target was inside the instance, or at a missing path next to the shadow otherwise; no link in the copy points outside it. `TestUpdateDryRunNeverWritesThroughABrokenLink` fails on the previous copy.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:257:2026-10-10, seventh independent review (agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review): medium severity. The stand-in for an external broken link lost whether its parent directory exists, so with the target's directory present the dry-run said the update would fail while the update created the file. The stand-in's parent now exists exactly when the original's does. `TestUpdateDryRunAgreesOnABrokenLinkIntoAnExistingDirectory` fails on the previous copy.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:259:2026-10-10, eighth independent review (agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review): medium severity. A broken link at the top of the instance (`AGENTS.md` pointing into a missing directory) was left out of the copy, so with `--force` the dry-run predicted success where the update fails. Top-level links to files and broken top-level links are now copied as links. `TestUpdateDryRunKeepsABrokenTopLevelLink` fails on the previous copy.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:261:2026-10-10, ninth independent review (agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review): medium severity, outside symlink layouts. Directories were recreated 0755, so with `.pose` read-only the update failed while the dry-run said it would change nothing. The copy now applies each directory's original permissions after copying, deepest first, and makes them writable again to remove the copy. `TestUpdateDryRunKeepsDirectoryPermissions` fails on the previous copy.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:263:2026-10-10, tenth independent review (agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review): medium severity. The copy read every file at the root, so an unrelated unreadable file (mode 000) made the dry-run fail where the update succeeds. An unreadable file is now reproduced as an empty file with the same mode, and an unreadable directory as an empty one with its mode, so the update meets the same refusals; comparisons skip what cannot be read. `TestUpdateDryRunToleratesUnreadableFiles` fails on the previous copy.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:265:2026-10-10, after the tenth independent review (a directory with mode 0100 can be read by name but not listed, so the copy came out empty): the maintainer decided that POSE 7.4.0 ships without this spec. Its changelog fragment is withdrawn from `.pose/changelogs/unreleased/`, so 7.4.0's notes do not announce the dry-run; the spec stays open and is redone for 7.5.0 with the approach of the open follow-up (the update recording what it would do instead of running on a copy). The copy-based dry-run already on main stays in the code until then.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:277:The registered `update-preview-integration` check and fresh strict native collection pass146/146 at source `a7af88f`. Current review and governed lifecycle disposition are recorded in the closeout report.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:279:- R1 [satisfied] capability:update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update evidence:integration test:TestUpdatePreviewParityAcrossUpdateBranches test:TestUpdatePreviewNamesEachDecisionRequestAsTheUpdateDoes test:TestUpdatePreviewForceStagesInstructionsBeforeFinalGate test:TestUpdatePreviewHasNoPhysicalMutationEvents\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:280:- R2 [satisfied] capability:update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update evidence:integration test:TestUpdatePreviewDoesNotCallLostEvaluationNoChange test:TestUpdatePreviewDistinguishesRefusedOperationsFromNoOp test:TestUpdatePreviewSourceReviewFilesystemReachability test:TestUpdatePreviewUnreadableEmptySkillDirectoryIsIncomplete test:TestUpdatePreviewRetentionPartialRemovalIsIncomplete\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:285:The historical D1 report below describes the rejected copier and remains audit history. The replacement qualification and linked closeout report carry current source, evidence, review and lifecycle disposition.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:289:D2 uses one shared update execution with an explicit operation-scoped in-memory view. Reads see staged files, original source discovery stays authoritative, and complete previews report file effects, engine stamps and individual request semantics. Unknown access, umask, inode alias, special-file or removal effects remain INCOMPLETE rather than successful no-ops. Native apply is unchanged. Fresh canonical strict validation passes146/146 at5bb89dd, with zero skips/errors; security boundary guards fix the six PR202 CodeQL findings and preserve intended local and projected paths; see [the closeout report](../reports/2026-10-23-b29-pending-closeout.md) and [implementation evidence](../reports/2026-10-22-b29-update-preview-implementation.md). Source review R1/R2/R3 rejections and fixes remain historical; actual current review and lifecycle disposition are recorded in the closeout report.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update.md:298:- Symlink layouts. Eight review rounds each found a rarer layout where the copy and the instance differed; all eight are fixed and tested. On 2026-10-10 the maintainer decided that the ninth round is the last for this spec: a symlink layout not yet covered is a residual risk tracked by the follow-up below, and only a defect outside symlink layouts blocks closing. The copy never points a link outside itself, so an uncovered layout can make the dry-run's prediction wrong, not make it write into the instance or elsewhere.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-review-check-time-and-output-regression-test.md:2:slug: pose-review-check-time-and-output-regression-test\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-review-check-time-and-output-regression-test.md:20:O tempo e a saída de `review-check` num repositório com histórico real passam a ter um teste de regressão com limiar fixado, em vez de medição manual.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-review-check-time-and-output-regression-test.md:24:As specs `pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once` e `pose-governance-audit-skips-pure-git-reads` reduziram o `review-check` de cerca de 56 s para cerca de 25 s com a saída idêntica, mas só provaram o tempo e a saída por medição manual; qualquer regressão volta sem teste que a pegue.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-review-check-time-and-output-regression-test.md:36:- R1: Um teste opt-in mede o `review-check` de um repositório sintético de histórico e artefatos fixados e falha acima de um limiar declarado antes da medição.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:51:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-22-b38-pending-review-r1.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:69:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/release_review_regression_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:70:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/release_review_regression_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:71:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/release_review_r2_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:74:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-b38r5-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:75:- created: .pose/results/b38r5-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:76:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/release_review_r6_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:77:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-b38r6-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:78:- created: .pose/results/b38r6-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:81:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/release_review_r4_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:83:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-b38r4-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:84:- created: .pose/results/b38r4-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:86:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_release_archive_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:87:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-b38r2-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:88:- created: .pose/results/b38r2-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:94:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-b38-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:95:- created: .pose/results/b38-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:168:B38 entregue: o manifest passa por um contrato estrito (schema suportado, campos desconhecidos recusados, versão e caminhos limpos, projeções `specs`/`categories`/`breaking` e `release_input_digest` recompostas a partir dos fragments congelados); `release check` e `release status` verificam a tag pela sua própria árvore (tag leve ou anotada resolvida ao commit; manifest, notas, fragments congelados e fonte de versão lidos como blobs desse commit), recusam tag sem snapshot qualquer que seja o worktree, não tornam obsoleto um cut correto por commit, evidência ou ciclo posteriores, e reportam como limite a fonte de versão que não pode ser recomputada. A décima terceira revisão independente (`agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review`, Claude/Anthropic, o mesmo vendor do implementador: sem separação de vendor, só de execução e de contexto, porque o Codex está indisponível até 2026-10-24) aprovou no HEAD `07e77f89` sem bloqueante, com atestação sem envelope; ver o [parecer](../reports/2026-10-19-b38r13-claude-independent-review.md).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:187:- [open] Recusar `version_evidence.kind: null` no manifest. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:188:- [open] Harmonizar os filtros de arquivos auxiliares entre o snapshot e o worktree. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:189:- [open] Expor os limites e a integridade do candidato nos diagnósticos do status. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:190:- [open] Ampliar o padrão do check de integração desta spec para os consumidores novos. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:191:- [open] Usar o carregador estrito da policy de changelog em plan e prepare. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:192:- [open] Reconciliar o texto de authoring da spec com a implementação e a validação efetivamente executadas, mantendo separado o closeout pendente. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:193:- [open] Explicitar o tratamento de links de worktree com bytes idênticos aos do snapshot da tag. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:194:- [open] Fazer os smokes históricos recusarem leituras com erro e execuções com zero fixtures. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:195:- [open] Distinguir um cut de uma prova de adoção em `governedReleaseWitness`: um manifest sob policy explicitamente não adotada não deve, sozinho, impor adoção depois que a policy opcional deixa de existir; preservar a recusa de perdas e leituras inconclusivas. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:196:- [open] Fazer `releaseInputs` recusar entradas do inventário que não são diretório ao calcular a versão anterior, como o checker e o status. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:197:- [open] Usar o carregador estrito da policy de changelog nos fragments pendentes do checker e de `checkRelease`. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:198:- [open] Harmonizar o julgamento de tags fora de SemVer entre o checker e o status em projetos adotados. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:199:- [open] Validar pelo contrato estrito a policy da árvore da tag em `TagHoldsAdoptedReleasePolicy`, em vez de só ler `adopted_at`. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:201:- [open] Qualificar com regressão dedicada a variante de linha ruim em `packed-refs`, preservando o contrato de erro já compartilhado pelo inventário e pela resolução explícita de tags. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:202:- [open] Considerar um `GIT_DIR` perdido em `GitNotARepository`. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:203:- [open] Não reprovar o `pose check` por uma tag SemVer que aponta para árvore ou blob. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:204:- [open] Derivar de novo `previous_version` e informá-lo como limite. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:205:- [open] Fazer `release check` não descartar `ForeignFragmentClaims` em silêncio quando o archive ou as specs não puderem ser lidos. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:206:- [open] Evitar que o status leia o snapshot e a policy da árvore de cada tag de um projeto não adotado antes de descartá-la (cerca de 2,9 s com 300 tags). (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:207:- [open] Fazer o status usar a mesma testemunha de adoção do checker quando a policy de hoje foi apagada: hoje só um corte no worktree conta, e uma tag sem manifest cuja árvore não traz a adoção some do status e das obligations quando a adoção é provada só pelo manifest de outra tag (o `pose check` reprova, e `open-next` continua recusando). (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-release-manifest-tag-integrity.md:213:Historical native done and R13 approval remain unchanged as historical events. A separate source review of the current main merge found a medium two-release selection variant of R11-L14: broken newer tag omitted with successful Git exit could promote an older verified release for open-next. It was reproduced before fixing; unknown/corrupt ref is not proven missing, and tag inventory diagnostics now propagate through shared status/plan/check/backfill consumers. Current strict collection 143/143 and final separate sealed review of `rvb-ef842bee6b11a74f` approved; no release is prepared/published, no tag/history is rewritten.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-one-follow-up-format.md:25:`(owner:@alias crit:low|medium|high review:YYYY-MM-DD)`. Anything else is\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-one-follow-up-format.md:27:no review date — so it never becomes overdue.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-one-follow-up-format.md:30:fields after a dash instead: `— owner:unowned crit:low review:…`. Twenty-seven\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-one-follow-up-format.md:121:- A follow-up whose prose mentions `owner:` or `review:` without being metadata\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-one-follow-up-format.md:186:  count is 0, and the 27 items carry `crit:low` and a review date in `pose\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-one-follow-up-format.md:196:- R1 [satisfied] <both spec templates show `- [<disposition>] <text> (owner:@alias crit:low|medium|high review:YYYY-MM-DD)` and state that any other placement is ignored>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-one-follow-up-format.md:205:  a review date, so they surface when due.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-changelog-adoption-is-the-instances.md:118:  practice. Stamping is what the review contracts already do, and it is the only\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-changelog-adoption-is-the-instances.md:172:- [open] Report a changelog adoption date earlier than the instance's own first spec, so an instance that inherited this repository's date before the fix can see that it is gating by a date that is not its own (owner:unowned crit:low review:2027-03-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-changelog-adoption-is-the-instances.md:173:- [done] The shipped review policy still carries this repository's adoption dates — `adopted_at` 2026-08-02, `component_aware_adopted_at` 2026-08-13, `review_bundles_adopted_at` 2026-08-14, `evidence_vocabulary_reconciled_at` 2026-09-08 — and a fresh `pose install` copies them, while the changelog policy beside it is stamped with the install day. `adopted_at` is the cutoff `pose check` uses to require review closeouts, so an instance importing a history of done specs is judged by someone else's date. Measured 2026-09-11 on a 5.0.2 install. Decide whether install stamps these like the changelog date. Resolved, reconciled 2026-10-04 (spec pose-open-backlog-reconciliation): pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.pose/policy/review.json carries no adoption dates.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-governance-git-reads-batched-by-commit.md:20:As cerca de 240 execuções de `git log -1 -- <path>` de um `review-check` viram uma leitura agrupada que dá, para cada caminho, o mesmo commit que a execução individual dá.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-governance-git-reads-batched-by-commit.md:24:Depois das specs de engine, o `review-check` leva cerca de 25 s e cerca de 14 s são esses `git log -1 -- <path>` (cerca de 57 ms cada num histórico de 2 800 commits). Agrupá-los muda a semântica da simplificação de histórico de merges, então a equivalência tem de ser provada, não suposta.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-governance-git-reads-batched-by-commit.md:38:- R3: A medição mostra o ganho no `review-check` com a saída idêntica.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-federated-proof-reads-each-input-once.md:41:- R4: What a review bundle's bytes declare about their scope shall be parsed once per content digest, each file keeping its own artifact path in a loss.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-federated-proof-reads-each-input-once.md:61:- `pose/review_operation_view.go`: parse do cabeçalho por digest do conteúdo.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-federated-proof-reads-each-input-once.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-federated-proof-reads-each-input-once.md:71:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_header_cache_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-federated-proof-reads-each-input-once.md:160:- [open] F1: o `check` recalcula o material federado inteiro para cada escopo (`checkReviewCloseout` → `ReadIndex` → `checkIndexInputs` → `BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn`), e cada worker retém a própria read view: no harne8, 37 min com 4 workers e mais de 11 GB com 16. Calcular o material uma vez por processo, com chave no fechamento de entradas da read view, e limitar a memória por worker. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:high review:2026-11-22)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-manual-merge-backs-up-only-local-edits.md:134:- Context: review of pose#103 — the first version recorded every section of the\n.pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets.md:24:Em 2026-11-14 o mantenedor do harne8 respondeu a revisão de configuração 7.4.1: adotar `closeout-review-policy` com `when-justified`. A prévia de `pose adopt --request` mostrou só `adopt.apply=false`, sem nenhuma mudança, mas o `--apply` gravaria `milestone_review_required=never` e `roadmap_review_required=never`, os padrões do catálogo: a instância teria valores que ninguém escolheu, sem aviso. A adoção foi feita pelo caminho direto, que mostra os valores. No mesmo `pose update`, o manual instalado no harne8 passou a dizer \"o perfil de revisão Claude deste repositório\", texto que descreve o perfil do próprio pose-dist.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets.md:27:- O caminho por solicitação continua recusando o par de valores (decisão da spec `pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit`, teste `TestCloseoutReviewPolicyAdoptRequestRefusesThePair`).\n.pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets.md:37:- R1: The preview of an answered adoption request shall name every policy change its apply writes, the catalog adoption included, as the direct adoption path does.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets.md:38:- R2: For closeout-review-policy, the preview shall say that the request adopts the catalog default and name the command that chooses other values.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets.md:39:- R3: The distributed manual shall describe the sandboxed Claude review profile as the one pose-dist qualified for its own reviews, not as the installing repository's.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets.md:60:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/configuration_review_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets.md:71:Composto por `pose adopt --request` e `pose setup`. Check permanente `adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/cli -run 'TestAnAnsweredAdoptionPreviewNamesThePolicyItWrites|TestConfigurationReview|TestCloseoutReviewPolicyAdoptRequestRefusesThePair' -count=1`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets.md:118:- R1 [satisfied] test:TestAnAnsweredAdoptionPreviewNamesThePolicyItWrites check:adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets.md:144:- [open] F1: deixar a revisão de configuração perguntar os valores de uma capacidade parametrizada (a política de fechamento) nas próprias opções da solicitação, para que a resposta do mantenedor decida também os valores. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-13)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-22-pose-release-closeout-skill-policy-link.md:6:depends_on: pose-review-bundle-component-discovery-and-governance-paths\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-report-a-demanded-class-nothing-produces.md:19:Report, as a `pose doctor` finding, an evidence class the selected review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-report-a-demanded-class-nothing-produces.md:23:`review.evidence-vocabulary` asks whether a class *could* be emitted by some\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-report-a-demanded-class-nothing-produces.md:167:- [open] Let a project record that a demanded class is imported on purpose, so the finding distinguishes evidence that arrives from elsewhere from evidence nobody produces (owner:unowned crit:low review:2027-03-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-report-a-demanded-class-nothing-produces.md:168:- [done] Register checks emitting `a11y` and `e2e` in this repository, or reconcile the profiles that demand them — the new check reports both, and both are real. Neither, and the report was wrong: `evidence_classes` is a disjunction, so every criterion listing `e2e` also accepted `integration` or `unit`, both produced here; and `a11y` belongs to `frontend-review`, selected by `languages: [javascript, typescript]`, which no component here has. Corrected in `pose-class-producers-reads-the-disjunction`. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-12-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-recurrence-effectiveness.md:61:- [x] Confirm baseline and fixtures against [DORA metrics](https://dora.dev/guides/dora-metrics/): the escalation workflow asked for a 45-day review with no data source — escalation creation was implicitly success; history JSONL carried no duration/cost; context resumed from knowledge:contract-baseline-handoff.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-recurrence-effectiveness.md:66:- [x] Test sparse data, regressions and ineffective interventions: `recurrence_effect_test.go` covers effective drop, ineffective regression with governed-action output and `--fail-ineffective` blocking, combined sparse+incomplete warnings and registration validation; recurrence-escalation workflow updated to register at ship time and review with the command. ([reference](https://dora.dev/guides/dora-metrics/))\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-recurrence-effectiveness.md:74:- ADR `.pose/adr/2026-07-19-recurrence-intervention-effectiveness-measurement.md` (Accepted): registered interventions + deterministic history projection over manual memory-based review and over external analytics; warnings force INCONCLUSIVE instead of misleading verdicts; blocking is opt-in; aggregation by task/context only, never individuals.\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-recurrence-effectiveness.md:106:review by measurement), operating-manual documentation and ADR. The loop's\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-recurrence-effectiveness.md:117:- [spawned: pose-governance-gate-activation] Register the first real intervention when recurrence-check next flags a task, and review its verdict after the window. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-changelog-and-dor-policy-types.md:217:- [done] Ship `changelog.json` with an empty `adopted_at` rather than this repository's own date, which every instance currently inherits — same family as the self-referential policy roots of issue #17. Done in `pose-changelog-adoption-is-the-instances`, and it needed three changes rather than one: shipping empty alone broke every fresh install, because `pose check` refused an empty date with `adopted_at is required`. The template ships empty, `pose install`/`pose update` stamp the day the instance received the policy, and an empty date now means the contract is not adopted. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-12-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-09-pose-changelog-and-dor-policy-types.md:218:- [open] Let a configured changelog category declare its heading, instead of capitalising its own name (owner:unowned crit:low review:2027-03-09)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-07-pose-recurrence-check-resolved-clusters.md:124:- [spawned: pose-recurrence-flapping-signal] Detect a task that alternates fail and pass many times in the window, as a separate non-blocking signal (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-04-pose-progressive-spec-surface.md:160:Delivers --surface, surface-aware lint and pose specs facts; R2 is implemented as specs facts. Each requirement is traced to its tests and matrix checks under Validation. Reviewed by agent:claude-opus-5-5 in the same session that implemented it; no separate execution or person reviewed it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read.md:29:Preserve declared legacy answers and SSH verification after key rotation, as required by pose-signed-action-answers R7. Do not reauthorize an old role against today's membership, auto-upgrade declared history or change adoption policy. This delta does not complete review-attestation disclosure, waiver authority or the entire B04 re-use contract.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read.md:73:- [x] Generate current global native validation, seal review, and obtain different-actor judgment.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read.md:74:- [x] Apply native closeout only after review verification and acceptance.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read.md:101:current results are in .pose/results/delivery-validation.json. Independent review was approved by agent:independent-codex-pr179 and the\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read.md:103:journal is answered/satisfied; current evidence/review and final closeout state\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read.md:111:Local gofmt, lint-spec, artifact-check --strict and check --strict passed; the latter retained 30 existing warnings. These structural checks used the published 7.4.1 binary. The available Go archive is truncated: compile -V segfaults, so no local Go test success or race-detector execution is claimed. The module validate attempt is retained as FAILURE (Go unavailable in PATH; 128 required checks failed). Functional evidence comes from the CI Go suite. Remaining governance and security jobs must finish before review readiness.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read.md:117:Native closeout accepted on 2026-10-15 after explicit maintainer acceptance: `act-3ee9344e0652cc60` answered/satisfied, revision 2 (declared). Admission used bundle `rvb-cfe993ee0dbf209f`, attestation `rva-370e6fda5e127a19`, strict 132/132 on published subject `9d89a2a0`, and approved native verify/review-check. `close --resume` performed the lifecycle transition; admission closeout-check reports terminal=true with no blockers. Current post-publication review and closeout snapshots are in `.pose/results/b01-action-*`. This closes this spec only; B01 remains partial.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read.md:123:for current execution evidence and review/closeout state. Preserve R1–R5, D1 and\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read.md:128:A journal-contained SSH signature proves its signed bytes, not an immutable historical authorization receipt. Issuer pin revocation remains live. General historical trust/re-use, waiver authority and review-attestation disclosure remain separate backlog deltas.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read.md:132:- [done] B04's scoped historical trust and review-source reuse contract was closed natively and published by #178; it explicitly does not establish immutable historical authorization. Consume its spec/closeout evidence rather than infer delivery from the merge.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:7:depends_on: pose-abm-review-authority\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:40:- Não resolver semanticamente se uma decisão é boa; isso continua no review.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:171:- [x] Reconcile artifacts, review bundle and closeout; the delivery target is\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:194:- Consequences: reviewers gain a falsifiable basis; external evidence remains\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:197:  fields without a review-owned disposition.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:242:  panic/stub debt. Knowledge consulted: `knowledge:adr-component-aware-review-plans-review`,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:243:  `knowledge:adr-sealed-review-bundles-review`, and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:244:  `knowledge:module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:263:  delivery-integrity projection for review evidence.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:264:- 2026-09-19: sealed review bundle `rvb-91654b0568782f68` and approved\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:265:  attestation `rva-e39a822c7d959c07` were verified fresh. The review retained\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:272:  sealed review/attestation checks passed.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:289:- This slice does not implement structural delta, progressive review or\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:300:to review. Publication remains intentionally pending until a delivery\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:311:- Review: `pose review verify spec:pose-abm-design-basis` returned\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:327:  - [<disposition>] <what remains and why> (owner:@alias crit:low|medium|high review:YYYY-MM-DD)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:332:ignored: the item reads as unowned, with no criticality and no review date, and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:349:  local e de governança (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-19)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-design-basis.md:353:  a resolvê-los (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-19)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:2:slug: pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:13:delivers: governance:review-subject-classifies-engine-records\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:16:# Spec: The review subject classifies every record the engine writes\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:22:Every path the engine writes under `.pose/` shall have a review-subject class, so a scope that carries one can be sealed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:26:On 2026-10-10 Harne8's `harne8-adopt-pose-v7-2-0` could not be sealed: `pose review bundle --seal` refused `unclassified review subject path .pose/review-ledgers/legacy-harne8-agents-20261010T032511Z.json`, a ledger `pose adopt signed-attestations` itself wrote in 7.3.0. Any project that adopted signed attestations through the ledger is stuck the same way. A scan of the engine's source found four more names it writes and the classifier did not know.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:30:A path that decides authority is reviewed with its scope; evidence about work is not.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:36:- R1: `.pose/review-ledgers/` shall be classified as governance and included in the review subject.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:37:- R2: `.pose/review-runs/`, `.pose/events/`, `.pose/investigations/`, `.pose/telemetry.json`, `.pose/continuous-closeout.json` and `.pose/pose-validate.log` shall be classified as derived evidence, `.pose/schema-version` and `.pose/usage/` as governance, and `.pose/LICENSE` and `.pose/NOTICE` as documentation, like the repository's own.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:44:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:45:- created: .pose/starts/pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:46:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:47:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:48:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/install_review_subject_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:49:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_engine_dirs_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:50:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.amendments.jsonl\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:54:- governance:review-subject-classifies-engine-records module:pose-mcp profile:release-governance entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:63:- Rationale: a review of the classifier alone would not have found the gap; the scan found it, and four more.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:69:2026-10-10, independent review (agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review, fallback reviewer): high and medium. The scan read only three packages, so `.pose/usage/` (the usage verdict journal, written by `internal/usage`) had no class and the seal refused it; and the patterns skipped names with an extension, missing `.pose/telemetry.json`, `.pose/continuous-closeout.json` and `.pose/pose-validate.log`. The scan now walks the whole module and matches extensions; the four names are classified, R2 and R3 amended. The widened scan fails on the previous classifier listing exactly those four.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:71:2026-10-10, second independent review (agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review, fallback reviewer): high severity. `.pose/LICENSE` and `.pose/NOTICE`, which install copies, had no class, and the scan's patterns skipped upper-case names. They are classified as documentation; the patterns accept any case and underscores (with `AGENTS.md` and `POSE.md`, which only follow `.pose` in a `git status` argument list, excluded); and because the scan reads string patterns, a second test checks every file a fresh install and an update actually write under `.pose/`. Both tests fail on the previous classifier naming exactly these two files.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:73:2026-10-10, third independent review (agent:independent-claude-opus-5-5-review, fallback reviewer): the code was approved; the spec failed `lint-spec --strict` once closed. Its amendment log began with a `semantic` event and no baseline, so R1 and D1 read as added after the start, and D1 had no `Basis`. D1 now names its basis and a baseline event acknowledges the current nodes; `lint-spec --strict` on a copy marked done passes. The amendment gate runs only on done specs, which is why it surfaced after `pose close`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:77:`TestEveryEngineDirectoryUnderPoseIsClassified` and `TestLegacyLedgerIsAGovernanceRecord` fail on the previous classifier (the scan lists events, investigations, review-ledgers, review-runs and schema-version) and pass on the new one.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:81:- R1 [satisfied] governance:review-subject-classifies-engine-records evidence:unit test:TestLegacyLedgerIsAGovernanceRecord\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:82:- R2 [satisfied] governance:review-subject-classifies-engine-records evidence:unit test:TestEveryEngineDirectoryUnderPoseIsClassified test:TestUsageVerdictJournalIsAGovernanceRecord\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:83:- R3 [satisfied] governance:review-subject-classifies-engine-records evidence:unit test:TestEveryEngineDirectoryUnderPoseIsClassified test:TestEveryFileTheEngineWritesUnderPoseIsClassified\n.pose/specs/2026-10-10-pose-review-subject-classifies-engine-records.md:89:Every directory and file the engine writes under `.pose/` has a review-subject class; the legacy ledger is reviewed as governance.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:2:slug: pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:6:depends_on: pose-review-subject-submodule-classification\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:9:delivers: capability:review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:12:# Spec: Materialize sealed gitlinks during review dispatch\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:18:Allow a governed review to reach the reviewer when its sealed subject includes a materialized gitlink. A detached checkout of the parent commit currently leaves an empty directory at the gitlink and fails worktree identity verification.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:30:Initialize unrelated submodules, resolve a remote URL or review changes inside a submodule.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:42:Use the validated origin's local submodule and stage a standalone detached checkout inside the private review worktree. Keep its private Git directory adjacent to that worktree. See the [ADR](../adr/2026-11-20-materialize-review-gitlinks-from-the-sealed-local-origin.md).\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:46:- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:47:- created: .pose/adr/2026-11-20-materialize-review-gitlinks-from-the-sealed-local-origin.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:50:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:51:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:52:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_gitlinks.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:54:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:58:- capability:review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:64:- [ ] Qualify the candidate against the engine gates and a real Harne8 review.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:72:Run the CLI regression against the parent first. It must reach sealing and fail before the adapter with the empty submodule identity error. After the fix, assert the exact scoped revision and nested payload, absence of unrelated checkouts, skipped hooks, unchanged origin and worktree cleanup. Exercise repeat dispatch for a stable tree digest and hidden-worktree changes for rejection before execution. Run existing dispatch, containment and snapshot tests, then CI and the native Harne8 review.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-20-pose-review-dispatch-materializes-sealed-gitlinks.md:82:The CLI fixture reached the empty gitlink identity error on the parent commit and passed after local materialization. Harne8 reached its real Opus review and confirmed cleanup on the adopted engine fixture. The focused engine review reproduced retained private metadata above 128 MiB. The correction checks tree sizes before transfer and inventories the private Git stores separately. Candidate qualification is pending.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-15-pose-discovery-gitignore-inside-submodules.md:127:- Context: review of PR #115 pointed out that line output C-quotes a\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:2:slug: review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:11:delivers: surface:review-policy-adoption\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:14:# Spec: review adoption dates belong to the instance that earned them\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:20:`.pose/policy/review.json` is not in `SelfReferentialPolicyFiles`, so this\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:21:repository's live review policy is copied byte-for-byte into the embedded\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:23:repository's review adoption dates instead of stamping the target's own.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:33:`component_aware_adopted_at: 2026-08-13`, `review_bundles_adopted_at: 2026-08-14`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:45:completed between its own start and a leaked date, it is laxer — work nobody reviewed\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:50:The neutral template a fresh instance receives decides what review means in every new\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:53:turn review off or on for existing instances, whose live file is never replaced by\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:63:- R1: `review.json` is shipped as an explicit neutral template rather than as a copy\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:70:  pinned by a test that installs from it and resolves a review plan.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:71:- R5: The parity contract still refuses drift, with `review.json` compared against its\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:76:Add `review.json` to `distpolicy.SelfReferentialPolicyFiles` and write its neutral\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:79:and `review_bundles` start enabled, and no dates at all — and pin them.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:83:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:84:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:85:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_policy_adoption_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:89:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.pose/policy/review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:104:- surface:review-policy-adoption module:pose-mcp/internal/cli profile:cli-surface entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:127:`pose-dist-records-its-own-contract-adoption`: choosing what review means in every\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:128:new repository is a contract decision that deserves its own review, and folding it\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:143:| Parity holds | `go test ./internal/scaffold -run TestEmbeddedDistMatchesPoseDist -count=1` | `review.json` compared against its neutral template |\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:148:test failed with `differs: [.pose/policy/review.json]`, which is what revealed that\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:155:`review_bundles_adopted_at=2026-08-14`, `evidence_vocabulary_reconciled_at=2026-09-08`,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:163:- The template ships the current contract shape — review enabled, component-aware\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:164:  and review-bundles on, the three shipped scope profiles — with no dates and no\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:174:review requires the date that says when the instance received it. That coupling is\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:178:Defect injection, and one correction to my own method: removing `review.json` from\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:186:A dedicated integration producer, `review-policy-adoption-integration`, was\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:193:`surface-check --spec review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances --strict` exits 0 with\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:195:`surface:review-policy-adoption` comes from a run of the containing module, so\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:206:approved; `review-check` fresh and approved; `closeout-check` terminal.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:215:### Resumed review of the integration producer\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:219:Codex review pass inspected the neutral template, absent-only stamping, and the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:237:criteria, eleven tools and eight evidence items. Explicit review by\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:238:`agent:codex-review-policy-adoption`, attestation `rva-9d329c0d355c8422`, is fresh\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:239:and approved; `review verify` reports `closed`. The first attestation in this pass,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:249:  `TestEmbeddedDistMatchesPoseDist` — `review.json` is excluded from the wholesale\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:251:- R2 [satisfied] surface:review-policy-adoption evidence:integration\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:252:  check:review-policy-adoption-integration test:TestInstallStampsItsOwnReviewAdoption\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:256:  resolves a review plan\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:262:  review plan from the installed result\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:270:A distribution no longer hands a project another repository's review history. The\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:278:instance receives changes what review means in every new repository, and the tests\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-review-policy-adoption-is-the-instances.md:286:- [open] The v1 migration fallback dates above (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-self-update-handoff-path.md:165:- [done] Exercise the download-replace-handoff sequence against a local release fixture, so the release run is not the first to run it. Done in `pose-release-boundary-rehearsal`: a local server serves the release metadata and archive, a pose binary built at an older version downloads and replaces itself, and restoring `os.Executable()` in the handoff reproduces the v2.0.0 `fork/exec .../pose.old` failure locally. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-11-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-waiver-and-supersession-authority.md:6:depends_on: pose-action-answers-reverify-on-read, pose-review-disclosure-requires-proof, pose-policy-scope-validation, pose-action-request-resolution, pose-action-requests\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-waiver-and-supersession-authority.md:67:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-24-b09-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-waiver-and-supersession-authority.md:153:| Contract/debt | `pose assess integrate` / `pose assess tech-debt` | review changes and residual markers |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-waiver-and-supersession-authority.md:166:Targeted B09 regressions, signed CLI/MCP roundtrips, race and the final global matrix (149/149) passed. Separate code review round 2 approved the correction; sealed native review/closeout are recorded by their own gates.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-waiver-and-supersession-authority.md:174:- R7 [satisfied] test:TestActionLifecycleMCPProofOnlyAndBoundIssuerControl test:TestActionLifecycleCLISupersessionPreservesPreviewIdentity\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-waiver-and-supersession-authority.md:183:A coleta final no HEAD `6bb4c79` passou 149/149; race e scanners passaram. Artifact-check reconciliou 44 claims/45 observações sem erros (bundles derivados têm tratamento próprio), surface-check retornou um target, 149 resultados e zero findings, e o índice foi publicado e verificado antes do selo final. Bundle `rvb-3280abe765d3b8e7`, atestação `rva-2c351d7043c5e90d`, reviewer `agent:independent-codex-b09-review` (execução real `/root/b09_review`, OpenAI GPT-6.1-sol, mesmo fornecedor/modelo, separação declarada; sem confirmação humana nem independência cognitiva comprovada). Review verify e review-check passaram, fresh/approved.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-waiver-and-supersession-authority.md:185:O comando `pose close spec:pose-action-waiver-and-supersession-authority` publicou `done` e `completed_at: 2026-10-24`. Foi usado o fluxo manual nativo com os mesmos gates de review/entrega/trace e CAS; o coletor recuperável recusou somente as saídas de relatório/history que não constam como paths gerados admitidos. Não houve edição manual do lifecycle nem alteração de policy. Os relatórios de implementação e revisão registram a correção F1, coleta inicial com falha de paridade e renovação da proveniência após o commit dos índices.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-action-waiver-and-supersession-authority.md:189:Ver [relatório de implementação](../reports/2026-10-24-b09-implementation.md) e [revisão separada](../reports/2026-10-24-b09-independent-review.md) para evidência, correção F1 e limites reais.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:20:canônico de review, para que complexidade durável possa ser ligada a\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:30:- O subject vem do mesmo `ReviewBundleSubject` usado no review; não há diff\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:44:  o vínculo causal fica para o review/Design Basis.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:92:- `pose assess discover|integrate|tech-debt` e os contratos de review atuais\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:95:  `assess-design`/review bundle quando o producer estiver disponível.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:104:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go` e `review_bundle.go`: producer\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:118:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:119:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:120:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:160:producer `assess-design` no review bundle. O vínculo causal R/A/D continua uma\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:198:- [x] Selar bundle, registrar julgamento explícito e verificar review.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:209:  com coverage explícita e review-owned judgment.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:211:  subject de review.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:215:  review responder se cada custo é justificável.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:237:- `pose assess integrate` and `pose assess tech-debt` during review because\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:241:- `pose review verify spec:pose-abm-structural-delta` before any closeout.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:244:2026-09-19: spec activated on `main` after `pose-abm-review-soundness` and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:247:`knowledge:adr-sealed-review-bundles-review`,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:248:`knowledge:adr-component-aware-review-plans-review` and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:249:`knowledge:module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:257:review pair `rvb-e6dd3404f95ccf63` / `rva-bc7e30e6586ff1b0` was fresh and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:259:intentionally requires a new sealed review. Closeout remains intentionally in\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:296:remains an explicit review judgment. Unsupported manifest ecosystems remain\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-structural-delta.md:301:  capability (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-19)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:2:slug: pose-delegated-review-round-protocol\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:7:depends_on: pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger, pose-delegated-review-brief, pose-delegation-handoff\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:12:delivers: capability:delegated-review-rounds\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:15:# Spec: Each review round starts from the findings of the last one\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:21:Make the rounds of a delegated review one process: the brief of a round after the first carries the previous round's findings, the reviewer must account for each of them and sweep the subject in one pass, and the engine measures whether the rounds converge.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:25:Origin: B06 (2026-10-17), the largest consolidation unit so far. Four review rounds returned 19, 12, 10 and 6 findings. Each round reviewed the new commit afresh, so a finding \"partially fixed\" came back as a new finding two rounds later, and the reviewer stopped at the first medium finding each time, handing the rest to the next round. Nothing in the record says which findings of round N were verified fixed in round N+1, how many rounds a scope has taken, or whether they converge. That is exactly the information a maintainer needs to decide between another round, a different reviewer and a human adjudication.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:35:Resuming an interrupted run (`pose-delegated-review-run-continuity`); deciding the verdict; merging findings across unrelated scopes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:41:- R1: The round of a bundle shall be derived from the supersession chain of its scope in the ledger (round 1 for a bundle that supersedes none) and shall be shown by `pose review verify`, `status` and insights.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:42:- R2: For a bundle of round 2 or later, `pose review brief` shall add a section built mechanically from the previous round's completed run: every finding with its identifier, severity, disposition and evidence digest, and the commit it was made against. Text written by the implementer shall stay in its labelled notes.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:43:- R3: The brief shall instruct the reviewer to state for each prior finding whether it is `fixed`, `partial`, `not-fixed` or `superseded`, with evidence, before reporting anything new, and to report every finding it can establish in this round, with a completeness statement naming what it swept.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:46:- R6: When `routing.rounds` is `continue-thread` (the default), a round after the first shall resume the thread's current session; it shall open a new session, recording the reason, when the agent's vendor changes, the supersession chain is broken, the session can no longer be resumed, or the scope reaches the round threshold. When `routing.rounds` is `cold-session`, every round shall open a new session. The run shall record the session lineage and `pose review verify` shall disclose it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:47:- R7: `pose insights` shall report, per scope, findings per round, the share of prior findings fixed, partial and not-fixed, and rounds to approval; `pose review verify` shall warn when a scope passes the policy's round threshold (default 5), recommending a different agent or a human adjudication.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:72:- modified: .pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:73:- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:74:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:75:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:76:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:78:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:81:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:87:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:88:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:89:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_rounds_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:90:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:91:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:94:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_task_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:101:`delegate_task_test.go` and `.gitleaksignore` change with this spec only to clear the Security workflow: a synthetic credential a fixture of `pose-delegation-task` wrote out (commit `fb06eca`) is pinned by its exact fingerprint, and the fixture now builds it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:105:- capability:delegated-review-rounds module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:119:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:127:- Rationale: the maintainer's decision of 2026-10-26 in the delegation ADR. A reviewer that already read the subject verifies its own findings without a full re-read, and the risk that it anchors on its earlier verdict is carried by R2–R5 and R9, which make every prior finding an explicit, evidenced entry whatever the session remembers. The original choice of a cold session is kept as the policy alternative\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:129:- Falsifier: insights showing continued rounds accept more prior findings as `fixed` that a later round or a cold reviewer finds still open, or converge no faster than cold rounds\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:133:- Minimal option: ask in prose for an exhaustive review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:136:- Consequences: a reviewer that stops early produces an invalid draft, not a quiet approval\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:142:- Selected option: the draft is the fenced code block whose info string is `pose-draft`, at the end of the reviewer's final message: JSON with schema `pose.review.draft/v1`, `decision`, `findings` (`id`, `severity`, `disposition`, `file`, `line`, `summary`) and, from round 2, `prior_findings` and `sweep`, decoded strictly; the brief of every review round asks for it (template `review-brief/2`), and any decision line outside the block that does not state the block's decision, however many there are, makes the draft invalid. Fences are whole lines, LF or CRLF: the opening line is exactly the info string, the block closes at the first line that is exactly three backticks, and a fence line in any other form, or a second block, is an error, never a block read as absent. An account names only open findings of the scope's rounds. Where there is a block, its decision is the run's decision for every reader (wait, insights, verify, run provenance); the decision line is read only for drafts without one. A message carries one block; a finding's own identifier never takes the reserved round prefix `R<n>-`, so the identity a finding is carried under is injective. The maintainer chose this format on 2026-10-27, for this spec and for `pose-delegated-review-conclusions`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:144:- Consequences: round 1 briefs change, against the compatibility note \"Round 1 briefs are unchanged\": they ask for the block so that round 2 has identified findings to carry. A round-1 draft without the block is still valid; it only leaves the next round with nothing to carry, which the next brief says. Runs briefed with `review-brief/1` keep verifying: the brief a run was sent is re-rendered with the template whose digest it recorded\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:150:- Selected option: a round is a sealed bundle of the scope a completed, unsuperseded review run concluded on; the rounds before a bundle are those whose concluding run ended no later than the second the bundle was sealed in, ordered by when those runs ended. A finding first reported in round N is identified `R<N>-<id>`; it leaves the open set only when a later draft reports it `fixed` with evidence, or `superseded`: unaccounted, reported `fixed` without evidence, `partial` or `not-fixed`, it stays open under that identifier, so an invalid account never closes a finding. A draft of the chain that cannot be read closes nothing and adds nothing; the brief says so and the next round opens a new session. A loss in the run history or in the sealed bundles that may concern the scope, a run of the scope whose bundle is missing, or a previous round whose record is not intact make the derivation, and so the brief, refuse; the earlier reviewers' text is quoted in the brief as data. The number of rounds a metric reports is the highest any run of the scope recorded, and a run records its round, and a continuation its predecessor's thread, from the start\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:152:- Consequences: a reseal of the same content is not a new round; a bundle a review never concluded on is not a round\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:167:A fixture scope with three seeded defects reviewed over three rounds by a fake adapter: round 2 must account for each prior finding, a draft that omits one is refused, a `partial` keeps its identity, the section is byte-stable, rounds 2 and 3 continue the thread's session and are disclosed, a vendor change and the round threshold each open a new session with its reason, `cold-session` opens one every round, a continued session's draft that omits a prior finding is refused like a cold one, and insights report the convergence figures for continued and cold rounds; a tampered prior run makes the brief refuse.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:171:- R1 [satisfied] Ledger-derived rounds and lineage are disclosed by verify, delegate ls and insights; test:TestReviewRoundsContinueTheThreadAndAccountForFindings and test:TestReviewRoundsSurviveLossesAndResumes cover recorded and active/continued rounds. The deprecated review status projection has the accepted low follow-up f-r4-01.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:172:- R2 [satisfied] Prior findings come from the intact ledger, are quoted as data and retain their evidence reference and reviewed commit; test:TestReviewRoundsCarryOpenFindings and test:TestReviewRoundsHoldAgainstTheFirstReview cover carry, stable rendering and tampering refusal.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:178:- R8 [satisfied] The maximum recorded round survives failed/superseded conclusions; rejecting history stays visible. Verified by test:TestReviewRoundMetricsNeverLowerOrLaunder and check:delegated-attempt-ledger-integration.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:186:Milestone `rounds` of roadmap `delegation`: ledger-derived rounds and stable finding identities; a quoted, byte-stable prior-findings section in generated review-brief/2 with review-brief/1 matching preserved; strict pose-draft decisions and account/sweep validation; continued and explicitly cold sessions with private lineage; invalid-draft refusal in wait, proof and run-backed approval; active/terminal disclosure; and per-mode convergence trajectories, shares and approval rounds. Later rounds reuse the session captured by a concluding handoff, delivering the integration deferred as R10 of pose-delegation-handoff.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:188:### Independent review and evidence\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:190:Maintainer-authorized reviewer `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review` (Codex/OpenAI), another vendor than implementer Claude/Anthropic, Claude Opus 5.5 session `f2a4d9f2-d557-4064-ae96-6ed52bb47cd2`. The `agent:independent-` prefix is an engine-required declaration, not authenticated separation. Identity is declared; this instance's attestations are unsigned.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:192:Approved implementation commit `fa0c589aac678fe548e3725f745ba6628cef3e8f`, sealed bundle `rvb-aaec9b9e16165671`, attestation `rva-78b867ebfada5dcb`. The seal explicitly names `anthropic/claude-opus-5-5` from the reviewing Codex environment; its missing Anthropic session-reference warning is expected and no implementation execution digest was invented. Native verify reported fresh, approved and ready-to-close before the guarded lifecycle transition.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:194:All findings from review rounds 1–3 are reconciled as fixed. Round 4 records only the low-severity accepted-risk finding `f-r4-01` below. Expiring operational context and a reproduction recipe are retained in knowledge:delegated-rounds-legacy-status. Complete local reports, overlays and probes remain in `.review-work/round1/` through `.review-work/round4/`, deliberately untracked.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:198:Global `pose validate --strict`: 158/158 checks passed; component `pose-mcp` strict validation: 155/155 passed; zero failures, errors or skips. Canonical structured evidence is `.pose/results/delivery-validation.json`. Independent vet, Windows/Darwin builds, both locale full suites without session markers, selected race and Dash checks passed. Production omission mutations for R2/R4/R5/R6 were detected; the third-review regression failed against f84812e production. The positive 96-candidate fence corpus, selection permutations and composed handoff-to-next-round session probe passed. The pinned, redacted Gitleaks workflow command passed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:204:The existing executor-declaration and cognitive-assurance limits remain: fake-agent tests establish engine behavior, not a provider receipt or guaranteed reviewer cognition. Continue-thread retains the maintainer-accepted anchoring trade-off under full-brief/account safeguards, explicit cold reasons, threshold and measurable trajectories. The deprecated status presentation gap is accepted only at low severity because canonical delegate ls, persisted runs, verify and approval retain the correct round.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:208:- [open] f-r4-01: Carry round and thread through deprecated review status interrupted summaries and text, or explicitly document its narrower legacy projection before alias retirement; add JSON/text regressions. See knowledge:delegated-rounds-legacy-status. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-26)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-brief-ties-every-conclusion-refusal.md:7:depends_on: pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-governance-gate-activation/spec.md:62:  shall be reviewed and their verdicts recorded.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-governance-gate-activation/spec.md:111:  to review. Prefer cleanup first, flip second, in separate commits.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-governance-gate-activation/spec.md:128:- [ ] R6: review the first audit run and the first recurrence intervention\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-governance-gate-activation/spec.md:178:- R6 [waived: calendar-bound, nothing to review yet] — the first quarterly audit is dated 2026-10-01 and the first recurrence intervention needs recurrence-check to flag something; neither can be reviewed before it happens\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-governance-gate-activation/spec.md:200:- Debt citations in `.pose/reviews/` still name `DEBT-001`. Reviews are\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-governance-gate-activation/spec.md:236:- [done] R2's archaeology found the opposite of what was feared: the eleven specs are three weeks old and all describe live behaviour, so every one earned a real trace and none was archived. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-23)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-governance-gate-activation/spec.md:237:- [open] R6: review the first quarterly audit run (2026-10-01) and the first real recurrence intervention (`validate-native`, registered 2026-08-14; knowledge:escalation-validate-native), then record both verdicts. The intervention window ends 2026-09-28 and the audit cannot be reviewed before it runs. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-governance-gate-activation/spec.md:238:- [done] Both delivered rather than amended: licenses now resolve in the SBOM (pose-sbom-license-inventory) and the signing rejection path is exercised on every CI run (tests/release/verify-negative.sh). F2: `pose-cyclonedx-sbom` R1 and `pose-release-signing` R3 were waived in their retrofitted traces because the behaviour was never actually delivered — licenses are absent from the SBOM and the signing rejection path has never fired. Decide whether to deliver them or amend the requirements. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-09-18)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-onboarding-spec.md:22:`pose install` scaffolds a first spec, `pose-onboarding`, in a new instance: adopting POSE in this project is itself the first piece of governed work, with requirements (identity declared, a maintainer who can prove answers, the commit gate, the capability defaults reviewed, the install committed), tasks that point to `pose setup`, and checks a newcomer can run. It is the first exemplar of how POSE works, in the project's own repository.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-onboarding-spec.md:40:- R1: `pose install` on a new instance shall create `.pose/specs/<date>-pose-onboarding.md` (status draft), in the install's locale, with requirements for project identity, a maintainer able to prove answers, the commit gate, the reviewed capability defaults and the committed install, tasks naming the `pose setup` steps, and deterministic checks.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-compat-gate-manual-refresh-assertion.md:164:- [done] Assert the same preservation property for POSE.md, which takes the same merge path but is not customized by the upgrade-lab fixture. Done in `pose-compat-gate-pose-md-preservation`; it turned out not to be the same path — the appended note stays in AGENTS.md but is dropped from POSE.md and survives only in `POSE.md.pose-backup`, so the gate now exercises the backup branch it never had. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-doctor-selected-profiles-only.md:13:# Spec: Doctor reports only the review profiles policy selects\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-doctor-selected-profiles-only.md:18:Narrow `review.evidence-vocabulary` to the profiles `.pose/policy/review.json`\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-doctor-selected-profiles-only.md:19:selects, so it reports on the review plans an instance builds rather than on\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-doctor-selected-profiles-only.md:20:every file in `.pose/review-profiles/`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-doctor-selected-profiles-only.md:28:[!] review.evidence-vocabulary 4 review profile(s) demand evidence classes no\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-doctor-selected-profiles-only.md:29:    registered check may emit: backend-review.json, frontend-review.json,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-doctor-selected-profiles-only.md:61:  `overlay_profiles` in the review policy.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-doctor-selected-profiles-only.md:64:- R3: The check shall stay silent when the review policy cannot be read, rather\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-doctor-selected-profiles-only.md:93:  the same silence as an instance with no review policy, and preferable to\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-doctor-selected-profiles-only.md:102:- [x] Increment 1: Read the selected refs from the review policy (R1, R3)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-doctor-selected-profiles-only.md:175:- [done] Audit the doctor fixtures for others that pass by scanning rather than through the path production takes. Delivered by `pose-doctor-fixtures-exercise-production-path`, which found three unreached behavioural branches and covered them. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-11-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-reuse-is-sealed-signing-stays-live.md:25:to be the question: `reviewer_independence` is already sealed in the plan,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-reuse-is-sealed-signing-stays-live.md:33:was permitted is a property of the review that happened: read live, a project\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-reuse-is-sealed-signing-stays-live.md:69:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go` — the gate, the seal, and the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-reuse-is-sealed-signing-stays-live.md:76:- modified: .pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-reuse-is-sealed-signing-stays-live.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-10-pose-reuse-is-sealed-signing-stays-live.md:176:- [done] Assert that `require_signed_attestations` is the only live policy read left in the bundle validator, so sealing it by symmetry with the others fails rather than passing quietly. Done in `pose-only-the-signing-gate-is-read-live`: the validator's own source is read and any policy field but that one fails, naming the field; the signing requirement going missing fails too, naming what a bundle sealed earlier would be exempt from. A companion assertion requires every sealed gate to be consulted. (owner:unowned crit:medium review:2026-12-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:39:- R4: Require valid source review/delivery evidence and consumer trust acceptance for required external children. A done status or copied attestation alone must fail. Preserve explicit local composition criteria and judgment.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:40:- R5: Recheck pinned inputs at close application and invalidate affected coordinator reviews on material change, authorization revocation or evidence supersession. Cache keys include project, revision, contract, policy and authorization scope.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:43:- R8: Expose the same plan, readiness and blockers in CLI/MCP/index/projection. Keep historical bundles under their sealed semantics; version schemas, preview adoption and retain rollback that refuses unreadable new contracts.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:55:Extend Roadmap/Milestone models, readiness, roadmap checks and review manifests. Keep one source verifier and local outcome review; use bounded recursion and existing evidence classes. Do not fetch networks or mutate child repositories during read/check.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:64:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:65:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:72:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:104:Version new metadata through existing schema/capability mechanisms. Preview\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:120:- [x] Obtain explicit review and governed closeout; disposition follow-ups and refresh assessments.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:126:- Prefer the existing Store/roots/review contracts over a second authority or resolver.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:150:- `pose review verify spec:pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance` and `pose closeout-check spec:pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance` before `pose close spec:pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:168:read-only roadmap acceptance report is now shared by closeout, review bundles,\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:170:review verification uses the same authorized resolver as the coordinator;\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:171:invalid/cyclic graphs stop before recursive source review. No consumer\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:178:Autonomous review approved sealed bundle `rvb-b5d482a5bf68ff8d` on 2026-09-24;\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:184:- R3 [satisfied] `TestFederatedAcceptanceComposesReviewedSiblingRoadmapAndStalesOnSourceRevision`; `TestFederatedManifestIsSealedAndInvalidatesCoordinatorReview` — the manifest records selected source revisions and digests, source trust, review bundle and evidence; changed inputs alter the sealed digest.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:185:- R4 [satisfied] `TestFederatedAcceptanceNegativeStatusOnlySpecCannotClose`; `TestFederatedAcceptanceComposesReviewedSiblingRoadmapAndStalesOnSourceRevision` — status alone is insufficient; reviewed source evidence and consumer trust are required.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-21-pose-federated-roadmap-acceptance.md:186:- R5 [satisfied] `TestFederatedManifestIsSealedAndInvalidatesCoordinatorReview` — changed source revision and revoked project authorization invalidate the coordinator review; closeout recomputes the current snapshot.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-marker-stop-joins-heartbeat.md:25:`markDelegationActive` starts a goroutine that rewrites the marker's heartbeat; `stop` closes the goroutine's channel and removes the marker without waiting for it. A heartbeat already past its byte check when stop runs renames its new marker into place after the removal, and a finished run reads as running, then stalled, and can block its continuation. Found by the independent review of `pose-delegation-result-before-marker` (F04), reproduced there with a scheduling probe on the code before it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-marker-stop-joins-heartbeat.md:82:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-marker-stop-joins-heartbeat.md:101:A run's stop joins its heartbeat watcher before removing the active marker, and starts no heartbeat once it has asked, so a finished run's marker cannot come back. Independently reviewed by Codex over two rounds, who found the defect.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-marker-stop-joins-heartbeat.md:109:- [open] F1: remove a run's cancel request after its marker, or clean it by token, so a request published between the two unlinks leaves no side file (review round 1, HB03). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-delegation-marker-stop-joins-heartbeat.md:110:- [open] F2: release and join a held writer in the regression's failure paths before restoring its global hooks (review round 2, HB02). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-pose-dist-adopt-published-v6-0-4.md:46:- [x] Run strict checks, obtain review and close adoption.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-doctor-state-health.md:45:- created: .pose/review-bundles/rvb-6ef45b962e0680b0.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-doctor-state-health.md:46:- created: .pose/review-attestations/rva-35c5545984cd93b1.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-doctor-state-health.md:58:Knowledge consulted: knowledge:module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance;\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-doctor-state-health.md:66:- [x] Validate module and local consumer, review and close through POSE.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-doctor-state-health.md:96:  commit, so no review result is claimed by this log.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-doctor-state-health.md:100:  --component pose-mcp --update-state` and the sealed review/attestation gates\n.pose/specs/2026-09-19-pose-abm-doctor-state-health.md:134:  review:2026-10-03)\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-otel-observability.md:64:- [ ] Define POSE span, metric and log conventions with privacy review. ([reference](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/concepts/signals/))\n.pose/specs/2026-07-18-pose-otel-observability.md:113:- [open] Revisit OTLP log export (`go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/log` + `otlploghttp`) once both reach a stable `v1.x` release — currently alpha (`v0.x`), deliberately not adopted. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-10-19)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-actions-node24-bump.md:41:| actions/dependency-review-action | v4 | node20 | v5 | node24 |\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-actions-node24-bump.md:57:  reviewed on its own schedule.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-07-pose-actions-node24-bump.md:208:- [covered: pose-action-runtime-currency-gate] Runtime currency is detected by reading annotations on passing runs, which is how the Node 20 deprecation went unnoticed until it was already being forced. Consider a check that fails when a referenced first-party action declares a runtime GitHub has deprecated — the data is in each action's `action.yml` at its pinned tag. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-10-pose-usage-metrics.md:150:- [x] Regenerate the relevant embedded manuals and review the catalog golden.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-10-pose-usage-metrics.md:230:- [covered: pose-dora-five-metrics-v2] Migrate the DORA event/metric contract to production-scoped deployment rework rate and deployment-caused recovery semantics. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:high review:2026-09-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-10-pose-usage-metrics.md:231:- [spawned: pose-usage-findings-adjudication] Add explicit human confirmation of observed findings as `valid`, `wont-fix` or `false-positive`, preserving automatic observation counts separately from adjudicated outcomes. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-09-10)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-consolidation-batch-5-authoring.md:92:Gates locais e critérios de saída julgados no [bundle rvb-9e82d8d7f43ed0f8](../review-bundles/rvb-9e82d8d7f43ed0f8.json), com [atestação rva-48f0b7479739ed93](../review-attestations/rva-48f0b7479739ed93.json) de uma execução separada do Codex, mesmo fornecedor/modelo herdado. Sem alegação de identidade autenticada ou revisão entre fornecedores.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-consolidation-batch-5-authoring.md:99:compatibilidade e fidelidade de preview/update precisam de qualificação antes do código.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-upgrade-journey-starts-below-current.md:27:Since v7.0.0 was published (2026-10-07 23:05 UTC), the latest release equals a build of the same version, an update between them has nothing to review, and the journey failed with \"the update did not open a configuration review\" on every commit of main, turning CI red without any defect in the code under test. The last green run, on 25ed81e2, ran before the publication, when the latest release was v6.2.0.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-upgrade-journey-starts-below-current.md:42:- R2: When no published release is older than the engine under test, the journey shall fail naming that reason instead of testing an update with nothing to review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-upgrade-journey-starts-below-current.md:85:Run the journey check with the journeys enabled before and after the change: it fails at main 7f67249 with \"the update did not open a configuration review\" and passes after it, upgrading from v6.2.0 to the 7.0.0 build.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-08-pose-upgrade-journey-starts-below-current.md:111:Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-index-material-is-kept-per-repository-state.md:24:Toda operação de revisão confere se o índice que lê está em dia, e o material federado é uma das entradas dessa conferência. No harne8, com o pose-dist como dependência e o pin em dia, esse cálculo levou cerca de 90 s de um `closeout-check` de 140 s (perfil de CPU: `BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn`, por `checkIndexInputs`, 71% do tempo). Um servidor MCP de vida longa pagava isso em toda chamada. Os clientes do `conductor` esperam de 20 a 120 s, e o `TestReviewConfirmationRealEngine` passou de 31 minutos e reprovou numa chamada `pose_review_bundle`. A spec `pose-check-shares-the-federated-material` já compartilha o material dentro de um `check`; esta estende o compartilhamento entre operações do mesmo processo.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-index-material-is-kept-per-repository-state.md:27:- O material guardado só é reaproveitado depois de cada leitura que o construiu dar o mesmo resultado na operação atual.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-index-material-is-kept-per-repository-state.md:28:- Toda entrada do material reaproveitado entra no fecho e na auditoria final da operação atual.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-index-material-is-kept-per-repository-state.md:101:- Options considered: (a) chave no estado de cada repositório (HEAD, status, bytes sujos); (b) guardar o fecho de leituras de uma construção isolada e reproduzi-lo pela view de cada operação antes de reaproveitar.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-index-material-is-kept-per-repository-state.md:124:- Notes: duas chamadas `pose_closeout_state` de `spec:harne8-abm-governed-execution` no mesmo servidor MCP: sem cache, 138 s e 136 s; com o fecho, 144 s e 43 s, terminal nas quatro. Depois das correções F6 a F8, 45 s na segunda chamada, terminal (a primeira, 215 s, rodou junto com a suíte de testes). Sem a reprodução do fecho, o teste de entrada mudada reaproveita o material velho e o de reaproveitamento acusa que as leituras não entraram na view atual.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-index-material-is-kept-per-repository-state.md:152:- [open] F1: reduzir o custo da primeira construção do material federado (cerca de 90 s no harne8), por exemplo verificando em paralelo as dependências de outro projeto; com ela, a primeira chamada de um servidor MCP caberia nos tetos dos clientes do conductor. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:high review:2026-11-23)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-index-material-is-kept-per-repository-state.md:156:Rodada 1 (run rrn-8479af60445e994b, attestation rva-9a082cb52b517543, changes-requested): 5 bloqueadores, tratados por um desenho novo, escolhido pelo maintainer. F1 a chave tratava um diretório como marcador e não via repositórios aninhados; F2 um acerto devolvia o digest sem passar as entradas do material pela read view da operação, e a chave era lida fora dela; F3 arquivos ignorados pelo Git que o material lê não entravam na chave; F4 a chave lia qualquer objeto listado, inclusive um FIFO, sem limite; F5 o limite de 4.096 caminhos era conferido depois de todo o trabalho. A chave por estado de repositório saiu: o material é construído numa operação isolada, todo o que ela leu é o fecho, e cada acerto reproduz o fecho pela view da operação atual antes de reaproveitar. Isso cobre o que o material leu de fato (F1, F3), mantém as leituras na auditoria (F2) e não lê nada que o material não tenha lido (F4, F5).\n.pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-index-material-is-kept-per-repository-state.md:160:Rodada 3 (run rrn-42a25f179b94b626, changes-requested): 3 bloqueadores, todos corrigidos com teste que reprova sem a correção. F6 a construção isolada substituía o resolvedor que `withGovernanceReadView` acabara de ligar à operação isolada pelo resolvedor do chamador, ligado à operação do chamador; as leituras da dependência estrangeira caíam fora do fecho, e uma edição nela podia reaproveitar o digest velho. Agora o resolvedor fica ligado à operação isolada, e a reprodução roteia cada leitura como uma leitura normal, abrindo a view da raiz autorizada (`TestIndexMaterialClosureCoversTheForeignDependency`, com o construtor real). F7 a construção isolada usava a raiz do coordenador numa validação de raiz estrangeira; agora usa a raiz da store pedida (`TestIndexMaterialOfAForeignRootIsKeptForThatRoot`). F8 a chave não cobria resultados do resolvedor que não leem arquivo. A chave passou a cobrir a configuração do registro, a raiz ou o erro de cada projeto e os conflitos. As decisões de autorização são política por chamada (o servidor MCP avalia a policy do chamador); a construção registra cada decisão consultada, e um acerto pergunta de novo cada uma, auditada na chamada atual. Uma primeira correção, que recusava guardar com `Authorize`, desligou o cache em produção (148 s na segunda chamada no harne8) e foi trocada por essa. O teste cobre um projeto referenciado e não registrado, cuja decisão não muda nenhuma leitura, e reprova sem a nova pergunta (`TestIndexMaterialIsNotKeptAcrossAuthorizationOrRegistry`). Os achados F1 a F5 da rodada 1 continuam resolvidos pelo desenho do fecho.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:59:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-22-b30-pending-review-r1.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:65:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec_facts_review_regression_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:71:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-pose-b30r2-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:72:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-pose-b30r3-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:73:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-pose-b30r4-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:74:- created: .pose/results/b30r4-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:75:- created: .pose/results/b30r2-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:76:- created: .pose/results/b30r3-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:79:- created: .pose/reports/2026-10-18-pose-b30-independent-review.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:80:- created: .pose/results/b30-independent-review.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:169:- [open] Normalizar referências de componente quando forem paths e distinguir ID de componente de path na explicação do candidato. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:170:- [open] Projetar o frescor `unavailable` em vez de devolver erro quando o índice está ausente ou corrompido. (owner:@core crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:172:- [open] L03 da revisão r4: substituir a explicação genérica de freshness unknown pela causa observada, preservando status e reason conservadores. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:173:- [open] L04 da revisão r4: completar o desempate estrutural da ordenação de resultados sem alterar identidade, classificação ou retenção. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:174:- [open] L05 da revisão r4: limitar a saída da consulta de trailers de facts e conservar unknown/erro ao exceder, sem truncar a atribuição silenciosamente. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:175:- [open] L06 da revisão r4: conservar a identidade do run sem checks classificados ou explicitar que o frescor divulgado cobre a projeção de resultados, sem tratar zero checks como entrega comprovada. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-spec-facts-evidence-binding.md:181:Main merged without rewriting historical reviews. Separate Codex execution found three high findings; all reproduced in `/tmp/pose-b30-new-regressions-before.log` before fixes. Pin the generation before reading its graph, decode history JSON records and conservatively disclose retained explicit attribution without a bound history source, validate literal canonical Git paths including rename endpoints. No new policy adoption or automatic semantic judgment. Existing source review history remains changes-requested until a fresh review approves the final sealed subject.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:2:slug: retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:7:depends_on: review-verify-retains-completed-scopes\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:11:delivers: capability:completed-review-retention-precedence\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:31:Before 6.0.2 `review-check` fell back to the first; under 6.0.2 the scope lost its\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:59:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:60:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:61:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:62:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/completed_review_retention_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:69:- capability:completed-review-retention-precedence module:pose-mcp/internal/pose profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:87:- Distinguish a verdict from a validity failure. A rejection is a reviewer's\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:103:`rvb-5c52e77ba769c97b` / `rva-e2100d48dbb02eef`, approved, fails with `review tool\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:117:- R1 [satisfied] capability:completed-review-retention-precedence evidence:integration check:completed-review-retention-integration test:TestCompletedReviewRetention — a newer approval citing evidence absent from its bundle does\n.pose/specs/2026-09-29-retained-review-survives-an-invalid-newer-approval.md:119:- R2 [satisfied] capability:completed-review-retention-precedence evidence:integration check:completed-review-retention-integration test:TestCompletedReviewRetention — a newer rejected attestation still leaves the closed scope\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-followup-metadata-and-routing-integrity.md:32:- R1: Validar review como data real no calendário admitido, incluindo bissextos, meses/dias e formato canônico; data inexistente deve produzir meta_error, nunca campo válido ou resultado não vencido por falha silenciosa.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-followup-metadata-and-routing-integrity.md:35:- R4: Reconciliar spawned/covered/duplicate com destino ausente, abandonado, superseded ou ilegível; emitir candidato com origem, ID rastreado de B22, destino, motivo e coverage de B06. Encaminhamento registrado permanece história, sem converter automaticamente a disposition.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-followup-metadata-and-routing-integrity.md:87:| V4 — P06: spawned/covered/duplicate para abandoned/órfão/ilegível | Candidato com ID/origem/motivo; nenhuma disposition automática; coverage localizada. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-followup-metadata-and-routing-integrity.md:89:| V6 — Done adequado/inadequado e abandono explicitamente justificado | Evidência/âncora considerada; status sozinho não resolve intenção; decisão permanece visível. |\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-upgrade-journey-starts-below-the-newest-capability.md:22:Make the install-and-upgrade journey start from a published release that predates the engine's newest governed capability, so the update it exercises always has a configuration review to open.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-upgrade-journey-starts-below-the-newest-capability.md:26:Found while preparing 7.1.0: with the version bumped, the journey installed 7.0.0, the newest release older than the engine, and failed with \"the update did not open a configuration review\". 7.0.0 and 7.1.0 offer the same capabilities, so no review is owed: the engine was right and the journey's premise was wrong. Without the fix the journey would fail on every release that adds no capability.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-upgrade-journey-starts-below-the-newest-capability.md:30:The journey still starts from a published, checksum-verified release and still asserts the configuration review, the setup decisions and the idempotent second update.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-upgrade-journey-starts-below-the-newest-capability.md:55:- Options considered: (a) bound by the newest capability's `introduced_in`; (b) assert no review when nothing is new.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-upgrade-journey-starts-below-the-newest-capability.md:57:- Rationale: (b) would stop exercising the review, setup and second-update path on every release that adds no capability.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-upgrade-journey-starts-below-the-newest-capability.md:63:At engine 7.1.0 the journey failed in validate (`install-and-upgrade-journeys-integration`, \"the update did not open a configuration review\"); with the fix `POSE_JOURNEYS=1 go test ./internal/cli -run TestJourneysInstallAndUpgradeFromThePublishedRelease` passes, installing 6.2.0.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-09-pose-upgrade-journey-starts-below-the-newest-capability.md:78:- Reviewed in the same session that implemented it, with no separate reviewer execution: declared, not independent.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-journal-checkpoint-and-lock-recovery.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-journal-checkpoint-and-lock-recovery.md:149:- Rationale: Lock antigo pode continuar vivo; TTL e PID isolado não provam abandono.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-journal-checkpoint-and-lock-recovery.md:180:[review](../results/b13-independent-review.json).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-journal-checkpoint-and-lock-recovery.md:203:Claude/Anthropic, por `agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review`, autorizado pelo\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-journal-checkpoint-and-lock-recovery.md:208:O [parecer, Second round](../reports/2026-10-16-pose-b13-journal-checkpoint-lock-recovery-review.md)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-journal-checkpoint-and-lock-recovery.md:209:e a [evidência compacta das duas rodadas](../results/b13-independent-review.json)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:2:slug: pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:3:status: in-progress        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:13:delivers: capability:review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:16:# Spec: pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:21:Keep a delegated review run concludable when the reviewer ends while a process it started is still running, by terminating and reaping the run's remaining processes before the cleanup inventory.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:24:Round 2 of `pose-review-readiness-before-seal` (rrn-9d5816c780952f13) produced a complete draft with two valid findings, but its cleanup was `runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained` because a broad `go test` the reviewer started was still running. The run could not be concluded and its findings had to be carried by hand. On 2026-11-24 a dispatch stopped during setup left reservation `000002.json` of attempt `rat-cfa14ceb…` with no run: every later dispatch failed with `attempt … incomplete or unreadable`, and `pose delegate cancel` refused it as `stalled, not running`; the reservation had to be moved out of the repository by hand.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:30:Changing review independence, round accounting or the attestation preflight.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:36:- R2: A run whose leftover processes were terminated and reaped, and whose inventory then completes, shall be concludable; the run record shall say which processes were terminated.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:37:- R3: The review brief shall ask the reviewer to let every command it starts finish before ending.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:39:- R5: An attempt reservation whose dispatch was interrupted before its run was recorded shall not block later dispatches: `pose delegate ls` shall show it as abandoned with its cause, and `pose delegate cancel` (or the next dispatch) shall release it with a record, never by deleting the reservation.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:54:`pose-mcp` (review dispatch and conclusion), the manual and its embedded copy.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:57:- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:58:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:59:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:60:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:61:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:62:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:71:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:72:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:74:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:75:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:76:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:78:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:79:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:81:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_reap_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:90:- capability:review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:94:`pose delegate cancel` releases a stalled attempt that has no run, recording a failed run and its receipt. Brief template `review-brief/10`. The run record's `safety.limitations` names the processes the dispatch ended after the adapter.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:124:An abandoned attempt is closed by the records a failed run writes (a run record and its receipt), released only when its marker is stalled and its owner proven dead. Nothing is deleted from the ledger, and older engines read the result as an ordinary failed run.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:137:- 2026-11-24: implemented R1–R6. Each has a test that fails with its fix mutated out: the dispatch ends a process the adapter left in a session of its own (the test's leftover keeps writing into the runtime directory), the release records the failed run and receipt and removes the marker and its stall claim, a live owner is never released, and `review-brief/10` asks commands to finish while `/9` stays unchanged.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:139:- 2026-11-24: review round 1 (rrn-c5c082703d83c834) requested changes. N1: the reservation was published before the active marker, so a dispatch ended in between left an attempt nothing could release; the dispatch now marks the attempt active first and publishes the reservation after, and a stalled marker without a reservation is removed by the release. When marking itself fails, the dispatch still publishes the reservation and records the failed run and its receipt, keeping the contract of `pose-delegation-result-before-marker`. N2: `delegate ls` now names the abandonment cause and the release command, in text and JSON. N3: each process is pinned by a pidfd and its environment read again through it before SIGKILL, so a reused pid is never signalled. N4: a scan that cannot list `/proc` or read a process state fails; a process of this user whose environment cannot be read is counted and disclosed in the run record rather than skipped (L3). N5: the manual says the reaping is Linux-only. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out (N4's disclosure is not reproducible in a test: it needs a non-inspectable process).\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:140:- 2026-11-24: review round 2 (rrn-2c9fa8ac47c2fbab) requested changes. N1: a reservation an earlier engine left without any marker is now listed by `delegate ls` and released by `cancel` once it has no marker, receipt or run and is older than ten minutes (an earlier engine marked within moments of reserving). N2: a non-inspectable process of this user that did not exist before the adapter started may be the run's, so the scan fails and the run stays unconcludable; ones that predate the run are skipped and disclosed. N3: a release claims the attempt exclusively, so two cancels never record two runs. N4: `TestAnInterruptedDispatchIsReleasedAndTheNextOneRuns` interrupts a real dispatch after its reservation, sees the next dispatch refused with the release command, releases it and dispatches again. N5: a receipt that cannot be inspected is reported with its error. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out, except N5.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:141:- 2026-11-24: review round 3 (rrn-667b69e8c01c345c) requested changes. N1: the release claim records its owner; a claim whose owner is gone is taken over, and a release interrupted after recording its run completes with that run instead of recording another. N2: age proves nothing about a markerless reservation, so it is released only with `--confirm-abandoned`, the operator's assertion that no dispatch of it runs, which the recorded run states. N3: reservations and receipts that cannot be read are reported as losses by `delegate ls`. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:142:- 2026-11-24: review round 4 (rrn-97acfcc2809e32c2) requested changes. N1: `pose delegate cancel` now asks the release for every attempt that is not running, so a release interrupted after recording its run is completed even when the attempt already shows that run; an abandonment run no longer counts as the attempt's run when looking for orphans. N2: a stale claim is taken over by renaming it, which only one taker wins, then an exclusive publish. N3: with the run history incomplete, the release refuses to rule a run out and the listing reports why. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:143:- 2026-11-24: review round 5 (rrn-146bc70da7364cde) requested changes. N1: the published claim and its takeover protocol are replaced by an operating-system lock (`flock`) on a per-attempt lock file, which the kernel releases when its holder ends, so there is nothing to take over and no window between two takers. N2: a release that finds the receipt already published and the marker still stalled completes by removing the marker. N3: the release completes with any run the attempt already recorded (by its dispatch or by an earlier release), never writing a second one. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:144:- 2026-11-24: review round 6 (rrn-adf91bb46841bd66) requested changes. N1: an unreadable active marker may be a live attempt's, so no reservation is then taken as markerless. N2: a descendant that leaves the group, starts its own session and clears its environment is now ended too on Linux: the dispatcher makes itself a child subreaper, and after the adapter exits it ends every child reparented to it in another session, started after the adapter, that does not name another run's checkout, pinning each by pidfd and reaping it. N3: the disclosed count holds only processes that predate the run. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:145:- 2026-11-24: review round 7 (rrn-9abc2fe5dedc7478) requested changes. N1, N2: a subreaper that cannot be enabled or a run start that cannot be read now fails the cleanup instead of skipping the orphan scan. N3: a process start that cannot be read, in the baseline or the orphan scan, is an error, and a process absent from the baseline is never taken as preexisting. N4: the run record names the ended processes by pid only; their names, which the reviewer chooses, are not recorded. N4 has a test; N1–N3 are error paths the host cannot be made to produce in a test.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:146:- 2026-11-24: the matrix of round 8 failed `TestReviewDispatchRunsAndRecordsAdapters`, and the cause was the design, not the test: a subreaper is process-wide, so the dispatcher also adopted and ended children other code started in the same process (a detached delegation) and could reap a process another goroutine waited for. The subreaper moved into a review run shim: the dispatcher starts the adapter as `<pose> __pose-review-run-shim <adapter path> <argv>`, the shim makes itself the subreaper, runs the adapter as its only child, ends and reaps everything left in its subtree, reports the ended pids in a file the dispatcher reads, and returns the adapter's status, re-raising its signal so a lost process still reads as lost. The shim has no other children, so all it adopts is the run's. The pose command and the test binaries that dispatch enable it; another embedder starts the adapter directly. `TestAnOrphanThatClearedItsEnvironmentIsEnded` fails with the shim's reaping removed.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:147:- 2026-11-24: review round 8 (rrn-f19179878d867e9a) requested changes. N1: the environment entry is the reviewer's to set, so with the shim the dispatcher no longer searches by it; the shim's subtree is the run's by construction, and the search remains only for an embedder without the shim (L6). N2: the shim's report goes through a pipe passed as file descriptor 3, which the shim closes on exec, never through a path the reviewer can write. N3: a timeout sends the shim SIGTERM, and the shim ends the run's subtree before it exits; the group kill after the run stays the backstop. N4: the shim receives SIGTERM when its dispatcher ends (`PR_SET_PDEATHSIG`, checked against the dispatcher's pid at start) and ends the run, so a dead dispatcher never leaves a reviewer running. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:164:The release is driven through the Store, including after a real interrupted dispatch; the thin `pose delegate cancel` branch that calls it is not driven through the CLI, because a stalled marker there needs a dispatch process killed and three silent heartbeat intervals. N5 (the receipt inspection error) has no test: making the receipt path uninspectable also makes the reservation unreadable first.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:170:The dispatch ends the processes a run left running before its cleanup and names them in the run record; `pose delegate cancel` releases an attempt abandoned before its run was recorded; `review-brief/10` asks the reviewer to let its commands finish.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:174:`pose-mcp` (review dispatch, attempt ledger, delegation CLI, brief), the manual in both locales and its embedded copies.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:182:L1: on Linux a run's process escapes only while it keeps a live parent outside the run and neither the run's group nor its environment entry, for example one handed to a service manager; the cleanup inventory still fails a run whose files it keeps changing. L2: outside Linux only the process-group kill applies. L6: an embedder that does not enable the shim falls back to the search by the sealed-checkout entry, which a reviewer process can set. L4: a reservation an earlier engine left without a marker records no owner, so its release rests on the operator's confirmation, not on proof. L3: a process of this user that made itself non-inspectable cannot be matched: one that predates the run is skipped and counted in the run record, and one started during the run fails the cleanup, so such a run is not concludable.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:2:slug: pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:10:delivers: capability:review-subject-unclassified-removals\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:13:# Spec: An unclassified removal does not block a review bundle\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:18:Stop the review subject classifier failing closed on the deletion of a path\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:23:A spec that deleted a root-level dotfile cannot be reviewed:\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:26:[ERROR] unclassified review subject path .harne8-agent-sync.json\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:30:there is nothing to read and nothing to classify; the reviewable fact is the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:33:entire review to tell the reviewer nothing they cannot already see.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:35:The shape is familiar. `pose-review-subject-submodule-classification` fixed the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:37:`pose-review-subject-and-scope-precision` fixed the ordering of that fix in\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:41:content behind the path to review.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:64:  producing `unclassified review subject path` and shall keep blocking.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:78:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go` — subject classification and the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:80:- `.pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md` — the sealing\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:84:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:85:- renamed: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md -> .pose/changelogs/v2.0.0/pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:86:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:87:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:88:- modified: .pose/adr/2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:92:- capability:review-subject-unclassified-removals module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:98:  still recorded in the subject with its own class, so a reviewer sees it; and\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:99:  the alternative — refusing to review a deletion — has already cost more than\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:130:  prevent. (c) keeps the deletion visible to the reviewer and stops it being\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:131:  fatal — the reviewer decides whether deleting it mattered, which is the\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:132:  judgement a review is for.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:146:  was reviewed by an attestation issued before it existed. Widening the digest\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:147:  costs at most an unnecessary re-review; narrowing it costs a review that never\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:159:- Rationale: (c) is what review caught, and in this repository specifically it\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:195:  creation it must still produce `unclassified review subject path`. All eight\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:203:- R1 [satisfied] <review_bundle.go — the removal branch precedes the unclassified one and sets class removed with include true; TestReviewBundleDoesNotBlockOnAnUnclassifiedRemoval asserts no blocker names the path>\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:206:- R4 [satisfied] <reviewCriterionInputDigest includes class removed in the non-subject-sensitive subject slice; TestReviewCriterionReuseIsInvalidatedByAnUnclassifiedRemoval asserts the digest changes and that reuse of the prior verdict is rejected with \"input digest changed\">\n.pose/specs/2026-09-08-pose-review-subject-unclassified-removals.md:218:- [open] Consider reporting unclassified paths as a finding on the bundle rather than a blocker, so a reviewer sees them without the gate refusing (owner:unowned crit:low review:2026-12-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:2:slug: pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:10:delivers: capability:review-archive-coattributed-fragments\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:13:# Spec: Resolve archived review fragments co-attributed in a shared commit\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:17:Unblock a legitimate review subject containing another spec's archived fragment when the same immutable Git commit attributes that path to both specs. Reuse the existing ledger witness without inferring ownership from dependency declarations or filenames.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:19:At source HEAD 11d1630, review of pose-validate-report-carries-its-run fails on the archived pose-one-follow-up-format fragment. Both POSE-Spec lines are present in squash commit 7859fae11d745c772fbdaee5b40a2a27a549f396. Subject reading passes only the primary spec to the archival resolver.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:21:Reuse knowledge:adr-sealed-review-bundles-review: semantic identity must survive release archival while unproved content remains fail closed.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:25:- R1: Before and after committed archival, a shared-commit review subject shall have identical digests when the ledger names a co-attributed path owner.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:33:- created: .pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:34:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:35:- created: .pose/reports/2026-09-28-review-archive-coattribution.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:38:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:39:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_release_archive_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:42:- capability:review-archive-coattributed-fragments module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:51:- [x] Run native registered archive integration, module matrix, real preparation, review and closeout.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:60:Add a shared-commit fixture to the existing release-review suite; require an unchanged subject. Add disjoint-commit and wrong-path negatives; retain all existing owner, digest, ledger and symlink negatives. The registered release-review-archive-integration check runs these cases. Run the module's native matrix and the real scope preparation using the candidate build.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-28-pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments.md:66:- R4 [satisfied] report:.pose/reports/2026-09-28-review-archive-coattribution.md real scope prepares with zero blockers under the candidate CLI.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:18:Restore the hierarchical review gate to `locales/pt-BR/.agents/skills/pose-spec-closeout/SKILL.md`,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:23:version routes the closeout through the review gate — `pose review record`,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:24:`pose review-check`, `pose close`. The pt-BR version did not mention any of the\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:28:That is not a cosmetic gap. The review gate is exactly what `pose check\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:30:that fails the structural gate with `review closeout: record or remediate a\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:31:fresh review` — an error whose cause is not visible from its text. This session\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:35:The gap came from one commit: `feat: enforce hierarchical review closeout`\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:63:- R1: The translated skill shall instruct recording an immutable review\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:64:  attempt with `pose review record ... --apply`.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:65:- R2: It shall require `pose review-check spec:<slug>` to report a fresh,\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:66:  approved review before any lifecycle transition.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:116:- [x] R1: record the review attempt\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:147:  `review record`, `review-check` and `close`; the translation referenced none.\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:160:- R2 [satisfied] check:skills-check — step 3 requires `pose review-check spec:<slug>` with `fresh` and `approved`, and says stale attempts are superseded rather than edited\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:162:- R4 [satisfied] report:locales/pt-BR/.agents/skills/pose-spec-closeout/SKILL.md — the output requirements demand a fresh approved review, and the anti-patterns name the exact `pose check --strict` error that hand-editing produces\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:175:The translated closeout skill routes through the review gate it must pass, and\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:190:- [covered: pose-skill-command-parity] Nothing detects a translated skill that teaches a workflow the engine no longer has: `skills-check` validates contract conformance and passed through this entire defect. A parity check would have to compare only the POSE commands each side teaches — the token-level comparison used for the manuals would fight the deliberate format asymmetry between terse English skills and example-rich translations. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-10-08)\n.pose/specs/2026-08-08-pose-skill-closeout-gate-parity.md:191:- [covered: pose-skill-command-parity] Decided with evidence: the terse rewrite had dropped nine commands the translations still taught, so the translations were the more complete side and the English skills got them back; the format difference itself stays deliberate. Original item: decide the format question the drift exposed: English skills were rewritten terse (Codex-native, no code blocks) while translations kept an earlier example-rich shape, so the translations carry more concrete commands than the originals. Either the translations should be condensed to match, or the English skills lost detail worth restoring — but the two should not stay divergent by accident. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-setup-command.md:22:Add `pose setup`: the single place a person (or an agent on their behalf) sees the instance's configuration — identity, commit gate, capabilities in force, capabilities new since the last review, what needs setup — and the one next step, and, at a terminal, performs each step only after the person confirms it. `pose install` and `pose update` end by naming it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-setup-command.md:40:- R1: `pose setup` shall report, in this order: project identity, principals and keys (with the git identity's suggested principal and whether it is registered), the pre-commit gate, capabilities in force, capabilities new since the last configuration review, capabilities that need setup, and one next step with its command; `--json` shall return the same plan.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-setup-command.md:41:- R2: A capability shall count as new when it is off, undecided and introduced after the version recorded as `reviewed_version` in `.pose/policy/adoption-decisions.json` (every off, undecided capability when none is recorded); a fresh install shall record its engine version, and deciding the last new capability shall advance it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-setup-command.md:56:- `adoption-decisions.json` gains an optional `reviewed_version`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-05-pose-setup-command.md:123:`pose setup` (report, `--json`, interactive with explicit confirmation), `reviewed_version` and decision versions in the adoption record, capabilities to review, the install and update next steps, and doctor's `setup.capabilities`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-docs-and-manuals-match-5-0-2.md:26:followed, up to v5.0.2, and between them they changed what a review bundle\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-docs-and-manuals-match-5-0-2.md:43:- `pose review attest` was documented without `--criterion`, `--finding` or\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-docs-and-manuals-match-5-0-2.md:57:- Changing behaviour. The one behavioural defect found here — the shipped review\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-docs-and-manuals-match-5-0-2.md:95:- modified: .agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-docs-and-manuals-match-5-0-2.md:113:- modified: locales/pt-BR/.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-docs-and-manuals-match-5-0-2.md:119:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-docs-and-manuals-match-5-0-2.md:122:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/.agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md\n.pose/specs/2026-09-11-pose-docs-and-manuals-match-5-0-2.md:169:- Context: component-aware review and sealed bundles had no mechanism of their\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:2:slug: pose-review-subject-later-removal\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:11:delivers: capability:review-subject-later-removal\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:15:# Spec: A milestone review can be sealed after its specs closed and a later spec removed their files\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:21:Seal the review bundle of a milestone whose member specs are done and whose files a later spec removed, with the same answers `review verify` and `check --strict` already give for those specs.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:25:Closing the roadmaps `delegated-review` and `delegation` needs a sealed `milestone-integration@1` bundle per milestone. All eighteen refuse: (a) six of their specs declare `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_dispatch.go`, which `pose-delivery-later-removal` removed, and the review subject still tries to read it — the delivery graph accepts the removal, the review subject does not; (b) the seal requires each member spec to have a sealed bundle equal to the one prepared now, while a done spec's later commits (its closeout, the index, a later removal) change what is prepared — `review verify` and the closeout gate retain the approved review of a done scope, the milestone seal does not.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:30:- A retained child review is accepted only where the closeout gate already retains it: a done scope, the latest readable attestation approved, the attestation history complete.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:34:- Milestones whose members are not done, or roadmaps' own review rules.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:35:- Re-reviewing or re-sealing closed specs.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:41:- R1: When a review subject path is absent from the tree, and the delivery-integrity graph has, for every selected spec that observes the path, a removal of it by another spec that supersedes that very spec, the subject entry shall be digested from those witnesses (removing spec and deleting commit per observer) instead of failing as unreadable.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:43:- R3: Sealing a milestone (or roadmap) bundle shall accept a done child scope whose sealed bundle no longer equals the prepared one when the child's own review verification retains its approved review (closed, fresh, approved — lost history, a later negative review and a changed federated manifest excluded), recording the retained bundle as the child; otherwise the child shall still block, with the verification's cause.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:44:- R4: The eighteen milestone bundles of the roadmaps `delegated-review` and `delegation` shall prepare with no blocker under these rules; sealing them follows the engine specs for SR-R1-05, SR-R1-06 and SR-R1-07 (maintainer's direction, 2026-10-30).\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:62:Review bundle subject and child resolution in `internal/pose/review_bundle.go`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:66:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:67:- created: .pose/starts/pose-review-subject-later-removal.json\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:68:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-subject-later-removal.md\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:69:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:70:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_subject_later_removal_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:71:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_review_adoption_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:73:- created: .pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.amendments.jsonl\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:78:- capability:review-subject-later-removal module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:82:A review subject entry may carry a removal digest; a milestone bundle's child may be a retained closed review.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:86:- [x] Removal witness in the review subject\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:89:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:96:- Selected option: reuse the answers the engine already gives — the delivery graph's removal witness and the closeout gate's retained review\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:97:- Rationale: the closed specs' reviews are already fresh and approved for `review verify` and `check --strict`; a second, stricter answer at the milestone seal forces re-reviews that judge nothing new (maintainer's choice, 2026-10-30)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:105:Fixtures: a spec whose declared file a later spec removed seals its bundle with a removal entry; without the witness, or with a refused one, it refuses. A milestone whose done child changed after closeout seals with the retained child; a not-done child or a child with a rejected latest review blocks. Then the eighteen real milestones seal. Each rule shown failing on revert.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:109:- R1 [satisfied] check:review-subject-later-removal-integration test:TestReviewSubjectReadsALaterRemovalFromItsWitness test:TestMilestoneSubjectRemovalHoldsForEveryMember report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:814d1c1032d5501b574c8ceda715d7150896b2c4 — An absent subject path digests from the removals the delivery graph accepted for every selected spec observing the path it reads, keyed by that path before change-set reduction.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:110:- R2 [satisfied] check:review-subject-later-removal-integration test:TestReviewSubjectReadsALaterRemovalFromItsWitness test:TestReviewSubjectRemovalHoldsForEveryObserver test:TestMilestoneSubjectRemovalHoldsForEveryMember report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:814d1c1032d5501b574c8ceda715d7150896b2c4 — No witness, another path's or spec's, a refused removal, a spec's own removal, or any observer lacking one keeps the unreadable-path blocker, in every set order, action and containment.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:111:- R3 [satisfied] check:review-subject-later-removal-integration test:TestMilestoneSealRetainsADoneChildsApprovedReview test:TestRetainedChildFollowsItsVerification report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:814d1c1032d5501b574c8ceda715d7150896b2c4 — A done child whose preparation changed is accepted through the bundle its own review verification retains; not-done children, later negative reviews and revoked federated trust keep the blocker.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:112:- R4 [satisfied] check:review-subject-later-removal-integration report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:814d1c1032d5501b574c8ceda715d7150896b2c4 — All eighteen milestones of `delegated-review` and `delegation` prepare with zero blockers (independently reproduced by the reviewer); their seals wait on F1–F3.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:118:A review subject reads a path a later spec removed through the removal the delivery graph accepted for each observing spec, and a milestone seal accepts a done member through the review its own verification retains. Independently reviewed by Codex over four rounds (reports kept outside the checkout); 11 of 12 mutations killed, the survivor adjudicated equivalent by the reviewer.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:126:- [covered: pose-review-approval-follows-children] F1: make integration approval of a milestone or roadmap follow its descendants: a child's later rejection, lost attestation history or reopening revokes the parent's approval in preparation, verification and closeout (SR-R1-05). Next engine spec, before the eighteen milestone seals. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:high review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:127:- [covered: pose-removal-witness-freshness] F2: bind the Git and recorded-history inputs of indexed removal witnesses to generation freshness, or refuse a witness whose freshness is unknown, for review subjects as for delivery integrity (SR-R1-06, with LR-R1-10 / F4 of pose-delivery-later-removal). Next engine spec, before the eighteen milestone seals. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-30-pose-review-subject-later-removal.md:128:- [covered: pose-review-approval-follows-children] F3: make review retention after drift honour replacement lineage, including backdated or equal seal times, so matching and retained verification choose the same bundle (SR-R1-07). Next engine spec, before the eighteen milestone seals. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-06)\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-check-builds-the-delivery-graph-once.md:119:The corpus first: 528 review bundles, 515 attestations, 225 specs, 1077 markdown\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-check-builds-the-delivery-graph-once.md:153:approved; `review-check` fresh and approved; `closeout-check` terminal.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-20-check-builds-the-delivery-graph-once.md:191:  of identical work (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-11-20)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:2:slug: pose-review-readiness-before-seal\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:13:delivers: capability:review-readiness-before-seal\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:16:# Spec: pose-review-readiness-before-seal\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:21:Refuse at seal, and let the reviewer check inside its run, every condition the conclusion preflight and `pose close` would otherwise refuse after a full review round.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:24:Closing `pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks` took 23 review rounds. About seven were lost to conditions known before the reviewer started: a missing delivery declaration that `close` refused only after approval, a decision with no requirement basis, a finding id with a round prefix, `prior_findings` naming findings no concluded round holds open, criterion evidence outside the criterion's component, and a note file over 16 KiB. Each cost a seal, a delegated run and about 40 minutes.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:30:Capping review rounds, changing review independence, or judging the subject itself.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:35:- R1: `pose review bundle --seal` shall refuse a spec scope whose attributed changes touch a delivery root without a delivery declaration, or a governed path its artifacts do not declare, with the same findings `pose close` refuses (`undeclared-delivery`, `undeclared`).\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:37:- R3: A new `pose review draft-check <run|bundle> --draft <file>` shall run inside the review sandbox without writing. It reports every reason the conclusion preflight would refuse that draft: unreadable block, prefixed new finding ids, `prior_findings` outside the open findings, criterion evidence outside its component, undeclared decisions in mappings. It exits non-zero when any applies.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:38:- R4: The review brief shall instruct the reviewer to run `draft-check` on its draft before finishing, and list the open prior findings it must account for.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:39:- R5: `pose delegate` shall refuse a note file over the adapter limit with a message naming the note, its size and the limit, instead of the generic adapter-file error.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:40:- R6: When the instance has a conclusions issuer but the run is not concluded automatically, `pose delegate review` shall print the exact `pose review conclude <run>` command as the next step.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:57:- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:58:- created: .pose/adr/2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:59:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:60:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_draft_check.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:61:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:62:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:63:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:64:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:65:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:66:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:68:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_structure_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:69:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:70:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:71:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:72:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_seal_readiness_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:73:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:74:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_conclude.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:75:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:84:- capability:review-readiness-before-seal module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:87:New command `pose review draft-check`; new environment variables `POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_CONTEXT` and `POSE_REVIEW_CLI` set for delegated review runs; new brief template `review-brief/8`; `review bundle --seal` refuses two more conditions for new seals.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:90:The dispatch writes `pose-review-draft-context.json` to the run's private temporary directory; nothing is written to the repository.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:93:A draft check that drifted from the conclusion would mislead reviewers; it calls the same functions, and a test compares its reasons with the conclusion's refusal. Residual limits L1 and L2 are stated in the ADR.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:110:The draft check reuses the conclusion's parser, round accounting and attestation content checks, extracted as `attestationContentBlockers`, so it cannot accept what the conclusion refuses for content. It leaves out only the run's signature and identity, which do not exist before the run ends. See ADR `2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:114:The seal applies only the readiness rules whose inputs exist before the review: the delivery and artifact declarations and the decision basis, the latter only when a required criterion asks for structural mappings. Evidence and trace gates of `pose close` stay at close. A bundle already sealed is returned without being judged again.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:128:- 2026-11-23: review round 1 (rrn-fa6a6e8e1df0a0ba) requested changes. N1: the decision-basis refusal applied to plans with structural facts but no criterion asking for their mapping; it now requires a required `RequiresStructuralMapping` criterion. N2: `draft-check` rejected run ids; a run id now selects its bundle. N3: `live_policy_reads_test.go` was not declared; it is, and the seal now also refuses the `undeclared` artifact finding, which the round showed is known before the review too. The reviewer could not run `draft-check` because its shell resolved the installed `pose`; the dispatch now sets `POSE_REVIEW_CLI` to the dispatching engine and `review-brief/8` (not yet published) names it. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:129:- 2026-11-23: review round 2 (rrn-9d5816c780952f13) ran `draft-check` through `POSE_REVIEW_CLI` on its own draft, which passed, and found N4 and N5; its cleanup was incomplete because a broad test was still running, so it could not be concluded. N4: a draft over 4 MiB was judged by its prefix; drafts over the limit are now refused from a file or standard input. N5: naming the run's own bundle inside the sealed checkout ignored the dispatch context; the context now serves the run's bundle whether it is named or not, and another reference names the context's bundle when it cannot be read. Both fixes have tests that fail with them mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:152:The seal of a new spec bundle refuses an undeclared delivery or artifact and, when the plan asks for structural mappings, a decision basis that reaches no requirement. `pose review draft-check` reports what the conclusion step would refuse, inside the run, through a context the dispatch writes. The brief `review-brief/8` asks for it. `pose delegate` names an oversized note and the conclude command of a run nothing concluded.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md:156:`pose-mcp` (CLI and engine), the manual in both locales and its embedded copies, the ADR `2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal`.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-contract-nodes.md:26:- Evidência de origem: [review ABM](../reports/2026-09-18-pose-abm-review.md), achados Premissas sem identidade e racionalização posterior.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-contract-nodes.md:58:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-contract-nodes.md:79:`pose-dist/` (esta spec vive no próprio pose-dist); `review_bundle.go` não\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-contract-nodes.md:100:  estado), mudança `transition` para estado, origem (author/reviewer) e\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-contract-nodes.md:103:- Capability `contract_nodes_version: 1` na policy de review. Sem ela, o gate\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-contract-nodes.md:130:- [x] Executar matriz aplicável, obter review explícito e anexar evidência por R-ID.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-contract-nodes.md:148:- Contexto: a análise inicial propõe novos controles; o review confirmou limites que exigem implementação proporcional.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-contract-nodes.md:171:- `pose review verify spec:pose-abm-contract-nodes` antes da transição terminal.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-contract-nodes.md:190:reviews seladas consumidas pelo Harne8, renovadas em seguida.\n.pose/specs/2026-09-27-pose-abm-contract-nodes.md:218:- [done] Adotado no pose-dist em 2026-10-05 por decisão do maintainer (action request act-7d587a8e4f3bf0fc, após o shadow de pose-abm-capability-adoption sem efeito observável neste corpus); a adoção no Harne8 segue a spec harne8-adopt-agency-readiness. Item original: adotar `contract_nodes_version` nas instâncias depois do stop/go do piloto de campo, com baseline v2 das specs em pasta. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-01)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:2:slug: pose-roadmap-reviews-findings\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:6:depends_on: pose-milestone-review-proportional\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:11:delivers: capability:roadmap-reviews-findings\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:15:# Spec: What the roadmap reviews found\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:21:The defects the reviews of `epistemic-lifecycle`, `agency-readiness` and `pose-state-consistency-and-recovery` left open are closed, and the suite means the same in a reviewer's sandbox as it does here.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:25:A premise stops being watched the moment its spec is done, which is when a decision starts to rely on it. A reviewer's sandbox creates an empty `.git` above the temporary directory, which failed 333 tests in the full suite of the `pose-v7-onboarding-and-consolidation` review and the registered checks of `agency-readiness`, so an independent review could not see the suite green. A close reports refused over a spec it already moved to done, a refresh that published records failure, and an immutable publication falls back to a visible write after any link failure.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:45:- R7: A delegated run whose brief was accepted whole shall not fail because `Wait` closed the pipe before the writer did.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:64:`internal/pose/premise_validity.go`, `internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go`, `internal/pose/release_lifecycle.go`, `internal/pose/discovery.go`, `internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go`, `internal/pose/operation_result.go`, `internal/pose/writer_publication.go`, `internal/cli/review_closeout.go`, `internal/cli/closeout_plan.go`, `internal/cli/state_refresh.go`, `internal/cli/state.go`, `internal/cli/state_hooks.go`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:68:- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:69:- created: .pose/starts/pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.json\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:70:- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:77:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:80:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:87:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/roadmap_reviews_findings_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:88:- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/roadmap_reviews_findings_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:92:- capability:roadmap-reviews-findings module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:105:- [x] Independent review and closeout\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:110:- Basis: spec pose-review-archive-coattributed-fragments R3\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:119:- Minimal option: tell reviewers to ignore the failures\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:129:Each guard is seen failing under a mutant. The full suite passes with an empty `.git` above the temporary directory. In a user namespace without a root mapping, where the reviewer runs, root reads as uid 65534 and 59 delegation tests still fail on the ownership guard of the task state directory: that guard refuses correctly, so this spec names them and does not touch it.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:133:- R1 [satisfied] capability:roadmap-reviews-findings evidence:integration check:roadmap-reviews-findings-integration test:TestAPremiseOutlivesItsDelivery test:TestAWithdrawnPremiseAsksForNothing report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:21e17d61da9644f3b57b287fc5989eb6b43c3d96\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:134:- R2 [satisfied] check:roadmap-reviews-findings-integration test:TestAnEmptyGitDirectoryIsNoRepository test:TestEveryRepositoryGitFindsIsARepository test:TestAMarkerThatIsNoRepositoryEndsTheIgnoreWalk test:TestTheIgnoreWalkKnowsARepositoryByIdentity test:TestTheIgnoreWalkEntersARepositoryOnce report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:21e17d61da9644f3b57b287fc5989eb6b43c3d96\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:135:- R3 [satisfied] check:roadmap-reviews-findings-integration test:TestAnUnsyncedCloseSaysItClosed report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:21e17d61da9644f3b57b287fc5989eb6b43c3d96\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:136:- R4 [satisfied] check:roadmap-reviews-findings-integration test:TestAnUnsyncedRefreshDoesNotReadAsFailed test:TestAManualUnsyncedRefreshSaysSoAndSucceeds test:TestAStrictPolicyRefusesAnUnsyncedRefresh test:TestAStrictReplayDoesNotReadAsDurable test:TestAPolicyMadeStrictLaterAsksAgain test:TestACombinedRefreshFailureSaysBoth test:TestASkippedReplayIsNoDurabilityUnderAStrictPolicy report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:21e17d61da9644f3b57b287fc5989eb6b43c3d96\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:137:- R5 [satisfied] check:roadmap-reviews-findings-integration test:TestOnlyAMissingLinkFallsBack test:TestTheFallbackAnswersForItsDirectory test:TestACompleteFallbackReportsItsDurability report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:21e17d61da9644f3b57b287fc5989eb6b43c3d96\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:138:- R7 [satisfied] check:roadmap-reviews-findings-integration test:TestABriefAcceptedWholeIsDelivered report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:796a9b226bc2c4744152245e25c22c78bcb1837b\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:139:- R6 [satisfied] check:roadmap-reviews-findings-integration test:TestTheCleanupPlanHoldsBothCorpora report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:21e17d61da9644f3b57b287fc5989eb6b43c3d96\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:149:The in-place fallback stays non-atomic: a write cut short leaves a partial record, which readers of immutable records refuse and a retry of complete bytes cannot replace, so it has to be removed by hand. It also lets an identical retry see bytes the first writer has not synced yet. Removing the record automatically was tried and dropped: the name may no longer be this write's by then, and it deleted another writer's record under review. Under default policy, a deduplicated replay leaves `skipped` as the last entry, which hides the `durability-unconfirmed` warning of the entry before it. `EPERM` from a link is handled as this attempt's answer, not as proof the filesystem has no links. The 59 delegation tests named in round 2 of the review fail in a user namespace without a root mapping, where root reads as uid 65534: the ownership guard refuses correctly, and the rest of the suite passes there. `lifecycle-truth` cannot seal a bundle of its own (decision D2). Windows and macOS paths were cross-built and reviewed, not run.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:153:- [covered: pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did] F1: Stop `internal/cli/maintenance.go` accepting an empty `.git`, and resolve hook paths through git so a gitfile and a linked worktree work in `maintenance.go`, `doctor.go` and `setup.go` (review R2-F1). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:154:- [covered: pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did] F2: Report installation adoption for what it did when a policy publishes unsynced, including whether a second document is owed (review R2-F2). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:medium review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:155:- [covered: pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did] F3: Keep an unresolved `unsynced` visible to `pose state validate` through a default deduplicated replay (review R2-F3). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:156:- [covered: pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes] F4: Replace the prose test of the cleanup report with a deterministic inventory fixture, and retain the raw inventories (review F6). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:157:- [covered: pose-review-evidence-and-fixture-lifetimes] F5: Fix the flake of `TestTheWaitAcknowledgementNeverTouchesAnExistingEntry` under load, a cleanup race not seen in 60 isolated runs. (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n.pose/specs/2026-11-02-pose-roadmap-reviews-findings.md:158:- [covered: pose-effects-reported-for-what-they-did] F6: Render the `refresh_pending` marker of a lost refresh log as what it is in `pose state validate` and `pose doctor`, which read it as a failed refresh (review R4-F1). (owner:@oseiaspereira88 crit:low review:2026-11-27)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
