{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim.go && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go | sed -n '360,620p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tpackage pose\n     2\t\n     3\timport \"time\"\n     4\t\n     5\t// The review run shim (spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes,\n     6\t// review rounds 6 and 8): a descendant of the reviewer that leaves the\n     7\t// adapter's process group, starts its own session and clears its environment\n     8\t// matches neither the group kill nor the sealed-checkout entry. Making the\n     9\t// dispatcher a child subreaper caught it, but a subreaper is process-wide:\n    10\t// in the dispatching process it also adopted and ended children other code\n    11\t// started there (a detached delegation), and reaped processes another\n    12\t// goroutine was waiting for. The dispatcher therefore starts the adapter\n    13\t// through a shim, the same executable re-entered with ReviewShimArg, which\n    14\t// makes itself the subreaper, runs the adapter, and, once it exits, ends\n    15\t// every process left in its subtree. The shim has no other children, so\n    16\t// everything it adopts is the run's. A timeout asks the shim to stop with\n    17\t// SIGTERM, and the death of the dispatcher delivers it the same signal: in\n    18\t// both cases it ends the subtree before it exits (review round 8, N3, N4).\n    19\t\n    20\t// reviewReapWait bounds how long ending the run's leftover processes takes.\n    21\tconst reviewReapWait = 5 * time.Second\n    22\t\n    23\t// ReviewShimArg is the first argument that runs the executable as a review\n    24\t// run shim instead of the CLI.\n    25\tconst ReviewShimArg = \"__pose-review-run-shim\"\n    26\t\n    27\t// ReviewShimReportEnv tells the shim that the dispatcher passed it a report\n    28\t// pipe as file descriptor 3, and names the dispatcher's pid. The report never\n    29\t// goes to a path the reviewer can write (review round 8, N2).\n    30\tconst ReviewShimReportEnv = \"POSE_REVIEW_SHIM_REPORT\"\n    31\t\n    32\t// ReviewShimAvailable says the running executable handles ReviewShimArg. It\n    33\t// is set by the pose command and by the test binaries that dispatch; any\n    34\t// other embedder starts the adapter directly, without the shim.\n    35\tvar ReviewShimAvailable = false\n    36\t\n    37\t// reviewShimReport is what the shim found after the adapter exited.\n    38\ttype reviewShimReport struct {\n    39\t\tEnded []string `json:\"ended\"`\n    40\t\tError string   `json:\"error,omitempty\"`\n    41\t}\n   360\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n   361\t\t\t\t\tvar aerr error\n   362\t\t\t\t\tattempts, aerr = s.readDelegatedReviewAttempts(run.BundleID, &readBudget)\n   363\t\t\t\t\tif aerr != nil {\n   364\t\t\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, aerr.Error())\n   365\t\t\t\t\t}\n   366\t\t\t\t\tchecked[run.BundleID] = attempts\n   367\t\t\t\t}\n   368\t\t\t\t// The reservation names the attempt's first agent; a continuation's\n   369\t\t\t\t// agent is checked against its own predecessor by the continuation\n   370\t\t\t\t// chain (a resume keeps it, a handoff changes it).\n   371\t\t\t\tfound := false\n   372\t\t\t\tfor _, a := range attempts {\n   373\t\t\t\t\tif a.AttemptID == run.AttemptID && a.BundleDigest == run.BundleDigest && a.Scope == run.Scope && (a.Adapter == run.Adapter || run.continues() != \"\") && a.Reason == run.Reason {\n   374\t\t\t\t\t\tfound = true\n   375\t\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n   376\t\t\t\t\t}\n   377\t\t\t\t}\n   378\t\t\t\tif !found {\n   379\t\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"missing or conflicting attempt reservation \"+run.AttemptID)\n   380\t\t\t\t}\n   381\t\t\t}\n   382\t\t}\n   383\t\tfindings, ledgerErr := s.reviewRunLedgerFindings(\"\", &readBudget)\n   384\t\tif ledgerErr != nil {\n   385\t\t\tlost = append(lost, ledgerErr.Error())\n   386\t\t}\n   387\t\tlost = append(lost, findings...)\n   388\t\tlost = append(lost, s.reviewContinuationFindings(out)...)\n   389\t\treturn out, uniqueSorted(lost), nil\n   390\t}\n   391\t\n   392\t// DispatchPlan is what a dispatch will do.\n   393\ttype DispatchPlan struct {\n   394\t\tprovenance          *ReviewRunProvenance\n   395\t\tPendingContinuation *PendingReviewContinuation\n   396\t\tprocessTimeout      time.Duration\n   397\t\tpredecessor         *ReviewRun\n   398\t\t// handoff makes the continuation another agent's, with handoffSection\n   399\t\t// appended to the brief (spec pose-delegation-handoff).\n   400\t\thandoff        bool\n   401\t\thandoffSection string\n   402\t\tsession        string\n   403\t\t// round is the round of the scope the run reviews, and thread how a\n   404\t\t// round after the first relates to the previous round's session.\n   405\t\tround  int\n   406\t\tthread *ReviewThread\n   407\t\t// extraChannels are outputs the interruption classifier reads beside the\n   408\t\t// transcript and the output, each on its own: a task's stderr.\n   409\t\textraChannels  []string\n   410\t\tnotes          string\n   411\t\tExisting       *ReviewRun\n   412\t\tLimitOf        string\n   413\t\tReason         string\n   414\t\tPolicyDigest   string\n   415\t\tOriginWorktree string\n   416\t\tAdapter        string\n   417\t\tConfig         ReviewerAdapter\n   418\t\tBrief          ReviewBrief\n   419\t\tBundle         ReviewBundle\n   420\t\tSealedCommit   string\n   421\t\tPriorRuns      int\n   422\t\t// Effort is the requested effort level; \"\" means the agent's default.\n   423\t\tEffort string\n   424\t\t// Label, Purpose and Lead are recorded on the run (pose delegate).\n   425\t\tLabel   string\n   426\t\tPurpose string\n   427\t\tLead    string\n   428\t\t// Routing is set by pose delegate; without it the run is compared with\n   429\t\t// the implementation the plan read (spec pose-delegation-routing R8).\n   430\t\tRouting        *DelegationRoutingRecord\n   431\t\timplementation *ReviewBundleImplementation\n   432\t\t// Warnings are printed before the run starts. SameVendorWarning is set\n   433\t\t// when the plan's agent shares the implementation's vendor; a caller that\n   434\t\t// named the agent prints it, routing does not (R9).\n   435\t\tWarnings          []string\n   436\t\tSameVendorWarning string\n   437\t\t// OnStart is called once the attempt is reserved and its marker written,\n   438\t\t// so a detached run can hand its reference back (spec\n   439\t\t// pose-delegated-review-completion-signal R1).\n   440\t\tOnStart func(attempt string) error\n   441\t}\n   442\t\n   443\t// Implementation is the identity the plan compares its agent with.\n   444\tfunc (p DispatchPlan) Implementation() ReviewBundleImplementation {\n   445\t\tswitch {\n   446\t\tcase p.Routing != nil:\n   447\t\t\treturn p.Routing.Implementation\n   448\t\tcase p.implementation != nil:\n   449\t\t\treturn *p.implementation\n   450\t\t}\n   451\t\treturn ReviewBundleImplementation{Vendor: ImplementationUnknown, Model: ImplementationUnknown, Source: ImplementationDetected}\n   452\t}\n   453\t\n   454\t// replanContinuation plans a continuation again at execution, as a resume or\n   455\t// as a handoff to the same agent.\n   456\tfunc (s Store) replanContinuation(plan DispatchPlan) (DispatchPlan, error) {\n   457\t\tvar fresh DispatchPlan\n   458\t\tvar err error\n   459\t\tif plan.handoff {\n   460\t\t\tfresh, err = s.PlanReviewHandoff(plan.predecessor.RunID, plan.Adapter)\n   461\t\t} else {\n   462\t\t\tfresh, err = s.PlanReviewResume(plan.predecessor.RunID)\n   463\t\t}\n   464\t\tif err != nil {\n   465\t\t\treturn fresh, err\n   466\t\t}\n   467\t\t// What the caller set on the plan is kept: the hand-back of a detached run\n   468\t\t// and the routing that chose its agent (spec pose-delegation-mcp R4).\n   469\t\tfresh.OnStart, fresh.Purpose = plan.OnStart, plan.Purpose\n   470\t\tif fresh.Routing == nil {\n   471\t\t\tfresh.Routing = plan.Routing\n   472\t\t}\n   473\t\treturn fresh, nil\n   474\t}\n   475\t\n   476\t// PlanImplementationWithLead reads the plan's implementation again with the\n   477\t// --lead the caller declared, for a bundle that records none (R4), and records\n   478\t// the agent as named.\n   479\tfunc (s Store) PlanImplementationWithLead(plan *DispatchPlan, lead string) {\n   480\t\tplan.Routing, plan.Warnings, plan.SameVendorWarning = nil, nil, \"\"\n   481\t\ts.planImplementation(plan, lead)\n   482\t}\n   483\t\n   484\t// routingAgainstAnotherBundle refuses a routing decision made against an\n   485\t// implementation the plan's bundle does not record: the run would record an\n   486\t// identity and an independence it did not have (spec pose-delegation-routing\n   487\t// R8).\n   488\tfunc routingAgainstAnotherBundle(plan DispatchPlan) string {\n   489\t\tif plan.Routing == nil || plan.Routing.ImplementationFrom != ImplementationFromBundle {\n   490\t\t\treturn \"\"\n   491\t\t}\n   492\t\tsealed := plan.Bundle.Payload.Implementation\n   493\t\tif sealed == nil || !sameImplementation(*sealed, plan.Routing.Implementation) {\n   494\t\t\treturn \"the run was routed against another implementation than bundle \" + plan.Bundle.BundleID + \" records; route it again\"\n   495\t\t}\n   496\t\treturn \"\"\n   497\t}\n   498\t\n   499\t// planImplementation reads the identity a run of bundle is compared with,\n   500\t// records the agent as named unless routing chose it (R8, R9), and warns when\n   501\t// the policy still declares an identity the bundle overrides (R4).\n   502\tfunc (s Store) planImplementation(plan *DispatchPlan, lead string) {\n   503\t\timpl := ReviewBundleImplementation{Vendor: ImplementationUnknown, Model: ImplementationUnknown, Source: ImplementationDetected}\n   504\t\tfrom := ImplementationFromNone\n   505\t\tif policy, _, found, err := s.LoadDelegationPolicy(); err == nil && found {\n   506\t\t\tif read, readFrom, err := s.RoutingImplementation(plan.Bundle, policy, lead); err == nil {\n   507\t\t\t\timpl, from = read, readFrom\n   508\t\t\t}\n   509\t\t\tif plan.Bundle.Payload.Implementation != nil && policy.Provenance != nil && policy.Provenance.Implementation != (ModelIdentity{}) {\n   510\t\t\t\tplan.Warnings = append(plan.Warnings, \"provenance.implementation in the delegation policy is ignored: bundle \"+plan.Bundle.BundleID+\" records the implementation it was sealed by; remove the policy entry\")\n   511\t\t\t}\n   512\t\t}\n   513\t\tplan.implementation = &impl\n   514\t\tif plan.Routing == nil {\n   515\t\t\trecord := ExplicitDelegationRoute(plan.Adapter, impl, from)\n   516\t\t\tplan.Routing = &record\n   517\t\t}\n   518\t\tif knownIdentityPart(impl.Vendor) && normalizeIdentityPart(plan.Config.Vendor) == impl.Vendor {\n   519\t\t\tplan.SameVendorWarning = \"agent \" + plan.Adapter + \" shares the implementation's vendor (\" + impl.Vendor + \"); the run cannot achieve vendor independence\"\n   520\t\t}\n   521\t}\n   522\t\n   523\t// PlanReviewDispatch resolves the bundle, brief and adapter without running.\n   524\tfunc (s Store) PlanReviewDispatch(target, kind, notes, adapter string, reason ...string) (DispatchPlan, error) {\n   525\t\tif err := validateReviewNotes(notes); err != nil {\n   526\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, err\n   527\t\t}\n   528\t\tif len(reason) > 1 {\n   529\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: one rerun reason is accepted\")\n   530\t\t}\n   531\t\twhy := \"\"\n   532\t\tif len(reason) == 1 {\n   533\t\t\twhy = strings.TrimSpace(reason[0])\n   534\t\t}\n   535\t\tbrief, err := s.RenderReviewBrief(target, kind, notes)\n   536\t\tif err != nil {\n   537\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, err\n   538\t\t}\n   539\t\tbundle, err := s.LoadReviewBundle(brief.BundleID)\n   540\t\tif err != nil {\n   541\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, err\n   542\t\t}\n   543\t\tpolicy, found, err := s.LoadReviewersPolicyFor(brief.Kind)\n   544\t\tif err != nil {\n   545\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, err\n   546\t\t}\n   547\t\tif !found || len(policy.Adapters) == 0 {\n   548\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{Brief: brief, Bundle: bundle}, ErrNoReviewerAdapter\n   549\t\t}\n   550\t\tconfig, ok := policy.Adapters[adapter]\n   551\t\tif !ok {\n   552\t\t\tnames := make([]string, 0, len(policy.Adapters))\n   553\t\t\tfor name := range policy.Adapters {\n   554\t\t\t\tnames = append(names, name)\n   555\t\t\t}\n   556\t\t\tsort.Strings(names)\n   557\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: no reviewer adapter %q; configured: %s\", adapter, strings.Join(names, \", \"))\n   558\t\t}\n   559\t\tcommit := bundle.Payload.Subject.Head\n   560\t\tif commit == \"\" || RawHistoryGit(s.Root, \"cat-file\", \"-e\", commit+\"^{commit}\").Run() != nil {\n   561\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the bundle's sealed commit %q is not in this repository\", commit)\n   562\t\t}\n   563\t\torigin, err := dispatchWorktreeIdentity(s.Root)\n   564\t\tif err != nil {\n   565\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, err\n   566\t\t}\n   567\t\tplan := DispatchPlan{notes: notes, Reason: why, PolicyDigest: directoryDigestIn(s.fsys(), filepath.Join(s.Root, \".pose\", \"policy\")), OriginWorktree: origin, Adapter: adapter, Config: config, Brief: brief, Bundle: bundle, SealedCommit: commit, PriorRuns: 0}\n   568\t\truns, losses, err := s.ReadReviewRuns(bundle.BundleID)\n   569\t\tif err != nil {\n   570\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, err\n   571\t\t}\n   572\t\tif len(losses) > 0 {\n   573\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"review history incomplete: %v\", losses)\n   574\t\t}\n   575\t\tcontinued := map[string]bool{}\n   576\t\tfor _, r := range runs {\n   577\t\t\tif r.continues() != \"\" {\n   578\t\t\t\tcontinued[r.continues()] = true\n   579\t\t\t}\n   580\t\t}\n   581\t\tfor _, prior := range runs {\n   582\t\t\tif prior.Status == ReviewRunInterrupted && prior.SupersededBy == \"\" && !continued[prior.RunID] && prior.Interruption != nil && prior.Interruption.Cause == \"usage-limit\" && prior.Adapter != adapter {\n   583\t\t\t\tplan.LimitOf, plan.Reason = prior.RunID, \"limit-of:\"+prior.RunID\n   584\t\t\t}\n   585\t\t}\n   586\t\t_, currentCount, err := s.reviewAttemptAdmission(plan)\n   587\t\tif err != nil {\n   588\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, err\n   589\t\t}\n   590\t\tif _, _, err := reviewAdapterEnvironment(config, \"\", brief.Text, notes); err != nil {\n   591\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, err\n   592\t\t}\n   593\t\tplan.PriorRuns = currentCount\n   594\t\tif brief.Kind == ReviewBriefKindReview {\n   595\t\t\tif err := s.planReviewThread(&plan); err != nil {\n   596\t\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, err\n   597\t\t\t}\n   598\t\t}\n   599\t\ts.planImplementation(&plan, \"\")\n   600\t\tplan.provenance, err = s.prepareRunProvenance(plan, policy)\n   601\t\tif err != nil {\n   602\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, err\n   603\t\t}\n   604\t\treturn plan, nil\n   605\t}\n   606\t\n   607\t// ErrNoReviewerAdapter means the project configured no reviewer.\n   608\tvar ErrNoReviewerAdapter = errors.New(\"pose: no agent is configured in .pose/policy/delegation.json\")\n   609\t\n   610\t// RunReviewDispatch executes plan and records the run, failed or completed.\n   611\tfunc (s Store) RunReviewDispatch(plan DispatchPlan, now func() time.Time) (ReviewRun, error) {\n   612\t\treturn s.RunReviewDispatchContext(context.Background(), plan, now)\n   613\t}\n   614\t\n   615\t// RunReviewDispatchContext also propagates caller cancellation to the covered\n   616\t// process set. Cleanup has its own bounded context and never respawns the adapter.\n   617\tfunc (s Store) RunReviewDispatchContext(parent context.Context, plan DispatchPlan, now func() time.Time) (result ReviewRun, resultErr error) {\n   618\t\tif err := parent.Err(); err != nil {\n   619\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n   620\t\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go | sed -n '1,330p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tpackage pose\n     2\t\n     3\t// Releasing an abandoned attempt (spec\n     4\t// pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R5): a dispatch that\n     5\t// ends after reserving its attempt but before recording its run leaves a\n     6\t// reservation without a receipt. Every later dispatch of the bundle refuses\n     7\t// on it, and cancellation refused it because nothing runs. Once it is proven\n     8\t// abandoned, the attempt is closed by the same records a failed run writes:\n     9\t// a failed run naming the abandonment and its receipt. Nothing is deleted\n    10\t// from the ledger.\n    11\t//\n    12\t// Proof of abandonment: a marker that is stalled with its owner proven dead.\n    13\t// A reservation an earlier engine left without any marker (it reserved\n    14\t// before marking) records no owner, so nothing proves it abandoned: it is\n    15\t// listed once it is older than reviewOrphanReservationAge and has no\n    16\t// receipt or run, and released only on the operator's explicit confirmation,\n    17\t// which the recorded run states (review round 3, N2). One release runs at a\n    18\t// time per attempt under a lock the operating system releases when its\n    19\t// holder ends, so an interrupted release leaves nothing to take over (review\n    20\t// round 5, N1). A release is idempotent: it completes with a run the\n    21\t// attempt already recorded, whatever wrote it (N3), and with a receipt\n    22\t// already published it only removes the stalled marker (N2).\n    23\t\n    24\timport (\n    25\t\t\"errors\"\n    26\t\t\"fmt\"\n    27\t\t\"os\"\n    28\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    29\t\t\"strings\"\n    30\t\t\"time\"\n    31\t)\n    32\t\n    33\t// ErrAttemptNotAbandoned means the attempt is running, finished, or not\n    34\t// proven abandoned.\n    35\tvar ErrAttemptNotAbandoned = errors.New(\"pose: the attempt is not an abandoned reservation\")\n    36\t\n    37\t// reviewOrphanReservationAge is how old a reservation without any marker\n    38\t// must be to count as abandoned.\n    39\tconst reviewOrphanReservationAge = 10 * time.Minute\n    40\t\n    41\t// ReleaseAbandonedAttempt records the failed run of an attempt whose\n    42\t// dispatch ended before recording it, and removes its stalled marker. A\n    43\t// stalled marker whose reservation was never published is only removed; the\n    44\t// returned run is then empty.\n    45\tfunc (s Store) ReleaseAbandonedAttempt(attemptID string, now time.Time, operatorConfirmed bool) (ReviewRun, error) {\n    46\t\tif !validAttemptFileName(attemptID) {\n    47\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %q names no attempt\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned, attemptID)\n    48\t\t}\n    49\t\tmarkers, _, err := s.ListDelegationActive()\n    50\t\tif err != nil {\n    51\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    52\t\t}\n    53\t\tvar marker *DelegationActiveRun\n    54\t\tfor i := range markers {\n    55\t\t\tif markers[i].AttemptID == attemptID {\n    56\t\t\t\tmarker = &markers[i]\n    57\t\t\t}\n    58\t\t}\n    59\t\tif marker != nil && (marker.StalledAt == \"\" || marker.Liveness != LockOwnerDead) {\n    60\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: its owner is not proven gone\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned)\n    61\t\t}\n    62\t\tdir, err := s.delegationActiveDir(true)\n    63\t\tif err != nil {\n    64\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    65\t\t}\n    66\t\tlock, err := os.OpenFile(filepath.Join(dir, attemptID+\".release.lock\"), os.O_CREATE|os.O_RDWR, 0600)\n    67\t\tif err != nil {\n    68\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    69\t\t}\n    70\t\tdefer lock.Close()\n    71\t\tunlock, err := lockSpecTransferFile(lock)\n    72\t\tif err != nil {\n    73\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: another release of it is in progress\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned)\n    74\t\t}\n    75\t\tdefer unlock()\n    76\t\treturn s.releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed(attemptID, marker, now, operatorConfirmed)\n    77\t}\n    78\t\n    79\tfunc (s Store) releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed(attemptID string, marker *DelegationActiveRun, now time.Time, operatorConfirmed bool) (ReviewRun, error) {\n    80\t\tvar reserved *DelegatedReviewAttempt\n    81\t\tif marker != nil {\n    82\t\t\tattempts, err := s.readDelegatedReviewAttempts(marker.BundleID)\n    83\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    84\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    85\t\t\t}\n    86\t\t\tfor i := range attempts {\n    87\t\t\t\tif attempts[i].AttemptID == attemptID {\n    88\t\t\t\t\treserved = &attempts[i]\n    89\t\t\t\t}\n    90\t\t\t}\n    91\t\t\tif reserved == nil {\n    92\t\t\t\t// The dispatch ended between its marker and its reservation:\n    93\t\t\t\t// nothing blocks the bundle, and the marker alone is removed.\n    94\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, s.removeDelegationMarker(*marker)\n    95\t\t\t}\n    96\t\t} else {\n    97\t\t\tif !operatorConfirmed {\n    98\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: it has no marker, so nothing proves its dispatch ended; if no dispatch of it is running, confirm with --confirm-abandoned\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned)\n    99\t\t\t}\n   100\t\t\torphans, _, err := s.orphanReservations(now)\n   101\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   102\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n   103\t\t\t}\n   104\t\t\tfor i := range orphans {\n   105\t\t\t\tif orphans[i].AttemptID == attemptID {\n   106\t\t\t\t\treserved = &orphans[i]\n   107\t\t\t\t}\n   108\t\t\t}\n   109\t\t\tif reserved == nil {\n   110\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: no stalled marker and no reservation older than %s without a receipt\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned, reviewOrphanReservationAge)\n   111\t\t\t}\n   112\t\t}\n   113\t\tif _, err := os.Lstat(attemptReceiptPath(s.Root, *reserved)); err == nil {\n   114\t\t\t// A release that stopped after the receipt completes by removing\n   115\t\t\t// the stalled marker; with no marker there is nothing to release.\n   116\t\t\tif marker != nil {\n   117\t\t\t\treceipt, err := s.readAttemptReceipt(*reserved)\n   118\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   119\t\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n   120\t\t\t\t}\n   121\t\t\t\trun, err := s.LoadProvenanceReviewRun(receipt.RunID)\n   122\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   123\t\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n   124\t\t\t\t}\n   125\t\t\t\treturn run, s.removeDelegationMarker(*marker)\n   126\t\t\t}\n   127\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: it already has a receipt\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned)\n   128\t\t} else if !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   129\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"the receipt of %s cannot be inspected: %w\", attemptID, err)\n   130\t\t}\n   131\t\trun := ReviewRun{SchemaVersion: 1, Scope: reserved.Scope, BundleID: reserved.BundleID, BundleDigest: reserved.BundleDigest,\n   132\t\t\tKind: ReviewBriefKindReview, Adapter: reserved.Adapter, Reason: reserved.Reason, AttemptID: reserved.AttemptID,\n   133\t\t\tStartedAt: reserved.ReservedAt, ExitCode: -1, Purpose: DelegationPurposeReview,\n   134\t\t\tStatus: ReviewRunFailed, EndedAt: now.UTC().Format(time.RFC3339Nano)}\n   135\t\tif marker != nil {\n   136\t\t\trun.Kind, run.Purpose, run.Label, run.Round, run.StartedAt = DelegationKindForPurpose(marker.Purpose), marker.Purpose, marker.Label, marker.Round, marker.StartedAt\n   137\t\t\trun.Failure = DelegationAbandonedCause + \" (stalled at \" + marker.StalledAt + \"); released by pose delegate cancel\"\n   138\t\t} else {\n   139\t\t\trun.Failure = DelegationAbandonedCause + \" (reservation of \" + reserved.ReservedAt + \" with no marker, left by an earlier engine); released by pose delegate cancel on the operator's confirmation\"\n   140\t\t}\n   141\t\t// A run the attempt already recorded, by its dispatch or by a release\n   142\t\t// interrupted before the receipt, completes the attempt; no second run\n   143\t\t// is written for it.\n   144\t\trecorded, found, err := s.recordedAttemptRun(*reserved)\n   145\t\tif err != nil {\n   146\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n   147\t\t}\n   148\t\tif !found {\n   149\t\t\tif recorded, err = s.recordReviewRun(run, nil); err != nil {\n   150\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n   151\t\t\t}\n   152\t\t}\n   153\t\tif err := s.finishDelegatedReviewAttempt(*reserved, recorded); err != nil {\n   154\t\t\treturn recorded, err\n   155\t\t}\n   156\t\tif marker != nil {\n   157\t\t\treturn recorded, s.removeDelegationMarker(*marker)\n   158\t\t}\n   159\t\treturn recorded, nil\n   160\t}\n   161\t\n   162\t// recordedAttemptRun finds the latest run recorded for attempt a.\n   163\tfunc (s Store) recordedAttemptRun(a DelegatedReviewAttempt) (ReviewRun, bool, error) {\n   164\t\truns, lost, err := s.ReadReviewRuns(a.BundleID)\n   165\t\tif err != nil {\n   166\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, false, err\n   167\t\t}\n   168\t\tif len(lost) > 0 {\n   169\t\t\t// An unreadable run may be this release's: the history is unknown,\n   170\t\t\t// and the release does not write another (review round 4, N3).\n   171\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\"the run history of %s is incomplete, so an earlier release cannot be ruled out: %s\", a.BundleID, strings.Join(lost, \"; \"))\n   172\t\t}\n   173\t\tvar latest *ReviewRun\n   174\t\tfor i := range runs {\n   175\t\t\tif runs[i].AttemptID == a.AttemptID && (latest == nil || runs[i].EndedAt > latest.EndedAt) {\n   176\t\t\t\tlatest = &runs[i]\n   177\t\t\t}\n   178\t\t}\n   179\t\tif latest == nil {\n   180\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, false, nil\n   181\t\t}\n   182\t\treturn *latest, true, nil\n   183\t}\n   184\t\n   185\t// orphanReservations lists the reservations left without a receipt or a\n   186\t// marker, older than reviewOrphanReservationAge, and\n   187\t// says which reservations or receipts it could not read (review round 3, N3).\n   188\tfunc (s Store) orphanReservations(now time.Time) ([]DelegatedReviewAttempt, []string, error) {\n   189\t\tbase := filepath.Join(s.Root, reviewAttemptDir)\n   190\t\tdirs, err := os.ReadDir(base)\n   191\t\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   192\t\t\treturn nil, nil, nil\n   193\t\t}\n   194\t\tif err != nil {\n   195\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n   196\t\t}\n   197\t\tmarkers, markerLost, err := s.ListDelegationActive()\n   198\t\tif err != nil {\n   199\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n   200\t\t}\n   201\t\tif len(markerLost) > 0 {\n   202\t\t\t// An unreadable marker may be a live attempt's: nothing is known to\n   203\t\t\t// have no marker (review round 6, N1).\n   204\t\t\treturn nil, append([]string{\"abandoned reservations cannot be determined while an active marker is unreadable\"}, markerLost...), nil\n   205\t\t}\n   206\t\tmarked := map[string]bool{}\n   207\t\tfor _, m := range markers {\n   208\t\t\tmarked[m.AttemptID] = true\n   209\t\t}\n   210\t\truns, runLost, err := s.ReadReviewRuns(\"\")\n   211\t\tif err != nil {\n   212\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n   213\t\t}\n   214\t\tif len(runLost) > 0 {\n   215\t\t\t// Without the whole run history nothing is known to have no run.\n   216\t\t\treturn nil, append([]string{\"abandoned reservations cannot be determined while the run history is incomplete\"}, runLost...), nil\n   217\t\t}\n   218\t\t// A recorded run does not finish an attempt, its receipt does: a\n   219\t\t// reservation whose run was recorded without a receipt still blocks and\n   220\t\t// is released with that run (review round 5, N3).\n   221\t\t_ = runs\n   222\t\tvar out []DelegatedReviewAttempt\n   223\t\tvar lost []string\n   224\t\tbudget := reviewReadBudget(nil)\n   225\t\tfor _, d := range dirs {\n   226\t\t\tif !d.IsDir() {\n   227\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   228\t\t\t}\n   229\t\t\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(filepath.Join(base, d.Name()))\n   230\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   231\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"the reservations in \"+d.Name()+\" could not be listed: \"+err.Error())\n   232\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   233\t\t\t}\n   234\t\t\tfor _, e := range entries {\n   235\t\t\t\tif IsPublisherStaging(e.Name()) || !strings.HasSuffix(e.Name(), \".json\") || strings.HasSuffix(e.Name(), \".result.json\") {\n   236\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   237\t\t\t\t}\n   238\t\t\t\tvar a DelegatedReviewAttempt\n   239\t\t\t\tif err := readLedgerJSONBudgetIn(s.fsys(), filepath.Join(base, d.Name(), e.Name()), &a, budget); err != nil {\n   240\t\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"the reservation \"+d.Name()+\"/\"+e.Name()+\" could not be read: \"+err.Error())\n   241\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   242\t\t\t\t}\n   243\t\t\t\tif a.AttemptID != attemptIdentity(a) {\n   244\t\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"the reservation \"+d.Name()+\"/\"+e.Name()+\" does not match its identity\")\n   245\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   246\t\t\t\t}\n   247\t\t\t\tif marked[a.AttemptID] {\n   248\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   249\t\t\t\t}\n   250\t\t\t\tif _, err := os.Lstat(attemptReceiptPath(s.Root, a)); err == nil {\n   251\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   252\t\t\t\t} else if !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   253\t\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"the receipt of \"+a.AttemptID+\" could not be inspected: \"+err.Error())\n   254\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   255\t\t\t\t}\n   256\t\t\t\tat, err := time.Parse(time.RFC3339Nano, a.ReservedAt)\n   257\t\t\t\tif err != nil || now.Sub(at) < reviewOrphanReservationAge {\n   258\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   259\t\t\t\t}\n   260\t\t\t\tout = append(out, a)\n   261\t\t\t}\n   262\t\t}\n   263\t\treturn out, lost, nil\n   264\t}\n   265\t\n   266\tfunc (s Store) removeDelegationMarker(marker DelegationActiveRun) error {\n   267\t\tdir, err := s.delegationActiveDir(false)\n   268\t\tif err != nil {\n   269\t\t\treturn err\n   270\t\t}\n   271\t\tfor _, p := range []string{filepath.Join(dir, marker.AttemptID+\".json\"), stallClaimPath(dir, marker), cancelRequestPath(dir, marker)} {\n   272\t\t\tif err := os.Remove(p); err != nil && !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   273\t\t\t\treturn err\n   274\t\t\t}\n   275\t\t}\n   276\t\treturn nil\n   277\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go | sed -n '1,250p' && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t//go:build linux\n     2\t\n     3\tpackage pose\n     4\t\n     5\t// Leftover reviewer processes (spec\n     6\t// pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R1): an adapter such as\n     7\t// `codex exec` runs each command in a session of its own, so killing the\n     8\t// adapter's process group misses a command the reviewer left running, and\n     9\t// that command keeps writing into the run's runtime directory while the\n    10\t// cleanup inventory reads it. Every process of the run inherits\n    11\t// SealedCheckoutEnv naming the run's checkout, so the dispatch finds them by\n    12\t// that entry, ends them and waits for them before the inventory.\n    13\t//\n    14\t// Each process is pinned by a pidfd before it is signalled, and its\n    15\t// environment is read again through the pinned process, so a pid reused by\n    16\t// an unrelated process between the scan and the signal is never killed\n    17\t// (review round 1, N3). A scan that cannot list or read the state of the\n    18\t// processes fails. A process of this user whose environment cannot be read\n    19\t// (one that made itself non-inspectable) cannot be matched: one that already\n    20\t// existed before the adapter started is not the run's and is skipped; any\n    21\t// other may be the run's, so the scan fails and the run stays unconcludable\n    22\t// (review round 2, N2).\n    23\t\n    24\timport (\n    25\t\t\"bytes\"\n    26\t\t\"errors\"\n    27\t\t\"fmt\"\n    28\t\t\"io/fs\"\n    29\t\t\"os\"\n    30\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    31\t\t\"strconv\"\n    32\t\t\"strings\"\n    33\t\t\"syscall\"\n    34\t\t\"time\"\n    35\t\n    36\t\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n    37\t)\n    38\t\n    39\t// reapSealedCheckoutProcesses ends every process whose environment names\n    40\t// worktree as its sealed checkout and returns a description of each. An\n    41\t// error means the run's processes could not be proven ended within the bound.\n    42\tfunc reapSealedCheckoutProcesses(worktree string, baseline map[int]string) ([]string, int, error) {\n    43\t\tif worktree == \"\" {\n    44\t\t\treturn nil, 0, nil\n    45\t\t}\n    46\t\tentry := []byte(SealedCheckoutEnv + \"=\" + worktree)\n    47\t\tvar reaped []string\n    48\t\tseen := map[int]bool{}\n    49\t\tdeadline := time.Now().Add(reviewReapWait)\n    50\t\tunreadable := 0\n    51\t\tfor {\n    52\t\t\talive, opaque, err := reviewMarkedProcesses(entry)\n    53\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    54\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, err\n    55\t\t\t}\n    56\t\t\tunreadable = 0\n    57\t\t\tfor pid, start := range opaque {\n    58\t\t\t\tif prior, ok := baseline[pid]; !ok || prior != start {\n    59\t\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d of this user started during the run and cannot be inspected; it may be the run's and was not ended\", pid)\n    60\t\t\t\t}\n    61\t\t\t\tunreadable++\n    62\t\t\t}\n    63\t\t\tfor _, pid := range alive {\n    64\t\t\t\tif !seen[pid] {\n    65\t\t\t\t\tseen[pid] = true\n    66\t\t\t\t\t// Only the pid: the name is the reviewer's to choose and is not\n    67\t\t\t\t\t// recorded (review round 7, N4).\n    68\t\t\t\t\treaped = append(reaped, strconv.Itoa(pid))\n    69\t\t\t\t}\n    70\t\t\t\tif err := killPinnedMarkedProcess(pid, entry); err != nil {\n    71\t\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, err\n    72\t\t\t\t}\n    73\t\t\t}\n    74\t\t\tif len(alive) == 0 {\n    75\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, nil\n    76\t\t\t}\n    77\t\t\tif time.Now().After(deadline) {\n    78\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"%d process(es) of the run could not be ended\", len(alive))\n    79\t\t\t}\n    80\t\t\ttime.Sleep(50 * time.Millisecond)\n    81\t\t}\n    82\t}\n    83\t\n    84\t// reviewMarkedProcesses lists the live processes whose environment holds\n    85\t// entry, and counts this user's processes whose environment could not be\n    86\t// read. A process that is gone is skipped.\n    87\tfunc reviewMarkedProcesses(entry []byte) ([]int, map[int]string, error) {\n    88\t\tdirs, err := os.ReadDir(\"/proc\")\n    89\t\tif err != nil {\n    90\t\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"the run's processes could not be listed: %w\", err)\n    91\t\t}\n    92\t\tunreadable := map[int]string{}\n    93\t\tself, uid := os.Getpid(), os.Getuid()\n    94\t\tvar out []int\n    95\t\tfor _, d := range dirs {\n    96\t\t\tpid, err := strconv.Atoi(d.Name())\n    97\t\t\tif err != nil || pid == self {\n    98\t\t\t\tcontinue\n    99\t\t\t}\n   100\t\t\tmarked, err := reviewProcessMarked(pid, entry)\n   101\t\t\tswitch {\n   102\t\t\tcase reviewProcessGoneErr(err):\n   103\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   104\t\t\tcase err != nil:\n   105\t\t\t\tif owner, oerr := reviewProcessOwner(pid); oerr == nil && owner != uid {\n   106\t\t\t\t\tcontinue // another user's process never inherits this run's environment\n   107\t\t\t\t} else if reviewProcessGoneErr(oerr) {\n   108\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   109\t\t\t\t}\n   110\t\t\t\tstart, serr := processStartTime(pid)\n   111\t\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(serr) {\n   112\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   113\t\t\t\t}\n   114\t\t\t\tif serr != nil || start == \"\" {\n   115\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d start could not be read: %v\", pid, serr)\n   116\t\t\t\t}\n   117\t\t\t\tunreadable[pid] = start\n   118\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   119\t\t\tcase !marked:\n   120\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   121\t\t\t}\n   122\t\t\tzombie, err := reviewProcessZombie(pid)\n   123\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) || err == nil && zombie {\n   124\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   125\t\t\t}\n   126\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   127\t\t\t\treturn nil, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d state could not be read: %w\", pid, err)\n   128\t\t\t}\n   129\t\t\tout = append(out, pid)\n   130\t\t}\n   131\t\treturn out, unreadable, nil\n   132\t}\n   133\t\n   134\t// killPinnedMarkedProcess signals pid only through a pidfd opened on it,\n   135\t// after the environment read through that same pinned process still holds\n   136\t// entry.\n   137\tfunc killPinnedMarkedProcess(pid int, entry []byte) error {\n   138\t\tfd, err := unix.PidfdOpen(pid, 0)\n   139\t\tif errors.Is(err, unix.ESRCH) {\n   140\t\t\treturn nil\n   141\t\t}\n   142\t\tif err != nil {\n   143\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be pinned: %w\", pid, err)\n   144\t\t}\n   145\t\tdefer unix.Close(fd)\n   146\t\t// The pidfd names one process for its lifetime; if pid was reused before\n   147\t\t// it was opened, the new process does not carry this run's entry.\n   148\t\tmarked, err := reviewProcessMarked(pid, entry)\n   149\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) || err == nil && !marked {\n   150\t\t\treturn nil\n   151\t\t}\n   152\t\tif err != nil {\n   153\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be inspected: %w\", pid, err)\n   154\t\t}\n   155\t\tif err := unix.PidfdSendSignal(fd, unix.SIGKILL, nil, 0); err != nil && !errors.Is(err, unix.ESRCH) {\n   156\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be ended: %w\", pid, err)\n   157\t\t}\n   158\t\treturn nil\n   159\t}\n   160\t\n   161\tfunc reviewProcessMarked(pid int, entry []byte) (bool, error) {\n   162\t\tenviron, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid), \"environ\"))\n   163\t\tif err != nil {\n   164\t\t\treturn false, err\n   165\t\t}\n   166\t\tfor _, kv := range bytes.Split(environ, []byte{0}) {\n   167\t\t\tif bytes.Equal(kv, entry) {\n   168\t\t\t\treturn true, nil\n   169\t\t\t}\n   170\t\t}\n   171\t\treturn false, nil\n   172\t}\n   173\t\n   174\tfunc reviewProcessOwner(pid int) (int, error) {\n   175\t\tinfo, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid)))\n   176\t\tif err != nil {\n   177\t\t\treturn 0, err\n   178\t\t}\n   179\t\tst, ok := info.Sys().(*syscall.Stat_t)\n   180\t\tif !ok {\n   181\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d owner unavailable\", pid)\n   182\t\t}\n   183\t\treturn int(st.Uid), nil\n   184\t}\n   185\t\n   186\tfunc reviewProcessGoneErr(err error) bool {\n   187\t\treturn errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) || errors.Is(err, syscall.ESRCH)\n   188\t}\n   189\t\n   190\tfunc reviewProcessName(pid int) string {\n   191\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid), \"comm\"))\n   192\t\tif err != nil {\n   193\t\t\treturn \"?\"\n   194\t\t}\n   195\t\treturn strings.TrimSpace(string(raw))\n   196\t}\n   197\t\n   198\tfunc reviewProcessZombie(pid int) (bool, error) {\n   199\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid), \"stat\"))\n   200\t\tif err != nil {\n   201\t\t\treturn false, err\n   202\t\t}\n   203\t\t// The state follows the parenthesised command name.\n   204\t\tif i := bytes.LastIndexByte(raw, ')'); i >= 0 && i+2 < len(raw) {\n   205\t\t\treturn raw[i+2] == 'Z', nil\n   206\t\t}\n   207\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d state is unreadable\", pid)\n   208\t}\n   209\t\n   210\t// reviewOpaqueProcessBaseline records, before the adapter starts, the\n   211\t// processes of this user whose environment cannot be read, by pid and start\n   212\t// time: they cannot be the run's.\n   213\tfunc reviewOpaqueProcessBaseline() map[int]string {\n   214\t\t_, opaque, _ := reviewMarkedProcesses([]byte(SealedCheckoutEnv + \"=\\x00\"))\n   215\t\treturn opaque\n   216\t}\n     1\t//go:build !linux\n     2\t\n     3\tpackage pose\n     4\t\n     5\timport \"os/exec\"\n     6\t\n     7\t// reapSealedCheckoutProcesses has no portable way to read another process's\n     8\t// environment; outside Linux the process-group kill is the only termination.\n     9\tfunc reapSealedCheckoutProcesses(string, map[int]string) ([]string, int, error) { return nil, 0, nil }\n    10\t\n    11\tfunc reviewOpaqueProcessBaseline() map[int]string { return nil }\n    12\t\n    13\t// RunReviewShim is the Linux review run shim; elsewhere it is not used.\n    14\tfunc RunReviewShim(args []string) int { return 125 }\n    15\t\n    16\tfunc parseReviewShimReport([]byte) (reviewShimReport, error) { return reviewShimReport{}, nil }\n    17\t\n    18\tfunc stopReviewShim(cmd *exec.Cmd) func() error { return cmd.Cancel }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go | sed -n '1,230p' && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go | sed -n '1,280p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tpackage pose\n     2\t\n     3\t// Listing and naming delegated runs (spec pose-delegation-surface R11, and the\n     4\t// listing pose-delegated-review-completion-signal extends).\n     5\t//\n     6\t// A person and an agent follow a task, not a process: an attempt and its\n     7\t// continuations are one row, shown by their latest run. A reference names a\n     8\t// row by attempt, by any of its runs, by label or by a prefix of its session.\n     9\t\n    10\timport (\n    11\t\t\"fmt\"\n    12\t\t\"sort\"\n    13\t\t\"strings\"\n    14\t\t\"time\"\n    15\t)\n    16\t\n    17\t// DelegationAttempt is one attempt and its continuations.\n    18\ttype DelegationAttempt struct {\n    19\t\tAttemptID    string              `json:\"attempt_id\"`\n    20\t\tRuns         []string            `json:\"runs\"`\n    21\t\tLatestRun    string              `json:\"latest_run,omitempty\"`\n    22\t\tState        string              `json:\"state\"`\n    23\t\tPurpose      string              `json:\"purpose\"`\n    24\t\tAgent        string              `json:\"agent\"`\n    25\t\tVendor       string              `json:\"vendor,omitempty\"`\n    26\t\tModel        string              `json:\"model,omitempty\"`\n    27\t\tLabel        string              `json:\"label,omitempty\"`\n    28\t\tLead         string              `json:\"lead,omitempty\"`\n    29\t\tAccess       string              `json:\"access\"`\n    30\t\tScope        string              `json:\"scope\"`\n    31\t\tBundleID     string              `json:\"bundle_id\"`\n    32\t\tStartedAt    string              `json:\"started_at\"`\n    33\t\tEndedAt      string              `json:\"ended_at,omitempty\"`\n    34\t\tTurns        int                 `json:\"turns\"`\n    35\t\tLastStep     string              `json:\"last_step,omitempty\"`\n    36\t\tFailure      string              `json:\"failure,omitempty\"`\n    37\t\tInterruption *ReviewInterruption `json:\"interruption,omitempty\"`\n    38\t\t// Partial says an interrupted run kept a partial draft; TimeLeft is the\n    39\t\t// wait until its recorded reset, when there is one.\n    40\t\tPartial         bool   `json:\"partial,omitempty\"`\n    41\t\tTimeLeft        string `json:\"time_left,omitempty\"`\n    42\t\tActive          bool   `json:\"active\"`\n    43\t\tLiveness        string `json:\"liveness,omitempty\"`\n    44\t\tCancelRequested bool   `json:\"cancel_requested,omitempty\"`\n    45\t\t// HeartbeatAge is how long ago the running process last beat; a stalled\n    46\t\t// run is not active (spec pose-delegated-review-completion-signal R4, R6).\n    47\t\tHeartbeatAge string `json:\"heartbeat_age,omitempty\"`\n    48\t\tStalledAt    string `json:\"stalled_at,omitempty\"`\n    49\t\t// HookFailure is why the latest run's on_terminal hook failed (R7).\n    50\t\tHookFailure string `json:\"hook_failure,omitempty\"`\n    51\t\t// Round is the review round of the scope the latest run reviewed (spec\n    52\t\t// pose-delegated-review-round-protocol R1).\n    53\t\tRound    int `json:\"round,omitempty\"`\n    54\t\tsessions []string\n    55\t\tlatest   *ReviewRun\n    56\t}\n    57\t\n    58\t// Latest is the latest recorded run of the attempt, if any.\n    59\tfunc (a DelegationAttempt) Latest() *ReviewRun { return a.latest }\n    60\t\n    61\t// DelegationRunning is the state of an attempt whose process is still there;\n    62\t// DelegationStalled, of one whose process is gone without a record.\n    63\tconst (\n    64\t\tDelegationRunning = \"running\"\n    65\t\tDelegationStalled = \"stalled\"\n    66\t\t// DelegationAbandonedCause is the failure of a stalled attempt whose\n    67\t\t// dispatch ended before recording its run.\n    68\t\tDelegationAbandonedCause = \"abandoned: the dispatching process ended before the run was recorded\"\n    69\t)\n    70\t\n    71\t// ListDelegationAttempts groups every recorded run by attempt, adds the runs\n    72\t// in progress, and returns the losses the run history reports.\n    73\tfunc (s Store) ListDelegationAttempts() ([]DelegationAttempt, []string, error) {\n    74\t\t// The markers are read before the runs: a run publishes its record before\n    75\t\t// it removes its marker, so a reader that finds no marker for an attempt\n    76\t\t// it saw running finds its record (spec\n    77\t\t// pose-delegated-review-completion-signal R5).\n    78\t\tactive, activeLost, activeErr := s.ListDelegationActive()\n    79\t\truns, lost, err := s.ReadReviewRuns(\"\")\n    80\t\tif err != nil {\n    81\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n    82\t\t}\n    83\t\t// Task runs share the lifecycle, never the review history (spec\n    84\t\t// pose-delegation-task R7, R8).\n    85\t\ttasks, taskLost := s.ReadDelegationTaskRuns()\n    86\t\truns, lost = append(runs, tasks...), append(lost, taskLost...)\n    87\t\tbyAttempt := map[string]*DelegationAttempt{}\n    88\t\torder := []string{}\n    89\t\tfor i := range runs {\n    90\t\t\trun := runs[i]\n    91\t\t\tkey := run.AttemptID\n    92\t\t\tif key == \"\" {\n    93\t\t\t\tkey = run.RunID // a run recorded before attempts existed is its own attempt\n    94\t\t\t}\n    95\t\t\trow, ok := byAttempt[key]\n    96\t\t\tif !ok {\n    97\t\t\t\trow = &DelegationAttempt{AttemptID: key, StartedAt: run.StartedAt}\n    98\t\t\t\tbyAttempt[key] = row\n    99\t\t\t\torder = append(order, key)\n   100\t\t\t}\n   101\t\t\trow.Runs = append(row.Runs, run.RunID)\n   102\t\t\trow.latest = &runs[i]\n   103\t\t\tif run.SessionDigest != \"\" {\n   104\t\t\t\tif value, err := s.readReviewSession(run.SessionDigest); err == nil {\n   105\t\t\t\t\trow.sessions = append(row.sessions, value)\n   106\t\t\t\t}\n   107\t\t\t}\n   108\t\t\tevents, err := s.ReadDelegationEvents(run)\n   109\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   110\t\t\t\t// A turn count read from nothing would report a whole history.\n   111\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"the events of run \"+run.RunID+\" could not be read: \"+err.Error())\n   112\t\t\t} else {\n   113\t\t\t\tfor _, e := range events {\n   114\t\t\t\t\tif e.Kind == DelegationEventTurn {\n   115\t\t\t\t\t\trow.Turns++\n   116\t\t\t\t\t}\n   117\t\t\t\t}\n   118\t\t\t\tif len(events) > 0 {\n   119\t\t\t\t\trow.LastStep = delegationStepText(events[len(events)-1])\n   120\t\t\t\t}\n   121\t\t\t}\n   122\t\t}\n   123\t\tfor _, key := range order {\n   124\t\t\trow := byAttempt[key]\n   125\t\t\tlatest := row.latest\n   126\t\t\trow.LatestRun, row.State, row.Agent, row.Vendor, row.Model = latest.RunID, latest.Status, latest.Adapter, latest.Vendor, latest.Model\n   127\t\t\trow.Label, row.Scope, row.BundleID, row.EndedAt, row.Failure, row.Interruption = latest.Label, latest.Scope, latest.BundleID, latest.EndedAt, latest.Failure, latest.Interruption\n   128\t\t\trow.Purpose, row.Lead, row.Access = latest.Purpose, latest.Lead, DelegationAccessRead\n   129\t\t\tif latest.Access != \"\" {\n   130\t\t\t\trow.Access = latest.Access\n   131\t\t\t}\n   132\t\t\trow.Round = latest.Round\n   133\t\t\tif hook := s.ReadDelegationHook(latest.RunID); hook != nil {\n   134\t\t\t\trow.HookFailure = hook.Failure\n   135\t\t\t}\n   136\t\t\tif row.Purpose == \"\" {\n   137\t\t\t\trow.Purpose = DelegationPurposeForKind(latest.Kind)\n   138\t\t\t}\n   139\t\t\tif latest.Status == ReviewRunInterrupted {\n   140\t\t\t\trow.Partial = strings.TrimSpace(latest.Output) != \"\"\n   141\t\t\t\tif latest.Interruption != nil && latest.Interruption.ResetAt != \"\" {\n   142\t\t\t\t\tif at, err := time.Parse(time.RFC3339Nano, latest.Interruption.ResetAt); err == nil {\n   143\t\t\t\t\t\tleft := time.Until(at)\n   144\t\t\t\t\t\tif left < 0 {\n   145\t\t\t\t\t\t\tleft = 0\n   146\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n   147\t\t\t\t\t\trow.TimeLeft = left.Round(time.Second).String()\n   148\t\t\t\t\t}\n   149\t\t\t\t}\n   150\t\t\t}\n   151\t\t}\n   152\t\tif activeErr != nil {\n   153\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"active runs could not be read: \"+activeErr.Error())\n   154\t\t}\n   155\t\tlost = append(lost, activeLost...)\n   156\t\tfor _, marker := range active {\n   157\t\t\trow, ok := byAttempt[marker.AttemptID]\n   158\t\t\tif !ok {\n   159\t\t\t\trow = &DelegationAttempt{AttemptID: marker.AttemptID, Runs: []string{}, StartedAt: marker.StartedAt, Purpose: marker.Purpose, Access: DelegationAccessRead, Agent: marker.Agent, Label: marker.Label, Scope: marker.Scope, BundleID: marker.BundleID}\n   160\t\t\t\tbyAttempt[marker.AttemptID] = row\n   161\t\t\t\torder = append(order, marker.AttemptID)\n   162\t\t\t}\n   163\t\t\trow.State, row.Active, row.Liveness, row.CancelRequested = DelegationRunning, true, marker.Liveness, marker.CancelRequested\n   164\t\t\tif marker.Round > 0 {\n   165\t\t\t\trow.Round = marker.Round\n   166\t\t\t}\n   167\t\t\trow.EndedAt, row.Failure, row.Interruption, row.Partial, row.TimeLeft = \"\", \"\", nil, false, \"\"\n   168\t\t\tif beat, err := time.Parse(time.RFC3339Nano, marker.HeartbeatAt); err == nil {\n   169\t\t\t\trow.HeartbeatAge = time.Since(beat).Round(time.Second).String()\n   170\t\t\t}\n   171\t\t\tif marker.StalledAt != \"\" {\n   172\t\t\t\trow.State, row.Active, row.StalledAt = DelegationStalled, false, marker.StalledAt\n   173\t\t\t\tif row.LatestRun == \"\" {\n   174\t\t\t\t\t// The dispatch ended before recording its run: the cause and\n   175\t\t\t\t\t// the release are said, not left to inspection (review round\n   176\t\t\t\t\t// 1, N2).\n   177\t\t\t\t\trow.Failure = DelegationAbandonedCause + \"; release it with `pose delegate cancel \" + marker.AttemptID + \"`\"\n   178\t\t\t\t}\n   179\t\t\t}\n   180\t\t\t// A running run's progress comes from its live events (R12).\n   181\t\t\tif live, _, err := s.ReadDelegationLiveEvents(marker.AttemptID, 0); err == nil && len(live) > 0 {\n   182\t\t\t\tfor _, e := range live {\n   183\t\t\t\t\tif e.Kind == DelegationEventTurn {\n   184\t\t\t\t\t\trow.Turns++\n   185\t\t\t\t\t}\n   186\t\t\t\t}\n   187\t\t\t\trow.LastStep = delegationStepText(live[len(live)-1])\n   188\t\t\t}\n   189\t\t}\n   190\t\t// A reservation an earlier engine left without a marker or a run is\n   191\t\t// listed too, so it can be named and released (review round 2, N1).\n   192\t\tif orphans, orphanLost, err := s.orphanReservations(time.Now()); err != nil {\n   193\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"abandoned reservations could not be read: \"+err.Error())\n   194\t\t} else {\n   195\t\t\tlost = append(lost, orphanLost...)\n   196\t\t\tfor _, a := range orphans {\n   197\t\t\t\tif _, ok := byAttempt[a.AttemptID]; ok {\n   198\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   199\t\t\t\t}\n   200\t\t\t\tbyAttempt[a.AttemptID] = &DelegationAttempt{AttemptID: a.AttemptID, Runs: []string{}, StartedAt: a.ReservedAt, Purpose: DelegationPurposeReview, Access: DelegationAccessRead, Agent: a.Adapter, Scope: a.Scope, BundleID: a.BundleID,\n   201\t\t\t\t\tState: DelegationStalled, StalledAt: a.ReservedAt, Failure: \"no owner record: an earlier engine reserved it without a marker, so nothing proves its dispatch ended; if none is running, release it with `pose delegate cancel \" + a.AttemptID + \" --confirm-abandoned`\"}\n   202\t\t\t\torder = append(order, a.AttemptID)\n   203\t\t\t}\n   204\t\t}\n   205\t\tout := make([]DelegationAttempt, 0, len(order))\n   206\t\tfor _, key := range order {\n   207\t\t\tout = append(out, *byAttempt[key])\n   208\t\t}\n   209\t\tsort.SliceStable(out, func(i, j int) bool { return out[i].StartedAt < out[j].StartedAt })\n   210\t\treturn out, lost, nil\n   211\t}\n   212\t\n   213\tfunc delegationStepText(e DelegationEvent) string {\n   214\t\ttext := strings.Join(strings.Fields(e.Text), \" \")\n   215\t\tif len(text) > 80 {\n   216\t\t\tcut := 77\n   217\t\t\tfor cut > 0 && !utf8RuneStart(text[cut]) {\n   218\t\t\t\tcut--\n   219\t\t\t}\n   220\t\t\ttext = text[:cut] + \"...\"\n   221\t\t}\n   222\t\tswitch e.Kind {\n   223\t\tcase DelegationEventToolCall:\n   224\t\t\treturn \"▶ \" + text\n   225\t\tcase DelegationEventToolOutput:\n   226\t\t\tif e.ExitCode != nil && *e.ExitCode != 0 {\n   227\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"✗ exit %d\", *e.ExitCode)\n   228\t\t\t}\n   229\t\t\treturn \"✓ exit 0\"\n   230\t\tcase DelegationEventTurn:\n     1\tpackage cli\n     2\t\n     3\t// pose delegate: the one surface for delegated executions (spec\n     4\t// pose-delegation-surface; ADR 2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface).\n     5\t//\n     6\t// pose review governs the subject (bundle, brief, attestation, verify);\n     7\t// pose delegate governs executions: who runs, with which access, and what\n     8\t// happened. review, adjudicate and smoke run through the delivered dispatch\n     9\t// path; the lifecycle commands read the same run records.\n    10\t//\n    11\t// Every subcommand takes the common flags with one meaning (R2): where a\n    12\t// command starts a run they set it (--agent, --access, --label, --lead);\n    13\t// where it names or lists runs they select them, and a run that does not\n    14\t// match is not the one named; --dry-run changes nothing anywhere.\n    15\t\n    16\timport (\n    17\t\t\"context\"\n    18\t\t\"crypto/rand\"\n    19\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n    20\t\t\"errors\"\n    21\t\t\"fmt\"\n    22\t\t\"io\"\n    23\t\t\"os\"\n    24\t\t\"os/signal\"\n    25\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    26\t\t\"regexp\"\n    27\t\t\"sort\"\n    28\t\t\"strconv\"\n    29\t\t\"strings\"\n    30\t\t\"syscall\"\n    31\t\t\"time\"\n    32\t\n    33\t\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n    34\t)\n    35\t\n    36\tconst delegateUsageText = \"pose delegate <review|adjudicate|smoke|task|ls|watch|wait|resume|handoff|cancel|agents> [args] [--agent auto|<name>] [--access read|sandboxed|write|full] [--label <name>] [--lead <vendor>] [--dry-run] [--json]\"\n    37\t\n    38\t// Versioned JSON documents of pose delegate (R10).\n    39\tconst (\n    40\t\tdelegateRunSchema    = \"pose.delegate.run/v1\"\n    41\t\tdelegatePlanSchema   = \"pose.delegate.plan/v1\"\n    42\t\tdelegateListSchema   = \"pose.delegate.ls/v1\"\n    43\t\tdelegateCancelSchema = \"pose.delegate.cancel/v1\"\n    44\t\tdelegateAgentsSchema = \"pose.delegate.agents/v1\"\n    45\t\tdelegateErrorSchema  = \"pose.delegate.error/v1\"\n    46\t)\n    47\t\n    48\t// Subcommands named by the ADR whose behaviour a later spec delivers.\n    49\tvar delegatePlanned = map[string]string{}\n    50\t\n    51\tvar (\n    52\t\tdelegateLabelRE = regexp.MustCompile(`^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$`)\n    53\t)\n    54\t\n    55\t// commonDelegateFlags are taken by every subcommand.\n    56\tvar commonDelegateFlags = []string{\"--agent\", \"--access\", \"--label\", \"--lead\", \"--dry-run\", \"--json\"}\n    57\t\n    58\t// tr picks the message for the session's locale.\n    59\tfunc tr(english, portuguese string) string { return cliText(cliLocaleValue(), english, portuguese) }\n    60\t\n    61\ttype delegateFlags struct {\n    62\t\tagent, access, label, lead, reason, noteFile string\n    63\t\trequest                                      string\n    64\t\tto, cd, effort, promptFile, session          string\n    65\t\taddDirs                                      []string\n    66\t\tnoNetwork, record, confirmAbandoned          bool\n    67\t\tdryRun, jsonOut, active, wait, detach        bool\n    68\t\tverbose, noFollow                            bool\n    69\t\tlines                                        int\n    70\t\twaitMax, timeout, refresh                    time.Duration\n    71\t\tpositional                                   []string\n    72\t}\n    73\t\n    74\t// parseDelegateFlags reads the common flags and the extra ones a subcommand\n    75\t// takes; problem is a message for the person, in their locale.\n    76\tfunc parseDelegateFlags(args []string, extra ...string) (delegateFlags, string) {\n    77\t\tf := delegateFlags{waitMax: 24 * time.Hour}\n    78\t\tpermit := map[string]bool{}\n    79\t\tfor _, name := range append(append([]string(nil), commonDelegateFlags...), extra...) {\n    80\t\t\tpermit[name] = true\n    81\t\t}\n    82\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(args); i++ {\n    83\t\t\targ := args[i]\n    84\t\t\tname, inline, hasInline := strings.Cut(arg, \"=\")\n    85\t\t\t// A lone - names stdin (spec pose-delegation-task R1).\n    86\t\t\tif arg == \"-\" || !strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") {\n    87\t\t\t\tf.positional = append(f.positional, arg)\n    88\t\t\t\tcontinue\n    89\t\t\t}\n    90\t\t\tif !permit[name] {\n    91\t\t\t\treturn f, tr(\"unknown or inapplicable flag \"+name, \"flag desconhecida ou inaplicável \"+name)\n    92\t\t\t}\n    93\t\t\tswitch name {\n    94\t\t\tcase \"--dry-run\", \"--json\", \"--active\", \"--detach\", \"-v\", \"--no-follow\", \"--no-network\", \"--record\", \"--confirm-abandoned\":\n    95\t\t\t\tif hasInline {\n    96\t\t\t\t\treturn f, tr(name+\" takes no value\", name+\" não recebe valor\")\n    97\t\t\t\t}\n    98\t\t\t\tswitch name {\n    99\t\t\t\tcase \"--dry-run\":\n   100\t\t\t\t\tf.dryRun = true\n   101\t\t\t\tcase \"--json\":\n   102\t\t\t\t\tf.jsonOut = true\n   103\t\t\t\tcase \"--detach\":\n   104\t\t\t\t\tf.detach = true\n   105\t\t\t\tcase \"-v\":\n   106\t\t\t\t\tf.verbose = true\n   107\t\t\t\tcase \"--no-network\":\n   108\t\t\t\t\tf.noNetwork = true\n   109\t\t\t\tcase \"--record\":\n   110\t\t\t\t\tf.record = true\n   111\t\t\t\tcase \"--confirm-abandoned\":\n   112\t\t\t\t\tf.confirmAbandoned = true\n   113\t\t\t\tcase \"--no-follow\":\n   114\t\t\t\t\tf.noFollow = true\n   115\t\t\t\tdefault:\n   116\t\t\t\t\tf.active = true\n   117\t\t\t\t}\n   118\t\t\tcase \"--wait-until-reset\":\n   119\t\t\t\tf.wait = true\n   120\t\t\t\tif hasInline {\n   121\t\t\t\t\td, err := time.ParseDuration(inline)\n   122\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil || d <= 0 || d > 24*time.Hour {\n   123\t\t\t\t\t\treturn f, tr(\"--wait-until-reset takes a duration up to 24h\", \"--wait-until-reset recebe uma duração de até 24h\")\n   124\t\t\t\t\t}\n   125\t\t\t\t\tf.waitMax = d\n   126\t\t\t\t}\n   127\t\t\tdefault:\n   128\t\t\t\tvalue := inline\n   129\t\t\t\tif !hasInline {\n   130\t\t\t\t\t// --prompt - reads stdin (spec pose-delegation-task R8).\n   131\t\t\t\t\tif i+1 >= len(args) || strings.HasPrefix(args[i+1], \"-\") && !(name == \"--prompt\" && args[i+1] == \"-\") {\n   132\t\t\t\t\t\treturn f, tr(name+\" needs a value\", name+\" precisa de um valor\")\n   133\t\t\t\t\t}\n   134\t\t\t\t\tvalue = args[i+1]\n   135\t\t\t\t\ti++\n   136\t\t\t\t}\n   137\t\t\t\tswitch name {\n   138\t\t\t\tcase \"--agent\":\n   139\t\t\t\t\tf.agent = value\n   140\t\t\t\tcase \"--access\":\n   141\t\t\t\t\tif !containsString([]string{posemodel.DelegationAccessRead, posemodel.DelegationAccessSandboxed, posemodel.DelegationAccessWrite, posemodel.DelegationAccessFull}, value) {\n   142\t\t\t\t\t\treturn f, tr(\"--access takes read, sandboxed, write or full\", \"--access recebe read, sandboxed, write ou full\")\n   143\t\t\t\t\t}\n   144\t\t\t\t\tf.access = value\n   145\t\t\t\tcase \"--label\":\n   146\t\t\t\t\tif !delegateLabelRE.MatchString(value) {\n   147\t\t\t\t\t\treturn f, tr(\"--label takes letters, digits, '.', '_' and '-' (64 at most)\", \"--label aceita letras, dígitos, '.', '_' e '-' (no máximo 64)\")\n   148\t\t\t\t\t}\n   149\t\t\t\t\tf.label = value\n   150\t\t\t\tcase \"--lead\":\n   151\t\t\t\t\tvendor, model, err := posemodel.ParseLead(value)\n   152\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   153\t\t\t\t\t\treturn f, tr(\"--lead takes <vendor>[/<model>], such as openai or anthropic/claude-opus-5-5\", \"--lead recebe <vendor>[/<modelo>], como openai ou anthropic/claude-opus-5-5\")\n   154\t\t\t\t\t}\n   155\t\t\t\t\tf.lead = vendor\n   156\t\t\t\t\tif model != \"\" {\n   157\t\t\t\t\t\tf.lead += \"/\" + model\n   158\t\t\t\t\t}\n   159\t\t\t\tcase \"--reason\":\n   160\t\t\t\t\tf.reason = value\n   161\t\t\t\tcase \"--session\":\n   162\t\t\t\t\tf.session = value\n   163\t\t\t\tcase \"--request\":\n   164\t\t\t\t\tf.request = value\n   165\t\t\t\tcase \"--lines\":\n   166\t\t\t\t\tn, err := strconv.Atoi(value)\n   167\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil || n < 1 || n > 1000 {\n   168\t\t\t\t\t\treturn f, tr(\"--lines takes a number from 1 to 1000\", \"--lines recebe um número de 1 a 1000\")\n   169\t\t\t\t\t}\n   170\t\t\t\t\tf.lines = n\n   171\t\t\t\tcase \"--refresh\":\n   172\t\t\t\t\td, err := time.ParseDuration(value)\n   173\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil || d < 0 || d > time.Hour {\n   174\t\t\t\t\t\treturn f, tr(\"--refresh takes a duration from 0 to 1h (0 turns the preview's refresh off)\", \"--refresh recebe uma duração de 0 a 1h (0 desliga a atualização do preview)\")\n   175\t\t\t\t\t}\n   176\t\t\t\t\tf.refresh = d\n   177\t\t\t\tcase \"--timeout\":\n   178\t\t\t\t\td, err := time.ParseDuration(value)\n   179\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil || d <= 0 {\n   180\t\t\t\t\t\treturn f, tr(\"--timeout takes a positive duration\", \"--timeout recebe uma duração positiva\")\n   181\t\t\t\t\t}\n   182\t\t\t\t\tf.timeout = d\n   183\t\t\t\tcase \"--to\":\n   184\t\t\t\t\tf.to = value\n   185\t\t\t\tcase \"--cd\":\n   186\t\t\t\t\tf.cd = value\n   187\t\t\t\tcase \"--add-dir\":\n   188\t\t\t\t\tf.addDirs = append(f.addDirs, value)\n   189\t\t\t\tcase \"--effort\":\n   190\t\t\t\t\tf.effort = value\n   191\t\t\t\tcase \"--prompt\":\n   192\t\t\t\t\tf.promptFile = value\n   193\t\t\t\tcase \"--note-file\":\n   194\t\t\t\t\tf.noteFile = value\n   195\t\t\t\t}\n   196\t\t\t}\n   197\t\t}\n   198\t\treturn f, \"\"\n   199\t}\n   200\t\n   201\tfunc cmdDelegate(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n   202\t\tif len(args) == 0 {\n   203\t\t\tdispatchCommandHelp(\"delegate\", nil, stdout, cliLocaleValue())\n   204\t\t\treturn 0\n   205\t\t}\n   206\t\tsub, rest := args[0], args[1:]\n   207\t\tif spec, planned := delegatePlanned[sub]; planned {\n   208\t\t\treturn delegateUsage(stdout, stderr, rest, sub, tr(\"not available yet; it is delivered by spec \"+spec, \"ainda não está disponível; é entregue pela spec \"+spec))\n   209\t\t}\n   210\t\tswitch sub {\n   211\t\tcase posemodel.DelegationPurposeReview, posemodel.DelegationPurposeAdjudicate, posemodel.DelegationPurposeSmoke:\n   212\t\t\treturn cmdDelegatePurpose(root, sub, rest, stdout, stderr)\n   213\t\tcase posemodel.DelegationPurposeTask:\n   214\t\t\treturn cmdDelegateTask(root, rest, stdout, stderr)\n   215\t\tcase \"ls\":\n   216\t\t\treturn cmdDelegateLs(root, rest, stdout, stderr)\n   217\t\tcase \"resume\":\n   218\t\t\treturn cmdDelegateResume(root, rest, stdout, stderr)\n   219\t\tcase \"cancel\":\n   220\t\t\treturn cmdDelegateCancel(root, rest, stdout, stderr)\n   221\t\tcase \"agents\":\n   222\t\t\treturn cmdDelegateAgents(root, rest, stdout, stderr)\n   223\t\tcase \"wait\":\n   224\t\t\treturn cmdDelegateWait(root, rest, stdout, stderr)\n   225\t\tcase \"watch\":\n   226\t\t\treturn cmdDelegateWatch(root, rest, stdout, stderr)\n   227\t\tcase \"handoff\":\n   228\t\t\treturn cmdDelegateHandoff(root, rest, stdout, stderr)\n   229\t\t}\n   230\t\treturn delegateUsage(stdout, stderr, rest, sub, tr(\"unknown subcommand\", \"subcomando desconhecido\")+\"\\n\"+tr(\"Usage: \", \"Uso: \")+delegateUsageText)\n   231\t}\n   232\t\n   233\t// delegateUsage reports a usage error: exit 2, as text, or as the error\n   234\t// document when the caller asked for --json (R10).\n   235\tfunc delegateUsage(stdout, stderr io.Writer, args []string, command, msg string) int {\n   236\t\tfor _, arg := range args {\n   237\t\t\tif arg == \"--json\" {\n   238\t\t\t\twriteDelegateJSON(stdout, map[string]any{\"schema\": delegateErrorSchema, \"command\": command, \"error\": msg, \"usage\": true})\n   239\t\t\t\treturn 2\n   240\t\t\t}\n   241\t\t}\n   242\t\thandBackRefusal(map[string]any{\"schema\": delegateErrorSchema, \"command\": command, \"error\": msg, \"usage\": true}, 2)\n   243\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose delegate \"+command+\": \"+msg)\n   244\t}\n   245\t\n   246\tfunc writeDelegateJSON(stdout io.Writer, doc any) {\n   247\t\t// Every error document a detached run writes is handed back (B03); a\n   248\t\t// caller that knows its exit code hands it back first.\n   249\t\tif m, ok := doc.(map[string]any); ok && m[\"schema\"] == delegateErrorSchema {\n   250\t\t\tcode := 1\n   251\t\t\tif m[\"usage\"] == true {\n   252\t\t\t\tcode = 2\n   253\t\t\t}\n   254\t\t\thandBackRefusal(m, code)\n   255\t\t}\n   256\t\tenc := json.NewEncoder(stdout)\n   257\t\tenc.SetIndent(\"\", \"  \")\n   258\t\t_ = enc.Encode(doc)\n   259\t}\n   260\t\n   261\t// delegateFail reports a failure as text or as the error document.\n   262\tfunc delegateFail(stdout, stderr io.Writer, jsonOut bool, command string, code int, err error) int {\n   263\t\tmsg := strings.TrimPrefix(err.Error(), \"pose: \")\n   264\t\tdoc := map[string]any{\"schema\": delegateErrorSchema, \"command\": command, \"error\": msg}\n   265\t\t// The reason code of a refusal is the same over MCP (spec\n   266\t\t// pose-delegation-mcp R5).\n   267\t\tif code := posemodel.DelegationReasonCode(err); code != \"\" {\n   268\t\t\tdoc[\"reason_code\"] = code\n   269\t\t}\n   270\t\tvar ambiguous *posemodel.ErrDelegationRefAmbiguous\n   271\t\tif errors.As(err, &ambiguous) {\n   272\t\t\tdoc[\"candidates\"] = ambiguous.Candidates\n   273\t\t}\n   274\t\thandBackRefusal(doc, code)\n   275\t\tif jsonOut {\n   276\t\t\twriteDelegateJSON(stdout, doc)\n   277\t\t\treturn code\n   278\t\t}\n   279\t\tif code == 2 {\n   280\t\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose delegate \"+command+\": \"+msg)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'review-brief/10|let every command|commands? (it starts|started) finish|finish before ending' POSE.md locales/pt-BR/POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'review-brief/10|let every command|commands? (it starts|started) finish|finish before ending' POSE.md locales/pt-BR/POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\"","aggregated_output":"pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1071:**Conclusões de reviews delegadas.** `pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <nome>] [--apply] [--json]` registra a conclusão de um run de review concluído: a mensagem final do run traz a conclusão tipada no bloco pose-draft — `criteria` (`id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` como `<classe>:<ref>`, `rationale` e, quando o plano pede mapeamentos estruturais, `mappings`) e `tools` (`id`, `component`, `disposition`, `evidence`, `rationale`), que o brief do template `review-brief/10` (o texto que uma versão de template renderiza é congelado por um digest de referência, então mudá-lo exige uma nova versão) pede e para o qual declara as regras que o motor confere antes de registrar (um critério de julgamento aprovado traz uma justificativa, sua evidência é uma ref que o bundle selou, um critério com finding nomeia um finding do draft, fatos estruturais são respondidos como `mappings`; um draft que quebra uma delas é recusado inteiro; uma rodada depois da primeira também nomeia os findings pelos quais responde com os identificadores que o brief lista, com a rodada, nunca um F1 solto) — e o motor assina a prova do run e a atestação com o issuer nativo, `--issuer` ou `conclusions.issuer` em `.pose/policy/delegation.json` (a chave fica fora do projeto), e a registra pelo mesmo writer de domínio e preflight de `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign`. Um finding de follow-up com `action`, `owner` e `review_by` vira um risco aceito quando sua severidade é uma que a política de review selada aceita (low por padrão); qualquer outro finding fica aberto. Uma conclusão que rejeita também é registrada e bloqueia o escopo até o bundle mudar. Um run que não é uma review concluída, foi substituído, não capturou proveniência, tem limpeza ou registro incompletos, não traz draft válido para sua rodada, ou cujo bundle não governa mais, não registra atestação: seu registro de conclusão, no diretório `review-conclusions` de `.pose`, guarda os motivos. Um run conclui uma vez: um lock que o sistema libera quando o processo termina é mantido da primeira leitura à última escrita, concluí-lo de novo devolve seu registro, e uma reserva deixada por uma conclusão interrompida só é completada pela atestação que ela registrou se essa atestação verificar como a conclusão do run; caso contrário o run é concluído no lugar dela. Quem quer que a assine, uma atestação de um run com brief `review-brief/3` a `/10` declara a conclusão daquele run: critérios, ferramentas ou findings que o draft não declarou são recusados. Com `delegated_review: true` na policy de review e `conclusions.issuer` definido, `pose delegate review` registra a conclusão no momento em que o run termina; caso contrário nada é automático. Um run de adjudicação ou de smoke conclui do mesmo jeito, sob os mesmos checks, lock e recusas, e nunca como aprovação. O brief do template `adjudication-brief/2` lista as questões que a spec do escopo registra — cada decisão `D<n>` e requisito `R<n>` — e o bloco pose-draft responde cada uma em `questions` (`id`, `verdict` holds|does-not-hold|cannot-determine, `evidence`, `rationale`); o veredito é registrado como registro de adjudicação da spec no diretório `adjudications` de `.pose`, e o `lint-spec` reprova, e o `close` recusa, uma questão que a adjudicação do bundle atual diz não se sustentar e avisa sobre uma que ela não pôde determinar ou sobre um registro que não verifica. O brief do template `smoke-brief/2` pede `surfaces` (`ref`, `outcome` observed|not-observed|not-reachable, `commands`, `observed`), uma por delivery target; as observações são registradas como resultados de validação da classe de evidência `smoke`, um check obrigatório por alvo que passa quando foi observado e é evidência só daquele alvo daquela spec, com head, data e proveniência tirados do run e do índice atual, no diretório `results/smoke` de `.pose`, que o `surface-check` lê ao lado do results path, de modo que um delivery profile pode exigir `smoke`. Um veredito que não responde exatamente o que seu brief pediu não registra nada; todo registro é verificado na leitura — a prova do run verifica e ele é o que o draft do run conclui — e um que não verifica não produz nada. Runs com brief `adjudication-brief/1` e `smoke-brief/1` continuam verificando com o próprio template.\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1075:**Runs que deixam trabalho para trás.** No Linux, depois que o adaptador termina, o envio também encerra todo processo cujo ambiente nomeia o checkout selado do run (`POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT`), o que pega comandos que o revisor iniciou em sessão própria e roda o adaptador sob um shim de run de review, o mesmo executável reentrado, que é o subreaper da subárvore do run e encerra o que o run deixa nela, mesmo um processo que abriu sessão própria e limpou o ambiente; o shim faz o mesmo num timeout e quando o envio termina, e relata por um pipe que o revisor não herda; cada um é fixado por um pidfd e conferido de novo antes do sinal. Ele espera que terminem e os lista em `safety.limitations` do run antes do inventário de limpeza, declarando ali os processos do mesmo usuário anteriores ao run cujo ambiente não pôde ser lido (um iniciado durante o run que não pode ser lido derruba a limpeza); nas outras plataformas só o grupo de processos é encerrado; o brief do template `review-brief/10` pede ao revisor que deixe seus comandos terminarem. O envio marca a tentativa como ativa antes de publicar a reserva, então um envio que termina antes de registrar o run sempre deixa uma tentativa parada, que `pose delegate ls` lista com a causa, e `pose delegate cancel <tentativa>` a libera quando o dono está comprovadamente encerrado, registrando um run com falha e o seu recibo; uma liberação roda por vez, sob um lock que o sistema libera junto com quem o detém, e uma liberação conclui com qualquer run que a tentativa já registrou em vez de gravar outro. Uma reserva que um motor anterior deixou sem marcador não registra dono: `pose delegate ls` a lista depois de dez minutos, e `pose delegate cancel <tentativa> --confirm-abandoned` a libera com a confirmação do operador de que nenhum envio dela está rodando.\nPOSE.md:1074:**Conclusions of delegated reviews.** `pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <name>] [--apply] [--json]` records the conclusion of a completed review run: the run's final message carries its typed conclusion in the pose-draft block — `criteria` (`id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` as `<class>:<ref>`, `rationale`, and `mappings` where the plan asks for structural mappings) and `tools` (`id`, `component`, `disposition`, `evidence`, `rationale`), the brief of template `review-brief/10` (the text a template version renders is frozen by a golden digest, so a change to it takes a new version) asks for them and states the rules the engine checks before it records one (a judgment criterion passed carries a rationale, its evidence is a ref the bundle sealed, a finding criterion names a finding of the draft, structural facts are answered as `mappings`; a draft that breaks one is refused whole; a round after the first also names the findings it accounts for by the identifiers the brief lists, with their round, never a bare F1) — and the engine signs the run's proof and the attestation with the native issuer, `--issuer` or `conclusions.issuer` in `.pose/policy/delegation.json` (the key stays outside the project), and records it through the same domain writer and preflight as `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign`. A follow-up finding with `action`, `owner` and `review_by` becomes an accepted risk when its severity is one the sealed review policy accepts (low by default); any other finding stays open. A rejecting conclusion is recorded too and blocks the scope until the bundle changes. A run that is not a completed review, is superseded, captured no provenance, has an incomplete cleanup or record, carries no valid draft for its round, or whose bundle no longer governs, records no attestation: its conclusion record, in the `review-conclusions` directory of `.pose`, keeps the reasons. A run concludes once: a lock the system releases when the process ends is held from the first read to the last write, concluding it again returns its record, and a reservation an interrupted conclusion left is completed from the attestation it recorded only if that attestation verifies as the run's conclusion, otherwise the run is concluded in its place. Whoever signs it, an attestation of a run briefed with `review-brief/3` to `/10` states that run's conclusion: criteria, tools or findings its draft did not declare are refused. With review policy `delegated_review: true` and `conclusions.issuer` set, `pose delegate review` records the conclusion the moment the run completes; otherwise nothing is automatic. An adjudication or a smoke run concludes the same way, under the same checks, lock and refusals, and never as an approval. The brief of template `adjudication-brief/2` lists the questions the scope's spec records — each decision `D<n>` and requirement `R<n>` — and the pose-draft block answers each in `questions` (`id`, `verdict` holds|does-not-hold|cannot-determine, `evidence`, `rationale`); the verdict is recorded as an adjudication record of the spec in the `adjudications` directory of `.pose`, and `lint-spec` fails, and `close` refuses, on a question the current bundle's adjudication says does not hold and warns on one it cannot determine or on a record that does not verify. The brief of template `smoke-brief/2` asks for `surfaces` (`ref`, `outcome` observed|not-observed|not-reachable, `commands`, `observed`), one per delivery target; the observations are recorded as validation results of evidence class `smoke`, one required check per target that passes when it was observed and is evidence of that target of that spec only, its head, time and provenance taken from the run and the current index, in the `results/smoke` directory of `.pose`, which `surface-check` reads beside the results path, so a delivery profile may demand `smoke`. A verdict that does not answer exactly what its brief asked records nothing; every record is verified on read — its run's proof verifies and it is what the run's draft concludes — and one that does not yields nothing. Runs briefed with `adjudication-brief/1` and `smoke-brief/1` keep verifying with their template.\nPOSE.md:1078:**Runs that leave work behind.** On Linux, after the adapter exits, the dispatch also ends every process whose environment names the run's sealed checkout (`POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT`), which catches commands a reviewer started in a session of its own, and it runs the adapter under a review run shim, the same executable re-entered, which is the subreaper of the run's subtree and ends whatever the run leaves in it, even a process that started its own session and cleared its environment; the shim also does so on a timeout and when its dispatcher ends, and reports through a pipe the reviewer does not inherit; each is pinned by a pidfd and checked again before it is signalled. It waits for them and lists them in the run's `safety.limitations` before the cleanup inventory, and discloses there the processes of the same user that predate the run and whose environment could not be read (one started during the run that cannot be read fails the cleanup); on other platforms only the process group is ended; the brief of template `review-brief/10` asks the reviewer to let its commands finish. The dispatch marks an attempt active before it publishes its reservation, so a dispatch that ends before recording its run always leaves a stalled attempt, which `pose delegate ls` lists with its cause, and `pose delegate cancel <attempt>` releases it once its owner is proven gone, recording a failed run and its receipt; one release runs at a time, under a lock the system releases with its holder, and a release completes with any run the attempt already recorded instead of writing another. A reservation an earlier engine left without a marker records no owner: `pose delegate ls` lists it once it is ten minutes old, and `pose delegate cancel <attempt> --confirm-abandoned` releases it on the operator's confirmation that no dispatch of it runs.\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:81:\treviewBriefTemplateFinishCommands = \"review-brief/10\"\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md:1061:**Conclusions of delegated reviews.** `pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <name>] [--apply] [--json]` records the conclusion of a completed review run: the run's final message carries its typed conclusion in the pose-draft block — `criteria` (`id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` as `<class>:<ref>`, `rationale`, and `mappings` where the plan asks for structural mappings) and `tools` (`id`, `component`, `disposition`, `evidence`, `rationale`), the brief of template `review-brief/10` (the text a template version renders is frozen by a golden digest, so a change to it takes a new version) asks for them and states the rules the engine checks before it records one (a judgment criterion passed carries a rationale, its evidence is a ref the bundle sealed, a finding criterion names a finding of the draft, structural facts are answered as `mappings`; a draft that breaks one is refused whole; a round after the first also names the findings it accounts for by the identifiers the brief lists, with their round, never a bare F1) — and the engine signs the run's proof and the attestation with the native issuer, `--issuer` or `conclusions.issuer` in `.pose/policy/delegation.json` (the key stays outside the project), and records it through the same domain writer and preflight as `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign`. A follow-up finding with `action`, `owner` and `review_by` becomes an accepted risk when its severity is one the sealed review policy accepts (low by default); any other finding stays open. A rejecting conclusion is recorded too and blocks the scope until the bundle changes. A run that is not a completed review, is superseded, captured no provenance, has an incomplete cleanup or record, carries no valid draft for its round, or whose bundle no longer governs, records no attestation: its conclusion record, in the `review-conclusions` directory of `.pose`, keeps the reasons. A run concludes once: a lock the system releases when the process ends is held from the first read to the last write, concluding it again returns its record, and a reservation an interrupted conclusion left is completed from the attestation it recorded only if that attestation verifies as the run's conclusion, otherwise the run is concluded in its place. Whoever signs it, an attestation of a run briefed with `review-brief/3` to `/10` states that run's conclusion: criteria, tools or findings its draft did not declare are refused. With review policy `delegated_review: true` and `conclusions.issuer` set, `pose delegate review` records the conclusion the moment the run completes; otherwise nothing is automatic. An adjudication or a smoke run concludes the same way, under the same checks, lock and refusals, and never as an approval. The brief of template `adjudication-brief/2` lists the questions the scope's spec records — each decision `D<n>` and requirement `R<n>` — and the pose-draft block answers each in `questions` (`id`, `verdict` holds|does-not-hold|cannot-determine, `evidence`, `rationale`); the verdict is recorded as an adjudication record of the spec in the `adjudications` directory of `.pose`, and `lint-spec` fails, and `close` refuses, on a question the current bundle's adjudication says does not hold and warns on one it cannot determine or on a record that does not verify. The brief of template `smoke-brief/2` asks for `surfaces` (`ref`, `outcome` observed|not-observed|not-reachable, `commands`, `observed`), one per delivery target; the observations are recorded as validation results of evidence class `smoke`, one required check per target that passes when it was observed and is evidence of that target of that spec only, its head, time and provenance taken from the run and the current index, in the `results/smoke` directory of `.pose`, which `surface-check` reads beside the results path, so a delivery profile may demand `smoke`. A verdict that does not answer exactly what its brief asked records nothing; every record is verified on read — its run's proof verifies and it is what the run's draft concludes — and one that does not yields nothing. Runs briefed with `adjudication-brief/1` and `smoke-brief/1` keep verifying with their template.\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md:1065:**Runs that leave work behind.** On Linux, after the adapter exits, the dispatch also ends every process whose environment names the run's sealed checkout (`POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT`), which catches commands a reviewer started in a session of its own, and it runs the adapter under a review run shim, the same executable re-entered, which is the subreaper of the run's subtree and ends whatever the run leaves in it, even a process that started its own session and cleared its environment; the shim also does so on a timeout and when its dispatcher ends, and reports through a pipe the reviewer does not inherit; each is pinned by a pidfd and checked again before it is signalled. It waits for them and lists them in the run's `safety.limitations` before the cleanup inventory, and discloses there the processes of the same user that predate the run and whose environment could not be read (one started during the run that cannot be read fails the cleanup); on other platforms only the process group is ended; the brief of template `review-brief/10` asks the reviewer to let its commands finish. The dispatch marks an attempt active before it publishes its reservation, so a dispatch that ends before recording its run always leaves a stalled attempt, which `pose delegate ls` lists with its cause, and `pose delegate cancel <attempt>` releases it once its owner is proven gone, recording a failed run and its receipt; one release runs at a time, under a lock the system releases with its holder, and a release completes with any run the attempt already recorded instead of writing another. A reservation an earlier engine left without a marker records no owner: `pose delegate ls` lists it once it is ten minutes old, and `pose delegate cancel <attempt> --confirm-abandoned` releases it on the operator's confirmation that no dispatch of it runs.\nlocales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1071:**Conclusões de reviews delegadas.** `pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <nome>] [--apply] [--json]` registra a conclusão de um run de review concluído: a mensagem final do run traz a conclusão tipada no bloco pose-draft — `criteria` (`id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` como `<classe>:<ref>`, `rationale` e, quando o plano pede mapeamentos estruturais, `mappings`) e `tools` (`id`, `component`, `disposition`, `evidence`, `rationale`), que o brief do template `review-brief/10` (o texto que uma versão de template renderiza é congelado por um digest de referência, então mudá-lo exige uma nova versão) pede e para o qual declara as regras que o motor confere antes de registrar (um critério de julgamento aprovado traz uma justificativa, sua evidência é uma ref que o bundle selou, um critério com finding nomeia um finding do draft, fatos estruturais são respondidos como `mappings`; um draft que quebra uma delas é recusado inteiro; uma rodada depois da primeira também nomeia os findings pelos quais responde com os identificadores que o brief lista, com a rodada, nunca um F1 solto) — e o motor assina a prova do run e a atestação com o issuer nativo, `--issuer` ou `conclusions.issuer` em `.pose/policy/delegation.json` (a chave fica fora do projeto), e a registra pelo mesmo writer de domínio e preflight de `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign`. Um finding de follow-up com `action`, `owner` e `review_by` vira um risco aceito quando sua severidade é uma que a política de review selada aceita (low por padrão); qualquer outro finding fica aberto. Uma conclusão que rejeita também é registrada e bloqueia o escopo até o bundle mudar. Um run que não é uma review concluída, foi substituído, não capturou proveniência, tem limpeza ou registro incompletos, não traz draft válido para sua rodada, ou cujo bundle não governa mais, não registra atestação: seu registro de conclusão, no diretório `review-conclusions` de `.pose`, guarda os motivos. Um run conclui uma vez: um lock que o sistema libera quando o processo termina é mantido da primeira leitura à última escrita, concluí-lo de novo devolve seu registro, e uma reserva deixada por uma conclusão interrompida só é completada pela atestação que ela registrou se essa atestação verificar como a conclusão do run; caso contrário o run é concluído no lugar dela. Quem quer que a assine, uma atestação de um run com brief `review-brief/3` a `/10` declara a conclusão daquele run: critérios, ferramentas ou findings que o draft não declarou são recusados. Com `delegated_review: true` na policy de review e `conclusions.issuer` definido, `pose delegate review` registra a conclusão no momento em que o run termina; caso contrário nada é automático. Um run de adjudicação ou de smoke conclui do mesmo jeito, sob os mesmos checks, lock e recusas, e nunca como aprovação. O brief do template `adjudication-brief/2` lista as questões que a spec do escopo registra — cada decisão `D<n>` e requisito `R<n>` — e o bloco pose-draft responde cada uma em `questions` (`id`, `verdict` holds|does-not-hold|cannot-determine, `evidence`, `rationale`); o veredito é registrado como registro de adjudicação da spec no diretório `adjudications` de `.pose`, e o `lint-spec` reprova, e o `close` recusa, uma questão que a adjudicação do bundle atual diz não se sustentar e avisa sobre uma que ela não pôde determinar ou sobre um registro que não verifica. O brief do template `smoke-brief/2` pede `surfaces` (`ref`, `outcome` observed|not-observed|not-reachable, `commands`, `observed`), uma por delivery target; as observações são registradas como resultados de validação da classe de evidência `smoke`, um check obrigatório por alvo que passa quando foi observado e é evidência só daquele alvo daquela spec, com head, data e proveniência tirados do run e do índice atual, no diretório `results/smoke` de `.pose`, que o `surface-check` lê ao lado do results path, de modo que um delivery profile pode exigir `smoke`. Um veredito que não responde exatamente o que seu brief pediu não registra nada; todo registro é verificado na leitura — a prova do run verifica e ele é o que o draft do run conclui — e um que não verifica não produz nada. Runs com brief `adjudication-brief/1` e `smoke-brief/1` continuam verificando com o próprio template.\nlocales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1075:**Runs que deixam trabalho para trás.** No Linux, depois que o adaptador termina, o envio também encerra todo processo cujo ambiente nomeia o checkout selado do run (`POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT`), o que pega comandos que o revisor iniciou em sessão própria e roda o adaptador sob um shim de run de review, o mesmo executável reentrado, que é o subreaper da subárvore do run e encerra o que o run deixa nela, mesmo um processo que abriu sessão própria e limpou o ambiente; o shim faz o mesmo num timeout e quando o envio termina, e relata por um pipe que o revisor não herda; cada um é fixado por um pidfd e conferido de novo antes do sinal. Ele espera que terminem e os lista em `safety.limitations` do run antes do inventário de limpeza, declarando ali os processos do mesmo usuário anteriores ao run cujo ambiente não pôde ser lido (um iniciado durante o run que não pode ser lido derruba a limpeza); nas outras plataformas só o grupo de processos é encerrado; o brief do template `review-brief/10` pede ao revisor que deixe seus comandos terminarem. O envio marca a tentativa como ativa antes de publicar a reserva, então um envio que termina antes de registrar o run sempre deixa uma tentativa parada, que `pose delegate ls` lista com a causa, e `pose delegate cancel <tentativa>` a libera quando o dono está comprovadamente encerrado, registrando um run com falha e o seu recibo; uma liberação roda por vez, sob um lock que o sistema libera junto com quem o detém, e uma liberação conclui com qualquer run que a tentativa já registrou em vez de gravar outro. Uma reserva que um motor anterior deixou sem marcador não registra dono: `pose delegate ls` a lista depois de dez minutos, e `pose delegate cancel <tentativa> --confirm-abandoned` a libera com a confirmação do operador de que nenhum envio dela está rodando.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
