{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go | sed -n '1,245p' && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go | sed -n '1,135p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t//go:build linux\n     2\t\n     3\tpackage pose\n     4\t\n     5\t// Leftover reviewer processes (spec\n     6\t// pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R1): an adapter such as\n     7\t// `codex exec` runs each command in a session of its own, so killing the\n     8\t// adapter's process group misses a command the reviewer left running, and\n     9\t// that command keeps writing into the run's runtime directory while the\n    10\t// cleanup inventory reads it. Every process of the run inherits\n    11\t// SealedCheckoutEnv naming the run's checkout, so the dispatch finds them by\n    12\t// that entry, ends them and waits for them before the inventory.\n    13\t//\n    14\t// Each process is pinned by a pidfd before it is signalled, and its\n    15\t// environment is read again through the pinned process, so a pid reused by\n    16\t// an unrelated process between the scan and the signal is never killed\n    17\t// (review round 1, N3). A scan that cannot list or read the state of the\n    18\t// processes fails. A process of this user whose environment cannot be read\n    19\t// (one that made itself non-inspectable) cannot be matched: one that already\n    20\t// existed before the adapter started is not the run's and is skipped; any\n    21\t// other may be the run's, so the scan fails and the run stays unconcludable\n    22\t// (review round 2, N2).\n    23\t\n    24\timport (\n    25\t\t\"bytes\"\n    26\t\t\"errors\"\n    27\t\t\"fmt\"\n    28\t\t\"io/fs\"\n    29\t\t\"os\"\n    30\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    31\t\t\"strconv\"\n    32\t\t\"strings\"\n    33\t\t\"syscall\"\n    34\t\t\"time\"\n    35\t\n    36\t\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n    37\t)\n    38\t\n    39\t// reapSealedCheckoutProcesses ends every process whose environment names\n    40\t// worktree as its sealed checkout and returns a description of each. An\n    41\t// error means the run's processes could not be proven ended within the bound.\n    42\tfunc reapSealedCheckoutProcesses(worktree string, baseline map[int]string) ([]string, int, error) {\n    43\t\tif worktree == \"\" {\n    44\t\t\treturn nil, 0, nil\n    45\t\t}\n    46\t\tentry := []byte(SealedCheckoutEnv + \"=\" + worktree)\n    47\t\tvar reaped []string\n    48\t\tseen := map[int]bool{}\n    49\t\tdeadline := time.Now().Add(reviewReapWait)\n    50\t\tunreadable := 0\n    51\t\tfor {\n    52\t\t\talive, opaque, err := reviewMarkedProcesses(entry)\n    53\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    54\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, err\n    55\t\t\t}\n    56\t\t\tunreadable = 0\n    57\t\t\tfor pid, start := range opaque {\n    58\t\t\t\tif prior, ok := baseline[pid]; !ok || prior != start {\n    59\t\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d of this user started during the run and cannot be inspected; it may be the run's and was not ended\", pid)\n    60\t\t\t\t}\n    61\t\t\t\tunreadable++\n    62\t\t\t}\n    63\t\t\tfor _, pid := range alive {\n    64\t\t\t\tif !seen[pid] {\n    65\t\t\t\t\tseen[pid] = true\n    66\t\t\t\t\t// Only the pid: the name is the reviewer's to choose and is not\n    67\t\t\t\t\t// recorded (review round 7, N4).\n    68\t\t\t\t\treaped = append(reaped, strconv.Itoa(pid))\n    69\t\t\t\t}\n    70\t\t\t\tif err := killPinnedMarkedProcess(pid, entry); err != nil {\n    71\t\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, err\n    72\t\t\t\t}\n    73\t\t\t}\n    74\t\t\tif len(alive) == 0 {\n    75\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, nil\n    76\t\t\t}\n    77\t\t\tif time.Now().After(deadline) {\n    78\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"%d process(es) of the run could not be ended\", len(alive))\n    79\t\t\t}\n    80\t\t\ttime.Sleep(50 * time.Millisecond)\n    81\t\t}\n    82\t}\n    83\t\n    84\t// reviewMarkedProcesses lists the live processes whose environment holds\n    85\t// entry, and counts this user's processes whose environment could not be\n    86\t// read. A process that is gone is skipped.\n    87\tfunc reviewMarkedProcesses(entry []byte) ([]int, map[int]string, error) {\n    88\t\tdirs, err := os.ReadDir(\"/proc\")\n    89\t\tif err != nil {\n    90\t\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"the run's processes could not be listed: %w\", err)\n    91\t\t}\n    92\t\tunreadable := map[int]string{}\n    93\t\tself, uid := os.Getpid(), os.Getuid()\n    94\t\tvar out []int\n    95\t\tfor _, d := range dirs {\n    96\t\t\tpid, err := strconv.Atoi(d.Name())\n    97\t\t\tif err != nil || pid == self {\n    98\t\t\t\tcontinue\n    99\t\t\t}\n   100\t\t\tmarked, err := reviewProcessMarked(pid, entry)\n   101\t\t\tswitch {\n   102\t\t\tcase reviewProcessGoneErr(err):\n   103\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   104\t\t\tcase err != nil:\n   105\t\t\t\tif owner, oerr := reviewProcessOwner(pid); oerr == nil && owner != uid {\n   106\t\t\t\t\tcontinue // another user's process never inherits this run's environment\n   107\t\t\t\t} else if reviewProcessGoneErr(oerr) {\n   108\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   109\t\t\t\t}\n   110\t\t\t\tstart, serr := processStartTime(pid)\n   111\t\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(serr) {\n   112\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   113\t\t\t\t}\n   114\t\t\t\tif serr != nil || start == \"\" {\n   115\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d start could not be read: %v\", pid, serr)\n   116\t\t\t\t}\n   117\t\t\t\tunreadable[pid] = start\n   118\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   119\t\t\tcase !marked:\n   120\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   121\t\t\t}\n   122\t\t\tzombie, err := reviewProcessZombie(pid)\n   123\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) || err == nil && zombie {\n   124\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   125\t\t\t}\n   126\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   127\t\t\t\treturn nil, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d state could not be read: %w\", pid, err)\n   128\t\t\t}\n   129\t\t\tout = append(out, pid)\n   130\t\t}\n   131\t\treturn out, unreadable, nil\n   132\t}\n   133\t\n   134\t// killPinnedMarkedProcess signals pid only through a pidfd opened on it,\n   135\t// after the environment read through that same pinned process still holds\n   136\t// entry.\n   137\tfunc killPinnedMarkedProcess(pid int, entry []byte) error {\n   138\t\tfd, err := unix.PidfdOpen(pid, 0)\n   139\t\tif errors.Is(err, unix.ESRCH) {\n   140\t\t\treturn nil\n   141\t\t}\n   142\t\tif err != nil {\n   143\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be pinned: %w\", pid, err)\n   144\t\t}\n   145\t\tdefer unix.Close(fd)\n   146\t\t// The pidfd names one process for its lifetime; if pid was reused before\n   147\t\t// it was opened, the new process does not carry this run's entry.\n   148\t\tmarked, err := reviewProcessMarked(pid, entry)\n   149\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) || err == nil && !marked {\n   150\t\t\treturn nil\n   151\t\t}\n   152\t\tif err != nil {\n   153\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be inspected: %w\", pid, err)\n   154\t\t}\n   155\t\tif err := unix.PidfdSendSignal(fd, unix.SIGKILL, nil, 0); err != nil && !errors.Is(err, unix.ESRCH) {\n   156\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be ended: %w\", pid, err)\n   157\t\t}\n   158\t\treturn nil\n   159\t}\n   160\t\n   161\tfunc reviewProcessMarked(pid int, entry []byte) (bool, error) {\n   162\t\tenviron, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid), \"environ\"))\n   163\t\tif err != nil {\n   164\t\t\treturn false, err\n   165\t\t}\n   166\t\tfor _, kv := range bytes.Split(environ, []byte{0}) {\n   167\t\t\tif bytes.Equal(kv, entry) {\n   168\t\t\t\treturn true, nil\n   169\t\t\t}\n   170\t\t}\n   171\t\treturn false, nil\n   172\t}\n   173\t\n   174\tfunc reviewProcessOwner(pid int) (int, error) {\n   175\t\tinfo, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid)))\n   176\t\tif err != nil {\n   177\t\t\treturn 0, err\n   178\t\t}\n   179\t\tst, ok := info.Sys().(*syscall.Stat_t)\n   180\t\tif !ok {\n   181\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d owner unavailable\", pid)\n   182\t\t}\n   183\t\treturn int(st.Uid), nil\n   184\t}\n   185\t\n   186\tfunc reviewProcessGoneErr(err error) bool {\n   187\t\treturn errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) || errors.Is(err, syscall.ESRCH)\n   188\t}\n   189\t\n   190\tfunc reviewProcessName(pid int) string {\n   191\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid), \"comm\"))\n   192\t\tif err != nil {\n   193\t\t\treturn \"?\"\n   194\t\t}\n   195\t\treturn strings.TrimSpace(string(raw))\n   196\t}\n   197\t\n   198\tfunc reviewProcessZombie(pid int) (bool, error) {\n   199\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid), \"stat\"))\n   200\t\tif err != nil {\n   201\t\t\treturn false, err\n   202\t\t}\n   203\t\t// The state follows the parenthesised command name.\n   204\t\tif i := bytes.LastIndexByte(raw, ')'); i >= 0 && i+2 < len(raw) {\n   205\t\t\treturn raw[i+2] == 'Z', nil\n   206\t\t}\n   207\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d state is unreadable\", pid)\n   208\t}\n   209\t\n   210\t// reviewOpaqueProcessBaseline records, before the adapter starts, the\n   211\t// processes of this user whose environment cannot be read, by pid and start\n   212\t// time: they cannot be the run's.\n   213\tfunc reviewOpaqueProcessBaseline() map[int]string {\n   214\t\t_, opaque, _ := reviewMarkedProcesses([]byte(SealedCheckoutEnv + \"=\\x00\"))\n   215\t\treturn opaque\n   216\t}\n     1\t//go:build linux\n     2\t\n     3\tpackage pose\n     4\t\n     5\timport (\n     6\t\t\"os\"\n     7\t\t\"os/exec\"\n     8\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n     9\t\t\"strconv\"\n    10\t\t\"strings\"\n    11\t\t\"syscall\"\n    12\t\t\"testing\"\n    13\t\t\"time\"\n    14\t)\n    15\t\n    16\t// Review round 1, N3: a pid that no longer names a process of the run, as\n    17\t// after reuse by an unrelated process, is never signalled.\n    18\tfunc TestAPidThatLostTheRunsEntryIsNotKilled(t *testing.T) {\n    19\t\tother := exec.Command(\"sleep\", \"30\")\n    20\t\tif err := other.Start(); err != nil {\n    21\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    22\t\t}\n    23\t\tfor i := 0; i < 200 && reviewProcessName(other.Process.Pid) != \"sleep\"; i++ {\n    24\t\t\ttime.Sleep(10 * time.Millisecond)\n    25\t\t}\n    26\t\tt.Cleanup(func() { _ = other.Process.Kill(); _ = other.Wait() })\n    27\t\tentry := []byte(SealedCheckoutEnv + \"=/nonexistent/run-checkout\")\n    28\t\tif err := killPinnedMarkedProcess(other.Process.Pid, entry); err != nil {\n    29\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    30\t\t}\n    31\t\ttime.Sleep(100 * time.Millisecond)\n    32\t\tif zombie, err := reviewProcessZombie(other.Process.Pid); err != nil || zombie {\n    33\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a process without the run's entry was killed: zombie=%t %v\", zombie, err)\n    34\t\t}\n    35\t\t// The same process carrying the entry is ended.\n    36\t\tmarked := exec.Command(\"sleep\", \"30\")\n    37\t\tmarked.Env = append(marked.Environ(), string(entry))\n    38\t\tif err := marked.Start(); err != nil {\n    39\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    40\t\t}\n    41\t\t// Until exec, /proc shows the parent's environment.\n    42\t\tfor i := 0; i < 200; i++ {\n    43\t\t\tif ok, _ := reviewProcessMarked(marked.Process.Pid, entry); ok {\n    44\t\t\t\tbreak\n    45\t\t\t}\n    46\t\t\ttime.Sleep(10 * time.Millisecond)\n    47\t\t}\n    48\t\tif err := killPinnedMarkedProcess(marked.Process.Pid, entry); err != nil {\n    49\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    50\t\t}\n    51\t\tif err := marked.Wait(); err == nil {\n    52\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"the marked process was not ended\")\n    53\t\t}\n    54\t}\n    55\t\n    56\t// opaqueProcess starts a process of this user whose environment cannot be\n    57\t// read (it makes itself non-dumpable), or skips without python3.\n    58\tfunc opaqueProcess(t *testing.T) *exec.Cmd {\n    59\t\tt.Helper()\n    60\t\tif _, err := exec.LookPath(\"python3\"); err != nil {\n    61\t\t\tt.Skip(\"python3 is not available\")\n    62\t\t}\n    63\t\tcmd := exec.Command(\"python3\", \"-c\", \"import ctypes,time; ctypes.CDLL(None).prctl(4,0,0,0,0); time.sleep(30)\")\n    64\t\tif err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\n    65\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    66\t\t}\n    67\t\tt.Cleanup(func() { _ = cmd.Process.Kill(); _ = cmd.Wait() })\n    68\t\tfor i := 0; i < 300; i++ {\n    69\t\t\tif _, err := reviewProcessMarked(cmd.Process.Pid, []byte(\"x\")); err != nil && !reviewProcessGoneErr(err) {\n    70\t\t\t\treturn cmd\n    71\t\t\t}\n    72\t\t\ttime.Sleep(10 * time.Millisecond)\n    73\t\t}\n    74\t\tt.Skip(\"the process never became non-inspectable\")\n    75\t\treturn nil\n    76\t}\n    77\t\n    78\t// Review round 2, N2: a non-inspectable process that existed before the run\n    79\t// is not the run's; one that started during it may be, and the scan fails\n    80\t// instead of reporting the run's processes ended.\n    81\tfunc TestANonInspectableProcessStartedDuringTheRunFailsTheScan(t *testing.T) {\n    82\t\tbefore := opaqueProcess(t)\n    83\t\tbaseline := reviewOpaqueProcessBaseline()\n    84\t\tif _, ok := baseline[before.Process.Pid]; !ok {\n    85\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the baseline misses process %d\", before.Process.Pid)\n    86\t\t}\n    87\t\tif _, opaque, err := reapSealedCheckoutProcesses(\"/nonexistent/run-checkout\", baseline); err != nil || opaque == 0 {\n    88\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a process that predates the run failed the scan or was not counted: %d %v\", opaque, err)\n    89\t\t}\n    90\t\tduring := opaqueProcess(t)\n    91\t\tif _, _, err := reapSealedCheckoutProcesses(\"/nonexistent/run-checkout\", baseline); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"started during the run\") {\n    92\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"process %d, started during the run, did not fail the scan: %v\", during.Process.Pid, err)\n    93\t\t}\n    94\t}\n    95\t\n    96\t// Review round 6, N2: a descendant that leaves the group, starts its own\n    97\t// session and clears its environment is still ended with the run.\n    98\tfunc TestAnOrphanThatClearedItsEnvironmentIsEnded(t *testing.T) {\n    99\t\tif _, err := exec.LookPath(\"setsid\"); err != nil {\n   100\t\t\tt.Skip(\"setsid is not available\")\n   101\t\t}\n   102\t\tpidFile := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"orphan.pid\")\n   103\t\tf := provenanceRunFixture(t, \"fixture-vendor\", \"fixture-model\", func(a *ReviewerAdapter) {\n   104\t\t\ta.Containment = containmentPolicy()\n   105\t\t\ta.Command = []string{\"sh\", \"-c\", `cat >/dev/null; setsid env -i /bin/sh -c 'echo $$ > \"$1\"; while :; do sleep 0.05; done' sh \"$1\" </dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1 & ` +\n   106\t\t\t\t`i=0; while [ ! -s \"$1\" ] && [ $i -lt 100 ]; do sleep 0.05; i=$((i+1)); done; printf 'decision: approved\\n'`, \"sh\", pidFile}\n   107\t\t})\n   108\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(pidFile)\n   109\t\tif err != nil {\n   110\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the orphan never started: %v\", err)\n   111\t\t}\n   112\t\tpid, _ := strconv.Atoi(strings.TrimSpace(string(raw)))\n   113\t\tt.Cleanup(func() { _ = syscall.Kill(pid, syscall.SIGKILL) })\n   114\t\tif zombie, err := reviewProcessZombie(pid); err == nil && !zombie {\n   115\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the orphan that cleared its environment survived the run (status %s: %s)\", f.run.Status, f.run.Failure)\n   116\t\t}\n   117\t\tif f.run.Status != ReviewRunCompleted || !strings.Contains(strings.Join(f.run.Safety.Limitations, \"\\n\"), \"(orphaned)\") {\n   118\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the run did not complete naming the orphan: %s %s %v\", f.run.Status, f.run.Failure, f.run.Safety.Limitations)\n   119\t\t}\n   120\t\t// Review round 7, N4: the record names the pid, never the process name\n   121\t\t// the reviewer chose.\n   122\t\tfor _, limit := range f.run.Safety.Limitations {\n   123\t\t\tif strings.Contains(limit, \"(orphaned)\") && strings.Contains(limit, \" sh \") {\n   124\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the recorded limitation carries a process name: %q\", limit)\n   125\t\t\t}\n   126\t\t}\n   127\t\tif !strings.Contains(strings.Join(f.run.Safety.Limitations, \"\\n\"), strconv.Itoa(pid)+\" (orphaned)\") {\n   128\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the recorded limitation does not name the pid: %v\", f.run.Safety.Limitations)\n   129\t\t}\n   130\t}\n   131\t\n   132\t// waitGone waits for pid to end (or be a zombie) and reports whether it did.\n   133\tfunc waitGone(pid int, within time.Duration) bool {\n   134\t\tdeadline := time.Now().Add(within)\n   135\t\tfor time.Now().Before(deadline) {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'L[1-6]|reviewReapWait|shim|Known gaps|Residual risks' .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md && git rev-parse HEAD && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'L[1-6]|reviewReapWait|shim|Known gaps|Residual risks' .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md && git rev-parse HEAD && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"61:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim.go\n62:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\n102:The leftover processes are found by the `POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT=<checkout>` entry of their environment, which every process of the run inherits; a process that clears its environment escapes, and the existing cleanup inventory still fails that run (L1). Reading another process's environment needs Linux and the same user; elsewhere the group kill stays the only termination (L2).\n139:- 2026-11-24: review round 1 (rrn-c5c082703d83c834) requested changes. N1: the reservation was published before the active marker, so a dispatch ended in between left an attempt nothing could release; the dispatch now marks the attempt active first and publishes the reservation after, and a stalled marker without a reservation is removed by the release. When marking itself fails, the dispatch still publishes the reservation and records the failed run and its receipt, keeping the contract of `pose-delegation-result-before-marker`. N2: `delegate ls` now names the abandonment cause and the release command, in text and JSON. N3: each process is pinned by a pidfd and its environment read again through it before SIGKILL, so a reused pid is never signalled. N4: a scan that cannot list `/proc` or read a process state fails; a process of this user whose environment cannot be read is counted and disclosed in the run record rather than skipped (L3). N5: the manual says the reaping is Linux-only. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out (N4's disclosure is not reproducible in a test: it needs a non-inspectable process).\n146:- 2026-11-24: the matrix of round 8 failed `TestReviewDispatchRunsAndRecordsAdapters`, and the cause was the design, not the test: a subreaper is process-wide, so the dispatcher also adopted and ended children other code started in the same process (a detached delegation) and could reap a process another goroutine waited for. The subreaper moved into a review run shim: the dispatcher starts the adapter as `<pose> __pose-review-run-shim <adapter path> <argv>`, the shim makes itself the subreaper, runs the adapter as its only child, ends and reaps everything left in its subtree, reports the ended pids in a file the dispatcher reads, and returns the adapter's status, re-raising its signal so a lost process still reads as lost. The shim has no other children, so all it adopts is the run's. The pose command and the test binaries that dispatch enable it; another embedder starts the adapter directly. `TestAnOrphanThatClearedItsEnvironmentIsEnded` fails with the shim's reaping removed.\n147:- 2026-11-24: review round 8 (rrn-f19179878d867e9a) requested changes. N1: the environment entry is the reviewer's to set, so with the shim the dispatcher no longer searches by it; the shim's subtree is the run's by construction, and the search remains only for an embedder without the shim (L6). N2: the shim's report goes through a pipe passed as file descriptor 3, which the shim closes on exec, never through a path the reviewer can write. N3: a timeout sends the shim SIGTERM, and the shim ends the run's subtree before it exits; the group kill after the run stays the backstop. N4: the shim receives SIGTERM when its dispatcher ends (`PR_SET_PDEATHSIG`, checked against the dispatcher's pid at start) and ends the run, so a dead dispatcher never leaves a reviewer running. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out.\n163:### Known gaps\n181:### Residual risks\n182:L1: on Linux a run's process escapes only while it keeps a live parent outside the run and neither the run's group nor its environment entry, for example one handed to a service manager; the cleanup inventory still fails a run whose files it keeps changing. L2: outside Linux only the process-group kill applies. L6: an embedder that does not enable the shim falls back to the search by the sealed-checkout entry, which a reviewer process can set. L4: a reservation an earlier engine left without a marker records no owner, so its release rests on the operator's confirmation, not on proof. L3: a process of this user that made itself non-inspectable cannot be matched: one that predates the run is skipped and counted in the run record, and one started during the run fails the cleanup, so such a run is not concludable.\ned727c72f1c6e1ce52c26e8f1fabcb3926a6eb01\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"agent_message","text":"The active spec defines residual limits L1, L2, L3, L4, and L6; it has no L5, though the implementer notes refer to one. I’m checking the supplied sealed bundle for the authoritative spec text before treating that as a documentation discrepancy or an unresolved assumption."}}
