dation ran but could not build in this read-only sandbox; the sealed build/e2e/integration/unit evidence was used. The checked-out spec defines L1, L2, L3, L4 and L6; it has no L5 despite the implementer note.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified the standard CLI enables the run shim, fd 3 is not inherited, and dead-owner release requires a stalled marker. Unresolved assumptions are that the shim can inspect and signal every child and can publish its full report; N2 and N3 capture those failures. Accepted spec limits are shimless embedder environment matching (L6), non-Linux group-only cleanup (L2), external live-parent escape (L1), markerless legacy reservation confirmation (L4), and non-inspectable process handling (L3).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The run shim confines subreaper scope, but an inspection failure exits before the subtree is fully reaped and the dispatcher-only owner marker lets release proceed after dispatcher death.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The CLI additions are additive and a released reservation is represented as an ordinary failed run plus receipt; run/receipt schemas remain unchanged.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Attempt identifiers are validated, abandonment is a typed refusal, live owners are refused, and read/receipt failures retain context.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change stays within pose-mcp and does not alter REST, MCP, protobuf, or event contracts. The integration assessment's unobserved HTTP consumers are outside the changed surface.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A report larger than the reader limit can block before the shim returns; truncated JSON produces a generic unreadable-report failure and loses the PIDs the run record should name.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Earlier run records retain their meaning; the new release writes the existing failed-run and receipt formats, and the CLI flag is additive.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"An unbounded descendant list can block report publication and prevent a fully reaped run from completing its required record and conclusion path.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d32807cefe47d21\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The process-scoped shim addresses the cause that process-group kills miss detached sessions while avoiding dispatcher-wide subreaper adoption and reviewer-controlled environment authority. The release records preserve ordinary run semantics. The design assessment observed no structural deltas; N2 and N3 are implementation gaps.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The root and localized manuals, scaffold copies, and runtime limitation text still describe environment-based cleanup as the normal path.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The documented cleanup guarantee and diagnostic limitations do not match the standard CLI's shim behavior, so operators cannot rely on the stated process-selection and disclosure behavior.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R2 is not met when the ended-PID report exceeds 64 KiB; N3 also leaves a process-liveness gap when cleanup fails after dispatcher death.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation, tests and manual updates align with the spec's review cleanup and abandoned-attempt scope.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A reviewer descendant can remain alive after the shim's fail-fast inspection path while release proves only that the dispatcher has died.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d32807cefe47d21\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A per-run subreaper shim is the smallest sufficient ownership boundary for detached descendants; a process-wide subreaper or reviewer-controlled environment matching would broaden authority. The shim and lock-file release follow D1/D2, but report bounds and cleanup-failure liveness still need correction.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran to exit 0.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d32807cefe47d21\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran; no structural deltas were observed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran without persistence; changed cleanup and release files contain no TODO/FIXME/stub markers.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess integrate --no-persist\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The scan completed but reported three unobserved HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp), which are outside this change's contracts.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs have invalid follow-up metadata and it reported an uncovered panic in pose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache.go:334, outside this subject.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Closeout-check requires a completed review attestation; this review is not authorized to record one.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Review-check runs after an attestation; this review is not authorized to record one.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"reachability:pose-mcp/go/review-assurance-disclosure-reachability\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran strict surface-check: one target, zero findings.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Strict validation was run but all steps failed before execution because the sandbox denied Go temporary-workdir/cache writes; sealed evidence contains passing build/e2e/integration/unit results.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Module validation was run but all steps failed before execution because the sandbox denied Go temporary-workdir/cache writes; sealed pose-mcp evidence contains passing build/e2e/integration/unit results.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nPOSE_DRAFT'","aggregated_output":"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\n## Review summary\n\nTwo medium blockers remain: the shim can block while publishing a large PID report, and a cleanup inspection error can leave descendants alive after dispatcher death. The manuals and recorded containment limits also describe the shimless environment scan as the normal Linux path; I recorded that as a low follow-up.\n\nThe focused Go tests and `go vet` passed. `surface-check` passed with zero findings, and `artifact-check` exited 0. Both strict validation commands ran but could not build because the read-only sandbox blocked Go temporary-workdir and cache writes; I relied on the sealed passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence. `review-check` and `closeout-check` are deferred because they require an attestation, which this review is not authorized to record.\n\nThe review rules applied were security, backend-go, and documentation-style. No repository changes were made; the worktree remains clean.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"POSE.md\",\n      \"line\": 1078,\n      \"summary\": \"The manuals and recorded containment limits still describe environment matching and unreadable prior-process disclosure as the normal Linux path. The standard CLI instead uses the run shim's subtree; environment matching is only the shimless embedder fallback. Update the English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies, plus the safety limitation text.\",\n      \"action\": \"Correct the manuals, scaffold copies, and runtime safety limitation to describe the shim as the normal Linux path and environment matching as the shimless fallback.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-08\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\n      \"line\": 1055,\n      \"summary\": \"The parent reads at most 64 KiB from the shim report, while the shim writes the complete unbounded ended-PID list. For a large list the reader stops draining and the shim blocks after reaping; dispatch waits until timeout/WaitDelay, then parses truncated JSON and marks cleanup incomplete. A fully reaped run becomes unconcludable and loses the full PID report.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N3\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 138,\n      \"summary\": \"The first unreadable /proc stat aborts subtree reaping. If the dispatcher has died, PDEATHSIG reaches this fail-fast path and the shim can exit with run descendants still alive; the marker tracks only the dispatcher PID and abandoned-attempt release checks only that owner's liveness, so cancel can later release the attempt while a reviewer process remains.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R8-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1081-1093 — the normal shim path skips environment matching, but the shimless embedder fallback remains (spec residual L6).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R8-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:979-983; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:27-31; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go:146-162.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R8-N3\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1049-1055; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:110-112; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go:164-185.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R8-N4\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:50-63,133-139; pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_active.go:100,272; pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:59-60.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed all paths in the sealed change list: Linux/other process reaping, shim startup/reporting, dispatch/cancellation, attempt reservation/release/listing and CLI, review brief/template digest, documentation and scaffold copies. Also read the spec requirements, decisions, residual limits and known gaps. Ran focused tests and vet; strict surface check passed. Strict full and module validation ran but could not build in this read-only sandbox; the sealed build/e2e/integration/unit evidence was used. The checked-out spec defines L1, L2, L3, L4 and L6; it has no L5 despite the implementer note.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified the standard CLI enables the run shim, fd 3 is not inherited, and dead-owner release requires a stalled marker. Unresolved assumptions are that the shim can inspect and signal every child and can publish its full report; N2 and N3 capture those failures. Accepted spec limits are shimless embedder environment matching (L6), non-Linux group-only cleanup (L2), external live-parent escape (L1), markerless legacy reservation confirmation (L4), and non-inspectable process handling (L3).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The run shim confines subreaper scope, but an inspection failure exits before the subtree is fully reaped and the dispatcher-only owner marker lets release proceed after dispatcher death.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The CLI additions are additive and a released reservation is represented as an ordinary failed run plus receipt; run/receipt schemas remain unchanged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Attempt identifiers are validated, abandonment is a typed refusal, live owners are refused, and read/receipt failures retain context.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The change stays within pose-mcp and does not alter REST, MCP, protobuf, or event contracts. The integration assessment's unobserved HTTP consumers are outside the changed surface.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A report larger than the reader limit can block before the shim returns; truncated JSON produces a generic unreadable-report failure and loses the PIDs the run record should name.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Earlier run records retain their meaning; the new release writes the existing failed-run and receipt formats, and the CLI flag is additive.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"An unbounded descendant list can block report publication and prevent a fully reaped run from completing its required record and conclusion path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-7d32807cefe47d21\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The process-scoped shim addresses the cause that process-group kills miss detached sessions while avoiding dispatcher-wide subreaper adoption and reviewer-controlled environment authority. The release records preserve ordinary run semantics. The design assessment observed no structural deltas; N2 and N3 are implementation gaps.\",\n      \"mappings\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The root and localized manuals, scaffold copies, and runtime limitation text still describe environment-based cleanup as the normal path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The documented cleanup guarantee and diagnostic limitations do not match the standard CLI's shim behavior, so operators cannot rely on the stated process-selection and disclosure behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R2 is not met when the ended-PID report exceeds 64 KiB; N3 also leaves a process-liveness gap when cleanup fails after dispatcher death.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The implementation, tests and manual updates align with the spec's review cleanup and abandoned-attempt scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A reviewer descendant can remain alive after the shim's fail-fast inspection path while release proves only that the dispatcher has died.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-7d32807cefe47d21\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A per-run subreaper shim is the smallest sufficient ownership boundary for detached descendants; a process-wide subreaper or reviewer-controlled environment matching would broaden authority. The shim and lock-file release follow D1/D2, but report bounds and cleanup-failure liveness still need correction.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran to exit 0.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-7d32807cefe47d21\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran; no structural deltas were observed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence; changed cleanup and release files contain no TODO/FIXME/stub markers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" assess integrate --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan completed but reported three unobserved HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp), which are outside this change's contracts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs have invalid follow-up metadata and it reported an uncovered panic in pose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache.go:334, outside this subject.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Closeout-check requires a completed review attestation; this review is not authorized to record one.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Review-check runs after an attestation; this review is not authorized to record one.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/review-assurance-disclosure-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran strict surface-check: one target, zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Strict validation was run but all steps failed before execution because the sandbox denied Go temporary-workdir/cache writes; sealed evidence contains passing build/e2e/integration/unit results.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Module validation was run but all steps failed before execution because the sandbox denied Go temporary-workdir/cache writes; sealed pose-mcp evidence contains passing build/e2e/integration/unit results.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
